window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS=(window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2301,"title":"Chapter 2301: An Absurd Theory(2)","paragraphs":["The entire room fell silent after Xie Mey revealed to them that Kulas had fallen sick literally the day after their departure.","In order to properly test his theory, Kulas made it so that even if he were to fall sick after Tian Yang had left, they wouldn’t tell him.","\"Can we even call this a coincidence anymore?\" Ren Xia sighed out loud. \"Now, we need to see if Kulas recovers after your return. If he does...\"","Ren Xia didn’t dare to finish her sentence due to how ridiculous it would make her sound.","Tian Yang was also perplexed by the situation. Why would Kulas fall sick the moment he left the palace? Was he somehow involved with Kulas’ situation?","Thus, Tian Yang and Ren Xia began living within the palace once again, patiently waiting for any changes from Kulas.","One month... three months... half a year later.","\"...\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia’s jaws dropped with disbelief when Kulas suddenly appeared before them with a broad smile on his face, looking as healthy as ever.","\"You...\" Tian Yang opened his mouth but closed it almost immediately after finding himself speechless.","\"I am pretty much convinced that you’re the cure to my situation,\" Kulas declared with a serious face. \"However...\"","He turned to look at Ren Xia and continued, \"That said, there’s also a possibility that you might be the cause instead. After all, you are always with my brother.\"","Since Ren Xia followed Tian Yang wherever he went, there was a chance that Ren Xia might be the one who was helping him recover.","Thus, in order to rule out any possibility, Kulas asked Tian Yang to leave the palace again. However, this time, Ren Xia had to stay behind.","Although Ren Xia despised the idea of leaving Tian Yang after spending the last several thousand years by his side, she had no choice if she wanted this testing to be over with.","Tian Yang left the palace a few days later, while Ren Xia stayed behind.","\"Even if one of us might be the reason you’re recovering from your phenomenon, it won’t solve anything unless we figure out the core issue of it,\" Ren Xia said to Kulas. \"It’s not like we can stay by your side for the rest of our lives, after all.\"","Kulas sighed, \"I am well aware of that. However, it’s a starting point.\"","Kulas and Ren Xia continued their conversation, mostly with Ren Xia asking about the situation between the Giant Race and the Three Pillars of Heaven.","However, halfway into their conversation, Kulas had a mood swing and attacked Ren Xia.","\"Kulas, you son of a bitch... I knew I was right to remain alert even if you looked normal.\"","Ren Xia cursed at him after avoiding his surprise attack.","Fortunately, Ren Xia was also at the True Immortal Realm, and she had been cautious of Kulas since Tian Yang left.","Kulas continued to attack Ren Xia while exuding immense killing intent. His family, who were always on alert and ready to act, quickly arrived to assist her.","This was Ren Xia’s first time seeing Kulas during one of his mood swings, and what she witnessed left her baffled.","\"You call this a mere ’mood swing’?\" she muttered with a dumbfounded look on her face.","Kulas’s appearance had visibly shifted, his skin flushing an unnatural crimson, like an overripe tomato.","\"He looks possessed!\" Ren Xia remarked as she worked with Kulas’ family to subdue him.","\"Hey! How do we calm him down?!\" she asked.","\"We can’t do anything but wait!\" Xie Mey replied. \"Once he’s in this state, he will go on a rampage until he falls unconscious.\"","\"Damn it! And how long will this last?!\"","\"It typically lasts for a few hours, but it could last as long as several days!\"","A few hours later, Kulas suddenly stopped moving, and his red complexion began to return to normal. However, Kulas didn’t fall unconscious as Xie Mey had said.","\"What happened? I came back as soon as I got your message.\" A familiar voice suddenly resounded.","Standing by the door was Tian Yang, who purposefully didn’t travel too far from the Giant’s Continent and immediately returned upon receiving Ren Xia’s message, as she had contacted him the moment Kulas attacked.","\"This crazy son of a bitch attacked me in the middle of our conversation,\" Ren Xia said. \"And seeing how he calmed down the moment you returned, I guess we can only accept his theory as reality. For some reason, you’re keeping whatever phenomenon is causing him to rampage and turn sick at bay.\"","Kulas, who had returned to normal, first offered his apologies to Ren Xia for attacking her before speaking to Tian Yang.","\"So, as long as you stay at the palace, I won’t have any mood swings.\"","However, Tian Yang then said, \"Have you forgotten about what happened during the incident with the Three Pillars of Heaven? I was still at the palace at that time. Yet, you still had a mood swing, even killing one of them.\"","\"That’s...\" Kulas shook his head. \"I cannot explain that.\"","At that time, Tian Yang was chatting with Jing Ruye and Sun Rouxi inside his room, which wasn’t far away from the throne room.","\"But if you’re still not convinced, I am willing to do a few more tests,\" he then said.","Tian Yang sighed, \"There’s no need. Who knows what might happen if we keep triggering your mysterious illness?\"","\"A phenomenon that won’t trigger if you are here, huh? I have never heard of anything this bizarre before.\" Chao Shuying, who was also there, said out loud.","\"What if he’s the reason our father is sick in the first place?\"","Someone there suddenly uttered.","\"Which bastard dares to utter such nonsense?\" Kulas was the first to respond, and he glared in the direction from which the voice came, his gaze full of anger.","If looks could kill, he would be able to massacre an entire army with his current expression."]},{"number":2302,"title":"Chapter 2302: Four Thousand Years","paragraphs":["The one who made the remark subconsciously trembled in fear and hid behind his mother after hearing Kulas’ words and sensing his killing intent.","\"Even if you’re my own son, I won’t tolerate such bullshit!\" Kulas spoke as he started walking toward his son. \"I won’t kill you, but I also won’t hesitate to disown you!\"","Seeing this, Tian Yang quickly spoke, \"Relax. He has a good reason to be suspicious of me. I would do the same if I were in his shoes. Save your energy for something more useful, like figuring out the cause of your illness. No, it cannot even be called an illness. It’s more like a phenomenon at this point.\"","\"By the way, what did you speak to the Three Pillars of Heaven about previously? Perhaps the subject had triggered your phenomenon.\" Ren Xiaa suddenly asked.","\"Well, we talked about...\" Kulas started his sentence but abruptly halted midway. \"Now that I think about it, what did we talk about?\"","He wore a pondering look on his face as he tried to recall what he spoke about with the Three Pillars of Heaven. Yet, no matter how hard he tried, he couldn’t seem to remember anything prior to his mood swing.","It was extremely odd, considering that he typically only lost memories of the time he spent while affected by the phenomenon. This implied that the phenomenon might have begun the moment their conversation began, which is why he couldn’t remember anything.","\"So, what now?\" Tian Yang asked. \"Although I may be able to prevent the phenomenon from occurring by being near you, it doesn’t fix the core issue at hand.\"","\"Just preventing it is good enough for now,\" Kulas said. \"Once I deal with the issue with the Three Pillars of Heaven, I will focus on finding a real cure.\"","He turned to look at Ren Xia and continued, \"Sorry, but I will have to borrow your husband for some time.\"","She frowned and replied, \"Why are you making it sound so weird? We’ll just be living here like before.\"","\"No, it won’t be like before, especially since we are at war. But don’t worry, I’ll ensure your safety even at the cost of my life.\"","Tian Yang laughed, \"Big words from someone who still hasn’t defeated me once. We can protect ourselves, so focus on your own issues.\"","Thus, Tian Yang and Ren Xia returned to living within the palace. However, just as Kulas said, it was different from before. From the tense atmosphere to the constant alertness around him, it made Tian Yang feel as though he was still fighting the Immortal Clans, even though he was not involved in the war personally.","Time passed in a flash, and Kulas remained healthy for the next two hundred years, further proving that Tian Yang’s presence kept his phenomenon at bay.","Then, another three hundred years passed.","It has been five hundred years since Tian Yang started staying at the palace, and Kulas hasn’t had a single mood swing, putting his family at ease. Although his family no longer were suspicious of Tian Yang, they definitely still didn’t like him. The reason? It was simply due to jealousy.","Forget about his own children; even his wives were envious of their relationship.","\"Aren’t you jealous of your husband’s relationship with ours?\" One of them suddenly asked Ren Xia when they crossed paths in the halls.","Ren Xia chucked, \"Why would I be jealous? If anyone is jealous, it would be Kulas. If he were born a woman, he would’ve definitely fallen head over heels for Tian Yang.\"","\"That’s...\"","Kulas’ wife couldn’t believe how bold and rude Ren Xia was towards Kulas.","\"You speak as if you are close to my husband. I thought you were just Senior Tian’s partner?\"","\"I wouldn’t call us close, but we were once engaged with each other. Of course, it wasn’t of our own free will but the result of our parents’ selfishness. Because of that, we’d often argue. It’s the exact opposite relationship he has with my husband.\"","After that conversation, Ren Xia began getting to know Kulas’ wives who weren’t Chao Shuying, as they’d start approaching her to complain about Kulas, and she found it highly entertaining.","As time continued to pass, the Three Pillars of Heaven’s assault on the Giant Race became more frequent, with giants being attacked almost once a week.","But despite all that, the Giant Race remained unyielding. If anything, their power grew, fueled by their anger toward the Three Pillars of Heaven.","By now, two thousand years have passed since their war began. Although most of the world was still unaware of it, some of the more influential and powerful factions have started to realize it. While they didn’t plan to join the war, they began preparing for the worst-case scenario.","As for the progression in cultivation, nobody has managed to break through past the True Immortal realm yet.","Then, another two thousand years passed.","It has been four thousand years since Kulas’ last mood swing, and because it has been so long, Kulas has begun to believe he has been cured. However, the moment he started being hopeful, the phenomenon returned.","It happened on one sunny day, while Kulas was cultivating with one of his wives. In the midst of their cultivation, Kulas had a mood swing and gravely injured her, nearly killing her, had Tian Yang not arrived in time to stop him.","\"Fuck! Why has it returned after so long?!\" Tian Yang cursed as he witnessed Kulas’ phenomenon with his own eyes for the first time.","\"Hey! Wake the hell up!\"","Tian Yang fought Kulas with incredible difficulty. Since Kulas never stopped training, even increasing the amount he trained, he had almost caught up to Tian Yang. Not only that, but the phenomenon boosted his strength tremendously.","Of course, the naked sight of Kulas, who was just cultivating with his wife, didn’t help at all.","Fortunately, Ren Xia and the others came to assist him. However, even with help, Kulas was almost unstoppable, and their clash destroyed over half of the palace over the next several days."]},{"number":2303,"title":"Chapter 2303: Acting as Giant Emperor Kulas","paragraphs":["When Kulas finally calmed down after days of rampaging, his appearance underwent another drastic transformation, turning from a massive, unstoppable giant to that of a sickly old man with one foot in his grave.","He’d gotten so weak that he could hardly speak, much less stand.","After Kulas collapsed, his family brought him to his room to rest.","\"To think it would happen again right when we were beginning to feel hopeful that he’d fully recovered...\"","His family sighed, looking defeated and depressed as they stood around the bed.","\"So, what now?\" Ren Xia asked Tian Yang.","Tian Yang clenched his fists, feeling a sense of helplessness wash over his entire being.","\"We’ve tried countless things in the past four thousand years, but alas... In the end, we were unable to figure out anything about his illness. At this rate, I will have no choice but to head to the Holy Continent.\"","\"That might not be a good idea,\" said Ren Xia. \"And I am not saying this because I don’t want you to go. I mean, I don’t, but if you leave, there’s a chance that Kulas’ illness might worsen. You have suppressed his illness by being near him, and despite his current situation, you might still be suppressing it. If you suddenly leave... his illness will worsen, and that’s the best scenario. Worst-case, he’ll die.\"","Tian Yang found Ren Xia’s words to be very logical. If he were still suppressing Kulas’ illness even at this moment, that suppressed illness might go on a rampage the moment he leaves.","Although it wasn’t definitive and merely a theory, it was an immense risk that Tian Yang didn’t dare to take, as his sworn brother’s life was on the line.","Unable to leave the palace, Tian Yang continued trying to solve the mystery behind Kulas’ illness from within. Unfortunately, he was not a medical expert, so he mostly helped Chao Shuying as her assistant.","Several more years passed, but Kulas hasn’t woken up from his slumber even once, even though he used to wake up once a year.","Kulas’ coma left his family in a precarious position, especially with the war against the Three Pillars of Heaven still ongoing. Fortunately, the Giant Race was already accustomed to such conflicts and knew how to respond even without Kulas’s direct command. Even so, the absence of their leader could not be ignored. If the Three Pillars of Heaven were to learn of this, they would undoubtedly launch a full-scale assault.","One day, Kulas’ wives approached Tian Yang.","\"Senior Tian... This may sound very sudden, but do you think you can act as the Giant Emperor for the time being?\"","\"What?\" Tian Yang almost couldn’t believe his ears.","\"We heard from our husband that he acquired the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique from you, so you should be able to transform your body.\"","\"But why are you asking me? Your sons can do it without the technique.\" Tian Yang said.","\"Yes, but you’re the only one at the True Immortal realm. Although we could replicate his appearance, we cannot do the same with his cultivation, as it’ll be easily discovered.\"","\"We’re not asking you to lead the Giant Race or fulfill the role of an emperor. We just need you to show up and meet visitors once in a while so the Three Pillars of Heaven won’t realize that our husband is absent.\"","\"If they learn that our husband is bedridden, they will definitely attack the Giant Continent with full force. If that happens... we will all perish before our husband even wake up.\"","Hearing this, there was no way Tian Yang could refuse, so he agreed to pretend to be Kulas.","Thus, Tian Yang had a new routine in his life. Once every few months, he would disguise himself as Kulas to meet with people and wander the continent just to reveal his presence.","Of course, Kulas’ family didn’t leave Tian Yang alone and had Xie Mey, who was the most familiar with him, assist him during the meetings.","They continued with this farce for several hundred years, and Tian Yang had gotten so good at pretending to be Kulas that even his family would sometimes mistake him for the real Kulas.","Because of his efforts, the Three Pillars of Heaven remained oblivious about Kulas’ real condition.","One day, one of Kulas’ wives approached Tian Yang.","\"Senior Tian... allow me to apologize in advance, but I have a request for you...\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Back when my husband was still healthy, he would regularly interact with us... embrace us,\" she said softly. \"Now, with him like this, that’s no longer possible. It’s been hundreds of years since we’ve embraced anyone, and with the war and everything else, we’re all stressed and pent up...\"","She hesitated before continuing, \"...Do you think you could help us?\"","Tian Yang couldn’t believe what he was hearing.","\"You... Are you really asking me to sleep with my sworn brother’s wives while he is bedridden?\" he responded with a deep frown on his face.","\"Leave. I will pretend this interaction never happened, but don’t you dare bring this subject up again in the future.\"","The wife sighed. Although she had anticipated such a response, she was still disappointed.","After apologizing to Tian Yang again, she left with an embarrassed feeling around her.","\"Unbelievable...\" Tian Yang shook his head.","The following year, Chao Shuying suddenly approached Tian Yang with a panicked look.","\"S-Senior Tian! This is an emergency!\"","\"What happened? Did the Three Pillars of Heaven attack again?\"","\"No! It’s even worse than that! Some of our children have begun to have mood swings!\"","\"What?!\" Tian Yang exclaimed.","He immediately followed Chao Shuying to another room, where several of Kulas’ children were being restrained after going on a rampage.","\"Did this just happen?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Well... about that...\" Chao Shuying rubbed her eyes and sighed, revealing, \"Honestly, they have been showing signs for the last several years. However, we weren’t certain it was the same illness affecting our husband, so we decided to watch over them for the time being until we were certain.\""]},{"number":2304,"title":"Chapter 2304: A Shocking Discovery","paragraphs":["\"Even if you weren’t certain, you should’ve told me about it!\" Tian Yang spoke loudly.","\"Sorry...\" Seeing his expression, Chao Shuying could only apologize like a child who knew they’d done something wrong.","\"So, does this mean the illness is contagious?\" Ren Xia suddenly asked.","\"We considered that at first, but we don’t believe that is the case,\" Chao Shuying said. \"If it were contagious, it would’ve affected all of us much earlier.\"","\"If it’s not contagious, then they got it through other methods, such as their bloodline.\" Ren Xia remarked before turning to Tian Yang, staring at him with a perplexed face.","\"What is it?\" he asked. \"If you know something, tell me.\"","She sighed before speaking, \"What if the illness is caused by the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique? What if it contaminated his bloodline? I considered this before, but I quickly tossed that thought away because if that were the case, his children would also be affected by the illness. Since it was exclusive to Kulas at that time, I thought that wasn’t the case. However, now that his children are also affected...\"","Tian Yang and Chao Shuying’s eyes widened at Ren Xia’s speculation.","Although it sounded ridiculous, it was the most logical explanation.","\"The Great Mammoth Body Refinement was something I acquired in Han Zexian’s Tomb, and the possibility that it might be a corrupted technique never crossed my mind, but now...\"","While countless cultivation techniques in the world function flawlessly, there also exist those that are fundamentally flawed or even harmful to their users. The most common among them are techniques that grant immense power with little apparent effort at first—only for the cultivator to suffer a violent death later, when the hidden flaws of the technique finally manifest.","Such techniques are exceedingly rare in the modern era due to advances in cultivation knowledge. However, in the Primordial Era, when the cultivation world was still in its infancy, they were far more common.","Tian Yang couldn’t believe how naive and trusting he had been. Han Zexian was a mysterious individual, someone the world knew almost nothing about, so why had he trusted the man’s cultivation techniques so completely, without even questioning them?","Yet Tian Yang was far from alone in this. Almost everyone who had ventured into Han Zexian’s tomb had trusted its rewards without question.","Perhaps the merciless trials themselves were to blame, grinding away doubt. After all, who would believe that someone willing to design trials where failure meant death would leave behind a corrupted technique as a reward?","\"There’s only one way to confirm this speculation...\" Tian Yang suddenly spoke. \"I have to study the technique until I have full comprehension.\"","\"It’s too risky! What if it also affects you?!\" Ren Xia rejected the idea.","Tian Yang smiled and said, \"Relax, I am only studying it with the intent of increasing my comprehension. I am not actually going to train it.\"","Starting from that day, Tian Yang spent nearly all of his time studying the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique.","Time continued to pass, and as Tian Yang’s comprehension of the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique eventually surpassed even Kulas’ own understanding, more and more of Kulas’ children started to fall sick.","\"I thought it was just a coincidence at first, but there’s no doubt that the illness is more likely to affect men than women,\" said Chao Shuying.","Over two hundred of Kulas’ children had fallen ill at this point, but only three of them were female.","\"Any progress with the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique?\" she then asked Tian Yang.","He nodded and responded with confidence, \"There is definitely something odd about the technique, and I am very close to understanding it.\"","More than two thousand years had passed since Kulas fell into a coma. The Giant Race’s war with the Three Pillars of Heaven dragged on, its end nowhere in sight. However, as more and more of Kulas’s children began to fall ill, it became inevitable that the Three Pillars of Heaven would realize something was wrong.","It wasn’t only the Three Pillars of Heaven who sensed that something was wrong. The giant citizens of the continent also noticed the palace’s growing absence of presence, not to mention the constant disturbances emanating from within.","Another two hundred years later, even giants with no direct relation to Kulas began to suffer from similar mood swings. And because these episodes occurred openly within the cities, it became virtually impossible to prevent the truth from spreading.","During their mood swings, giants would attack any visitors who entered the continent. As a result, people eventually stopped visiting altogether.","Seeing an opportunity, the Three Pillars of Heaven seized upon these incidents as a pretext to officially declare war on the Giant Race, branding them a threat to humanity.","\"The Giant Race has finally revealed its fangs! They have always harbored ill intent toward humanity! We sensed that something was wrong long ago, but lacked the evidence—until now! There is a reason they abandoned their humanity to form their own race!\"","With such words, the Three Pillars of Heaven spread their propaganda throughout the Divine Heaven, instantly turning the Giant Race against humans.","A year after the Three Pillars of Heaven’s official declaration of war, Tian Yang finally unraveled the mystery behind the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique.","\"T-This is... impossible!\" Tian Yang was left in shock by the discovery.","\"What did you discover?\" Ren Xia asked him.","He gritted his teeth and replied, \"There is another technique within the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique...\"","\"What sort of technique?\"","He looked at her and continued, \"A communication technique.\"","\"What?\" Ren Xia raised her eyebrows in puzzlement.","However, Tian Yang shook his head and apologized, \"Sorry, but this is all I can tell you for now, as it contains forbidden information that requires your longevity to understand.\"","With a resolute expression, Ren Xia responded, \"You’ve kept it to yourself for long enough, my dear. Why don’t you share some of that burden with me? Even if I have to sacrifice some of my longevity, I want to know.\""]},{"number":2305,"title":"Chapter 2305: Contacting the Outer God Again","paragraphs":["After hearing Ren Xia’s words, Tian Yang sighed before responding in a worried voice, \"I had to sacrifice several million years of longevity to learn this information. If it weren’t for the pills, I would’ve never been able to learn it.\"","\"A few million years, huh?\" Ren Xia muttered in a low voice.","She’d be lying if she said she wasn’t worried about losing so many years of her longevity. However, as his partner, she didn’t want Tian Yang to endure the burden alone.","After pondering for a moment, she spoke, \"I am willing to lose a few million years if it means I can finally walk beside you. Although we’ve been together for so long, it always feels like I am slightly trailing behind you.\"","\"Ren Xia...\"","\"Please, let me be selfish... really selfish for once...\" she glared at him with a pleading gaze.","\"Also, it’ll give me more motivation to break through to the next realm if I suddenly lose a few million years of my lifespan, and I don’t know how much longer I have left to live.\"","Although cultivators who entered the Immortal Realm are called Immortals and are said to have an unlimited lifespan, that was only a speculation.","A defeated smile tugged at Tian Yang’s lips as he spoke, \"Fine, I’ll tell you. However, I’ll stop the moment I sense anything even slightly wrong. Hell, we don’t even know if a cultivator at the True Immortal realm has that much longevity.\"","He proceeded to reach for his spatial ring before retrieving Han Zexian’s diary, something he kept even though he had memorized all of its content.","\"This is Han Zexian’s diary, something I found inside his cavern. Try not to be too shocked about what you read.\"","He handed the diary to her, his hand uncontrollably trembling slightly.","\"Thank you...\" Ren Xia accepted the diary and took a moment to mentally prepare herself.","Once she was prepared, she opened the diary and began reading it.","A few seconds later, she lifted her head to look at Tian Yang and asked, \"How do I know if my longevity is being consumed? I don’t feel any different.\"","\"You don’t?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows, looking puzzled by her statement.","When he first read the diary, he felt fatigued the instant he did, even though he had been perfectly normal before.","He then explained to her about his own experience.","\"Nope, I don’t feel any different, much less fatigued.\" Ren Xia said. \"Maybe I’ll feel it after reading some more.\"","She immediately went back to the diary.","As she delved deeper into the contents of Han Zexian’s diary, her eyes widened with shock and disbelief at the discovery of the Outer Gods’ existence, incomprehensible beings with unfathomable strength who lived beyond their world.","While the diary dumbfounded Ren Xia, Tian Yang stared at her with an astonished look of his own.","\"How much have you read?\" he suddenly asked her.","\"I’m almost done with it,\" she calmly replied.","\"And you still feel completely fine?\"","\"Yes,\" she nodded.","\"How?! Is it because you are at the True Immortal realm, and a few million years is nothing but a drop in the bucket, hence why you don’t even feel it being consumed?\" he wondered out loud. \"No... even if that’s the case, there’s no way you wouldn’t feel that much lifespan being forcefully drained!\"","\"I don’t know what to tell you.\" Ren Xia shrugged as she returned to finishing the last few sentences in the diary.","A few moments later, she closed the diary and placed it down.","\"Outer Gods, huh? I am still trying to grasp my head around such an existence actually existing...\"","\"They really exist. I personally spoke with one, after all.\"","\"What?\" Ren Xia looked at him with wide eyes.","\"What were they like? What did you talk about?\"","Tian Yang recalled his meeting with the ten-armed Outer God to her.","\"He said he’d grant me a wish. I asked for talent, but he said that I already had it, so he gave me something else. As for what the something is... I have no clue. He also said that we’d meet again, but it’s been several thousand years since that meeting.\"","\"Hey... are you sure you’re feeling fine?\" Tian Yang continued with a worried frown. \"If you’re trying to act tough so I wouldn’t be worried, it’s actually having the opposite effect.\"","Ren Xia chuckled and said, \"I swear I am feeling fine. What about you? Are you sure you had to sacrifice your longevity to learn this information?\"","Tian Yang nodded, \"Of course. I even tested it on some people from the Immortal Clans before. When I gave them the diary to read, they would all scream in pain until they stopped. When I forced them to listen to it, they all died a violent death.\"","Ren Xia raised an eyebrow and asked, \"What were you trying to achieve by doing that?\"","\"I wanted to test the limit of this information and its restrictions. Unfortunately, I didn’t really learn anything.\"","\"Well, I am completely fine even after reading the whole thing, so something might’ve changed.\"","\"I guess so... but we should remain alert in case the effects are delayed.\"","\"Anyway, let’s get back on topic. The Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique had a communication technique hidden within it. While it differs from the one in Han Zexian’s tomb, the similarities suggest it reaches out to an Outer God—just not the one I spoke with.\"","\"Does that mean Kulas used this technique and contacted the Outer God?\"","\"That’s... possible. However, we won’t know for sure until Kulas wakes up and we question him.\"","\"I know this will sound insensitive, but will he even wake up? It’s been thousands of years, you know?\"","Tian Yang sighed, \"I won’t give up until his last breath.\"","Suddenly, he thought of an idea.","\"Wait a second. If an Outer God is involved with Kulas’ situation, perhaps I can ask another Outer God for help? I still remember the communication technique, so it might be possible to call for him again.\""]},{"number":2306,"title":"Chapter 2306: Contacting the Outer God Again(2)","paragraphs":["\"You want to contact an Outer God? Are you sure that’s... safe?\" Ren Xia wore a worried frown on her face after hearing Tian Yang’s words.","\"It should be. Nothing happened last time, and he didn’t seem annoyed by it. If anything, he’s probably expecting me to contact him again,\" he replied.","\"Be careful then...\" Ren Xia left the room a moment later.","Once he was prepared, Tian Yang recited the communication technique.","\"O ancient gods beyond the veil of reason, where time coils and the stars weep—heed my call! I invoke the Nameless, whose shadows consume light, whose whispers unravel fate! Through the fracture of all that is, through the silence where even Dao crumbles... descend and make this world your own!\"","Nothing happened for a few seconds, but Tian Yang wasn’t as impatient as last time.","After several minutes of waiting, he finally felt his consciousness being drawn out of his body and speeding into the heavens.","After what felt like an eternity, he was in the starry sky again, and hovering before him was a massive entity with ten arms, surrounded by an unfathomable aura.","\"I knew you’d seek me again, but to think you’d do it so soon,\" said the Outer God.","\"It’s been several thousand years, though...\"","Tian Yang wasn’t as overwhelmed by the god’s presence this time.","\"I have lived for billions... trillions of years. A few mere thousand years is no different than yesterday.\"","\"Trillions of years...?\" Tian Yang was left speechless by its casual remark.","His world wasn’t even a million years old, yet the god before him had lived trillions of years? As ridiculous as it sounded, he didn’t doubt it.","\"So, why have you contacted me this time, mortal?\"","\"I have a question—a favor of sorts. But first, if I am bothering you, you can send me away, and I won’t bother you again.\"","\"It’s fine, I am not bothered. It’s not like there’s anything else for me to do. I left behind a method to contact me for a reason.\"","\"In that case, may I ask for your help? I have this friend who...\"","Tian Yang proceeded to tell the god about Kulas’ situation and the communication technique hidden within the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique.","\"Have you tried contacting the being through the technique yet?\" The Outer God asked.","\"Of course not. If Kulas’ situation was caused by that technique and Outer God, I don’t want to get involved with them.\"","\"Yet you didn’t hesitate to contact me?\"","\"I was curious at that time, and I had put so much effort and sacrificed so much of my lifespan. With that said, you don’t seem dangerous.\"","\"That is a foolish thing to assume. Fortunately for you, I am unlike the others, who wouldn’t hesitate to sacrifice your kind for their own entertainment.\"","\"How many Outer Gods are out there? And why are they doing this? Is it just for entertainment?\"","\"I cannot answer your first question, as you lack the longevity to know. As for your second question, it is true for some, but now all of them are trying to be entertained.\"","\"So if I want to learn about the Outer Gods, I need sufficient longevity? Does this apply to everyone?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Yes, all beings in your world require sufficient sacrifice to learn about us.\"","\"Then how come someone I know managed to learn about the Outer Gods’ existence without any sacrifice? At least that’s what she said.\"","\"That is not possible,\" said the Outer God. \"They have either already paid the sacrifice before, or they don’t realize it.\"","’There’s no way Ren Xia already knew of the Outer Gods based on her reaction after reading Han Zexian’s diary. Does this mean she simply didn’t realize her longevity was being sacrificed? Like how some people can’t feel pain?’ Tian Yang wondered inwardly.","\"Let’s get back on topic. About your friend’s issue... it is definitely caused by another Eternal—what you call Outer Gods. However, there’s nothing I can do to help unless I confront that Eternal directly.\"","\"That’s...\"","Tian Yang didn’t even need to ask to know that this Eternal wouldn’t go through the trouble for a mere mortal, so he didn’t say anything.","However, the Eternal continued, \"Even if I want to help you, I would need to know the identity of the one behind it.\"","\"Huh? You’re actually willing to help me?\"","\"Well, that will depend on whether you’ll return the favor and the identity of the Eternal.\"","\"What do you need from me?\" Tian Yang asked.","He wasn’t surprised to hear that the Eternal wanted something from him, almost as if he’d anticipated it somewhere in his consciousness.","’There’s nothing that is truly free in this world, after all,’ he sighed inwardly.","\"I am looking for something. That is the most I can tell you right now, due to your lack of longevity.\"","\"The only ways for me to extend my lifespan are through treasures or cultivation,\" Tian Yang said. \"The amount of treasures required to gain enough longevity is simply unfeasible, leaving cultivation as the only option. But the entire cultivation world has been stalled at the True Immortal Realm for thousands of years, unable to advance further despite our awareness of Celestial Qi.\"","\"I am aware of the situation in your world. Since I need you to improve your cultivation to achieve my own goals, I shall assist you with reaching the next realm.\"","\"Really?!\" Tian Yang was ecstatic to hear such words.","\"I cannot directly improve your cultivation,\" the Outer God said. \"So instead, I will show you what you need to ascend.\"","As one of its ten arms pointed at him, Tian Yang felt something click within his mind—a sudden, profound realization, almost as if he had an enlightenment.","\"This will be all for now. If you want me to help your friend, learn the identity of the Eternal behind him. Until next time, mortal. Ah, one last thing before I send you away. You may call me...\"","When Tian Yang came back to it inside his room, he muttered, \"Shura, huh? I wanted to ask him about the gift he gave me, but I guess that will have to wait until next time.\""]},{"number":2307,"title":"Chapter 2307: Soul Cultivation","paragraphs":["\"I’m done. Did you wait long?\"","After his meeting with Shura concluded, Tian Yang went outside and spoke with Ren Xia.","\"Huh? Did you fail to contact the Outer God?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"No, I succeeded. What made you think that I’d failed?\" he asked with a puzzled face.","\"I have been out here for less than a minute,\" she replied.","\"Really?\" Tian Yang mumbled with a dumbfounded face.","While he didn’t speak with Shura for long, it definitely lasted for several minutes, not to mention how long it felt for his consciousness to enter the starry sky just to meet Shura.","\"Not only did I speak with the Outer God, but I even received help from him. I’ll tell you more inside.\"","Ren Xia nodded and went back inside the room.","Once the doors closed, Tian Yang recalled his conversation with Shura.","\"The beings we call Outer Gods call themselves Eternals, and they have existed for trillions of years.\"","\"T-Trillions of years?!\" Ren Xia exclaimed in shock.","It was simply an unimaginable amount of time for someone who has only lived a few measly thousands of years.","\"Not only did he say he’d help with Kulas’s situation—as long as I uncover the identity of the Eternal interfering with him—but he also showed me how to reach the next cultivation realm,\" Tian Yang said, unable to hide his excitement.","\"Huh? How does that even work?\" she asked.","\"It’s hard to put into words,\" he replied. \"It was as if he fed the knowledge directly into me, almost like passing on a technique. It felt exactly like a moment of sudden realization... like enlightenment itself.\"","\"So... are you going to break through to the next cultivation realm soon?\" she then asked.","A bittersweet smile suddenly tugged at his lips, and he replied in a somewhat defeated voice, \"Just because I know the path required to enter the next realm, it doesn’t mean I’ll be able to get there soon. As a matter of fact, even with this knowledge, I highly doubt I’ll be able to break through in the next ten... fifty thousand years.\"","\"Fifty thousand years?! That long?!\" Ren Xia exclaimed with a bewildered face.","He nodded. \"At least fifty thousand years, so it could take even longer. And it’s only this short because the answers were given to me. If I had to figure this out by myself, it could’ve easily taken ten times as long.\"","\"Why does it take that long? Is it because of our understanding of Celestial Qi?\"","\"That is only a small portion. After we reach a certain level of understanding, we must cultivate Celestial Qi and also our souls.\"","\"What? Did you just say our... soul?\" Ren Xia raised an eyebrow at his last word.","In that era, the concept of cultivating one’s soul was still in its infancy. The soul was the most sensitive and vulnerable part of any being, so most were reluctant to tamper with it, leaving only madmen willing to attempt such cultivation.","Because the subject was so rarely explored, there were scarcely any soul cultivation techniques in existence. And even if such techniques were freely offered, few—if any—would dare to practice them.","\"So... did the Outer—Eternal give you a cultivation technique to strength the soul?\" she then asked.","Tian Yang shook his head.","\"Unfortunately, he did not.\"","Ren Xia sighed, \"Although it’s great that we now know how to reach the next realm, it doesn’t really help. Not only do we need to create a cultivation technique for Celestial Qi, but we also need to cultivate our soul.\"","\"Oh.\" Tian Yang suddenly spoke, \"While he didn’t give me a soul cultivation technique, he did give me a cultivation technique to cultivate Celestial Qi.\"","\"Really?!\" Ren Xia’s eyes shone with bright excitement.","Tian Yang smiled at her reaction and asked, \"You want it, too? I thought you wanted to ascend to the next realm through your own efforts.\"","Ren Xia sighed and said, \"This and trying to sense Celestial Qi are two different things. Even I must admit that I am not talented enough to create a cultivation technique for Celestial Qi with my own efforts—at least not for several million years.\"","\"Alright, I’ll share the technique with you... but not now. I need to examine it to make sure there’s nothing wrong with it first,\" he said.","Despite what Shura said, there was no guarantee that he wouldn’t try to mess with him, as the Great mammoth Body Refinement technique did.","\"It’s good to be cautious, especially when we are dealing with beings that are still beyond our comprehension,\" Ren Xia nodded. \"Be careful.\"","\"In the meantime... I will leave the continent to look for a soul cultivation technique,\" she added.","\"Are you sure?\"","She nodded.","\"Even if we have a cultivation technique for Celestial Qi, we still need one for our souls. Unfortunately, there’s really nothing for me to do here to help Kulas, and I have been idling enough.\"","\"I understand. When will you leave?\"","\"I’ll leave in a few months.\"","\"Alright.\"","Several months later, Ren Xia left Giant’s Continent to search for a soul cultivation technique. Meanwhile, Tian Yang remained on the continent and started studying the cultivation technique without cultivating it.","A hundred years passed in the blink of an eye, and Ren Xia returned to the palace.","\"How was the search?\" he asked.","\"It was a waste of time,\" Ren Xia rested her body on Tian Yang’s as she sighed out loud. \"Although I found several soul cultivation techniques, they were all trash and had a high fatality rate. However, on my way back here, I heard of a certain rumor—that the Three Pillars of Heaven have recently developed a safe and powerful soul cultivation technique.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow at this information.","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven, huh? So they still have the time to create new techniques while in the middle of a war,\" he sighed.","\"Honestly, I was thinking about going there to check things out, but I wanted to return first to get your opinion,\" Ren Xia suddenly said."]},{"number":2308,"title":"Chapter 2308: Auction for the Soul Cultivation Technique","paragraphs":["\"You want to visit the Holy Continent?\" Tian Yang frowned at Ren Xia’s words. \"Even though you keep saying that you don’t want me to go?\"","\"Well, we are not going there with the same objectives. You want to investigate the Three Pillars of Heaven while I am merely trying to learn more about their soul cultivation technique,\" she replied with a shrug.","Tian Yang sighed, \"Now that I know that the Three Pillars of Heaven are not the ones behind Kulas’ situation, I no longer have any reason to investigate them. If only they weren’t at war with the Giant Race.\"","\"Speaking of investigating... have you had any progress with figuring out the identity of the Eternal behind Kulas’ illness?\" Ren Xia then asked.","He sighed, \"I have tried, but the Eternal isn’t answering me.\"","He’d tried contacting the Eternal using the communication technique found within the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique, but unlike Shura, this Eternal refused to meet him, no matter how long he waited.","And not wanting to bother the Eternal too much, he decided to attempt to contact the Eternal once every thousand years. While that may seem like a long time, if he considered an Eternal’s experience and how differently they sensed time, even a thousand years was short.","To an Eternal, the passage of a thousand years might be no different from a single day, making daily contact seem inconsequential. However, Tian Yang refused to take such a reckless risk, as provoking an Eternal was not something he was willing to gamble with.","\"Anyway, even if you went to the Holy Continent, would they let you in? What’s the point of going there if you cannot even get the soul cultivation technique?\" Tian Yang then asked.","\"Actually, they plan on selling the soul cultivation technique,\" Ren Xia revealed, leaving Tian Yang speechless.","\"Why would they sell something so valuable?\" he asked.","She shrugged.","\"Who knows?\"","\"It’s probably defective, then. Even to this day, they’ve kept the information about Celestial Qi a secret. If it were truly something that would benefit them, they wouldn’t give it away. There’s no way a safe soul cultivation technique wouldn’t benefit them. And I highly doubt the Three Pillars of Heaven are in need of money.\"","\"Well, we wouldn’t know unless we have the technique in our hands,\" said Ren Xia. \"There are not many people who are richer than us right now, especially after we raided the Immortal Clans’ treasury. Kulas also said we can use their resources if we ever need to, so we’re almost guaranteed to outbid everyone. It’s not like we have any other use for our wealth.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang sighed, \"Do whatever you want.\"","\"Then I’ll go buy the soul cultivation technique. The auction won’t start for another ten years, so I’ll stay here until then.\"","Over the next several years, the auction for the soul cultivation technique spread like wildfire. The Three Pillars of Heaven guaranteed its safety, but even they couldn’t completely eliminate the people’s suspicions, who all had the same worry as Tian Yang.","If the soul cultivation technique was truly safe and revolutionary, why would the Three Pillars of Heaven, known for keeping things for themselves until they no longer needed them, sell off such a priceless technique so quickly after developing it? Something was amiss.","Of course, the Three Pillars of Heaven had a response for the growing doubt.","\"This soul cultivation technique may be powerful and safe, but it has extremely harsh requirements, so not just anyone can cultivate it. In fact, no one else besides the creator has been able to cultivate it successfully, hence why we are parting with it. Moreover, the decision to sell this technique was also made by its creator.\"","Ten years passed in the blink of an eye, and Ren Xia left the Giant Continent to participate in the auction for the soul cultivation technique.","The auction ended up being the most successful and largest auction to date, which surprised nobody, as this was the Three Pillars of Heaven’s first time doing such an event.","Millions—tens of millions of cultivators and wealthy individuals participated in the auction.","Before the auction began, the Three Pillars of Heaven revealed half of the soul cultivation technique to everyone present, giving them a small taste.","\"Heavens! What a powerful soul cultivation technique! And this is only half of the entire technique?!\"","Even though only half of the technique was revealed, the experienced cultivators present were still able to gauge its power from that alone. The Three Pillars of Heaven were also unconcerned about anyone completing the remaining half, as the technique was extraordinarily complex. Unless someone possessed unfathomable talent, as well as the same mindset and experience as its creator, there was virtually no chance of finishing it.","When the auction officially began, the very first bid reached an astounding one hundred million spirit stones! It was an amount that instantly removed over two-thirds of the competition there.","However, that was just the beginning, as the very next bid was two hundred million, instantly doubling the previous bid.","Seeing how rapidly the price was climbing, everyone expected the auction to end quickly. After all, only a single item—the soul cultivation technique—was up for sale, and at this pace, it would be over in a matter of minutes. Many had traveled for months, even years, just to attend, and the prospect of it ending so abruptly left more than a few feeling dissatisfied.","However, to everyone’s absolute surprise, the auction would go on for hours with two people directly going against each other.","\"One billion spirit stones,\" Ren Xia casually bid.","\"One billion and one million spirit stones.\" Her opponent bid half a second later.","Although Ren Xia could easily increase the bid by tens of millions at once, she decided to mess with her opponent.","\"One billion and two million spirit stones.\"","\"One billion and three million spirit stones.\"","An hour later...","\"Three billion, five million, and one hundred thousand spirit stones!\"","\"Three billion, five million, and two hundred thousand spirit stones!\" Ren Xia countered.","Thus, the auction dragged on."]},{"number":2309,"title":"Chapter 2309: Auction for the Soul Cultivation Technique(2)","paragraphs":["\"Heavens! Who is that woman bidding against Senior Ru Bing, who is known as the Gold Emperor—the wealthiest individual in the world?!\"","\"I don’t recognize her, but she’s definitely disguising her true appearance right now.\"","Ren Xia’s wealth and relentless bidding against the Gold Emperor left every guest there in awe, especially those who were in the business scene and understood how astonishing it was to fight the Gold Emperor with money.","However, some people there doubted whether Ren Xia really had so much wealth.","\"What if she’s just bidding out of her ass just to increase the price of the soul cultivation technique?\"","\"In the presence of the Three Pillars of Heaven and so many people? There’s no way anyone would be that foolish!\"","Eventually, the bid reached an astonishing five billion spirit stones.","\"Five billion, two hundred million, and one thousand spirit stones!\" The Gold Emperor shouted with clenched fists.","\"Five billion, two hundred million, and two thousand spirit stones.\" Ren Xia countered in a calm voice, sounding as if she were just ordering a simple dish at a restaurant.","’Fuck! I do not believe that bitch truly has so much money!’ The Gold Emperor cursed inwardly.","\"Going once...\"","\"Going twice...\"","\"And—\"","\"SEVEN BILLION!\" The Gold Emperor countered at the very last second, increasing the price by two whole billion in one go.","\"Seven billion spirit stones?!\"","Everyone was stunned by the Gold Emperor’s bid. Even as the richest individual in the world, such an amount would strain his finances for a very long time. And for what? A soul cultivation technique that even the geniuses of the Three Pillars of Heaven had failed to cultivate. It seemed nothing short of a reckless waste.","The Gold Emperor, of course, understood this better than anyone. But at this point, he was no longer bidding for the technique itself. This had become a matter of pride—and he refused to lose to some nobody.","After making his bid, the Gold Emperor stood up and glared at Ren Xia.","\"I do not believe you can outbid me! Even if you do, I doubt you actually have that much money!\" he shouted at her.","Before she could respond, he continued, \"If you can beat me, I’ll eat all of the jewelry on me before everyone today!\"","As the richest individual in the world, the Gold Emperor naturally enjoyed flaunting his wealth, his entire body adorned with expensive jewelry.","\"Going once...\"","Ren Xia calmly met the Gold Emperor’s gaze and sneered, \"I hope you didn’t eat breakfast today, then.\"","\"Going twice...\"","\"Ten billion spirit stones!\" Ren Xia loudly declared.","\"?!?!\"","The Gold Emperor’s eyes widened with shock and disbelief at her counter.","\"T-There’s no way you can actually pay such an amount! Even if you do, you’ll definitely become homeless afterward!\" The Gold Emperor exclaimed.","\"Going once!\"","\"Goince twice!\"","\"And... sold! To the young lady at seat 194,224 for ten billion spirit stones!\"","Unsurprisingly, the Gold Emperor did not try to compete with Ren Xia’s ten billion, allowing her to win.","However, just because he lost the auction didn’t mean he’d have to immediately eat his own jewelry, as Ren Xia still had to prove that she had won legitimately by paying the ten billion.","After winning the auction, Ren Xia stood up and said to the Gold Emperor, \"You should prepare to follow through in your own words.\"","Then, she went to pay for the soul cultivation technique.","It took several minutes, but the auctioneer eventually finished counting Ren Xia’s payment.","\"I have confirmed the payment of ten billion spirit stones! Thank you! Here is your soul cultivation technique!\"","The auctioneer immediately handed the technique to her.","\"Heavens! She actually paid ten billion without batting an eye!\"","Once it was confirmed that Ren Xia had paid the amount, everyone at the auction turned to look at the Gold Emperor.","\"...This is...\"","The Gold Emperor swallowed nervously as millions of gazes suddenly converged on him, cold sweat pouring down his body.","After a brief moment of silence, he cursed aloud, \"Fuck!\"","Then, without hesitation, he began stripping the jewelry from his body and swallowing it one piece at a time—starting with the rings on his fingers, followed by the crystal-adorned bracelets on his arms, his earrings, and finally his necklaces. As for the larger pieces that couldn’t be swallowed whole, he forcibly shattered them into smaller fragments before downing them as well.","The Gold Emperor wore so much jewelry that it took several minutes for him to finish swallowing it all, while everyone watched wide-eyed, not daring to blink.","Once he was done, he shouted, \"I AM A MAN OF MY WORDS! DO YOU HEAR ME, YOU—?!\"","The Gold Emperor looked around, but he couldn’t find Ren Xia.","\"What? Where did she go?!\"","He questioned the auctioneer, who quickly replied with a stiff expression, \"Um... she left the moment you finished swallowing your first jewelry...\"","The Gold Emperor coughed up a mouthful of blood in anger when he learned that Ren Xia hadn’t even bothered to stay until the end.","He wasn’t the only one left stunned. The others were equally dumbfounded. No one had even noticed her departure, as their attention had been entirely fixed on the Gold Emperor.","What transpired at the auction spread like wildfire that very day, with people everywhere scrambling to uncover Ren Xia’s identity.","A few days after the auction, Ren Xia returned to the palace and reunited with Tian Yang.","\"Tada!\" Ren Xia proudly revealed the soul cultivation technique to Tian Yang upon her return.","\"How did you come back so fast?\" Tian Yang was more puzzled by her transportation speed than anything, as the Holy Continent was on the opposite side of the world.","\"By using the teleport formations that they’ve recently started to build around the world. They’re incredibly convenient, albeit a little expensive. It required several trips through many cities and a few million spirit stones, but it only took five days to reach the Holy Continent,\" she explained."]},{"number":2310,"title":"Chapter 2310: Kulas Awakens","paragraphs":["\"Teleport formations, huh? Since when did they start building those?\" Tian Yang wondered out loud.","\"Several hundred years ago. I heard the construction was being financed by the Three Pillars of Heaven, too.\"","\"Do they have nothing else to do? They’re getting much more involved with the world now, even though they barely had a presence not too long ago.\"","\"It probably has something to do with their war against the Giant Race,\" said Ren Xia.","\"Anyway, here is the soul cultivation technique.\"","She took out the technique from her spatial ring and handed it to him.","\"Hm? Aren’t you going to learn it first?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"I already took a look at it on my way back here. Unfortunately, I don’t have what it takes to cultivate it,\" she sighed.","\"Huh?\" Tian Yang raised an eyebrow, clearly puzzled.","Since he hadn’t been present at the auction, he had no way of knowing that the technique had been put up for sale precisely because only its creator had ever managed to cultivate it successfully.","Seeing his expression, Ren Xia quickly explained everything to him.","\"A soul cultivation technique that only its creator can cultivate, huh? This isn’t the first technique with such restrictions, so I’m not surprised. But...\"","Tian Yang looked at Ren Xia with a weird face.","\"Did you really have to spend ten billion spirit stones—our entire fortune on it? I know we have no need for money right now, but things might change in the future...\"","They’d managed to amass such wealth after looting all of the Immortal Clans, but Ren Xia had spent it all in a single auction for a technique that had a high chance of not even benefiting them. Tian Yang couldn’t fathom her thoughts.","A somewhat stiff smile tugged at Ren Xia’s lips as she replied, \"I figured that if anyone in this world could cultivate the technique, it’d be you.\"","Tian Yang facepalmed.","\"That’s your reason for spending that much money? Are you sure you weren’t just messing around and got ahead of yourself?\" Tian Yang glared at her, reading her like an open book.","\"I-I may have gotten ahead of myself at the end, but there’s no use dwelling on it now. It’s not like we can refund it.\"","\"Forget it. Let me see the technique.\"","Tian Yang grabbed the technique from her and immediately started reading it the next moment.","\"So, what do you think about it?\" Ren Xia asked him a minute later.","\"...\"","Tian Yang didn’t respond and remained fixated on the technique.","\"Dear?\"","Thinking that he didn’t hear her, she called out to him again.","\"...\"","However, Tian Yang remained silent.","In his eyes, the vast universe seemed to shrink until only he remained—alone, with the soul cultivation technique as the sole thing within his grasp.","Seeing the profound look in his eyes, Ren Xia stopped trying to bother him and patiently waited for him to wake up.","Tian Yang would not move an inch or even blink once for the next four hours, but eventually, he closed his eyes, delving deep inside his mind, where a name would resound repeatedly.","\"Heaven’s Indomitable Soul.\"","After staying in that state for nearly two weeks straight, Tian Yang finally opened his eyes and took a deep breath.","\"So you’ve finally returned to reality,\" Ren Xia’s voice resounded a moment later.","He lifted his head to look at her, who was standing in front of him with a worried look on her face.","\"How long was I out?\" he asked in a puzzled voice.","\"Two entire weeks.\"","\"I see...\"","\"I can assume that you’ve successfully cultivated the technique, right?\" she then said.","He nodded and replied, \"Yes, but this technique... It’s not complete.\"","\"What? The Three Pillars of Heaven sold an incomplete technique?\" Ren Xia frowned, feeling like she’d been scammed.","\"Actually, I’m not sure. It looks and feels complete, but my instincts are telling me otherwise. I’ll need to spend more time before I can be certain,\" he said.","\"Who made this technique?\" he then asked.","Ren Xia shrugged.","\"They never revealed the creator’s identity, and I doubt they ever will.\"","\"I wouldn’t be surprised if that were the case.\"","\"So, what do you think about the technique?\" Ren Xia then asked.","Tian Yang pondered for a moment before responding, \"It’s a good technique... No, it’s an amazing technique. Whoever created it is definitely a genius. Whether it’s safe or not, I’ll have to cultivate it to see for myself.\"","Ren Xia sighed, \"Lucky you. Now that you have a soul cultivation technique, you’ll be able to ascend to the next realm without any issue. I, on the other hand, still need one.\"","\"Although I am not sure it’ll work, I can try teaching you the technique once I master it,\" he said.","\"Okay.\" She nodded.","Even though Tian Yang now had a soul cultivation technique, he didn’t immediately start cultivating it and continued to focus on his Celestial Qi first.","Another hundred years passed in the blink of an eye, and during one random morning, Tian Yang, who had been cultivating in his room, suddenly opened his eyes.","\"This aura!\" He stood up and turned to face the direction of Kulas’ room.","\"Hey! This aura!\" Ren Xia’s voice resounded a second later.","Then, she entered his room and exclaimed, \"Kulas is awake!\"","Tian Yang nodded, but there was a deep frown on his face.","\"What’s wrong?\" she asked him.","\"You should stay here. I’ll meet Kulas alone.\"","\"What? Why?\"","\"I’m afraid there might be something wrong with him.\"","\"Then we should definitely stick together! What if he attacks you?!\"","\"I’ll be fine. Also, I can sense a familiar feeling coming from his aura...\"","\"Anyway, just stay here for now. I’ll call for you if I need help.\"","Tian Yang didn’t elaborate further and left the next moment, leaving Ren Xia speechless.","When he arrived at Kulas’s room, several of his wives were already there. Yet, for some reason, they merely stood outside, staring at the door with nervous expressions, as though afraid to open it."]},{"number":2311,"title":"Chapter 2311: Shura’s Gift","paragraphs":["\"Senior Tian!\"","When Kulas’ wives saw him, the stress on their faces instantly weakened, and they appeared more relieved.","\"What’s wrong? Why aren’t you going inside?\" he asked them.","The women turned to look at the door and swallowed nervously, before one of them responded, \"There’s an inexplicable feeling coming from the room... No matter how much we try to open it, our instincts prevent us from doing so.\"","\"Is that so? Then get back. I’ll check on Kulas alone.\"","Tian Yang walked to the door and opened it without any issue.","The moment the door opened, a sinister aura surged out of the room, causing the women outside to collapse unconscious.","Tian Yang felt overwhelmed by the aura, but he managed to hang onto his consciousness.","Despite the dreadful feeling, Tian Yang entered the room and closed the door behind him.","The inside of the room was pitch black, and Tian Yang could still see Kulas’ silhouette by the bed, but he wasn’t lying on it. Rather, he was standing beside it.","Tian Yang narrowed his gaze and spoke in a cautious tone, \"Who are you?\"","Although the figure belonged to Kulas, Tian Yang felt something was off—like he was standing before a different person.","Kulas turned his head with stiff movements until his red eyes glared at Tian Yang.","\"So you are the one who has been interfering with my plans. A mere mortal like you...\"","Tian Yang frowned as he instantly realized that he was currently in the presence of the Eternal behind Kulas’ illness.","\"Are you an Eternal?\" Tian Yang had to confirm his identity.","\"Oh? You knew about us?\"","The Eternal responded in a surprised voice.","\"No, I shouldn’t be surprised. This makes perfect sense. After all, there’s no way a mortal could cut off my influence.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Tian Yang asked, genuinely puzzled by the Eternal’s words.","The Eternal narrowed his gaze at Yuan.","\"Who is the Eternal ordering you to mess with me?\"","\"I think you’re misunderstanding something. Nobody is ordering me to do anything.\"","\"Do you really expect me to believe you? You, who has been granted a ’gift’ by an Eternal?\"","The Eternal’s words made Tian Yang recall the ’gift’ that Shura gave him during their first meeting. However, he was never told what that gift was.","\"I really don’t know what you’re talking about.\"","\"The power to reduce another Eternal’s influence... Whoever is behind you must be really powerful.\"","It was really subtle, but there was a hint of fear within the Eternal’s voice.","\"What...?\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened at the Eternal’s words.","He has the power to reduce Eternals’ influence? Is that why Kulas’ illness wouldn’t trigger when he was around? It finally made sense. Yet, he couldn’t fathom why Shura would grant him such a gift.","\"Whoever is behind you... Tell them to stop interfering with me, Zaaran!\"","Tian Yang finally learned the identity of the Eternal behind Kulas’ illness, and it was in a fashion that he never anticipated.","\"What do you want with Kulas? Why are you trying to kill him?\" Tian Yang suddenly asked.","\"Kill him? Why would I kill such a useful puppet?\" Zaaran sneered before continuing in an angry voice. \"The reason he hasn’t been able to wake up and finish his transformation is because of your interference, mortal!\"","\"What? Transformation?\"","\"Did you really think a mortal like him would be able to create something like the Giant Race? If it weren’t for you, he would’ve completed his transformation into a new existence—a true giant ages ago! But because of you, it was halted, and I am forced to possess his body and forcefully awaken him!\"","Tian Yang was left speechless by the revelation. He could never have imagined that the cause of Kulas’s mood swings and illness was his ongoing transformation into a true giant—and that Tian Yang himself was the reason Kulas could not complete it, leaving him trapped in a coma.","However, if becoming a true giant required Kulas to descend into madness, then Tian Yang would rather see the transformation fail altogether. In fact, he’d purposefully prevent it from happening.","\"Why are you trying to turn Kulas into a true giant? What is your goal here?\" Tian Yang then asked.","\"Isn’t it obvious?\" The Eternal responded with a cold smile. \"I am doing this because he asked for it! Of course, I am not helping him for free. However, that is none of your business.\"","The Eternal suddenly started walking toward Tian Yang.","However, the Eternal abruptly stopped moving after only taking two steps.","\"Tsk.\" The Eternal sucked his teeth in annoyance and muttered in a low voice. \"Which reckless bastard gave you such a power? They must be out of their mind!\"","Even though the Eternal wanted to approach Tian Yang, his power that reduced Eternals’ influence made it difficult for the one possessing Kulas’ body to approach him, as it would weaken his control over the body.","Tian Yang then said, \"I don’t care what arrangements you made with Kulas, but I won’t allow you to play with his life as you please, even if you are an Eternal.\"","\"Hahaha! And what do you think you, a mere mortal, can do to stop me?! Although you may be able to weaken our influence, you are overestimating your powers!\"","The Eternal laughed out loud as he unleashed immense killing intent.","Sensing the killing intent, Tian Yang instinctively acted and swung his arm, punching Kulas right in the face.","\"Wake up!\"","Kulas was sent flying to the other side of the room and slammed into the wall.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Kulas stood up and looked at Tian Yang, but his red eyes had disappeared and returned to their original color.","\"I’m sorry for troubling you like this...\" Kulas sighed.","While the Eternal had possessed his body, Kulas was conscious the entire time and witnessed their conversation.","\"Why didn’t you tell me that you were in contact with an Eternal?\" Tian Yang asked with narrowed eyes, his voice full of disappointment."]},{"number":2312,"title":"Chapter 2312: Leaving Kulas Behind","paragraphs":["\"Am I... that untrustworthy?\" Tian Yang looked at Kulas with a saddened face.","\"N-No! That’s not it!\" Kulas immediately responded, his voice full of pain. \"You know there’s no one I trust more than you in this world. However, I didn’t want to trouble you—harm you with my knowledge.\"","\"If you’re worried that my longevity might be in jeopardy, then it was needless worry. In fact, you should’ve known that I was aware of their existence when I mentioned that I learned of forbidden knowledge that cannot be shared in Han Zexian’s tomb.\"","Kulas sighed, \"Indeed, I have considered that possibility. But I wasn’t certain, nor did I want to risk it. Moreover, that’s not what truly worried me. The Eternal helping me... I was worried that he might try to harm you.\"","\"Well, now that I know everything—almost everything, care to fill in the gaps for me?\" Tian Yang asked.","Kulas nodded and explained, \"I learned of the communication technique hidden within the Great Mammoth Body Refinement while I was still inside the Immortal Confinement Dungeon, and I tried it out as a last-ditch effort. That’s when I met the Eternal, who introduced himself as Zaaran. I pleaded with him for help, and he agreed but under one condition—that I must find something for him.\"","\"Since it was my darkest time and I was desperate, I accepted Zaaran’s terms. In return, he bestowed upon me a gift—my bloodline that allowed for the creation of the Giant Race. Then, under his instructions, I started building my own empire within the continent.\"","Tian Yang then asked, \"What did Zaaran want you to find for him?\"","He remembered that Shura also wanted him to find something when he asked him to help Kulas, but refused to tell him because he wasn’t prepared to hear it.","\"Honestly, I still have no idea what Zaaran wants me to find. He said that he’ll tell me once I’m strong enough, when I reach the next realm. Oh, he was also the one who told me about Celestial Qi, even giving me a cultivation technique to cultivate it.\"","Kulas sighed loudly before continuing, \"I know it’s a little late, but I apologize for lying. I didn’t actually discovery Celestial Qi myself, and I kept the technique to myself because I didn’t want you to be suspicious of me.\"","Hearing this, Tian Yang began to doubt Shura even more. After all, Shura appeared to share the same goal as Zaaran, and for all he knew, the two might even be working together.","However, why would Shura give him the power to weaken an Eternal’s influence, which ended up interfering with Zaaran’s plans?","\"Then do you know of an Eternal by the name of—\" Tian Yang was about to ask Kulas if he knew Shura’s name, but Kulas abruptly stopped him.","\"Don’t tell me anything! Although I may be fine now, this is only temporary. In fact, I can feel my consciousness slowly slipping away with every passing moment. I’ll definitely return to being a madman soon, and Zaaran will learn everything you tell me.\"","Kulas looked at Tian Yang with a bitter smile and said, \"Brother... I need you to do something for me...\"","\"If you’re telling me to leave you, then you can—\"","\"Sorry, but I am not asking you.\" Kulas interrupted in a stubborn voice. \"You must leave before Zaaran takes control of my body again, and while you’re at it, please take my family with you—at least those who are still sane. This disease that’s currently affecting me will eventually affect everyone related to my bloodline, so my family and the entire Giant Race will lose their mind soon.\"","\"No!\" Tian Yang angrily shouted. \"I will not leave you behind again! I have the power to weaken an Eternal’s influence, so as long as I am by your side—\"","\"NO!\" Kulas responded with an even louder roar. \"Your mysterious power is no longer effective! It can no longer stop Zaaran’s influence on me!\"","\"Then what are you going to do once I leave?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Do I really have to say it?\" Kulas sighed.","\"...\"","Tian Yang fell silent, but he had a good idea what Kulas had in mind.","’He’s going to end his own life before the madness consumes him...’ Tian Yang gritted his teeth and clenched his fists in frustration until they bled, feeling as helpless as before.","\"Damn it! I thought I’d finally become strong enough to protect those close to me!\" he screamed at the top of his lungs. \"Why is there always something fucking with me?! One thing after another—there’s no end to this bullshit!\"","\"You’re plenty strong already, brother.\" Kulas suddenly said. \"However, no matter how strong you are, there will always be something beyond your control, especially if that thing is a god-like being that has existed for tens of billions of years before us.\"","\"Ugh!\"","Kulas suddenly groaned in pain.","\"Kulas!\"","\"Leave! Now!\" Kulas shouted at him. \"I am already a lost cause, but my family... You can still protect them! Please! I will endure it for as long as I can, so hurry!\"","\"Fuck!\" Tian Yang cursed out loud and left the room the next moment.","\"Thank you for everything, brother... And goodbye...\" Kulas muttered as he watched Tian Yang close the door.","\"Goodbye, Kulas...\"","Outside, Kulas’ wives had woken up and were anxiously waiting.","\"W-What happened to our husband?\"","They asked Tian Yang the moment he left the room.","Tian Yang responded with clenched fists, \"Kulas is awake, but...\"","After a moment of silence, he continued, \"This will be hard to swallow, but Kulas is no longer the man that you once knew, and his illness is not curable. Before he sent me away, he asked me to take his family away from this place, where it’ll be safe. If you haven’t been affected by the illness, come with me.\"","\"Are you asking us to abandon our husband?! There’s no way I will do that!\"","One of them immediately responded.","Tian Yang glared at her and spoke, \"Then stay here. I do not have the time or energy to convince you. And I am merely following Kulas’ wishes. However, I can’t force you to leave if you don’t want to. I will leave at dawn. Be outside at the front gate if you wish to follow me.\"","Without another word, Tian Yang turned around and disappeared, returning to Ren Xia to explain the situation to her."]},{"number":2313,"title":"Chapter 2313: Leaving Kulas Behind(2)","paragraphs":["\"We will leave this continent.\"","\"Huh?\"","Ren Xia looked at Tian Yang with wide eyes, as those were his first words after returning.","\"What about Kulas?\"","Tian Yang shook his head and sighed.","Then, he explained the entire situation to her.","\"I get the gist of the situation, but... Are you really going to leave him behind?\" Ren Xia looked at him with a worried frown.","Although she was slightly worried for Kulas, she was far more concerned for Tian Yang in this sort of situation, as it could easily develop into a heart demon in the future.","Tian Yang wore a resolute expression on his face as he replied, \"I am not leaving him behind. But it’s also true that we cannot help him—at least not in our current state. Once we leave, I will focus on trying to breakthrough to the next realm and figure out what these Eternals want from us!\"","\"If Kulas even lasts long enough for us to help him...\" Ren Xia remarked.","Tian Yang clenched his fists and said, \"Kulas is strong... I believe that he won’t do something as foolish as ending himself!\"","\"Anyway, we’re leaving at dawn, and we’ll be taking whoever wants to leave with us.\"","\"All of them?\" Ren Xia raised an eyebrow.","\"Of course not. I will only take those who haven’t been affected by the illness, and those who are willing to leave with us.\"","\"But only some of his wives and daughters aren’t affected...\" Ren Xia narrowed her gaze at him.","Tian Yang sighed, \"Relax, I have no intention of touching Kulas’ family, even if he is no longer here.\"","\"I didn’t say anything, though,\" she said.","\"But I know what you’re thinking.\"","\"Do you, really?\" Ren Xia sneered. \"I was actually thinking that if you truly had some feelings for them, I wouldn’t mind accepting a few more sisters.\"","Tian Yang looked at her wide eyes, his gaze full of disbelief.","He shook his head and sighed, \"This isn’t the time for jokes. Let’s get ready to leave.\"","\"I wasn’t joking, though...\" she muttered.","A few hours later, Tian Yang and Ren Xia went to the front gate and waited for dawn, which was only an hour away.","Half an hour later, a large group of people, around two hundred, walked out of the palace with a heavy atmosphere around them.","This entire group consisted of women, with more than half of them being Kulas’ wives. Since the children were directly connected to Kulas by blood, they were more likely to be affected by the Kulas’ bloodline.","Naturally, Tian Yang had noticed long ago that the women were less likely to be affected by the illness, but there was nothing he could really do, even with that information.","When the group stopped before them, one of them stepped forward and said, \"This is everyone who hasn’t been affected by the illness yet. We all had a long talk, and although we all showed up, not all of us will leave. Some of us have decided to stay behind and remain with our husbands.\"","Soon, about a third of the group separated from the rest and approached Tian Yang.","\"We have all decided to leave with you...\"","Tian Yang looked at the group. There were several that he recognized and some that he didn’t. Those he recognized consisted of Chao Shuying, Xie Mey, and the women who asked him to embrace them in Kulas’ stead in the past.","As for those who decided to stay behind, most of them were Kulas’ earliest wives—those who had been there since the beginning.","\"That’s all?\" Tian Yang asked to confirm.","\"Yes, we have all decided to stay here with our husband, regardless of what happens.\"","Tian Yang nodded.","\"Good luck. I’ll leave Kulas in your care.\"","Tian Yang didn’t linger and immediately left the continent with Ren Xia and those who willingly followed him.","Meanwhile, inside his own room, Kulas held a dagger in his grasp, pointing the sharp blade toward his own chest.","\"So he’s finally left...\" he muttered.","Once he confirmed that Tian Yang had left, a determined light flickered within his gaze.","\"I will not let you harm my brother, Zaaran, even if it’s the last thing I do!\"","Without hesitation, Kulas brought the dagger toward his heart, piercing it.","Kulas’ body fell onto the ground the next moment, quickly creating a puddle of blood, and the light in his eyes dimmed.","However, just as the light faded and almost vanished, it suddenly brightened, even turning bright red.","He lifted himself off the ground and muttered, \"What a foolish mortal. Did you really think you’d be able to stop me with such cowardly tricks?\"","Zaaran looked into the distance and smiled.","\"Now that the interference is gone, I can finally finish the transformation.\"","Shortly after Tian Yang left the Giant Continent, he suddenly halted and turned around.","\"That’s...\"","His eyes widened when a crimson sphere appeared out of thin air and enveloped the entire continent, resembling the Immortal Ensaring Vault used by the Immortal Clans in the past.","\"What is that?!\" Xie Mey exclaimed after seeing the crimson dome.","\"I will be right back!\"","Tian Yang gritted his teeth and immediately rushed back to the continent. However, the crimson barrier completely blocked his attempt.","He tried to destroy the barrier, but even his strongest attack was unable to leave a mark on it.","\"What are you doing?\"","When he attempted to launch another attack, Ren Xia suddenly appeared behind him and stopped him. \"You have already decided to leave Kulas behind. You can’t turn back now, no matter what happens from this point forth.\"","\"I...\"","\"What can you do even if you return now?\" she sighed.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang turned around and returned to the group.","\"Sorry for the delay. Let’s leave quickly,\" he said to them before speeding into the horizon, away from the Giant Continent.","Soon, news of the Giant’s Continent being covered in a crimson dome that even the Three Pillars of Heaven couldn’t penetrate spread throughout the world."]},{"number":2314,"title":"Chapter 2314: A Sudden End to the War","paragraphs":["After leaving the Giant’s Continent, Tian Yang brought Kulas’ family to a safe location before entering seclusion to focus on pushing his cultivation base to the next realm.","A hundred years... a thousand years... ten thousand years.","Years passed in the blink of an eye, and even after twenty thousand years, the Giant’s Continent remained sealed by the mysterious crimson dome.","The crimson dome was so durable that even the Three Pillars of Heaven were unable to damage it, even after thousands of years of effort, much less destroy it.","Eventually, the Three Pillars of Heaven gave up on trying to invade the Giant’s Continent. However, they remained vigilant and constantly monitored the continent.","As more and more time passed and the crimson dome showed no sign of weakening, the Three Pillars of Heaven started to lose interest, and their war with the Giant Race came to an unexpected halt.","Thirty thousand years... forty thousand years... fifty thousand years later.","\"How is your progress?\" Ren Xia approached Tian Yang and asked. \"Your aura is getting sharper by the day, so your breakthrough should be pretty close, no?\"","Tian Yang slowly opened his eyes after hearing her voice, and his aura that was gushing with Celestial Qi was immediately suppressed until it was essentially nonexistent.","\"I have already reached my limit with Celestial Qi. I cannot refine more at this level, even if I want to. Unfortunately, I am still nowhere near close to reaching the next realm.\"","\"Really? Even though you said it was achievable within fifty thousand years?\"","\"That was just a guess.\"","\"What about now? Now that you’re getting closer, you should have a rough idea how long it’d take, right?\"","Tian Yang sighed. \"While it’s true that I’ve essentially reached my limit with Celestial Qi, arriving at this level made me realize it isn’t the most important factor for my breakthrough. What truly matters is the soul, and I have only recently begun cultivating it.\"","\"Speaking of cultivating your soul... how’s the soul cultivation technique? Did you manage to complete it?\" Ren Xia asked.","He shook his head.","\"I had my hands full with Celestial Qi, so where would I find the time to complete it? However, I am certain that it’s not finished.\"","\"Is it even safe to cultivate an unfinished technique?\"","\"Normally, it isn’t, but this technique is unlike any technique I have seen before. It may not be complete, but it functions like one.\"","\"If it doesn’t matter, then what’s the point of completing it?\" Ren Xia wore a puzzled expression on her face.","\"It may not affect my ability to cultivate it, but it will definitely affect its effectiveness. If I am going to offend a god-like being that lives beyond our world, I’ll need to get as strong as I can so that I can protect what’s important to me.\"","Tian Yang then asked, \"Anyway, what’s been going on outside lately? What are the Three Pillars of Heaven up to these days?\"","\"Just the usual. They’re getting more and more involved with the rest of the world. But they seem to have picked up their pace recently. They’re definitely up to something,\" she said.","Ever since their war with the Giant Race came to a halt, the Three Pillars of Heaven began actively expanding their influence throughout the Divine Heaven. Although they had always been untouchable and immensely influential, that power was largely confined to their own circle, and they rarely intervened in the outside world. Now, however, they were inserting themselves into nearly everything—from commerce to sects.","\"I see...\"","\"Anyway, I’ll stop bothering your cultivation and return to my own. There are many soul cultivation techniques being created these days, but I still haven’t found any suitable for me, so I’ll continue to focus on my Celestial Qi for now.\"","After giving Tian Yang a kiss on the lips, Ren Xia went to her own area to cultivate.","Time continued to pass, and in the blink of an eye, another twenty thousand years had passed. By now, over seventy thousand years have passed since Tian Yang left the Giant’s Continent.","\"I’m going out for a bit,\" Tian Yang said to Ren Xia.","Ren Xia looked at him with a smile and asked, \"Are you going to meet with her?\"","He silently nodded.","\"Alright. Try not to stay out too late,\" she said with a teasing smile, trying to sound like a mother.","After leaving, Tian Yang traveled to a city that would’ve taken him a decade to traverse if it weren’t for the teleportation formation. Although the teleportation formations were extremely convenient, they were still extremely expensive and were typically used for emergencies by wealthy figures or powerful cultivators.","In fact, even Tian Yang had to use them sparingly, especially after Ren Xia had spent most of their fortune on the soul cultivation technique.","Although they could easily earn plenty of money with their cultivation, they spent most of their time in seclusion, only leaving their personal world every few hundred years.","By this point, the names Tian Yang and Ren Xia—once feared throughout the world—had all but faded into obscurity, with barely anyone still aware of who they were.","After arriving at his destination, Tian Yang closed his eyes to cultivate while he waited for the other party to arrive.","\"You’re as diligent as ever. Do you ever rest?\" A familiar voice suddenly resounded a few minutes after Tian Yang’s arrival.","Tian Yang opened his eyes to look at the beautiful woman standing before him and smiled, \"And you look the same as ever, Sister Sun.\"","\"A gentleman would say something like ’you look even more beautiful than before’,\" she calmly teased.","\"A gentleman... or a womanizer?\"","Sun Rouxi chuckled, and the two of them started chatting.","After Tian Yang left the Giant Continent, the two would occasionally meet to catch up. However, their conversations were never merely casual. They also exchanged insights, knowledge, and discoveries related to cultivation.","\"So, what’s the Three Pillars of Heaven up to these days? Why are they expanding their influence so rapidly?\" Tian Yang suddenly asked, his expression turned serious."]},{"number":2315,"title":"Chapter 2315: Creator of the Soul Cultivation Technique","paragraphs":["\"You make it sound like the Three Pillars of Heaven are scheming something,\" Sun Rouxi said calmly after hearing Tian Yang’s question.","\"Am I wrong? You’re free to correct me if that’s the case,\" Tian Yang replied. \"There’s no way the Three Pillars of Heaven—who spent most of their existence in secrecy, isolated within their own bubble—would suddenly involve themselves in nearly everything for no reason.\"","\"Even if they are scheming something, what makes you think I’d be privy to such information?\" Sun Rouxi questioned with a narrowed gaze. \"Do you even know my position within the background?\"","\"I don’t, but I doubt you’re a nobody.\"","\"Oh? What gave you that impression?\"","Tian Yang answered with a calm smile, \"Would a nobody be able to travel to the Giant Continent while another group is there on important business, let alone bring a friend along?\"","\"You’re also talented enough to complete others’ unfinished techniques. I wouldn’t be surprised if you held an important position within your family.\"","Sun Rouxi chuckled, \"You never struck me as the keen type. You’re more like a reckless bull that charges headfirst into anything without thinking first.\"","\"Anyway, to answer your earlier question... the Three Pillars of Heaven are definitely planning something, but I do not know what that thing is. While my position within the family isn’t ordinary, it’s nothing too special, either. Most importantly, I spend most of my time in seclusion, only coming out to meet with you occasionally, so I don’t have the time to care about such trivial matters. As a matter of fact, I have no interest in whatever they are doing.\"","\"Trying to become the first to enter the next realm? How close are you?\" Tian Yang then asked.","\"Well, I have enough Celestial Qi, so I only need to cultivate my soul now. Unfortunately, I am not experienced enough to give you an estimate of when I’ll reach my goal. How about you?\"","\"I’m in the same boat. It took me so long just to cultivate my Celestial Qi. I cannot fathom how much longer cultivating my soul would take. Another fifty thousand years? A hundred thousand? Only time will tell.\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"Speaking of soul cultivation... what soul cultivation technique are you using? You don’t have to tell me if you don’t want to.\"","\"My soul cultivation technique is named Heaven’s Indomitable Soul.\"","\"Eh?\" Sun Rouxi’s eyes widened upon hearing this name, mouth even agape.","Tian Yang smiled and said, \"That’s right. It’s the one your family sold some time ago.\"","\"So you were the one who purchased it...\" Sun Rouxi muttered in a daze. \"Is this fate?\"","\"Well, it was Ren Xia who bought it.\"","\"...\"","Sun Rouxi suddenly fell silent, her gaze fixed on Tian Yang as though weighing a decision in her mind.","\"What’s wrong?\" he asked.","\"Since it’s you... I’ll let you in on a little secret.\"","\"Hm?\" Tian Yang raised an eyebrow.","\"It’s about the creator of that technique,\" she continued.","\"Oh?\"","Tian Yang’s eyes flickered with intrigue as he leaned in slightly, his attention fully captured.","\"The creator of that technique is... me!\" she revealed with a wide smile.","\"What?!\" Tian Yang leaned back in shock, his eyes and mouth agape.","He quickly snapped out of it and said, \"There’s no way! You’re messing with me!\"","Without explaining, Sun Rouxi started to recite the entire technique from the beginning to the end without missing a word.","\"That doesn’t prove anything... You could’ve just memorized it after reading it. It belonged to your family, after all.\"","Sun Rouxi sighed, \"I don’t know how else to convince you. To think you wouldn’t believe me, even though I risked so much to reveal this secret that only a few in the family know...\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang spoke, \"Are you... being serious?\"","\"What would I even gain from lying to you?\" she sneered.","\"No way...\"","Tian Yang could tell that she was being genuine just from her voice alone, leaving him speechless.","\"You actually created this technique? You’re even more amazing than I thought.\" Tian Yang swallowed nervously.","\"I did spend pretty much my entire life dedicated to it, after all.\"","\"And how long is that?\"","\"I started working on it shortly after I joined the Immortal Monastery, only finishing it a thousand years before it was sold.\"","\"Why’d you decide to sell it?\" Tian Yang continued to ask.","Sun Rouxi sighed softly. \"It wasn’t my decision. I wanted to share the technique openly, just to see if anyone besides me could cultivate it. But the family ignored my wishes and sold it for profit. They said the technique would naturally spread over time anyway, once no one proved capable of cultivating it, so they might as well profit from it. However, that never happened, and the new owner disappeared like a ghost after buying it.\"","She looked at him and smiled, \"I never thought it would land in your hand, much less you successfully cultivating it.\"","\"So, what do you think of my technique? Although it’s not the only technique I’ve created, it’s my proudest work,\" she spoke with an air of pride swirling around her, not even bothering to hide it.","Tian Yang chuckled and said, \"It’s obviously amazing. Even the best soul cultivation techniques that have come out recently cannot compare to it. However...\"","\"However?\" Sun Rouxi raised an eyebrow.","\"I think it can be improved,\" he continued with a smile.","Although Tian Yang had long referred to it as incomplete, he realized that wasn’t accurate. The technique was, in fact, complete, as it could be cultivated properly. Rather than being unfinished, it simply had room for improvement, and that was what he told her.","\"...Huh?\" Sun Rouxi’s jaw dropped after hearing his words.","Seeing her reaction, Tian Yang quickly realized his mistake. Telling the creator of the technique that it could be improved had been undeniably rude.","\"Sorry, I didn’t mean to offend you—\"","\"I don’t care about that,\" she quickly interrupted.","\"Tell me more,\" she continued with a solemn expression.","Instead of taking offense, she seemed genuinely intrigued, a spark of excitement flickering in her eyes."]},{"number":2316,"title":"Chapter 2316: Improving the Soul Cultivation Technique","paragraphs":["\"Uh... even if you tell me to explain... my understanding of the technique is nowhere near enough to explain it in detail,\" he said in a somewhat awkward tone.","Sun Rouxi frowned at his response and immediately responded, \"Then how do you know the technique could be improved? You got my hopes up for nothing!\"","\"As I said, I don’t have enough experience to explain myself. I’ll do it once I reach a deeper understanding of the technique.’","\"Fine, I’ll wait. But if it turns out that you were lying to me, I’ll be very upset and angry at you.\"","Tian Yang nodded.","\"Alright.\"","The two of them chatted for a little longer before they parted and returned to their own dwelling.","Upon returning home, Tian Yang immediately entered seclusion to cultivate the soul cultivation technique.","Time continued to pass.","Five thousand years... ten thousand years... twenty thousand years.","\"How is your progress with the soul cultivation technique?\" Sun Rouxi asked Tian Yang on their sixth meeting since she revealed herself to be the creator of the Heaven’s Indomitable Soul technique.","Tian Yang smiled and said, \"Not much compared to last time, but I have reached a level of understanding where I can explain to you about why I think the technique can be improved.\"","\"I’m listening.\"","Tian Yang proceeded to explain his discovery and shared his thoughts on how he believes it can be improved.","Sun Rouxi didn’t respond for a long time after Tian Yang was finished.","Eventually, she looked at him with a cold smile and said, \"If you dare call yourself talentless after today, I’ll feed you to the pigs.\"","Tian Yang could only offer a silent smile in response.","\"Hey, where are you staying right now?\" Sun Rouxi suddenly asked. \"Are you still staying in your personal world?\"","\"Hm? I am. Why are you asking?\"","\"Make some space for two people. I’m going to stay with you for a while,\" she said.","\"What?!\" Tian Yang exclaimed. \"Why so suddenly?\"","\"What do you think? I want to improve the soul cultivation technique.\"","\"Can’t you just do it with the information I’ve provided you?\"","\"I can, but it won’t turn out the way you envisioned, and there is still room for your comprehension to grow. It’d be a hassle to meet like this every time I want to speak to you, so I’ll just stay with you until the cultivation technique is refined. Don’t worry, I won’t intrude on your time with your wife.\"","Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"That’s not what I am worried about. And room for two? Who else is coming with you?\"","\"Who else but Ruye?\"","\"Ah, Senior Sister Jing. You really stick close to each other, huh?\"","\"She’s the only close friend I have. And it wouldn’t be wise to leave her alone with my family for too long. They don’t really like her because of her original background, and she’s currently there as my ’servant’.\"","\"In any case, I don’t mind, but I need to speak with Ren Xia first. We share the world, after all.\"","\"Alright. Let’s meet again in ten years, then.\"","After they parted, Tian Yang returned home to let Ren Xia know the situation. Meanwhile, Sun Rouxi prepared for her departure from the family.","\"I was wondering when this day would come since you started meeting with her again,\" Ren Xia sighed after hearing the situation.","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Why would you be expecting this situation?\"","\"You really don’t know?\"","\"...\" Tian Yang remained silent.","\"...In any case, you don’t need my approval for such trivial matters. It’s not like we’re the only two occupying this world, anyway.\"","Ten years later, Tian Yang met up with Sun Rouxi, who brought along Jing Ruye this time.","\"What did your wife say?\" Sun Rouxi asked.","\"Does it even matter? You look like you’re already prepared to move in...\"","Sun Rouxi sighed, \"Do you have any idea how much effort it takes to sneak out every time I meet you? Because of that time I ran away from home to work as a sect elder in the Immortal Monastery, my family has been keeping a close eye on me since then.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow at her words and asked, \"What about this time?\"","\"I snuck out, of course. There’s no way they’d let me leave for an extended period of time alone. Hell, I’ll definitely be grounded once I return home.\"","\"Grounded...? It’s not like you’re a child...\" Tian Yang shook his head.","\"No... since you created such a powerful soul cultivation technique, they have a good reason for wanting to keep you safe.\"","\"Enough talking. Let’s go to your world before they realize I am gone. It was less bothersome before because they barely left the Holy Continent. However, they’re everywhere these days.\"","Thus, Tian Yang brought Sun Rouxi and Jing Ruye to his personal world.","\"Wow... so this is your personal world...\"","Sun Rouxi and Jing Ruye were left in awe after seeing it for the first time.","\"This place is so vast—much larger than even the ones at my family!\" Sun Rouxi said.","\"It was much smaller before, but we had to make some adjustments after a certain incident.\"","Although Tian Yang trusted Sun Rouxi, he kept the situation with Kulas a secret from her to avoid unnecessary risk.","\"Isn’t it expensive to maintain such a large world?\" Jing Ruye asked.","\"Yes, it requires half a million spirit stones a month to maintain it.\"","\"That much?! Where are you even getting that much money from?\" she asked.","\"Monster cores are very profitable these days, especially Immortal-level cores. A single one can easily sell for tens of millions of spirit stones.\"","\"Where do you even find the time to hunt for monster cores? Don’t you spend more of your time in seclusion?\" Sun Rouxi asked.","\"Yes, that’s why we’re getting help from others. We’re not the only ones living here.\"","\"Hm? Who else lives here?\"","\"That’s... I’ll tell you in the future.\" Tian Yang said.","\"Well, I don’t really care, so you don’t need to tell me if you don’t want to,\" said Sun Rouxi in a calm voice. \"Anyways, let’s get started with the soul cultivation technique.\"","\"Alright.\""]},{"number":2317,"title":"Chapter 2317: Sun Rouxi’s Feelings","paragraphs":["Sun Rouxi said, \"Although I want to improve the soul cultivation technique, I won’t be the one making the actual changes. You will, and I’ll assist you.\"","Tian Yang looked at her with a puzzled face.","\"Aren’t you the creator of the technique?\" he asked.","\"Yes, but the technique is already ’complete’ in my eyes. Even if I want to improve it, I don’t think I can. Therefore, I’ll assist by helping you improve your understanding, and if you have any questions about the technique, I’ll be able to answer them.\"","Thus, Sun Rouxi and Jing Ruye started living in Tian Yang’s private world.","A few days later—","\"Tian Yang, I almost forgot.\" Sun Rouxi suddenly approached him with a solemn look on her face. \"There’s something I need to tell you.\"","\"What is it?\" he looked at her with a raised eyebrow.","\"It’s related to the Three Pillars of Heaven and... the Immortal Clans.\"","\"What? The Immortal Clans? They’re still relevant?\" Tian Yang was genuinely surprised to hear their name after so long.","He had assumed they had vanished from the world entirely, as no one had spoken of them since their downfall.","Since he had never exterminated every last member of the Immortal Clans, they were undoubtedly still alive somewhere. However, they had weakened to such an extent that they could barely be recognized as an organization and went into hiding.","Sun Rouxi then spoke, \"Well, they had been in hiding ever since their downfall, so I’m not surprised you forgot about them. Anyway, right before I left my family, I heard that they’ve found the remnants of the Immortal Clans and offered to help them regain their footing.\"","\"What?\" Tian Yang immediately frowned at this information.","\"Why the hell would they do something like that?\"","Sun Rouxi shrugged, \"I don’t know the details since I only overheard some of the elders in my family talking about it, and I am only telling you because of your relationship with the Immortal Clans.\"","\"Did you hear anything else?\" he then asked.","She shook her head.","\"What are you going to do?\" she asked a moment later.","Tian Yang fell silent for a long minute before releasing a deep sigh.","\"I have already claimed my debt from the Immortal Clans, so whatever they do from this point forth is no longer my concern, even if they are trying to rebuild. As long as they don’t block my path, I’ll leave them be.\"","Sun Rouxi smiled and teased, \"You’ve really grown up.\"","\"Stop treating me like a kid.\"","\"Sure, sure.\"","They returned to working on the soul cultivation technique.","Time passed swiftly, and before they realized, over a hundred years had passed since Sun Rouxi started staying with Tian Yang.","\"Rouxi, we’ve been here for a hundred years now, you know?\" Jing Ruye suddenly remarked as she poured Sun Rouxi a cup of tea.","\"What about it? Are you wondering when we’ll return home?\" Sun Rouxi asked.","\"Well, I am curious about that, but that’s not what I am talking about.\" Jing Ruye said as she poured her own tea.","After she took a sip, she continued, \"I’m talking about your progress with Tian Yang.\"","\"Oh, the cultivation technique? We’re making tremendous progress every session.\"","Jing Ruye narrowed her eyes at Sun Rouxi and asked, \"Are you actually that dense, or are you pretending to be stupid? Please don’t mock me, Rouxi. I have been aware of your feelings for him since our days at the Immortal Monastery. Although I understood why you couldn’t go after him before, things are different now, no?\"","\"That’s...\" Sun Rouxi’s expression stiffened at Jing Ruye’s straightforwardness.","Jing Ruye smiled faintly as she continued, \"Even if you claim you see him as nothing more than a little brother, now that you’re both powerful cultivators who have lived for tens of thousands of years, there’s no way you still view him as the same immature brat you once did.\"","\"You may be a genius when it comes to creating techniques, but you’re still a naive maiden at heart.\"","Sun Rouxi shook her head and sighed, \"In this vast world, you’re the only one who would dare to talk to me in such a manner while knowing my background.\"","\"Well, we’re not sworn sisters for nothing,\" Jing Ruye chuckled.","After a moment of silence, Sun Rouxi spoke, \"Listen here, Ruye. Regardless of my feelings for Tian Yang, it doesn’t change the fact that he already has a partner. Who am I to interfere in their relationship?\"","Jing Ruye looked at her with a dumbfounded face.","\"Is that concern what’s preventing you from moving forward, or is that just a convenient excuse for your cowardice? You know that men with power and influence rarely limit themselves to a single wife, right? Even your father is no different.\"","\"Don’t bring my father into this. And if you really think there’s nothing wrong with it, why don’t you approach him?\" Sun Rouxi sneered.","\"Eh?\" Jing Ruye pointed at her own face and asked, \"Are you really giving me permission to approach him?\"","\"What...?\" Sun Rouxi raised her eyebrows, looking confused.","\"To be honest with you, Tian Yang is very attractive. Not only is he one of the most powerful men in the world, but he’s also handsome. If he weren’t living a seclusive life, he would be surrounded by women. As for me... I have been single my entire life, so I have no problems approaching him. The only reason I’ve held back is because of you, Rouxi. But if you truly don’t mind me approaching him, then...\"","Sun Rouxi stared at Jing Ruye, her best friend and sworn sister, with her mouth and eyes agape, looking bewildered by such a statement.","Seeing her response, Jing Ruye decided to take things a step further. She quickly gulped down the rest of her tea and stood up.","\"W-Where are you going?\" Sun Rouxi asked.","\"Hm? Isn’t it obvious? I have been single for long enough, and there’s an attractive, handsome man so close—\"","\"No! You can’t have him! I forbid you!\" Sun Rouxi suddenly slammed her teacup on the table, destroying both the cup and the table.","\"...\"","Seeing this, a stiff smile tugged at Jing Ruye’s lips."]},{"number":2318,"title":"Chapter 2318: Sun Rouxi’s Feelings(2)","paragraphs":["\"Haa...\" Jing Ruye released a deep sigh a moment later when Sun Rouxi refused to elaborate after her outburst.","\"You’re really cruel, Rouxi. Why are you forbidding me from approaching Tian Yang when you don’t even have any feelings for him? You’re no different from a child not sharing a piece of candy that doesn’t even belong to you.\"","\"Who said I don’t have any feelings for him?! I have had my eyes on him since the Immortal Monastery!\" Sun Rouxi immediately replied.","However, she’d subconsciously spoken, and when she realized what she had just said, her entire face flushed with redness.","\"W-Wait a second... That’s not—\" Sun Rouxi stopped midway when she couldn’t think of an excuse.","Jing Ruye touched the smug-looking smile on her face with a finger and teased, \"Now that wasn’t so bad, was it? Telling the truth, that is. I bet you feel like a mountain has been lifted off your shoulders now, especially when you’ve held such feelings in for so long.\"","Sun Rouxi opened her mouth, but no words came out. Then, her face flushed even redder when she realized that she really felt lighter.","\"Now you just need to say that straight to Tian Yang himself,\" Jing Ruye continued.","\"Impossible!\" Sun Rouxi exclaimed.","Jing Ruye sighed, \"Listen here, Rouxi. Your feelings will remain nonexistent until you actually tell him.\"","Sun Rouxi rubbed her eyes and sighed, \"Although you’ve been with the Sun Family for many years, there are still a lot of things you aren’t aware of about my family—my bloodline. Even if I wish to embrace Tian Yang, my bloodline forbids me from doing so.\"","\"That... doesn’t make any sense at all.\" Jing Ruye said with raised eyebrows.","\"Sorry, but this is something that I cannot share, even if it’s with you.\"","\"I...\" Sun Rouxi fell silent after a single word.","\"Let’s end this here. I’m tired.\"","Sun Rouxi didn’t give Jing Ruye a chance to object and quickly disappeared into her room.","A few months later, Tian Yang and Sun Rouxi got together for another study session.","\"Is there something on my face?\" Tian Yang asked when he noticed Sun Rouxi staring at his face with a weird expression.","\"H-Huh? Your face? N-No...\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang noticed that something was off about her but decided not to stick his nose into her business. He figured that if she wanted to tell him, she would.","\"Then let’s begin.\"","\"...\"","Despite her best efforts, Sun Rouxi couldn’t relax when in Tian Yang’s presence.","’Damn it! It’s all Ruye’s fault! If she hadn’t tricked me into saying all those weird things, I wouldn’t be like this! I can barely look at him in the eyes without blushing!’ she cried inwardly.","For the next several days, Sun Rouxi struggled to remain concentrated on improving the soul cultivation technique, as Tian Yang’s presence constantly occupied her mind.","From his scent to his handsome face, her mind would constantly wander to a weird place she’d never experienced before.","’What the hell am I doing? I need to get rid of these useless thoughts!’","Eventually, Tian Yang could no longer remain oblivious and sighed, \"Do you want to stop here? If anything is troubling you, I am willing to listen...\"","Tian Yang’s calm voice snapped Sun Rouxi back to reality.","’Even though I am supposed to be the mature one...’ she sighed inwardly.","\"Sorry, it’s nothing. Let’s continue.\"","Sun Rouxi managed to remain focused for the last several days.","\"Thanks for your time.\" Tian Yang said to her at the end of their session.","\"I have nothing but time,\" she calmly replied.","\"...How long do you intend to stay here? Until I improve the technique? That could take thousands of years.\"","\"I don’t care how long it takes. Even if it takes a million years, I am going to see this through until the very end. After all, this might be the last time that I will have any true freedom,\" she revealed with a heavy sigh.","Tian Yang frowned at her ominous words.","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"It’s family matters.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang spoke, \"Are your parents forcing you into a marriage?\"","Since this was a common problem within influential families, Tian Yang figured this might be the cause of Sun Rouxi’s concern. After all, she belonged to one of the top backgrounds in the world.","\"What?\"","However, Sun Rouxi looked at him with a dumbfounded face.","\"Of course not. What even gave you such thoughts?\"","\"I mean... isn’t that a common trend among women from influential backgrounds?\" Tian Yang asked.","Sun Rouxi sighed. \"That’s true—but do you know where I come from? The Three Pillars of Heaven. There’s no background more influential than ours, and arranged marriages are usually nothing more than political tools or ways to strengthen alliances.\"","\"That being said, it’s not like I have no pressure at all, especially these days, where the Three Pillars of Heaven are trying to spread their influence. I wouldn’t be surprised if they are considering it. However, I’d rather die than be forced to live with someone I don’t even like, and my family is very aware of that.\"","\"Then...\"","\"It’s because I ran away from home again, and this time it’s much longer than before. Once I return, I’ll definitely be grounded for a very, very long time.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Sun Rouxi then teased, \"What would you do if I were forced into an arranged marriage? Would you try to stop it?\"","Tian Yang fell silent for a bit before responding with a smile, \"If you ask for my help, I’ll do everything in my power to stop it.\"","Sun Rouxi’s eyes widened, her gaze flickering with delight at his response.","\"I see...\" she muttered before standing up. \"Then I’ll see you again next time.\"","However, instead of returning to her residence, Sun Rouxi went to find Ren Xia.","\"Sorry for bothering you, but can we talk for a bit?\" Sun Rouxi asked Ren Xia after she answered the door."]},{"number":2319,"title":"Chapter 2319: Sun Rouxi’s Feelings(3)","paragraphs":["Seeing Sun Rouxi standing before her, Ren Xia smiled and said, \"Is this related to Tian Yang?\"","Sun Rouxi hesitated for a brief second before silently nodding her head.","Ren Xia chuckled, \"I was wondering when you’d approach me. So, should I start calling you ’sister’ now?\"","\"H-Huh?\" Sun Rouxi stared at her with wide eyes filled with disbelief.","\"Hm? Aren’t you here to ask for my permission to approach Tian Yang?\" Ren Xia tilted her head and asked.","\"Well...\" Sun Rouxi swallowed nervously before asking, \"Why are you acting so casual about this? Another woman is asking to share your partner, you know? If I were in your shoes, I wouldn’t be able to remain so calm.\"","Ren Xia smiled and replied, \"You may know my husband, but you don’t know anything about me. Come inside. Let’s sit down first.\"","Once they were seated, Ren Xia continued, \"While I may seem calm and generous, I am actually a very selfish being. However, I am also rational, and I know that it’s unreasonable for me to hog Tian Yang for myself. A man as charming and powerful as Tian Yang is destined to have multiple partners, and quite frankly, I’m shocked and blessed to have him to myself for so long.\"","\"Anyway, I have already told him that if he were to find another lover, I wouldn’t intervene as long as that woman is decent enough, so you can rest assured that I won’t object as long as he accepts you.\"","\"I see... Thank you...\"","Sun Rouxi left shortly after.","’What a straightforward and charming individual. It’s no wonder Tian Yang fell for her...’ Sun Rouxi thought to herself as she returned to her own living quarters.","Although she had received Ren Xia’s approval, Sun Rouxi didn’t immediately approach Tian Yang. Not only was she not mentally prepared, but she still had to consider several things.","Time continued to flow like an endless river, and in the blink of an eye, another thousand years had passed. Yet, Sun Rouxi’s relationship with Tian Yang hadn’t progressed in the slightest.","\"Hey, what are you doing?\" Ren Xia suddenly approached Sun Rouxi with a slight frown and asked. \"It’s been a thousand years since I gave you my approval, so why aren’t you doing anything?\"","Sun Rouxi sighed, \"I need time to mentally prepare myself. Although it’s been a thousand years, the time we spent together only adds up to a few years.\"","\"I understand the first part, but you’re just trying to make excuses in the second part.\"","Ren Xia then asked, \"What are you worried about? That he might not accept your feelings?\"","\"...\"","Sun Rouxi remained silent, but her answer was as clear as day.","Ren Xia spoke a moment later, \"I can almost guarantee you that he won’t reject you. Even if he does, it’s not the end of the world. Do you have any idea how many times he’d rejected me before he accepted me?\"","\"Really?\" Sun Rouxi looked at her with a surprised face.","\"Of course.\"","Hearing such words, Sun Rouxi suddenly felt more courageous.","\"Fine... I’ll talk to him during our next session.\"","A few years later—","\"Thanks for today.\"","Tian Yang smiled at Sun Rouxi after their study session ended.","\"Hey, Tian Yang, I have a weird question for you.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"How do you see me?\"","\"I don’t quite understand—\"","\"You know exactly what I am trying to say!\" Sun Rouxi interrupted.","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang calmly responded, \"At first, you were like a mentor. But as we got closer, I started to see you as an elder sister.\"","Sun Rouxi spoke softly, \"Back then, you were just a reckless little troublemaker. Over time, though, I began to see you as a little brother. I do have a younger brother of my own, but we were never close—nothing like real siblings. You were the one who showed me what it truly felt like to have a brother.\"","She smiled, a hint of bitterness in her expression. \"But these days... no matter how much I want to keep seeing you that way, I can’t. Somewhere along the way, I started seeing you as a man.\"","\"Sister Sun...\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened at her words, and he swallowed nervously.","\"Don’t... Don’t call me that anymore...\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang fell silent, speechless at her unfamiliar behavior.","\"You don’t have to give me an answer right away, but I do hope that you’ll be able to give me one before I have to leave.\"","Not wanting Tian Yang to see her flushed face, Sun Rouxi quickly turned around and began walking away.","\"Wait!\"","However, Tian Yang swiftly stretched his arm and grabbed her soft hand, stopping her movements.","\"Wh-What is it?\" she asked in a nervous tone.","\"You don’t have to wait that long since I will give you an answer now...\"","Tian Yang suddenly pulled her toward him and directly into his embrace.","\"Tian Yang...\"","Sun Rouxi glared at his handsome face with flickering eyes, and before she realized, her eyes began closing by themselves.","Seeing her reaction, Tian Yang didn’t hesitate and moved his head closer until their lips touched.","After a moment of savoring each other’s saliva, Tian Yang pulled back and said with a smile, \"This is my answer. What should I call you now if not Sister Sun?\"","\"Just call me by my name...\"","\"Alright, Rouxi.\"","\"So... where do we go from here?\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang smiled and said, \"We can take this slowly if you want.\"","Tian Yang knew that she wasn’t as straightforward and touchy as Ren Xia, so he didn’t rush things with her.","\"Okay...\" Sun Rouxi nodded, her face still flushed.","From that day onward, Tian Yang and Sun Rouxi began meeting far more frequently. Their time together was no longer devoted solely to refining the soul cultivation technique, but also to gradually deepening their relationship.","As time passed, Sun Rouxi gradually shed her reserve and, following Ren Xia’s advice, even began to take a more assertive approach.","Then, one day, Sun Rouxi invited Tian Yang into her room, where their relationship took a step—several steps forward."]},{"number":2320,"title":"Chapter 2320: Embracing Sun Rouxi","paragraphs":["After Sun Rouxi invited Tian Yang into her room, she gently pulled him down onto the bed with her, her voice soft as she whispered, \"Be gentle... this is my first time.\"","Seeing her bashful expression, Tian Yang felt warmth surge through him, as though a raging flame had been lit within his heart.","Without any delay, Tian Yang helped Sun Rouxi undress before removing his own clothes.","\"You’re... beautiful,\" Tian Yang muttered as he gazed upon her flawless figure that looked as though it was sculpted by the Heavens themselves.","Her slender figure, porcelain-like skin, and a gaze so alluring it could soften even the coldest heart made her undeniably captivating.","Sun Rouxi was certainly beautiful, though not in a way that demanded attention at first glance like Ren Xia. Instead, she possessed a quiet allure—one that deepened and grew more enchanting the longer one looked.","\"Stop staring so much...\" Sun Rouxi muttered as she covered her bashful expression with her arms, but her subconscious actions left her twin peaks exposed.","With Sun Rouxi’s naked breasts beckoning his attention, Tian Yang could no longer control himself and immediately buried his face in them.","\"Ah?!\" Sun Rouxi released a surprised moan at the sudden sensation, her entire body shivering in delight.","\"Mmm~!\"","Sun Rouxi gently bit her lips as Tian Yang feasted upon her body like a starving beast.","Many minutes later, once Sun Rouxi was completely soaked downstairs, Tian Yang readied his sword and positioned it before her cave.","His gaze met hers, and after a moment of silence, Sun Rouxi quietly nodded her head.","After confirming her desire, Tian Yang no longer hesitated and pushed his sword into her entrance, penetrating deeply and drawing blood.","\"Aaah~!\" Sun Rouxi released her loudest moan yet.","\"Tian Yang~!\" She suddenly wrapped her arms around his body and embraced him tightly, her body trembling nonstop.","Tian Yang embraced her back before moving his body. His movements were slow and gentle at first, but as pleasure consumed him, his pace gradually quickened.","Even though this was her first time, Sun Rouxi showcased surprisingly high endurance, and the two of them went on to cultivate nonstop for the next several days.","\"If I were to go back in time and tell my past self about today, I doubt she’d believe me, even if beaten to death,\" Sun Rouxi suddenly joked as they rested on the bed, their body soaked in sweat.","Tian Yang chuckled before agreeing with her.","After that day, the two of them would always visit the bedroom after their study session, which became even more frequent.","\"Congratulations. It looks like two of you have finally become real partners,\" Jing Ruye said to Sun Rouxi after noticing a change in her aura.","\"Thank you... and I mean for pushing me forward. If it weren’t for you, I probably wouldn’t have been able to be honest with myself, let alone approach Tian Yang.\"","\"Don’t sweat it. This is what sworn sisters are for,\" she chuckled.","\"...\"","\"What is it?\" Jing Ruye asked when Sun Rouxi suddenly went silent.","\"You... Were you serious before? When you said that you fancied Tian Yang.\"","\"Huh?\" Jing Ruye’s eyes widened at her unexpected inquiry.","\"I know you likely said those things to force me to act, but if they were your true feelings... I wouldn’t mind if you also approached him.\"","\"...\"","After hearing her words, it was Jing Ruye’s turn to fall silent.","A moment later, she shook her head with a faint smile. \"While it’s true that Tian Yang is a very charming man, and I wouldn’t mind getting closer to him, my feelings aren’t as deep or resolute as yours. Even though we live in the same place and see each other often, we’re little more than acquaintances.\"","\"If I were to approach him with such half-hearted feelings, it would be an insult to both you and him.\"","\"If that’s how you really feel, I won’t press further,\" said Sun Rouxi.","Time continued to flow.","One hundred years... three hundred years... one thousand years.","\"Now that I have full mastery of the soul cultivation technique, I just need to actually refine the technique,\" said Tian Yang. \"And in order to do that, I will need to...\"","\"Enter seclusion, right?\" Sun Rouxi continued with a calm smile.","He nodded and said, \"Unfortunately, I don’t know when I’ll finish. It could take a year or a thousand years.\"","\"Don’t worry. No matter how long it takes, I’ll be here to wait for you.\"","Before entering seclusion, Tian Yang spent a few months with Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia. Of course, they spent most of their time in the bedroom.","A few years after Tian Yang entered seclusion, Ren Xia decided to leave the world to see if there was anything new happening outside.","As Ren Xia wandered through a nearby city, she overheard a conversation between some pedestrians, and this piece of information greatly bewildered her.","\"Wanna hear something interesting? Apparently, the crimson barrier that sealed off the Giant’s Continent for tens of thousands of years suddenly vanished.\"","\"What...?\" Ren Xia’s entire body stiffened the moment she heard such words.","\"Hey! Tell me everything you know about that!\" Ren Xia approached these pedestrians and retrieved a handful of spirit stones to show them.","The man swallowed nervously at the sight of the dazzling spirit stones and immediately continued, revealing everything he knew to her.","\"I heard it from a friend of mine—a sailing merchant who frequently crosses that area,\" the man said. \"He told me that on his return trip, the crimson dome that was always along his route had suddenly vanished.\"","\"How long ago was this?\"","\"He told me about it three days ago, but it’d been almost two months since he saw it.\"","Once the man had revealed everything he knew, Ren Xia paid him and immediately wandered off to learn more about the situation. However, even after weeks of asking around, she was unable to find any more information on the Giant’s Continent. Therefore, she decided to visit the place herself to confirm the rumors."]},{"number":2321,"title":"Chapter 2321: Overwhelming Bloodlust","paragraphs":["Although Ren Xia had decided to see for herself whether the crimson dome had really vanished or not, she didn’t immediately head there.","Instead, she returned home first to let Sun Rouxi know of the situation.","\"What? The crimson dome has vanished?\" Sun Rouxi was unsurprisingly surprised to hear this news.","\"It’s just a rumor right now, but I am going to confirm it with my own eyes. Although I would love to wait for Tian Yang to emerge from his seclusion before doing anything, we have no way to know when he’s coming out, and disturbing him will be dangerous, so I can only do this without him.\"","\"I understand what you’re trying to do, but it sounds dangerous,\" said Sun Rouxi.","\"Don’t worry, I won’t do anything reckless and will only be investigating from afar. Once I confirm that the crimson dome has truly vanished, I will immediately return to wait for Tian Yang before doing anything else.\"","\"Should I come with you just in case?\" Sun Rouxi offered to join her.","However, Ren Xia shook her head and said, \"No, you should stay here in case Tian Yang comes out early. Moreover, you’re being hunted by your family right now, correct? Unless you want to risk being caught, I suggest you stay here, where it’s safe.\"","\"If you say so.\"","Despite being older than Ren Xia, Sun Rouxi couldn’t help but view and respect her as an elder sister. Not only was Ren Xia Tian Yang’s first partner, but she had also played a crucial role in bringing Sun Rouxi and Tian Yang together.","Ren Xia left shortly after, traveling straight to the Giant’s Continent.","\"Heavens...\" Ren Xia muttered in a daze upon arriving at her destination and witnessing the situation with her own eyes.","\"It’s really gone...\"","The crimson dome that had sealed the Giant’s Continent for nearly a hundred thousand years had suddenly vanished without warning. However, that wasn’t all.","\"Not only did the barrier vanish, but this place... is overflowing with bloodlust!\"","Despite her vast experience and even having fought the Immortal Clans head-on, Ren Xia couldn’t help but tremble in fear as overwhelming bloodlust engulfed the entire continent, a visible red mist seeping from the land like steam rising from boiling water.","\"What the hell happened there?\" she swallowed nervously.","Although she wanted to use her divine sense to investigate, her instincts screamed at her to leave.","’I have already accomplished what I wanted to here, so there’s no point staying here. Let’s get out of here before something goes wrong...’","Ren Xia followed her instincts and turned around to leave.","However, right at that moment, Ren Xia suddenly felt a pair of eyes gazing directly at her.","’Fuck!’","Ren Xia didn’t even dare to turn around to face the gaze and continued fleeing at maximum speed.","Yet, even without looking, Ren Xia could tell who was looking at her.","’I knew it! That troublesome bastard is still alive!’","Fortunately, the person behind the gaze didn’t chase after her, and Ren Xia managed to return to land safely.","Even though Ren Xia had returned to land, she didn’t look back or stop moving until she returned to her personal world.","\"So? How did it go?\" Sun Rouxi sighed in relief after seeing Ren Xia return safely.","Ren Xia responded while clenching her fists, \"The barrier is gone. Not only that, but that place is overflowing with bloodlust. It felt like I was in the presence of a horde of starving wild beasts. Moreover... Kulas is still alive.\"","\"The Giant Emperor? You met him?\"","Ren Xia shook her head and explained, \"No, but I sensed his gaze on me. It was a terrifying feeling. Even now, I can feel his gaze searing my back.\"","Hearing this, Sun Rouxi fell silent with a pondering expression on her face.","\"What are you thinking about?\" Ren Xia eventually asked.","\"My family. There’s no way they don’t already know about this, and I am worried about what they might do now that the barrier that stopped their war is gone. Will they pretend the war never happened, or will they try to continue where they left off?\"","\"It’s been nearly a hundred thousand years since the war ended. Do you really think they’ll try to restart it after so long?\" Ren Xia swallowed nervously.","\"Although I don’t know why they even want to fight the Giant Race in the first place, I can say with certainty that they despise losing, and not winning the war is no different from losing. So, there’s a high possibility that they will restart the war, especially now that they’ve grown even more powerful.\"","Sun Rouxi understood her family better than anyone, and sure enough, the Three Pillars of Heaven had learned about the crimson done vanishing months ago and had been preparing to invade the Giant’s Continent ever since.","A year later, after completing their preparations, the Three Pillars of Heaven invaded the Giant’s Continent with the greatest force they had ever assembled.","However, their army—comprised of ten True Immortals, a hundred Golden Immortals, a thousand Silver and Bronze Immortals, and ten thousand Immortal Ascension cultivators—was annihilated within a single day, sending shockwaves through both the Three Pillars of Heaven and the entire world.","\"What?! Our entire force was annihilated in a single day?! That’s impossible!\"","When the news first broke, disbelief was universal, especially among the Three Pillars of Heaven.","\"I don’t know what happened on the continent, but every Life Tracking Tablet monitoring our forces has been shattered. That only happens when the lives they track are extinguished,\" revealed one of the elders.","\"To defeat so many Immortals in less than a day... this wouldn’t be possible even if everyone on that continent were an Immortal,\" another Elder speculated. \"There can only be one explanation—they possess someone who has surpassed the Immortal Realm... someone who has reached the next realm.\"","The moment this possibility was voiced, the entire hall fell silent, the atmosphere shifting dramatically."]},{"number":2322,"title":"Chapter 2322: The Final Push to the Next Realm","paragraphs":["\"Until we have an expert beyond the Immortal Realm ourselves, we must avoid fighting with the Giant Race. Fortunately, there’s a very high chance that their Giant Emperor won’t be able to leave their continent, so as long as we don’t approach them, they also can’t do anything to us!\"","\"Shouldn’t we give a proper name to the realm beyond the Immortal Realm now? Saying that every time is a mouthful.\"","\"There’s only one thing stronger than an Immortal—a God. So why don’t we just call it the God Realm?\"","\"God Realm, huh? Sounds good.\"","After realizing the possibility that Kulas had achieved the God Realm, the Three Pillars of Heaven instantly halted their assault on the Giant’s Continent. However, while they stopped attacking with large forces, they continued to send small groups of assassins and scouts to keep an eye on the Giant Race.","And just as the Three Pillars of Heaven had predicted, the Giant Race remained on the continent, seemingly with zero desire to leave for whatever reason.","Time continued to pass, and after a few more thousand years, Tian Yang emerged from his seclusion.","\"I did it! I have managed to refine the soul cultivation technique!\"","\"I’m glad for you, dear, and as much as I’d like to celebrate, there’s something you should know first,\" said Ren Xia.","The excitement on Tian Yang’s face instantly vanished at Ren Xia’s ominous words.","\"What happened?\" he asked in a solemn tone.","\"The crimson barrier that has sealed the Giant’s Continent for thousands of years is no longer present, and the Three Pillars of Heaven resumed their war with the Giant Race.\"","\"What?! When did this happen?! What about Kulas?!\" Tian Yang was full of questions.","\"It occurred three thousand years ago, a few years after you entered seclusion. Although the Three Pillars of Heaven attacked shortly after the crimson barrier vanished, they failed miserably and haven’t attempted to invade them again. As for Kulas... there’s no news of him, but he’s definitely alive.\"","Ren Xia recalled what she experienced when she went to check out the Giant’s Continent.","\"What? You went to the Giant’s Continent by yourself? That’s so dangerous and reckless!\" Tian Yang exclaimed.","\"You’re the last person I want to hear that from!\" Ren Xia rebuked.","Tian Yang sighed and then said, \"I’ll deal with that later. First...\"","He turned to look at Sun Rouxi and said, \"Here, let me share the new technique with you. If you cultivate it, your progress will definitely skyrocket.\"","Sun Rouxi nodded and accepted the new and improved soul cultivation technique.","\"What about you?\" Tian Yang looked at Ren Xia afterward. \"You might be able to learn this technique since it has been tweaked.\"","\"Although I already have a soul cultivation technique that I am cultivating, there’s no harm in trying, I guess...\"","Tian Yang transferred the technique to her the next moment.","\"Are you going to leave now that the technique has been improved?\" Tian Yang asked Sun Rouxi some time later.","\"I...\" Sun Rouxi hesitated for a moment before speaking, \"I have given this question much thought ever since I approached you. If our relationship hadn’t progressed, I would’ve definitely returned home. However, now that things are this way, I don’t really have any reason to return—No, I have a reason not to return. After all, if I return home, I won’t be able to see you again for god-knows-how-long, and I don’t want that.\"","\"Rouxi...\" A warm smile tugged on Tian Yang’s lips.","\"But...\" Sun Rouxi suddenly continued, \"I must warn you that my family will not sit still and will definitely hunt me down. If you don’t want to deal with that, then I’ll return to my family.\"","Tian Yang smiled and said, \"If I wasn’t scared of the Immortal Clans, what makes you think I would be afraid of the Three Pillars of Heaven?\"","\"My family is nothing like the Immortal Clans. It’s like comparing heaven and earth.\" Sun Rouxi shook her head.","\"I know. That’s not the point.\" Tian Yang said with a stiff smile.","\"Anyway, I’ll deal with the Three Pillars of Heaven if they ever try anything.\"","Ren Xia then spoke, \"As long as their war with the Giant Race continues, I doubt they will have the time to look for you.\"","She turned to look at Tian Yang and continued, \"What are you going to do now?\"","\"I will go outside to collect more information on the situation. Don’t worry, I won’t even approach the Giant’s Continent until I know of the full situation.\"","\"Alright. Then I’ll try to cultivate this soul cultivation technique.","Some time later, Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi entered seclusion while Tian Yang left the world to collect information.","After several years of investigation, Tian Yang learned everything he could and returned home.","\"Hm? You’re done already?\" Tian Yang was surprised to see that both of them had emerged from their seclusion so soon.","\"The soul cultivation technique doesn’t work for me,\" Ren Xia said.","\"Me neither, even though I can cultivate the original one perfectly fine...\" Sun Rouxi sighed, feeling depressed that she couldn’t experience the improved technique for some reason.","\"Is that so... That’s a pity.\"","\"Well, I kind of figured something like this would happen, anyway.\" Sun Rouxi shrugged.","\"So, what now?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang spoke, \"According to the rumors, Kulas has already reached the next realm, now known as the God Realm. Now that I have improved my soul cultivation technique, I am going to make the final push and attempt to enter the God Realm myself.\"","Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi nodded, as they also had the same idea.","\"Let’s play a game. The winner of this race will receive a favor from the other two.\" Ren Xia suddenly said.","\"I won’t lose this time,\" said Tian Yang.","\"A favor, huh? I’m in.\" Sun Rouxi nodded.","Thus, the three of them entered seclusion at the same time with the goal of entering the God Realm."]},{"number":2323,"title":"Chapter 2323: Entering the God Realm","paragraphs":["A thousand years... ten thousand years... a hundred thousand years have passed since Tian Yang and the others entered seclusion to break through to the next realm.","Despite how much time has passed, nobody has yet to emerge from their seclusion.","\"I have enough Celestial Qi, and my Soul Strength is even stronger than my Celestial Qi at this point. In fact, I can even feel myself standing only a step away from the God Ream. Yet, I cannot take that final step for some reason. I am missing something, but what?\"","Although he only needed to take one more step to enter godhood, Tian Yang wouldn’t figure out how to take that step for another five thousand years.","But eventually, he takes that final step and enters the God Realm.","\"I have achieved it! The God Realm!\" Tian Yang trembled with excitement as his entire body surged with Celestial Qi.","However, now that he had truly entered the God Realm, he could immediately tell that it was not the end—that beyond it stretched even higher levels, waiting to be reached.","After entering the God Realm, Tian Yang left seclusion to see if the other two had finished before him. However, when he walked out of his immortal cave and looked at the other two caves, the entrances were still closed, meaning that he was the first one to have a breakthrough.","\"I am first, huh?\"","Since he had no way of knowing when they would finish, Tian Yang left his world to gather information about the outside world and the current state of the Giant’s Continent.","Although a hundred thousand years passed in the blink of an eye for Tian Yang, it was a tremendous amount of time for everyone else.","In fact, the cultivation world experienced a tremendous surge in growth roughly fifty thousand years ago, when the Three Pillars of Heaven began sharing their cultivation techniques with others. Of course, these techniques were not given freely, and only those who agreed to ally with them in the war against the Giant Race were granted access.","As the Three Pillars of Heaven and the cultivation world continued to progress, the Giant Race remained quiet within their territory. But despite their seemingly secluded life, the Three Pillars of Heaven remained vigilant toward them, especially since none of their scouts had made it back.","Over the past hundred thousand years, the Three Pillars of Heaven launched two full-scale assaults on the Giant’s Continent. The first came twenty thousand years after their initial invasion, but when it failed just as miserably, they waited another seventy thousand years before attempting a second assault.","For their second assault, they had help from other powers. Yet, not a single one of them managed to make it out of the Giant’s Continent alive.","Moreover, Tian Yang learned that the cultivators from the Three Pillars of Heaven were still trying to enter the God Realm and that he was the first in this world, besides Kulas, to reach this level.","Although the Three Pillars of Heaven had decided not to attack the Giant’s Continent until they also had a cultivator in the God Realm after their first failure, they became impatient and attacked anyway.","\"Now that I have reached the God Realm, I should contact Shura again...\"","After preparing himself, Tian Yang used the communication technique to contact Shura.","Several minutes after the summoning, Tian Yang found his consciousness drifting through the starry sky like the previous two times.","\"It’s been a while, Senior Shura.\" Tian Yang greeted first.","\"Senior? I may be much older than you, but I do not care about mortal customs. Just call me by my name,\" said Shura.","\"I understand, Shura.\"","\"Looks like you have finally achieved the realm of godhood—at least in mortal terms. Now, I can finally tell you about my goal.\"","\"Before that, I want to tell you the name of the Eternal who is messing with my friend. His name is Zaaran.\"","\"Zaaran, huh? He’s a tough one to deal with... No, quite frankly, I don’t think there’s anything I can do to him, and it’s not because I lack the power to deal with him.\"","\"Then why?\" Tian Yang asked with a frown on his face.","\"He’s under a different group, and the leader of that group is even more troublesome, especially since he’s one of the three most powerful Eternals in the universe. Although I can speak with Zaaran, I cannot force him to stop, and he’s not the type who listens to others who aren’t in his group.\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang fell silent after hearing the situation from Shura. Although he didn’t want to say it, fearing it might offend Shura, Tian Yang no longer had a reason to help now that Shura couldn’t assist him with Kulas.","’It would be safer if I just say that I’ll continue to help him...’ he thought to himself.","Shura continued, \"While I cannot directly help you with your friend, I can tell you Zaaran’s weakness and how you can remove his influence from your friend.\"","\"Oh?\" Tian Yang’s eyes flickered with excitement and hope upon hearing such words.","\"Zaaran’s weakness is the Yin Element. As long as you destroy the connection between Zaaran and your friend, you will be able to sever Zaaran’s influence. I will also teach you a technique that will allow you to sense said connection.\"","Shura immediately transferred a technique into Tian Yang’s mind.","\"I gave you an additional gift to make up for my lack of ability. It will allow you to sense an Eternal’s influence. In other words, you will know if you come across a mortal influenced by an Eternal as long as you touch them.\"","Tian Yang was pleasantly surprised by the additional gift. In fact, this second gift was incredibly useful, as it allowed him to know if someone had been influenced by an Eternal.","\"There is one thing you must keep in mind about that power. Although it can sense an Eternal’s influence, it will only work on those weaker than me or near my level, so you won’t be able to sense it if that Eternal is much stronger than me,\" Shura warned."]},{"number":2324,"title":"Chapter 2324: Absolute Power","paragraphs":["After hearing Shura’s words, Tian Yang asked, \"If you don’t mind me asking, how strong are you compared to the others?\"","Shura pondered for a moment before responding in a confident voice, \"I am likely amongst the top ten strongest Eternals out there.\"","\"That’s pretty impressive, no?\"","\"Of course, it is.\"","\"Alright. Then what about your goal? What are you trying to look for? Is it the same thing that Zaaran is after?\" Tian Yang suddenly asked, trying to catch Shura off guard with his straightforward question.","Yet, Shura calmly responded with a clear voice, \"Yes, it is the same thing. In fact, every Eternal that is involved in your world are all looking for the same thing.\"","Hearing this, Tian Yang couldn’t fathom what was in his world that could possibly attract the attention of these god-like entities.","\"Aboslute Power.\" Shura spoke a moment later, revealing his goal, his voice full of longing.","\"It is a power left behind by the Absolute Being, the strongest Eternal to ever exist.\"","Tian Yang suddenly felt fatigued after learning of this information.","’My longevity had been sacrificed! And so much of it!’ he cried inwardly, feeling like hundreds of millions of years had been taken from him.","If he hadn’t reached the God Realm, this forbidden knowledge would’ve definitely killed him, even if he didn’t know the limit of his longevity.","\"If you—and all these other Eternals—desire this Absolute Power so much, why don’t you just come here and get it yourself rather than letting someone do it? Not only are you messing with our lives, but aren’t you afraid that we might steal the power for ourselves?\" Tian Yang asked after recovering some of his energy.","Shura burst out laughing at Tian Yang’s words and said loudly, \"If we were able to enter your world, we would’ve done so ages ago!\"","\"Unfortunately, the power of the Absolute Being prohibits us from getting close to your world. Our influence is also limited within your world, so we can only rely on the mortals to act as our limbs. And since most Eternals see mortals as nothing but tools, they don’t care about what happens to your people and are willing to go to extreme lengths to fulfill their own desire.\"","Tian Yang gritted his teeth and clenched his fists in frustration after learning the reason behind the Eternals’ activities within their world.","\"So the reason Zaaran destroyed Kulas’ and his family’s lives is just so he could find this Absolute Power? So they can become more powerful? What bullshit!\" Tian Yang roared at the injustice.","Shura then replied, \"The Absolute Power doesn’t just make us more powerful. It will literally make us the most powerful entity in this entire universe.\"","\"You guys are already powerful enough! Why do you need to become more powerful, let alone the most powerful being in the universe?!\" Tian Yang asked.","\"For the same reason you mortals continue to seek greater power. For the same reason the wealthy endlessly amass more wealth. For the same reason you pursued the God Realm even after attaining immortality,\" Shura said. \"Instinct and nature drive us all—we are no different in that regard. It is never enough... and it never will be.\"","Tian Yang couldn’t argue with Shura, as there was no fault in his words.","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang asked, \"Can you tell me more about this Absolute Being?\"","\"I would, but you lack longevity.\"","\"I still lack longevity? Even though I’ve reached the God Realm?\" TIan Yang was speechless.","\"Now that you’ve entered the God Realm, you should be aware that you’re only at the lowest level, and that there are more steps to climb before you truly achieve godhood.\"","Of course, Tian Yang was already aware of this fact. The cultivation realms before God Realm were all the same, so why would this realm be any different?","\"With that being said, there’s really no reason to sacrifice so much longevity just to learn about the Absolute Being. You already know the most important thing—that he was the most powerful being in this universe. Why do you need to know more? Why seek knowledge you have no use for?\"","\"That’s...\" Tian Yang didn’t know how to respond.","After a moment of silence, he sighed, \"You’re right. Then can you tell me how to find this Absolute Power?\"","Shura shook his head and said, \"Unfortunately, nobody knows how to find it. We are only certain that it exists within your world, but that is the limit of our knowledge.\"","\"Can’t say I’m surprised...\" Tian Yang muttered. If the Eternals knew the location of the Absolute Power, they would’ve already acquired it long ago.","\"Then what does it look like? And how would I know that I am close to it?\" he then asked.","\"Since nobody has ever seen the Absolute Power with their eyes, nobody knows what it looks like, but you should know that you’ve stumbled upon it the moment you do, since it will be unlike anything you’ve seen before.\"","\"What? Not only do you not know of its location, but you don’t even know what it looks like? You might as well tell me to find a ghost!\"","\"If you are thinking that the Absolute Power is in the form of a treasure or something similar, then you are wrong. It has no physical form. Also, since it has the power to restrict an Eternal’s power, then you will feel your powers weaken when you are near it, as I have gifted you some of my powers before.\"","\"Your gift? You mean my ability to weaken another Eternal’s influence?\" Tian Yang remarked. \"How would I know if such a power weakens when I can’t even feel it?\"","\"What did you just say?\"","Even though Tian Yang couldn’t see Shura’s face, he could somehow tell that there was a frown on it right this moment.","Shura continued speaking in a stern voice, \"The power to weaken an Eternal’s influence? I never gave you such a power! Explain yourself!\""]},{"number":2325,"title":"Chapter 2325: Searching for the Absolute Power","paragraphs":["\"Huh? You didn’t give me such an ability?\" Tian Yang wore a dumbfounded look on his face after hearing this. \"But that’s what Zaaran said.\"","\"I don’t care what Zaaran said! That bastard is too stupid to think because if he could, then he would know that I have no such powers! In fact, the only Eternal with the ability to weaken another Eternal’s influence is the Absolute Being!\" Shura responded.","\"Now! Explain to me why you think you have such power!\" he urged.","Tian Yang nodded and proceeded to explain what happened with Kulas—how Kulas would fall sick when he left, and how Zaaran’s influence would weaken whenever he was nearby.","\"HAHAHAHA!\"","Shura burst out laughing after learning everything, his loud voice shaking the starry sky and Tian Yang’s very soul.","\"Tian Yang, you little bastard! Not only have you already come across the Absolute Power, but you have likely even come into contact with it!\" Shura revealed loudly, unable to contain his excitement.","\"What?! I don’t remember doing such a thing!\" Tian Yang exclaimed. \"Are you sure it’s not a misunderstanding?\"","\"No, I am certain. I just checked your body for my power, but as expected, it’s not there. My power inside your body has been extinguished by the Absolute Being’s power! That, or my power never even reached you!\"","\"Try to retrace your steps! Do you remember coming into contact with anything otherworldly?\"","Tian Yang closed his eyes and recalled his entire life. Yet, he was unable to find anything like that.","\"No, but since I don’t know what the Absolute Power looks like, there’s no way for me to really know.\"","Shura sighed, \"I would look through your memories myself, but with the Absolute Power shielding you, I won’t be able to do such a thing. But this is still a great thing, since we know that you’ve come across it before, so it will only be a matter of time before we find it.\"","Tian Yang could see Shura’s massive silhouette trembling with immense excitement.","Seeing this, he couldn’t help but wonder if he could take the Absolute Being’s powers for himself. That way, he would finally have the power to fight back these Eternals. However, he also wasn’t sure if he could even acquire such unfathomable power as a mortal.","The Eternals wouldn’t use mortals to find the Absolute Power if the mortals even had a slight chance of obtaining it for themselves, after all.","\"So, what now?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"What...? I’m not sure, since this changes everything.\" Shura said. \"You’re likely the closest being to finding the Absolute Power right now, so I will give you my full support. Once you find it and I acquire it, I will grant you any wish you want. With the Absolute Being’s power, literally anything is possible.\"","Tian Yang suddenly realized something and said, \"If you take the Absolute Power... will our world still be safe from the Eternals?\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Shura spoke, \"The Absolute Being’s influence will probably linger for some more time, but it will definitely disappear eventually. However, without the Absolute Power, the Eternals will no longer have a reason to bother you. I can also promise to continue protecting your world with the power.\"","\"Okay,\" Tian Yang nodded.","Of course, he didn’t completely trust Shura even at this point. In fact, he was still thinking about acquiring the power for himself.","\"Anyway, you need to retrace your steps. Return to every place that you’ve been to,\" Shura then said. \"I also want you to contact me at every location. If I don’t respond to you, then it’s because you’re near the Absolute Being’s power.\"","\"I will do just that then.\"","\"I would grant you more powers to assist you, but as long as you are influenced by the Absolute Being’s powers, we, Eternals, won’t be able to influence you. Until next time, my fateful little friend.\"","Shura ended their connection at that point.","After Tian Yang returned to his world, he wanted to immediately start looking for the Absolute Power. However, he couldn’t just disappear without a word. Jing Ruye was in seclusion as well, so he couldn’t rely on her.","Instead of waiting for them to emerge from their cultivation, Tian Yang wrote on the ground with a sword, telling them that he will be out for some time.","Once he was done, Tian Yang left his personal world and began retracing his steps.","However, because of the situation at Giant’s Continent, he had no choice but to skip that place as well.","\"If I am going to retrace my steps, I might as well start from the very beginning.\"","With that thought in mind, Tian Yang returned to his origin—in the small village that he’d grown up in with Meng Lili.","However, since it’d been over a hundred thousand years since he left, when he returned, the village was no longer what he remembered. In fact, it had completely vanished from the face of the earth.","After taking a moment to reminisce his memories of Meng Lili, Tian Yang contacted Shura.","A few minutes later, Shura responded to his call.","\"I am in the village where I grew up after my parents abandoned me. This is where I will be starting my search for the Absolute Being’s power,\" he revealed to Shura.","\"I understand.\"","Shura ended the connection immediately, leaving no room for conversation.","Now that he’d confirmed the Absolute Power wasn’t present at his village, Tian Yang traveled to his next destination, the Immortal Monastery.","’Now that I think about it, I haven’t returned to the Immortal Monastery ever since that incident...’ Tian Yang thought to himself as he hovered before the Immortal Monastery.","Although the Immortal Monastery was completely different from the one in his memories since they had to rebuild after a certain incident, at least it was still there, and it even appeared to be doing even better than before it was nearly destroyed by the Immortal Clans."]},{"number":2326,"title":"Chapter 2326: Searching for the Absolute Power(2)","paragraphs":["Shortly after arriving at the Immortal Monastery, Tian Yang contacted Shura.","\"I am currently at the Immortal Monastery, where I spent the majority of my youth.\"","\"I see.\"","Shura ended the connection almost instantly.","Tian Yang didn’t immediately travel to the next destination. Instead, he lingered at the Immortal Monastery, silently observing them from the sky.","Although most of the sect had changed, he recognized several buildings and areas, such as the Bamboo Garden, which managed to survive the Immortal Clan’s attack due to it being disconnected from the main part of the sect.","After lingering above the sect for some time, Tian Yang noticed a presence approaching him from the sect.","A few moments later, a middle-aged man with sharp facial features stopped before Tian Yang and greeted, \"Greetings. I am the Sect Master of this sect, Wu Wing. Do you have any business with the Immortal Monastery?\"","The middle-aged man, the current Sect Master of the Immortal Monastery, sensed Tian Yang’s presence as soon as he arrived. Yet, he assumed Tian Yang was simply passing by and ignored him. But when Tian Yang lingered, however, he had no choice but to approach.","Moreover, since Tian Yang was in the God Realm and the Sect Master was only at the True Immortal realm, he couldn’t sense Tian Yang’s cultivation level.","’I can’t sense his cultivation even though we’re so close!’ The Sect Master cried inwardly after realizing this.","\"I used to be a disciple here,\" Tian Yang calmly replied. \"Before this place was renovated, that is. Are you responsible for rebuilding this place?\"","The Sect Master’s eyes widened slightly at Tian Yang’s words.","\"You’re a first generation disciple? Then you’re my Senior! What happened in the past must’ve been traumatic for you...\"","\"No, I was away at that time and managed to avoid it.\" Tian Yang shook his head.","\"Is that so... Anyway, to answer your question, no, I am not responsible for what you are seeing now. It was the last Sect Master and the disciples who stayed that did all of the work. I only replaced him a few years ago.\"","\"So you’re the third Sect Master, huh? Well, I was only reminiscing about the past. I apologize if my presence bothered you.\"","\"There’s no way! You’re a first generation disciple! If anything, it’s an honor to have you! Would you like a tour around the sect?\" Wu Wing suddenly asked.","Tian Yang didn’t immediately give a response.","After pondering for a moment, he nodded, \"Alright. I have some time.\"","Wu Wing then led Tian Yang to their front gate and started giving a tour himself.","\"What was life like in the sect back then?\" Wu Wing asked as they toured the sect.","Tian Yang recalled his own experience and the atmosphere of the sect and its disciples back then, comparing them to what he was looking at now.","\"What about the first sect master—our ancestor? What was he like?\"","Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"Unfortunately, I never got to meet him. But from what I heard, he was an ambitious individual who deeply cared for the sect and wanted it to stand at the top of the world.\"","He then asked, \"What happened to him after the incident?\"","\"The Ancestor has been in seclusion ever since the previous Sect Master took power.\"","\"So he’s still at the sect?\" Tian Yang raised an eyebrow.","\"Yes, that’s right. However, he hasn’t left for over a hundred thousand years. Honestly, we don’t know if he’s even still alive...\"","Tian Yang suddenly shifted his head to look in a certain direction. It was subtle, but he could sense a powerful aura coming from the direction, and it was still within the sect.","\"He’s still alive,\" Tian Yang calmly said.","Wu Wing’s eyes widened with shock.","\"Y-You can tell?!\"","Tian Yang offered a silent confirmation.","\"Thank you, Senior!\"","Wu Wing bowed to him.","\"By the way, I haven’t heard your name yet.\"","\"My name...\" Tian Yang hesitated for a moment before responding with a fake name. \"...is Xiao Yang.\"","Since he was the reason the Immortal Clans uprooted the Immortal Monastery, he didn’t dare to reveal his real name, as there was a good chance the Sect Master would recognize him.","\"Senior Xiao, then.\"","They continued to tour the sect.","Since the Sect Master himself was leading Tian Yang, their presence instantly attracted the attention of the disciples.","\"Who is that man besides the Sect Master?\"","\"I have never seen the Sect Master smile like that before!\"","Even the Sect Elders were intrigued by Tian Yang’s identity, but none of them dared to approach.","Eventually, they finished touring the sect.","\"Thank you for today, Sect Master. I am truly glad to see the Immortal Monastery, where I grew up, has become such a magnificent place.\"","\"It was a pleasure to meet you today, Senior Xiao. I have learned a lot about our own sect, even some lost knowledge. If you ever feel like visiting again, our sect will always welcome you.\"","The Sect Master retrieved a medallion and offered it to him.","\"As long as you have this medallion, you will be an honored guest at the Immortal Monastery.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Tian Yang didn’t linger and set off to his next destination.","A few days later, he arrived at a city near a vast ocean. Despite how much time has passed, the place looked almost identical to when he last visited.","This was where people went if they wanted to travel to the Giant’s Continent and where Tian Yang first met Huang Xiao Li and her family.","He contacted Shura shortly after arriving.","The connection went through, but they didn’t exchange any words, as Shura closed the connection almost immediately afterward.","\"The only place to check now would be the Giant’s Continent, but...\" Tian Yang pondered for a moment before flying across the vast ocean and towards the Giant’s Continent.","A few days later, he stopped when he could see his destination at the horizon. Yet, he didn’t try to get any closer and stared at it from a distance with wide eyes.","Even without needing to get close, he could sense an intense and malicious aura coming from the continent."]},{"number":2327,"title":"Chapter 2327: Searching for the Absolute Power(3)","paragraphs":["\"I don’t even need to get close to it to sense Zaaran’s influence that envelopes this entire place...\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"Kulas... are you still alive?\"","After lingering for some time, Tian Yang tried to contact Shura. Although he wasn’t on Giant’s Continent, he was close enough. If the Absolute Being’s powers existed on the Giant’s Continent, it would likely still affect him to some extent.","A minute later, Shura responded to his call.","\"I am currently at the Giant’s Continent, where I have spent the majority of my life.\"","Once again, Shura ended the connection without a word.","Afterward, Tian Yang prepared to visit other places. However, just as he turned around and began flying away, he sensed a powerful gaze directed at him.","Tian Yang instantly halted his movements and turned around to face the gaze that was coming from the Giant’s Continent.","The gaze felt familiar yet foreign at the same time.","\"Kulas... No... Zaaran!\" Tian Yang gritted his teeth and clenched his fists in frustration.","Now that he was in the God Realm, he was able to penetrate the invisible barrier that surrounded the Giant’s Continent and blocked off surveillance, looking directly into it with divine sense.","When Tian Yang used his divine sense to observe the situation, he was left utterly shocked by what he saw.","A massive gathering had formed around Colossal Mammoth City. Nearly the entire Giant Race surrounded it, their colossal bodies bowed in deep prostration as they worshipped the palace—or whatever resided within it.","When Tian Yang looked deeper and extended his divine sense inside the palace, he could see a massive silhouette seated in Kulas’ room, silently staring back at him with crimson eyes.","The instant Tian Yang’s gaze met the crimson eyes, a terrifying aura erupted from the silhouette, sending a violent ripple surging outward from the island and nearly lifting the surrounding ocean into the air.","The aura, without doubt, belonged to an expert in the God Realm, but Tian Yang could also sense something otherworldly mixed in.","Tian Yang didn’t dare to linger any longer and immediately fled the scene. He could tell just by the aura that he was no match for Zaaran at this moment, so there was no reason to endanger himself by staying there.","The eruption of that terrifying aura didn’t just drive Tian Yang away—it also alerted the experts watching the Giant’s Continent from nearby islands, most of whom belonged to the Three Pillars of Heaven.","Once they sensed the aura, they immediately reported back to the Three Pillars of Heaven, confirming their suspicions that Kulas had reached the God Realm.","Realizing that Kulas had evolved into a powerhouse they could no longer confront on their own, the Three Pillars of Heaven began aggressively forming alliances, claiming that the Giant Race would soon launch an invasion on the human race.","In truth, they had no concrete evidence that such an invasion would occur. The claim was merely a pretext—one used to further their own agenda. Little did they know, they were right on the money.","Tian Yang continued to backtrack his steps for the next few years, returning to every single location he’d gone in the past.","Unfortunately, even after going to every location, he was unable to find the Absolute Being’s power.","\"I have been to every location except one, but I no longer have access to that place,\" Tian Yang explained to Shura at the last location. \"Han Zexian’s Tomb. It existed on the Giant’s Continent before, but it has since disappeared.\"","Shura then spoke, \"The Absolute Power isn’t at that place.\"","\"How do you know?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Because the Absolute Power is too powerful to be contained in a small dimension like that. Moreover, you were able to contact me in the past from that location.\"","\"Oh, right... I almost forgot about that. Then what should I do now?\"","Shura pondered for a moment before responding, \"The Absolute Power might have sealed your memories—at least the part where you found it. The only way for you to fight the Absolute Power and regain your memories is to gain the power of Eternals.\"","\"What?\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened at such words. \"But I am a mortal. How can I obtain the power of an Eternal, much less wield it? Also, I thought that an Eternal’s power is useless against the Absolute Power, so how can I possibly...\"","\"Frankly, I don’t know if it’s possible for a mortal to wield our power. However, it’s worth trying. As for your other concern... I am also just guessing. There’s a chance it might work and a chance it won’t. There’s no way of knowing until you try. I’ll tell you more once you reach the next level.\"","\"Alright...\"","The connection ended there and Tian Yang returned home.","Upon returning to his own world, Tian Yang immediately resumed cultivation. Unable to contend with Kulas at his current level, he had no choice but to break through to the next realm, not to mention his situation with Shura.","Unfortunately, that was far easier said than done. Although Tian Yang knew exactly what was required for the next level, the demands were so immense that reaching it within any meaningful timeframe was all but impossible.","Yet, he had no choice but to try. Moreover, Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi had yet to emerge from their seclusion, so there wasn’t anything else he could do.","Five thousand years... ten thousand years... twenty thousand years after Tian Yang entered the God Realm, Sun Rouxi emerged from her seclusion.","\"Congratulations on your breakthrough.\"","Tian Yang could sense her breakthrough even before she emerged, so he was prepared to greet her the moment she came out of her immortal cave.","\"How long has it been since your breakthrough?\" Sun Rouxi asked him with a defeated smile after realizing that she wasn’t first.","\"About twenty thousand years, I guess.\"","\"If I had been able to cultivate the improved soul cultivation technique, I would’ve definitely come out first,\" she sighed.","\"Most likely.\" Tian Yang nodded, not refuting it."]},{"number":2328,"title":"Chapter 2328: What Makes Them Different?","paragraphs":["After Sun Rouxi emerged from her seclusion, Tian Yang briefed her about the current situation in the world, as well as his current goal.","\"What? You’re already aiming for the next level when you’ve just entered the God Realm?\" Sun Rouxi looked at him with concern. \"I know it’s natural for cultivators to always seek advancement, but you seem unusually rushed. Is this because of Kulas?\"","Since Tian Yang only revealed the information of Eternals to Ren Xia, Sun Rouxi was unaware of his full situation. However, she could tell that he was keeping something from her. Yet, she didn’t pursue it and patiently waited for him to reveal it once he was prepared.","\"Something like that,\" Tian Yang nodded.","\"I know I am just wasting my breath by saying this, but don’t push yourself too hard.\"","\"I won’t. I have already gotten past the hardest part, which is entering the God Realm. Now, it’s mostly a trial of endurance and patience since it’ll likely take twice as long to reach the next level.\"","Now that Sun Rouxi had emerged from her cultivation, Tian Yang’s daily routine changed slightly. Rather than spending all of his time cultivating, he would occasionally spend some time with her in the bedroom.","Time continued to pass, and after another twenty thousand years, Ren Xia also came out of her Immortal Cave, her cultivation now at the God Realm.","\"I’m last...?\" Ren Xia sighed with a defeated look after realizing that she was the last to enter the God Realm.","\"Tian Yang was first,\" Sun Rouxi said.","\"I guess we both owe you a favor then. Of course, you still owe me one, in case you forgot,\" Ren Xia said, reminding him of their previous bet.","\"Don’t worry, I haven’t forgotten,\" said Tian Yang before he briefed her on the situation.","\"What? You visited the Giant’s Continent? I know I don’t have the right to criticize you since I did the same thing, but... Haaah...!\" Ren Xia sighed out loud.","\"I didn’t go inside, but I saw the situation inside the continent with my divine sense,\" Tian Yang continued before explaining exactly what he saw to Ren Xia.","Ren Xia shivered after learning the situation and said, \"I guess the illness has spread to the rest of the Giant Race. I don’t even want to imagine what they might do next.\"","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven believe the Giant Race will invade our land,\" said Tian Yang.","Sun Rouxi shook her head and said, \"Knowing them, they are saying that just to make forming alliances easier.\"","\"Even if that’s true, I also think that the Giant Race will invade our land soon. They are looking for something, and they will stop at nothing to achieve their goal,\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"What are they looking for?\" Ren Xia asked with a raised eyebrow. \"And how do you know?\"","\"I... spoke with ’that’.\" Tian Yang gave a vague response since Sun Rouxi was present and he didn’t want to reveal the forbidden knowledge so suddenly.","\"That...?\" Sun Rouxi looked at him with a confused expression.","Meanwhile, Ren Xia immediately understood what he meant and nodded, \"I see.\"","She looked at Sun Rouxi a moment later and spoke, \"Don’t you think we should tell her about ’that’? She’s in the God Realm, so she has enough longevity.\"","Tian Yang and Sun Rouxi’s gaze met the next second.","\"There’s something we’ve been keeping a secret from you because it contains knowledge that requires you to sacrifice your longevity to learn.\"","\"I knew you were hiding something from me, but to think it was something like this... Alright, tell me. I don’t care if I have to sacrifice some of my lifespan,\" Sun Rouxi quickly came to a decision.","Tian Yang nodded and revealed the existence of Eternals to her, as well as Kulas’ real situation. However, he kept the knowledge about the Absolute Being and its power a secret for the time being.","\"Eternals, huh?\" Sun Rouxi muttered with a slightly surprised look on her face.","\"You’re not as shocked as I expected,\" Ren Xia remarked.","She shrugged lightly. \"I’ve spent most of my life surrounded by outrageous things, so I’ve grown somewhat resistant to this sort of revelation. In fact, now that I know about Eternals, I’ve finally solved one of the biggest mysteries of my life.\"","\"What’s that?\" Tian Yang inquired.","\"The Enlightened One,\" she replied with a solemn face. \"He claims to receive revelations and teachings from Heaven, and despite his undeniable results, I have always been skeptical of it. However, things are different now.\"","\"So you think that the Enlightened One is being backed by an Eternal?\" Ren Xia remarked.","\"It’s highly likely,\" Tian Yang said.","\"According to Shura, all of the Eternals are looking for the same thing within our world, and since they cannot approach our world for whatever reason, they require someone already here to do their bidding. In return, they’d grant their puppet power and knowledge.\"","\"Is that so...\" Sun Rouxi mumbled with a pondering face.","\"By the way, are you feeling okay?\" Tian Yang suddenly asked as he looked at Sun Rouxi.","\"Hm? I feel fine. Why do you ask?\" she calmly replied.","\"Seriously? You don’t feel even a little fatigued after sacrificing your longevity?\" Tian Yang looked at her with wide eyes.","Sun Rouxi nodded and said, \"I know what it feels like to have an unnatural amount of your longevity vanish in the blink of an eye, but I didn’t feel anything like that. In fact, I don’t think I had to sacrifice any longevity.\"","Tian Yang’s jaw dropped after hearing her words. Sun Rouxi’s situation was exactly the same as Ren Xia.","’Their longevity isn’t being sacrificed even after learning about Eternals? How is that possible?’ Tian Yang cried inwardly.","He was certain that those he forced to learn the forbidden knowledge had died after having all of their longevity sacrificed, so what makes Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia so different?","’Is it because I cultivated with them?’","A weird thought suddenly entered his mind."]},{"number":2329,"title":"Chapter 2329: The Giant Race Invades!","paragraphs":["’There’s no point overthinking about something I have no clue about. I should just treat it as a happy miracle that neither of them had their longevity sacrificed,’ Tian Yang thought to himself and immediately stopped pondering about it.","\"So what’s our plan now?\" Ren Xia asked some time later.","Tian Yang explained to her that he was already trying to advance to the next stage of God Realm.","\"I met Kulas—Zaaran when I visited the Giant’s Continent. Not directly, but I immediately knew that I lacked the power to stop him at my current level. If I want to have any hope of stopping him, I need to reach the next level before him.\"","\"The next stage, huh? That’ll probably take you another hundred thousand years if not two or three,\" Ren Xia remarked.","\"What do you plan on doing then?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Well, I can follow your lead and immediately continue my cultivation, but I need to stretch my body for a little first.\" Ren Xia responded before she suddenly grabbed his robes and started dragging him away. \"You can continue your cultivation... after you spend a few years with me.\"","\"You...\" Tian Yang was speechless.","Ren Xia looked at Sun Rouxi and added, \"You had plenty of ’alone time’ with him for the last twenty thousand years, so you won’t mind if I hog him for a few years, right?\"","Sun Rouxi could only silently shake her head with a smile on her face.","\"I’ll work on my cultivation techniques and see if I can improve Heaven’s Indomitable Soul,\" she said a moment later.","Thus, Ren Xia dragged Tian Yang into her bedroom, where they would cultivate with each other countless times for the next decade.","Once Ren Xia had her full and was satisfied, she finally released Tian Yang. However, right as Tian Yang prepared to enter another seclusion, Jing Ruye emerged from her seclusion with a defeated look on her face.","\"I... don’t think I have what it takes to enter the God Realm,\" she released a defeated sigh.","\"Hell, I’d only managed to get to True Immortal because of Sister Rouxi. If it hadn’t been for her assistance and the countless treasures she gave me, I doubt I would’ve ever entered the Immortal Realm.\"","\"It’s too early to give up. Most cultivators don’t successfully break through on their first seclusion,\" Sun Rouxi tried to encourage her.","\"That may be true for the other realms, but the God Realm is a real bottleneck for the untalented. It draws a line between the mediocre and those truly destined for cultivation. Forget entering the God Realm; after all this time I still can’t sense Celestial Qi.\"","\"Even if you give up on yourself, I won’t give up on you, so I will personally guide you,\" said Sun Rouxi.","\"You really don’t need to...\"","\"I have plenty of time, anyway.\"","\"Thank you... Sister Rouxi...\"","Thus, Sun Rouxi added guiding Jing Ruye into her routine, and Tian Yang entered seclusion again.","A few weeks later, Ren Xia decided to leave the private world to wander the outside for a breath of fresh air.","Yet, days after she left, Ren Xia immediately returned to the world.","\"It’s finally happened! The Giant Race has left their continent and begun their invasion!\" Ren Xia interrupted Sun Rouxi and Jing Ruye’s lecture, dumbfounding them with this news.","\"When did this happen? What is my family’s response?\" Sun Rouxi immediately inquired about the Three Pillars of Heaven’s reaction.","\"It started literally yesterday. The Three Pillars of Heaven response is what you’re likely thinking right now. They, alongside their alliance, are going to fight. It’s war. A real large-scale war between powerful cultivators. This is unprecedented.\"","\"Heavens... this will wreak catastrophic havoc across the world. Countless innocent lives will be lost...\" Jing Ruye covered her mouth, stunned by the thought of the chaos the war would bring. Any battle between two Immortals was devastating enough—she couldn’t fathom hundreds, perhaps thousands, of them clashing simultaneously across the land.","\"...\"","Sun Rouxi was speechless, but the disgust on her face was as clear as day.","\"Why do things like this have to happen when Tian Yang isn’t available? He’s definitely cursed.\" Ren Xia sighed.","Sun Rouxi then said, \"Fortunately, it hasn’t been long since he entered seclusion, so it’ll likely be fine even if we disturb him. In fact, the faster we do it the better.\"","Ren Xia shook her head and said, \"Even if he comes out of seclusion right now, there’s nothing he can really do unless he’s powerful enough to stop their leader—Kulas.\"","Sun Rouxi opened her mouth only to close it without uttering a word.","\"Let’s just watch and let it play out for now,\" Ren Xia spoke a moment later.","\"You’re right. There’s no need to act recklessly when we have little to no option at this moment.\"","Thus, Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi decided to let the war play out and watch from the shadows.","Although the Giant Race had finally left their land and visited the human world for the first time in tens of thousands of years, they didn’t invade all at once. They began by sending only a few giants to wreak havoc—seemingly testing the waters. Even so, the Three Pillars of Heaven and their allies struggled immensely, as it took dozens of experts at the Immortal Realm to handle a single giant at the same level.","Of course, it didn’t take long for the humans to realize just how powerful the Giant Race had become. Every single giant they fought were literally unstoppable, as they all resembled a madman who lost all reason and only acted upon their primal instinct.","\"What the hell is wrong with these giants?! They don’t react even after getting stabbed or losing their limbs! Even beasts run away or react to pain! It’s like we’re fighting undead beings!\"","The giants were so relentless that the only way to truly stop them was to destroy their heart or smash their brains. Otherwise, they would continue to struggle even if they lost all of their limbs. And this left the Three Pillars of Heaven—the human race absolutely terrified."]},{"number":2330,"title":"Chapter 2330: The Giant Emperor Enters the Battlefield","paragraphs":["\"Fucking hell! This monster refuses to give up even when half of his body is missing!\"","\"D-Don’t stop attacking! Stop wasting energy on his limbs and aim only for his heart and head! That’s the only way to stop these monsters!\"","The Divine Heavens shook throughout the day in multiple regions as the Giant Race invaded and the Human Race attempted to stop them.","The Three Pillars of Heaven had been confident they could crush the Giant Race at any time, but the war quickly shattered that certainty and filled them with unprecedented fear. Realizing they were struggling even while the giants merely tested them with small incursions, they began desperately recruiting more allies.","Those who had doubted the Three Pillars of Heaven’s real motive were forced to accept reality after the invasion really happened and agreed to join the alliance.","Thus, the creation of the world’s largest alliance was formed, with tens of thousands of large families and sects joining together to fight against the Giant Race.","Time passed. With the Giant Race striking only every few years, the humans had time to regroup and breathe—but each invasion saw the giants return stronger than before.","After a thousand years had passed, the Giant Race started invading even more frequently, attacking once a year and in larger numbers.","The Three Pillars of Heaven have tried to negotiate with the Giant Race several times during this period, but all of the messengers they sent to the Giant Continent never returned.","Ten thousand years later, the Giant Race stopped holding back and began invading the rest of the world in mass, instantly overwhelming the humans with their numbers.","With tens of thousands of giants let loose and rampaging around the world, the entire Divine Heavens was quickly engulfed in flames.","Thousands... tens of thousands of people died daily during the invasion, and the number of casualties only increased as the war dragged on.","In the midst of the war, the humans realized that the giants were moving in a pattern and that they only visited new places, meaning that once they explored a certain area, they would not return, almost as if they were searching for something.","Upon realizing this, those who could not fight took shelter in old battlefields. Although most of these places were destroyed beyond recognition, it was at least safe.","\"These giants are searching for something, and if we find it first, it could turn the tide of the war.\"","The Three Pillars of Heaven redirected part of their effort to the search, but with no clue what they sought, they were groping in the dark. Yet, that didn’t deter them from trying.","After another twenty thousand years, a cultivator from the Three Pillars of Heaven finally reached the God Realm. The world celebrated and recorded the unprecedented event—unaware that three other cultivators had attained the God Realm tens of thousands of years earlier.","With the emergence of this God Realm cultivator, the humans instantly turned the tide of the war, as the cultivator could single-handedly slaughter the giants, who were all still within the Immortal Realm.","However, since there was only one God Realm cultivator, there was only so much he could do against a massive army of giants that were spread throughout the Divine Heavens, not to mention that more giants would constantly invade the land.","But as time passed and more cultivators reached the God Realm, the humans started eliminating the giants faster than they could be replaced.","Nearly a hundred thousand years had passed since the Giant Race began their invasion, and just as humanity was regaining confidence, a sudden shift occurred, and for the first time, the Giant Emperor left the Giant Continent while leading an army.","\"T-The Giant Emperor is finally taking action for the first time since the beginning of the war!\"","\"What are their numbers?!\"","\"T-Ten thousand! This is their biggest invasion yet! The Emperor himself has probably led the remaining forces for one final push!\"","\"So we’ve finally reached the end, huh? Once we deal with the Giant Emperor and the rest of his forces, we can finally put an end to this war.\"","The Three Pillars of Heaven and countless backgrounds quickly came together, forming their most powerful and largest army yet to confront the Giant Emperor.","Shortly before the two sides clashed, a certain individual emerged from his seclusion.","\"Tian Yang! You’re finally out!\"","When Tian Yang emerged from his seclusion, the first person to greet him after a hundred thousand years was Jing Ruye.","Seeing the urgent expression on her face, Tian Yang immediately inquired about the situation.","\"What happened?\"","Jing Ruye wasted no time explaining everything to him.","\"The situation is worse than I thought...\" Tian Yang muttered, shaking his head at the news. He had expected the Giant Race to search their lands for the Absolute Power eventually, but he’d focused on cultivation—believing Sun Rouxi or Ren Xia would intervene if things ever grew dire.","\"Where’s Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia?\" he asked her a moment later.","\"They wanted to wait for you to finish your seclusion before acting, but they couldn’t sit still after hearing that the Giant Emperor had appeared and left a month ago to gather information on him. I would’ve gone with them, but they insisted that I stay here just in case you returned.\"","Tian Yang rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"These two idiots. Why didn’t they just come and get me when the situation is this dire?\"","\"Actually, they tried... Several times, at that. However, there was an invisible force around your Immortal Cave that prevented them from approaching you,\" Jing Ruye explained.","\"What?\" Tian Yang was surprised to hear this, as he had no idea what could’ve caused such a phenomenon. Unfortunately, he didn’t have the time to ponder about it.","\"Where is Kulas now?\" Tian Yang asked.","After Jing Ruye gave the location, he left his personal world and headed there at once with Jing Ruye following him since she no longer had a reason to stay behind."]},{"number":2331,"title":"Chapter 2331: Joining the Fight Against the Giant Emperor","paragraphs":["Somewhere in Divine Heaven, two massive armies faced off—one enormous in number, the other immense in size.","\"Giant Emperor, your atrocities against us humans will end here!\"","The person leading the human army shouted at the Giant Emperor who was leading an army of ten thousand giants.","\"You’ll stop me? With that pathetic army of yours?\" Kulas laughed out loud, his voice full of disdain.","Suddenly four figures radiating overwhelming auras stepped forward to face Kulas—each a God Realm cultivator.","\"There are four of us in the God Realm on our side, while you’re the only one on your side. The outcome of this war is already decided,\" one of them said.","Kulas smiled calmly. \"Four against one? If you’d had a few more, you might’ve stood a chance.\"","Kulas suddenly erupted with his hidden aura, flooding the area with a suffocating presence that instantly overwhelmed the four God Realm cultivators.","\"T-This is—!\"","\"He’s already achieved the second level of God Realm?! How is that possible?!\"","When the humans realized Kulas’s true cultivation, their confidence shattered and dread rippled through the ranks before the battle even began.","Deep frowns and grimaces contorted the four God Realm cultivators’ faces, as if they’d just swallowed a live fly.","Kulas laughed loudly; his voice shook the air, splintering the nearby mountains—already weakened by his presence—into crumbling shards.","Meanwhile, two figures with concealed presences watched the situation unfold from afar.","\"That son of a bitch has already broken into the second level! Even if Tian Yang emerges from seclusion now, he’ll still be a step behind,\" Ren Xia said, clenching her fists in frustration as Kulas’ presence washed over her.","\"Even if we join the battle to help, I don’t think we can beat him,\" Sun Rouxi said, frowning as she searched for a solution.","\"Our only hope is that Tian Yang reaches the second level before the battle ends.\"","At the same time, the final battle between humanity and the Giant Race erupted. While the four God Realm cultivators concentrated on Kulas, the rest of the forces engaged the giant army—and in the blink of an eye tens of thousands of miles of land were laid waste.","The moment the battle erupted, dozens of heaven-splitting martial techniques converged on Kulas, who towered above the tallest nearby mountain. His skin, now a deep crimson, repelled the assaults effortlessly without so much as a scratch.","\"Hahaha! It’d take almost no effort to kill you, but that’d be too boring, so let me enjoy this for a little bit!\" Kulas laughed out loud as he treated the fight like it’s nothing more than a casual game.","Meanwhile, the four God Realm cultivators fought with everything on the line. In their eyes, if they lost to Kulas, humanity would be doomed.","Time passed quickly, and in just three short days the humans had defeated over half of the giant army. Though they paid dearly, suffering hundreds of thousands of casualties.","Meanwhile, Kulas paid no mind to his dwindling forces, focusing instead on slowly wearing down the four God Realm cultivators, humiliating them with overwhelming prowess.","\"I doubt the battle will last until the end of the week at this rate...\" Sun Rouxi shook her head as she watched members from her own family being killed in action.","After a moment of silence, she continued.","\"At this rate, the battle will end before Tian Yang even shows up.\" Sun Rouxi turned to look at Ren Xia and continued, \"I want you to return home and see if you can wake up Tian Yang.\"","\"What are you going to do?\" Ren Xia asked even though she already had an idea.","\"I am going to join the battle,\" she calmly responded.","Ren Xia didn’t try to argue and nodded.","\"I will wake him from his seclusion even if I have blow up his Immortal Cave.\"","After saying such words, Ren Xia turned around and flew away.","However, before she could really go anywhere, a massive crimson barrier suddenly materialized around the battlefield, preventing her from leaving.","\"What the hell?!\"","\"Where do you think you’re going?\"","A loud voice resounded, causing Ren Xia to turn toward the sound, where Kulas was staring at her with a cold grin on his face.","\"Kulas, you bastard!\" Ren Xia growled with a frown on her face.","\"Did you really think I wouldn’t notice you watching from there? I was merely pretending that I didn’t notice!\" he laughed.","\"Where’s Tian Yang?\" Kulas then asked.","\"Why do you care?\"","\"I have been purposefully delaying the war just to see what he’d do, but turns out I had wasted my time.\"","\"If you want to see him that badly, let me go. I was about to fetch him before you intervened,\" Ren Xia said, silently hoping that Kulas would agree.","Kulas pondered for a moment before responding, \"No. It will be more entertaining to meet him after I kill everyone here. However, I will keep you alive so I could torture you right in front of him.\"","\"Is that so...\" Ren Xia mumbled.","\"I have always wanted to punch your annoying face, and this is the perfect opportunity!\"","Realizing that she had no other option, Ren Xia withdrew her weapon and flew at Kulas.","Seeing this, Sun Rouxi also joined the battle.","The members of the Three Pillars of Heaven were shocked to see Sun Rouxi.","\"Sun Rouxi! Where the hell have you been all these years?!\" One of the four God Realm cultivators exclaimed with disbelief after seeing her.","\"Save the talk for later!\" Sun Rouxi shouted as she retrieved a treasure that took the shape of a golden wheel.","\"Che!\"","Thus, Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi joined the battle against Kulas.","\"Hahaha! Things are finally getting entertaining!\" Kulas smiled as he unleashed even more aura.","\"Just how much more power is this monster hiding?!\"","\"I can’t breathe!\"","\"H-Help m—\"","Kulas’ pressure was so overwhelming that every cultivator below the Immortal Realm had their hearts burst from the strain, instantly annihilating half of the army."]},{"number":2332,"title":"Chapter 2332: Joining the Fight Against the Giant Emperor(2)","paragraphs":["With half of their forces killed in an instant, the human army was sent into a frenzy panic.","\"He killed so many of us with just his presence alone!\"","\"I-It’s over! That monster is too powerful!\"","\"Don’t give up yet!\" One of the four God Realm cultivators shouted at them, snapping them out of their panic.","\"Hurry up and deal with the rest of the giants! We’ll need as much help as we can get with the Giant Emperor!\" said another God Realm cultivator.","While the army regained their composure and continued to deal with the rest of the giants, Ren Xia and the other God Realm experts focused on Kulas.","Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi were obviously much stronger than the other four God Realm experts, and it didn’t take long for them to realize this fact.","\"Heavens! When did you achieve the God Realm?!\" One of them couldn’t help but ask Sun Rouxi.","\"Who is that woman?! To think there’d be such a powerful expert out there this entire time!\" Another questioned Ren Xia’s identity.","\"Are you bastards crazy?!\" Sun Rouxi snapped at them. \"This isn’t the time for side conversations!\"","Her words quickly snapped their minds back into order. However, even with the addition of Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi, the six of them were still struggling against Kulas. Moreover, they were certain that he was still hiding more power.","\"Sun Rouxi, do you have any idea how we can defeat this monster?!\" One of the four God Realm cultivators asked. \"You’re the smartest in our family, after all!\"","\"Why the hell are you asking me? What happened to the ’Enlightened One’? Why didn’t you ask him, Father? I’m sure he could guide you to victory with his prophecies!\" Sun Rouxi glared at the man, who turned out to be her father.","Her father, Sun Hongjia, gritted his teeth and responded, \"We’ve tried, but he’s been in a seclusion even before the war began. He’s spoken with us a few times through letters, but he’s never mentioned anything about the Giant Race or a war.\"","\"Then why didn’t you force him out of seclusion? Our entire world is at stake, you know?\"","\"I’m sure this is also within his prophecies. If the situation is truly as grave as it seems, then he would’ve already appeared.\"","Sun Rouxi clenched her fists and gritted her teeth in frustration at her father’s blind trust and faith in the Enlightened One.","’Even though so many years have passed, I see that you are still as foolish as before...’ Sun Rouxi sighed inwardly.","\"Unfortunately, I have no clue how we can defeat him,\" she shook her head a moment later.","\"I know someone who might, but he’s not here. If we can stall him long enough, perhaps...\"","\"You know someone who can defeat this monster when even the six of us combined cannot?! Who is this monster?!\" Sun Hongjia exclaimed in a shocked voice.","Sun Rouxi had a strong urge to respond with ’my dao companion’, but she managed to keep her control in check.","Time continued to pass, and at the end of the day, the human army managed to defeat the remaining giant army, allowing them to assist Sun Rouxi and the others. However, the pressure coming from Kulas’ aura was so intense that the Immortals couldn’t even approach without exhausting their spiritual energy to shield themselves from it.","It was at this point that the Immortals realized that they couldn’t help even if they wanted to, and all they could do was watch from afar as their remaining hope slowly gets beaten down by Kulas.","\"Tian Xianzhong!\" Sun Hongjia exclaimed when Kulas suddenly landed a fatal blow on one of them.","Tian Xianzhong was sent flying away, only stopping when the Immortals went to stop his fall.","\"I-I am still alive... but... I don’t think... I can... continue...\" he muttered as he coughed up many mouthfuls of blood.","\"One down!\" Kulas laughed madly, attacking them with nothing but his bare fists—each blow obliterating everything for miles with just the sheer force coming from his punches.","After taking care of one, Kulas became more aggressive as he picked up his pace, quickly defeating the second... then a third.","After another half a day, only Ren Xia, Sun Rouxi, and Sun Hongjia remained.","And not before long, Sun Hongjia also retired from the battle after losing both of his arms when he had no choice but to block Kulas’ attack directly with his body.","\"And now, there are only two left...\" Kulas smiled as he glared at Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia.","Although both of them were still in good shape and only suffered minor injuries up to this point, Kulas was completely fine in comparison, only sweating slightly, like he’d just finished a light jog.","\"You...\"","Kulas’ gaze suddenly halted on Sun Rouxi before asking in a curious voice, \"What is your relationship with Tian Yang?\"","\"Why do you care?\" she sneered.","\"So I can decide whether I should just kill you now or save you for later, like that bitch. So, are you also another woman who ensnared my sworn brother?\"","Sun Rouxi hesitated to answer, as there were many members of the Three Pillars of Heaven present as witness, including her own father.","\"I have no idea what you’re talking about,\" Sun Rouxi eventually responded with a stiff smile.","If there was a chance that they survived this, she didn’t want to entangle Tian Yang with her family’s drama.","\"In that case, you may die.\"","Kulas immediately attacked.","\"Hey, are you seriously going to ignore me?!\" Ren Xia cried out loud in disbelief when Kulas flew right past her and directly at Sun Rouxi.","With all of Kulas’ attention directly on her, Sun Rouxi felt the battle had increased in difficulty tremendously, reaching a point where she could only focus on evading and nothing else.","Ren Xia didn’t stop attacking Kulas, but he continued to ignore her, treating her as if she was just an insignificant fly that could be taken care of at will.","In just a mere hour, Sun Rouxi found herself on the verge of death, unable to retaliate. Had it not been for the life-saving treasures in her possession, she would’ve likely died several times already.","\"Stop your pointless struggle and die for me already!\" Kulas roared as his aura intensified even more.","The sudden shift in pressure caught Sun Rouxi off guard for a heartbeat—and Kulas seized the moment, landing a crushing, direct punch.","Sun Rouxi’s body—an ant before an elephant compared to Kulas’s fist—was sent flying, leaving a streak of blood across the sky.","\"Sun Rouxi!\" Ren Xia exclaimed with fear in her voice.","As she rushed to check on Sun Rouxi, Kulas intercepted and blocked her path, a malicious grin on his face before his fist slammed into her.","Kulas purposefully held back, so Ren Xia managed to survive it. Unfortunately, both of her arms were broken at that moment.","\"Now, how should I take care of you before Tian Yang arrives?\" Kulas mumbled in a low voice.","Meanwhile, the rest of the army fell into despair after seeing Kula defeat their final hope.","\"It’s really over now...\"","\"There’s nobody in this world who can stop him...\""]},{"number":2333,"title":"Chapter 2333: Appearing Just in Time","paragraphs":["Some time later, Kulas started to approach Ren Xia with a wide grin on his face.","\"I’ll just rip you limb from limb for now.\"","Kulas took several steps before suddenly halting his movements.","His head turned to look in a different direction from Ren Xia, and an excited grin appeared on his face as he exclaimed with exhilaration, \"He’s finally here!\"","In the next moment, a powerful ripple appeared from afar, and the crimson barrier that had blocked their view shattered into countless fragments that poured from the sky like a crimson rain.","\"KULAS!!!\"","An enraged voice resounded the next moment as a silhouette appeared from the horizon, quickly closing in on them.","Before anyone could make out the silhouette’s face, hundreds of swords materialized from thin air around Kulas and rained down upon him.","Kulas raised his arms in a defensive posture he had never used since the war began—then the blades struck, piercing his skin and drawing blood for the first time.","While the spectators were shocked by the scene of Kulas being injured, Ren Xia’s gaze never left the silhouette even for a split second.","\"You’re late, you idiot...\" she released a sigh of relief after seeing Tian Yang’s face.","Tian Yang stopped right beside Ren Xia and asked, \"Where’s Rouxi?\"","The smile on her face froze as her gaze shifted to where Sun Rouxi had crashed just seconds earlier.","\"She’s...\"","But before she could finish her sentence, Tian Yang interrupted, \"I can still sense her presence. Go to her. I’ll take care of Kulas myself.\"","Ren Xia silently nodded before rushing to Sun Rouxi without hesitation.","Kulas didn’t bother to stop Ren Xia this time, as his attention was now fully on Tian Yang.","\"You’ll take care of me? Even though you’re still in the first level of the God Realm?\" Kulas suddenly spoke with a smile on his face.","\"...\" Tian Yang didn’t respond.","Indeed, his cultivation was still at the first level of God Realm. Ren Xia didn’t notice simply because she was in no condition to pay attention to such details.","After a moment of silence, he calmly sighed, \"Unfortunately, I was unable to advance to the next level. However, that’s precisely why I managed to make it here in time to stop you.\"","Kulas tilted his head in a confused manner and spoke, \"Even if you have arrived before I could torture your lover, I fail to see how you’ll be able to stop me. That being said, even if you had advanced to the next level, you still wouldn’t be able to defeat me.\"","Tian Yang went silent again. He knew Kulas was right—that even if he arrived, he would not beat him. Still, learning Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia were in danger left him unable to stand idly by.","\"Hey, Kulas... No, Zaaran, I have a proposition for you.\"","\"What?\" Kulas raised his eyebrows.","\"I know why you’re doing all of this and what you’re looking for. What if I tell you that I know where to find it?\" Tian Yang said with a confident smile.","\"Hahaha! And here I was wondering what nonsense you’d spew! What the hell do you know about me?!\"","\"Absolute Power.\" Tian Yang spoke with voice transmission so that the others wouldn’t be able to hear it.","When Kulas heard the name, his laughing immediately stopped, and he glared at Tian Yang with a serious expression.","\"How the hell do you know about that? Did the Eternal behind you tell you?\" Kulas narrowed his eyes.","\"Not only that, but I have already found it. If you back off for now, I’ll tell you its location.\"","\"Bullshit! If you truly had the Absolute Power in your possession, you wouldn’t be here trying to bargain with me right now! Even if what you say is true, the Eternal behind you would never allow it! Why the hell are you trying to bargain with me when you can just hand it over to the one you’re working for?\"","\"Because I don’t trust him.\"","\"And you trust me? Do you really believe that I’d fall for such an obvious lie?\"","\"No, I don’t trust you either. In fact, I don’t trust any Eternal. And since you’re pretty much all the same in my eyes, I might as well bargain with someone who has what I want currently.\"","\"Are you referring to that bitch? You’re really going to give me the Absolute Power for a woman? I can easily destroy your world afterward with that power, you know?\"","\"That’s a risk I am willing to take.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Kulas asked, \"What proof do you have that you know where to find the Absolute Power?\"","\"Do you remember what you said to me? That I had a power that weakened your influence? That wasn’t a gift given to me by an Eternal. I have somehow acquired some of that power after coming into contact with the Absolute Power.\"","\"That’s—!!!\" Kulas’ eyes widened with shock after hearing such evidence.","Then, a massive grin tugged at his lips, one that reached from ear to ear.","\"Very well! You’ve got a deal! If you lead me to the Absolute Power, I, Zaaran, will not only spare you and your partner, but I will even leave your world alone! However, the moment I sense any bullshit, I’ll immediately kill you and everyone in this world.\"","Tian Yang nodded. \"Give me a moment.\"","He went to Ren Xia’s side, who was still feeding Sun Rouxi medicine. Jing Ruye, who purposefully waited before making an appearance, was also there, her eyes soaked in tears.","\"How is she?\" Tian Yang asked","\"Her life isn’t in danger, but she won’t be able to move for some time.\"","Tian Yang nodded and then said, \"I’m going to leave with Kulas for a bit. I’ll return once everything is over.\"","\"Alright. Make sure to explain everything once you’re back,\" she calmly nodded.","Without another word, Tian Yang returned to Kulas and said, \"Follow me.\"","In the blink of an eye, they both disappeared into the horizon, leaving everyone there puzzled and stunned."]},{"number":2334,"title":"Chapter 2334: Sealing Kulas’ Soul","paragraphs":["After leaving the battlefield, Tian Yang led Zaaran east.","As they traveled, Tian Yang questioned, \"If you’re just looking for the Absolute Power, why are you doing all of this? Was there really a need to start a war with us?\"","\"The fastest and most efficient way to find the Absolute Power is to conquer the world and search every inch of it without delay,\" Zaaran calmly answered.","\"Then why are you the only Eternal to make such drastic measures?\" Tian Yang continued to ask.","\"And how do you know that? I am certainly not the only Eternal with this idea. I am merely the first one to achieve it,\" he remarked with an arrogant smirk.","Tian Yang trembled at Zaaran’s words that implied there were multiple Eternals attempting to conquer the Divine Heavens.","\"However, once I acquire the Absolute Power, the other Eternals will lose interest in this world, so the faster you give it to me, the faster we’ll leave you alone.\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang silently gritted his teeth at Zaaran’s words that were very similar to what Shura told him.","A few days later, Tian Yang suddenly slowed down to a halt.","He turned around and faced Zaaran, who wore Kulas’ face and asked, \"I have one last question for you. Is Kulas still there?\"","Zaaran remained silent for a good second before responding with a smile, \"Of course, he’s still alive. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be able to make use of him.\"","\"What about his consciousness? What will happen to him once you leave?\"","\"His consciousness will return, but I cannot guarantee you that he will return to the person he was before.\"","Tian Yang tightened his fists at such words even though this was something he’d already anticipated.","\"Enough questions. How much longer before we reach the Absolute Power? If you are trying to delay this for whatever reason, I swear...\"","\"Relax, we’re almost there.\"","Tian Yang turned around and continued to move.","A few more days later, Tian Yang stopped again.","\"We’re here,\" he announced in a calm voice.","Zaaran’s eyes lit with excitement as he scanned the area. They were in the heart of a vast mountain range, surrounded by nothing but peaks and empty land.","Moments later, he frowned and spoke, \"Where the hell is the Absolute Power? I cannot sense it!\"","A subtle grin tugged at Tian Yang’s lips as he spoke, \"But it’s right in front of you.\"","\"What?!\"","Zaaran used multiple techniques, even one only available for Eternals, but when he still failed to see the Absolute Power, he erupted with anger, instantly wiping away the nearby mountains with his explosive aura.","\"You must be messing with me! How dare you try to make a fool out of me, you insignificant mortal!!!\" Zaaran roared, releasing his entire cultivation base.","The pressure coming from Zaaran’s aura was so immense that blood flowed from Tian Yang’s eyes and nose. Yet, the smile on his face only became more prominent.","\"What would I gain from lying to you?\" Tian Yang calmly shook his head. \"I am even willing to swear on my soul that it’s here.\"","\"Then why can I not see it?!\" Zaaran rebuked.","\"Why are you asking me, a mere mortal?\" Tian Yang shrugged.","\"I do not believe you! This is your last chance to tell me the truth! Otherwise, I will kill you and everyone in this world!\"","Tian Yang closed his eyes and sighed.","\"I’ll help you see it. However, your aura is too intense for me to even get close to you, so put it away,\" he said a moment later.","Zaaran hesitated for a brief moment but eventually listened and retrieved his aura.","Tian Yang slowly approached him.","\"Now, close your eyes.\"","Zaaran didn’t question it and closed his eyes.","\"I will now help you see the Absolute Power.\"","Tian Yang placed a finger on Zaaran’s forehead.","\"Once I tell you, open your eyes.\"","One second... two second... three seconds.","\"Okay, you can open your eyes now.\"","After ten seconds, Zaaran slowly opened his eyes with excitement.","\"What...?\"","But when he opened his eyes, the ruined mountains and desolate land were gone. Tian Yang was gone too, and Zaaran now found himself suspended in the starry sky... in his original body.","Zaaran was bewildered for a long moment before realizing that his connection to Kulas’ body had been forcefully severed and that he had been fooled by Tian Yang.","\"THAT FUCKING MORTAL!!!\" Zaaran erupted with rage, his fury sweeping the starry sky and extinguishing the flickering lights around him.","Meanwhile, Kulas’ consciousness slowly returned after Zaaran was removed from his body.","\"Tian Yang...\" Kulas glared at him with a stiff smile.","\"How are you feeling?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Fine... for now.\" Kulas sighed. \"I don’t know how you achieved this, but it’s only temporarily. Even now, my body refuses to listen to me.\"","\"I know...\"","A moment later, Kulas’ body started shrinking until he was the size of a human again.","Then, with stiff movements, Kulas extended his arms and gave Tian Yang a manly hug.","\"It’s a miracle that I get to have this brief moment with you. Now, kill me before he regains control and wreaks havoc in this world.\"","Kulas released Tian Yang and tilted his head, offering his neck.","Tian Yang silently nodded his head and raised his sword.","\"See you in my next life, brother.\" Kulas smiled.","Tian Yang’s arms trembled, and hesitation flashed in his eyes.","However, when he saw that Kulas’ eyes were beginning to turn crimson again, Tian Yang tightened his grip on the sword and shouted, \"Until next time, brother!\"","The next instant, a sword arc streaked through the sky, slashing across Kulas’ neck.","The cut was so swift and precise it seemed Kulas’ head remained attached, but in reality, he was decapitated.","However, Kulas didn’t immediately die because of his powerful cultivation, and Zaaran regained control the next second.","\"Don’t think you’ve won just because you destroyed this mortal’s body, you bastard!\" Zaaran roared. \"As long as his soul is unharmed, I can just create another vessel and walk this earth again! You can destroy his soul, but that will permamently remove him from this world and erase any chance of him being able to reincarnate! Moreover, I can always find another vessel to control! You will never win againgst me!\"","\"Shut up!\" Tian Yang shouted as he plunged his sword into Kulas’ heart.","\"I don’t care how long it takes. I swear I will get rid of a parasite like you!\"","With both the head and heart destroyed, Zaaran could no longer control Kulas’ body.","However, a moment later, Tian Yang could see Kulas’ soul escaping from the corpse and attempting to escape.","Many thoughts flashed inside Tian Yang’s head at that moment.","Suddenly, he retrieved a treasure from his spatial ring and used it to contain Kulas’ soul, preventing it from going anywhere.","\"Luckily, we didn’t sell all of the Immortal Clans’ treasures and kept a few useful ones to ourselves...\" Tian Yang mumbled.","\"Sorry for imprisoning you like this, Kulas, but this is neccassry. I hope for your understanding, and I will definitely free you from that parasite one day.\"","Some time later, Tian Yang returned to his world, where the others were waiting for him."]},{"number":2335,"title":"Chapter 2335: Arriving at the Holy Continent","paragraphs":["\"Tian Yang! You’re safe!\" Ren Xia leaped into his embrace the moment she noticed him entering their personal world.","Tian Yang quickly spread his arms to catch her, who immediately started kissing him.","\"What happened to Kulas?\" Ren Xia asked a moment later, her arms still wrapped around his neck.","\"I killed him... sort of...\" Tian Yang sighed.","He retrieved the treasure he used to seal Kulas’ soul and explained the situation, \"After destroying Kulas’ body, his soul attempted to escape, so I sealed it inside this treasure. If I hadn’t done so, Zaaran would’ve created another vessel for Kulas’ soul and returned to wreaking havoc again.\"","\"Does that mean a cultivator at the God Realm cannot die without their soul being destroyed? That we can replace our physical body endlessly?\" Ren Xia muttered with a dumbfounded face. \"Or is it because Kulas’ soul is being influenced by an Eternal that makes it possible?\"","Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"There’s still a lot we don’t know about the God Realm, but things should become clearer as time passes.\"","He looked around and asked, \"By the way, where’s Rouxi?\"","Ren Xia rubbed her eyes and released a soft sigh before responding, \"She went back with her family.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Did she choose to go back with them, or...\"","\"No, her father brought her back. I wanted to protest, but her injuries were more serious than I initially thought, and I was in no condition to stop them from taking her away. Jing Ruye also went back with her.\"","\"I understand.\" Tian Yang calmly nodded.","\"You’re a lot calmer than I expected you would be. What if she never returns?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"If she doesn’t return, I’ll just go to her. I have always wanted to visit the Holy Continent, anyway.\"","\"I see... What are you going to do now?\" she then asked.","\"I am going to visit Xie Mey and the others first. After that, I’ll continue my cultivation and hopefully advance to the next level.\"","\"Okay.\"","Tian Yang left the world for several months before returning and entering seclusion.","Time passed swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, a hundred years have passed since the war with the Giant Race concluded.","After the war, the world united to repair the devastation. For decades it enjoyed an unprecedented peace—until disturbances began to stir once more.","However, the disturbance lurked in the shadows, unknown to most of the world for a long time. Eventually it could no longer be contained, and it engulfed countless families across the world.","When Tian Yang emerged from his seclusion after five hundred years, he asked Ren Xia, \"Any news from Rouxi?\"","\"No, but her family’s in the spotlight again.\"","\"What is happening this time?\"","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven are trying to conquer the world,\" Ren Xia calmly responded.","\"Excuse me?\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened at her words, not daring to believe his ears for a moment.","\"I mean, they’re trying to take advantage of their position as the leader of the alliance during the war. Even though the war has ended, the Three Pillars of Heaven still want the alliance to continue with them as the leader, and with how many families and sects are involved in this alliance, it would make them the most powerful family in the world, essentially turning them into the emperor of this world,\" she elaborated.","Tian Yang rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"The Three Pillars of Heaven have always been the most powerful family in the world. But their power and influence were still limited. However, all of that would change if they had the backing of the majority of backgrounds in the world. What is the others’ reaction to this?\"","\"Well, half of them have already sided with the Three Pillars of Heaven and agreed to serve them, and that number is still growing. Even with half of them, the Three Pillars of Heaven is already powerful enough to rule this world.\"","Tian Yang then asked, \"Why would they agree to serve the Three Pillars of Heaven? Most wouldn’t agree to such a thing even if forced. Did the Three Pillars of Heaven offer them something in exchange for their loyalty?\"","\"Most likely, but they didn’t and wouldn’t reveal something like that, so the public has no way of knowing.\"","Tian Yang pondered for a moment before revealing, \"The Enlightened One, who is being influenced by an Eternal, is likely involved with this. Now that Zaaran’s invasion has been stopped, another Eternal must be trying to do the same thing.\"","\"Is there anything we can do?\" Ren Xia asked.","He shook his head.","\"Not right now.\"","\"Let’s just hope it doesn’t lead to another war...\" Ren Xia sighed.","Tian Yang proceeded to spend several years preparing for his visit to the Holy Continent.","\"I will be going to the Holy Continent now,\" he said to Ren Xia once he was prepared.","\"Are you sure you don’t want me to come with you?\"","He nodded.","\"Knowing that another Eternal is active, I don’t want you to even get close to the Holy Continent... at least until I know what we’re dealing with.\"","Ren Xia knew better than to argue with Tian Yang on this matter by now and quickly gave up on trying to convince him.","\"Be safe,\" she said right as he left the world.","After leaving, Tian Yang traveled directly to the Holy Continent—a place once off-limits but now open to virtually anyone.","\"So, this is the Holy Continent, huh? The spiritual energy in this place is ridiculously rich and dense. It’s no wonder they made this place their territory.\"","Tian Yang closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"...?\"","He opened his eyes a moment later and started looking around with a confused face.","\"What the...?\"","He began moving his limbs around as if testing them.","It took a moment, but clarity eventually hit him.","\"So, this is where the real trial begins, huh?\" Yuan muttered after regaining control of his body after reliving Tian Yang’s life for hundreds of thousands of years."]},{"number":2336,"title":"Chapter 2336: The Real Beginning of the Unique Trial","paragraphs":["After regaining control over his body, Yuan took a moment to ponder his situation and analyze the current condition of his body.","\"...\"","It didn’t take long before Yuan realized that he was unable to utilize any skills that did not belong to his current body. For example, he was unable to use God of War’s Astral Arts since it was not something Tian Yang learned. This also meant that he was not in his real body but one that was created by the trial.","’So, I have taken over Tian Yang’s body, and I am only able to use techniques that he could use...’","Once he understood this, Yuan used his divine sense to scan the Holy Continent.","’As I thought, it’s quite weak...’","Despite being at the second level of God Ascension, Tian Yang’s soul strength was nowhere near Yuan’s level while being a mere Immortal, not to mention how long Tian Yang had cultivated Heaven’s Indomitable Soul.","’Tian Yang may have been the first to refine Heaven’s Indomitable Soul, but he wasn’t the last.’","As someone who learned the most recent Heaven’s Indomitable Soul, Yuan could tell that the soul cultivation technique had been refined several more times after Tian Yang’s era, hence why his soul strength surpassed Tian Yang despite only having it for a few decades.","Some time later, Yuan made his way to the nearest—and only—city on the Holy Continent: the Heavenly City.","The Heavenly City sprawled over ten thousand miles, making it one of the largest cities in the world. It was so vast that most of its residents were cultivators, and the few mortals who lived there were wealthy merchants who could afford the mini-teleportation formations scattered throughout the city.","In this era the Holy Continent was called the Cultivators’ Paradise for its rich, abundant spiritual energy—an environment tailor-made for cultivation. But it wasn’t open to everyone, as only those who pledged allegiance to the Three Pillars of Heaven were permitted to enjoy it.","However, since there wasn’t any barrier that prevented people from entering, many cultivators would sneak onto its land to cultivate. Of course, if they were caught, they would be executed on the spot.","Upon arriving at the Heavenly City, Yuan was stopped by the guards at the gate.","\"Where is your Heavenly Medallion?\" asked one of the guards as he inspected Yuan from head to toe.","Another guard proceeded to explain, \"You’re supposed to have it on your body and visible to the naked eye at all times while you’re in the Holy Continent, or you could be mistaken as an invader and killed on the spot.\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"I don’t have one. Where can I get one?\"","The guards immediately frowned.","\"What the hell? So you’re an invader!\"","They immediately pointed their weapons at him.","Yuan calmly raised his arms and spoke, \"Was I supposed to request permission to enter this place before coming here? I wasn’t aware of that.\"","\"Identify yourself!\"","\"Yu—Tian Yang.\"","\"What? Did you just say Tian Yang?\"","The guards visibly trembled after hearing his name.","\"That’s right. You know me?\"","\"O-Of course! However, we’ll need some proof that you’re Tian Yang!\"","\"Evidence, huh?\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before releasing some of his aura.","\"T-This aura! The God Realm!\"","Once the guards recognized Yuan’s cultivation, his identity ceased to matter. With fewer than ten God Ascension cultivators in existence, each one commanded immense respect and veneration from everyone, and the Three Pillars of Heaven granted them special permission to enter the Holy Continent.","\"Please forgive us for being unable to recognize you, Senior Tian!\"","The guards immediately lowered their weapons and bodies to bow to him.","\"Please, take my Heavenly Medallion!\"","One of the guards even handed his own Heavenly Medallion to Yuan.","Yuan accepted the medallion and asked, \"Where can I find the Three Pillars of Heaven?\"","\"Normally, you’d need to send an audience request and wait in the city for your turn, which could take months if not years. With that being said, the Three Pillars of Heaven have already granted you special permission to visit their estate at your convenience,\" said one of the guards.","\"After all, you’re the hero who defeated the Giant Emperor and saved humanity.\"","Tian Yang had never announced to the world that he defeated Kulas. However, the news was still spread somehow.","\"Is that so? Then where do I go to meet them?\" Yuan then asked.","\"I can guide you there,\" said the guard who handed his own Heavenly Medallion to Yuan.","\"Alright.\"","After signing out of his post, the guard left the city and led Yuan toward the Three Pillars of Heaven.","\"If you don’t mind me asking, how did you defeat the Giant Emperor? Was there a trick to it? I heard that not even six God Realm Cultivators working together were able to hurt him, much less stop him.\"","\"I am much stronger than them. That’s all there is to it,\" Yuan calmly replied.","\"Is that so... Anyway, I am forever grateful to you for defeating the Giant Emperor. If you hadn’t stopped him, he would’ve likely pushed all of us to extinction.\"","\"...\"","The guard continued to lick Yuan’s boots for several hours until he realized that Yuan had stopped responding long ago.","Eventually, they arrived at their destination.","\"We have arrived at the Three Pillars of Heaven’s estate, the Heavenly Manor. Please wait here for a moment while I announce your presence.\"","The guard bowed to Yuan before rushing past the group of individuals waiting outside before disappearing inside.","\"...\"","Yuan gave the group a glance before ignoring them to focus on the massive estate in front of him.","’This place reeks of them...’ Yuan shook his head inwardly.","Although he may not be able to use his techniques, his senses were left untouched, so he could still sense Eternal Essence, which enveloped the entire place like a blanket.","Several minutes later, the guard returned with someone by his side—a handsome middle-aged man wearing red robes.","When the group beside Yuan saw the man, they immediately bowed.","\"We greet Patriarch Sun!\""]},{"number":2337,"title":"Chapter 2337: Sun Rouxi’s Position Within the Family","paragraphs":["\"You must be Tian Yang!\"","Patriarch Sun rushed to greet him, completely ignoring the group who greeted him first, not even bothering to give them a glance.","\"I was wondering when you would finally visit our Holy Continent! You have no idea how much I have been wanting to speak to you after that day!\"","Yuan ignored his enthusiasm and said, \"I am here to see Sun Rouxi. How is she?\"","\"My daughter? She’s currently in seclusion. If you want to see her, you’ll have to wait until she emerges.\"","\"Wait for her? That could take thousands of years.\"","\"That’s unlikely. Since she went into seclusion to finish healing her injuries and not to cultivate, it shouldn’t take too long,\" said Patriarch Sun. \"In the meantime, why don’t we have a conversation? It’s related to my daughter, too.\"","\"Alright.\"","Yuan nodded and calmly followed him away, leaving the other group speechless.","\"Who the hell was that? I have never seen anyone speaking so casually with Patriarch Sun before!\"","\"Patriarch Sun didn’t seem to mind it, either. He must be a big shot. But why don’t I recognize him?\"","\"Patriarch Sun called him Tian Yang, right? I know him.\"","Everyone there turned to the one who just spoke with anticipation.","\"He’s the one who showed up near the end of our war with the Giant Race. Apparently, he’s the one who defeated the Giant Emperor and ended the war.\"","\"What?! He’s the one who defeated the Giant Emperor—the one even six God Realm cultivators working together couldn’t defeat?!\"","The group erupted in shock upon learning Tian Yang’s identity.","Some time later, Patriarch Sun led Yuan into a private room.","After serving some tea, Patriarch Sun spoke in a sincere voice, \"Before we begin, I would like to thank you for defeating the Giant Emperor and saving our lives. If it weren’t for you... I don’t even dare to imagine the consequences of losing the war.\"","\"Un.\"","Yuan nonchalantly nodded as he sipped on the tea.","Immediately, he could sense his Celestial Qi growing stronger.","\"What do you think?\" Patriarch Sun smiled after noticing delight in Yuan’s eyes, and he proceeded to explain.","\"We only recently successfully crafted this tea. Not only does it require extremely rare ingredients, but it also takes a tremendous amount of time and effort to grow. Despite being the Patriarch of the Sun Family, this is only my second time savoring this tea.\"","\"Thank you. It was a delightful experience,\" Yuan said, gently placing his teacup down.","Patriarch Sun replied, \"I would offer you another, but convincing the others to part with even that single cup required considerable effort.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and said, \"Let’s get straight to the point. What do you want from me?\"","Patriarch Sun’s expression suddenly turned serious, and he spoke, \"Before that, I have a question for you. What is your relationship with my daughter, Sun Rouxi? This is very important for our upcoming topic, so please answer me truthfully.\"","\"...\"","After a brief moment of silence, Yuan calmly responded, \"We’re lovers.\"","He knew there was no point in lying and that there was a very good chance they were already aware of their relationship.","Patriarch Sun barely reacted to Yuan’s response, confirming his suspicions.","\"How did the two of you meet?\" Patriarch Sun continued to ask.","\"Does it really matter?\"","\"No, I am just curious.\"","\"Then you can ask Sun Rouxi herself.\"","\"Unfortunately, she’s not very fond of me. She would simply ignore me if I asked.\"","\"Is that why she ran away to the Immortal Monastery?\" Yuan inquired.","\"That... I guess you can say that.\"","After a moment of silence, Patriarch Sun continued, \"Anyway, let’s start the main topic. I don’t know how much my daughter has told you about our family, but since you have acknowledged yourself to be Sun Rouxi’s lover, you are obligated to join our family.\"","Yuan then said, \"Unfortunately, she didn’t tell me anything about her family.\"","\"Then you’ll have a lot to learn.\"","Yuan nodded. He didn’t mind joining their family since this was just a trial. He also needed to learn more about the Three Pillars of Heaven since he still lacked Tian Yang’s memories after he defeated Kulas and arrived at the Holy Continent.","\"Let’s start with Sun Rouxi, the eldest child of the Sun Family—a peerless genius whose innate comprehension allows her to create and grasp techniques that none have been able to rival thus far. A good portion of the techniques within our family were created by her, and if she didn’t create them, she was involved in their creation one way or another.\"","\"Of course, her talents don’t stop there, and she can finish incomplete techniques started by others. Furthermore, she can refine techniques without even mastering them. In terms of talent, Sun Rouxi is definitely at the top, not just within my Sun Family but the entire Three Pillars of Heaven.\"","\"Even though I am the Patriarch of the family, possessing more authority than her, Sun Rouxi’s influence throughout the three families far surpasses mine.\"","\"...\"","Yuan remained silent. Even though he was aware of Sun Rouxi’s talents, he didn’t expect her position within the Three Pillars of Heaven to be so prestigious.","’To think she made herself sound like some unimportant figure...’ Yuan shook his head inwardly.","However, after learning about Sun Rouxi’s influence, he became surprised and puzzled about her family’s lack of care during her disappearance.","Although Sun Rouxi remained hidden within Tian Yang’s world for most of the time, there was no word of her family looking for her. Given their massive influence and unlimited resources, they could’ve easily found her if they tried even slightly.","Yet, there wasn’t even a whisper about it, as if they didn’t try to look for her, which was weird considering her talents and value.","Unable to ignore his curiosity, Yuan decided to inquire.","\"Why didn’t you try looking for her when she ran away from home?\" he asked with a slightly narrowed gaze."]},{"number":2338,"title":"Chapter 2338: Heaven’s Envoy","paragraphs":["\"We’ve spent tens of thousands of years together. Yet her family seemed to have put in zero effort to find her, as if they didn’t care if she was missing or dead.\" Yuan continued in a grim voice.","\"Haaa... It’s not that we didn’t want to look for her,\" Patriarch Sun responded after releasing a deep sigh.","After a brief moment of silence, he continued, \"We wanted to look for her, but we received a prophecy from the Enlightened One.\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows and asked, \"A prophecy that tells you not to search for a missing person? What kind of nonsense is that?\"","\"It is the Will of Heaven. I have neither the authority nor the reason to question it,\" Patriarch Sun said with a solemn expression, his eyes clear and unwavering, filled with firm faith in the Enlightened One.","\"From what Rouxi told me, the Enlightened One has the ability to commune with ’Heaven’ and receive its guidance. Is that correct?\"","Patriarch Sun nodded.","\"The Enlightened One is Heaven’s envoy—a messenger sent by Heaven itself to guide us along the path to glory.\"","\"Then where was the Enlightened One during the war with the Giant Race?\" Yuan asked. \"He was absent throughout the entire conflict.\"","\"The Enlightened One does not need to act in order to be involved,\" Patriarch Sun replied calmly. \"Even inaction is the Will of Heaven. In the end, we were victorious.\"","Yuan’s eyes narrowed. \"No. We won because I stepped in. Without me, this place wouldn’t even exist anymore.\"","Patriarch Sun calmly nodded. \"That is true—you were the one who defeated the Giant Emperor. However, the Enlightened One had already foreseen it. We were unaware of this at the time, but after everything ended, he revealed the truth to us. He said that had he intervened, it would have altered our future and caused us to stray from the path of glory.\"","\"What a convenient excuse. And he’s a prophet now, too? I thought he could only speak with Heaven.\"","\"You’re mistaken. Although the Enlightened One possesses unfathomable power, he is not a prophet, as it was Heaven who foresaw everything. The Enlightened One merely received Heaven’s message.\"","\"...\"","Yuan was beginning to understand why Sun Rouxi disliked her family.","Although he could reveal the truth about the Enlightened One—and the existence behind it—to Patriarch Sun, doing so would be pointless. In fact, he would likely be dismissed as a madman.","\"I’d like to meet the Enlightened One. Would that be possible?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","Patriarch Sun shook his head and said, \"Meeting the Enlightened One is not easy. In fact, even I cannot meet him without his permission.\"","Yuan lifted an eyebrow.","\"Then how does he pass down Heaven’s Will?\"","\"The Enlightened One spends most of his time within the Celestial Chamber. If he wishes to speak with us, he will send out a scroll. Of course, if we wish to speak with him, we leave our messages in the Celestial Hall.\"","\"In that case, do you think I can write a message to him?\"","\"Of course.\"","Patriarch Sun retrieved a golden scroll from his spatial ring and placed it on the table before him.","\"You may write whatever message you wish to convey here, and I will send it to the Celestial Hall. That said, there is no fixed timeframe for when it will be read. It could be months—perhaps even years before the Enlightened One reads it.\"","Yuan silently nodded and started writing his message on the scroll with an ink brush.","A short sentence later, Yuan closed the scroll and handed it back to Patriarch Sun.","\"Now then, let’s talk about your relationship with my daughter,\" Patriarch Sun said after putting away the scroll.","\"Sun Rouxi is the eldest and most talented in our family. Although you have already proven your own capabilities by defeating the Giant Emperor, you’ll still need to receive the family’s approval before we can officially accept you into our family.\"","\"And how do I acquire said approval?\"","\"The Sun Family will hold a meeting with all elders one year from now. At the meeting, we will have a simple vote, where they either approve or disapprove of you. To be approved, you’ll need to be supported by at least half of the people there. There used to be twenty elders in the family, but after the war, we’re down to eight, so you’ll need at least approval from four of them.\"","\"In other words, I have a year to make these elders like me, huh?\" Yuan mumbled.","\"What will happen if I fail to join?\" he then asked.","\"Then your relationship with my daughter will end.\"","\"I see. Simple enough.\"","\"We will provide you with a living quarter during your one-year stay here. If you ever need anything, you may ask any of the servants around. Until the meeting, you’re still my daughter’s partner, and we will treat you like one,\" said Patriarch Sun.","\"Any questions for me before I send you to your quarter?\"","\"What am I not allowed to do during my stay?\"","\"There are only two rules you must keep in mind. One. Never approach the Celestial Hall, which leads to the Celestial Chamber. Two, do not approach or speak with the Enlightened One unless spoken to first,\" revealed Patriarch Sun in a solemn voice.","\"Failure to do so will result in your execution, even if you’re a God Realm cultivator.\"","\"Are you certain you can kill the one who defeated the Giant Emperor?\" Yuan asked, a provocative smile on his lips.","Patriarch Sun narrowed his eyes before replying calmly, \"You may have defeated the Giant Emperor, but you are still human. Moreover, as long as you remain on the Holy Continent, we hold the advantage. Had our battle with the Giant Emperor taken place here, we likely would have defeated him as well.\"","Yuan stayed silent, but the smile on his face remained.","\"Are you doubting me?\" Patriarch Sun couldn’t help but ask.","\"Of course not. After all, I am already aware of the countless powerful formations that envelop this place,\" he calmly replied."]},{"number":2339,"title":"Chapter 2339: Like a Cult","paragraphs":["\"That’s all I have for you now. If you don’t have any other questions, you may leave. I have already assigned a servant to you, and she’s waiting outside,\" said Patriarch Sun.","Yuan silently nodded and left the room shortly after.","Once outside, his servant greeted him with a polite bow, \"I will be in charge of you, Master Tian.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow after seeing the servant.","\"Jing Ruye?\" he muttered with a surprised expression.","The person before him was none other than Jing Ruye.","\"What are you doing?\" he subconsciously asked.","\"I was asked to take care of you by Patriarch Sun,\" she calmly replied.","\"Aren’t you Rouxi’s servant, though?\"","Although Sun Rouxi never treated Jing Ruye as a servant and only made her one in name to protect her, Jing Ruye’s official status within the family was only slightly above ordinary servants.","\"Yes, but Master Sun is currently in seclusion, and I am already familiar with you, so I was chosen for this job,\" she explained.","\"...\"","Jing Ruye’s unfamiliar demeanor made Yuan uneasy. When she lived with him with Sun Rouxi, she’d been carefree and friendly, like an outgoing neighbor. However, she was the opposite at this moment, acting serious and distant, as if they were complete strangers.","\"May I guide you to your living quarters now?\" Jing Ruye asked, still in a bowing position.","\"You don’t have to act so formal with me, you know?\" Yuan said.","\"Sorry, but that is not possible,\" she replied instantly, almost as if she had already anticipated he’d say such a thing to her.","\"Alright.\"","Yuan understood her position, and not wanting to trouble her, immediately dropped the matter.","\"Bring me to my room,\" he then said.","\"Yes, Master Tian.\"","Jing Ruye finally straightened her body and began leading Yuan to his living quarters, located only a few minutes away from the main household.","\"We’ve arrived.\"","\"Let’s have a chat inside, or are you not allowed to follow me inside?\" Yuan asked.","\"There is no problem with your request,\" she said.","Once they entered the building and closed the door, Jing Ruye immediately released a deep sigh.","\"What a pain in the ass,\" she muttered out loud, returning to her usual demeanor.","\"It’s good to see you again,\" Yuan said to her with a smile, acting like their initial meeting never happened.","Jing Ruye rubbed her eyes and sighed again, \"It’s only been about five hundred years since we last spoke, but it feels like an eternity. After spending so much time outside of this place, I completely forgot how suffocating this place can be.\"","Jing Ruye walked to a nearby couch and immediately collapsed onto it.","\"You have no idea how much I have suffered since returning to this place,\" she continued in a trembling voice.","Yuan took a seat beside her and asked, \"Tell me about it.\"","\"Since Sister Rouxi is the eldest and nearly untouchable in the family, she wasn’t punished for her actions. I, on the other hand, was punished for allowing her to run away, even saying things like I helped her escape. Does that even make sense? Who am I to tell her to return? It’s not like I can force her.\"","\"How were you punished?\" Yuan looked at her with a pitiful gaze.","\"They didn’t really do much to me at first because I had Sister Rouxi’s protection. However, once she entered seclusion, they started treating me like a lowly servant. Even though I am a servant, I am Sister Rouxi’s servant, so I barely did any chores, only ones related to her. But now that I am alone, they make me do everything, from washing clothes to cleaning the bathroom, chores usually done by the lowest ranked servants!\"","\"That’s it?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow. \"I was anticipating something much worse.\"","\"Do you have any idea how humiliating that is?!\" Jing Ruye snapped at him. \"I am an Immortal! I may be a servant, but I am still an Immortal cultivator! How can they make an Immortal do such mundane chores?!\"","Yuan shook his head with a smile and said, \"Alright, I get it. Now, tell me about Rouxi.\"","\"There’s really not much to say. After returning to the family, she focused on recovering, which didn’t take long. Then, she was questioned about her relationship with you. Of course, I was also questioned. She wanted to leave again, but she’d have to leave without me this time since I am under constant surveillance. She eventually gave up and entered seclusion.\"","\"Is that so...\"","\"Now, it’s your turn to explain.\" Jing Ruye then said, glaring at him.","\"I came here to see Rouxi, but I also wanted to investigate her family, specifically the one they call ’Enlightened One’,\" he said.","Jing Ruye’s eyes widened at his words, and she hastily responded, \"The Enlightened One?! Are you insane?! That’ll get you killed!\"","Before Yuan could speak, she continued, \"The Enlightened One holds unparalleled influence and authority within the Three Pillars of Heaven. If he wishes to kill someone, they will fulfill it without question or hesitation. In a way, this place is like a cult, and they all serve the Enlightened One like he is a real god.\"","\"Have you seen him before?\" Yuan asked.","\"I have. Once. However, no matter how hard I try, I cannot recall his facial features.\"","After a moment of silence, she asked, \"Why are you investigating the Enlightened One?\"","\"I just have a few questions for him, that’s all.\" Yuan shrugged.","\"I don’t know why you’re so interested in him, but I advise you to stay away from him. Almost everyone who has spoken to him became a different person afterward, almost like they’re possessed by something,\" she sighed.","\"Who are these people?\"","\"Mostly clan heads, sect leaders, and people in prestigious positions. They were all convinced to join the alliance and serve the Three Pillars of Heaven by the Enlightened One.\"","Hearing this, Yuan wondered if the Enlightened One had some sort of mind-controlling technique, which would definitely be troublesome to deal with."]},{"number":2340,"title":"Chapter 2340: Meeting the Enlightened One","paragraphs":["While Yuan spoke with Jing Ruye at his guest house, Patriarch Sun made his way to the Celestial Hall. Before entering, he opened the scroll with Yuan’s message in it and read it.","\"Ask your ’Heaven’ if it knows Zaaran...?\" Patriarch Sun tilted his head with a puzzled look on his face after reading Yuan’s message, unable to comprehend it.","’Is he looking for someone?’ he wondered inwardly.","After making sure the message didn’t contain anything malicious, Patriarch Sun entered the Celestial Hall, a massive building located on a floating island in the skies above the Holy Continent.","Upon arriving, Patriarch Sun walked down the hall until he reached the end and stood before a double door exuding divine aura and an otherworldly presence.","Without saying a word, he kowtowed on the ground and bowed to it—to the person inside.","Then, he stood up and placed Yuan’s message on the mountain of messages that were already piled up not far away.","Before leaving, Patriarch Sun bowed toward the double doors again.","As he turned and took two steps, the doors behind him slowly opened. Patriarch Sun froze, turning toward the doorway as a bright, divine light poured through, almost as if there was a sun inside the room. A moment later, a silhouette stepped out from the radiant glow.","\"Enlightened One.\" Patriarch Sun greeted him with a deep bow of reverence.","However, the Enlightened One completely ignored him and made a gesture at the mountain of messages, moving them inside his room.","A moment later, he spoke in an authoritative voice, \"How are the preparations?\"","Patriarch Sun immediately responded, \"The preparations are going smoothly with half of the families out there supporting your goal now.\"","\"In that case, proceed to the next step. I want the entire world to bow before me by the end of the year! This is Heaven’s Will!\"","\"As you wish...\"","Without another word, the Enlightened One disappeared into the light again, and Patriarch Sun left shortly after.","Inside the Celestial Chamber, the Enlightened One began reading the messages at random. Most of them prayed to him, while some prayed for blessings from Heaven.","Eventually, he reached a certain message.","\"Ask your ’Heaven’ if it knows Zaaran?\"","The Enlightened One immediately frowned upon recognizing the name Zaaran.","\"Which bastard sent me this message?!\" he exclaimed.","After a long moment of silence, the Enlightened One activated a certain communication technique.","\"Bahrah! We have an issue here! Someone is aware of your existence!\" The Enlightened One revealed to the unfathomably massive silhouette before him as the starry sky surrounded them.","\"I don’t see how that is an issue,\" said Bahrah.","\"What if they try to interfere with our plans like Zaaran did?\" The Enlightened One replied.","\"Hahaha!\" Bahrah laughed out loud. \"Zaaran? He’s too stupid to ruin my plans. In fact, I was the one to provoke him first, and he fell for it like the idiot he is.\"","\"I-Is that so...?\" The Enlightened One wore a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"This individual must be the one who stopped Zaaran’s invasion. If anything we should be thanking him for saving me some energy.\"","\"What should I do about him?\" The Enlightened One asked.","\"Nothing... No, I want you to try and recruit him. If I had someone like him under me, our plans will undoubtedly proceed much smoother.\"","\"Y-You want to recruit him?!\" The Enlightened One exclaimed in shock.","He opened his mouth only to quickly close it without uttering another word.","’Fuck! What about me? If I recruit that bastard and Bahrah favors him more than me, I could be replaced! I don’t want to risk that!’","The Enlightened One was worried that his position might be replaced, but he didn’t dare to voice his concerns out loud.","\"I... I will try,\" he said after a moment of silence, lacking the courage to reject Bahrah.","A few days later, Jing Ruye asked Yuan, \"How long do you intend on staying here?\"","\"You won’t get any approval from the elders by sitting around all day, you know.\"","\"I don’t really care about their approval,\" Yuan calmly replied.","\"What...? Then what will you do if you cannot join the family and are forced to end your relationship with Sister Rouxi?\"","\"Even if they are her family, they have no authority to dictate whether I can be with her or not.\"","\"Do you intend on fighting the Sun Family?\" Jing Ruye was speechless.","\"If I have to.\"","\"...\"","Jing Ruye went silent, dumbfounded. Just as she opened her mouth, a knock sounded at the door and interrupted her thoughts.","When she opened the door and saw who was standing outside, she hastily spoke, \"T-This servant greets the Patriarch!\"","\"Is Tian Yang here?\" Patriarch Sun asked.","\"I am.\" Yuan responded as he approached the door. \"Need something from me?\"","\"The Enlightened One has summoned you,\" he said with a solemn look on his face.","\"That was quick,\" Yuan replied with a calm smile.","\"He said this was urgent and that you needed to meet him right away.\"","\"Take me to him.\"","Patriarch Sun nodded and led him to the floating island above the Holy Continent.","\"Who is Zaaran?\" Patriarch Sun suddenly inquired.","\"So you read my message, too.\"","\"I had to ensure the contents weren’t malicious or offensive,\" he calmly explained.","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"I can tell you about Zaaran, but there is a price to pay.\"","\"What do you want for that information?\" Patriarch Sun asked, misunderstanding Yuan’s words as wanting payment for such information.","Yuan chuckled and said, \"It’s nothing like that.\"","\"Whatever the price is, I don’t care. Just tell me.\" Patriarch Sun insisted.","Yuan nodded and said, \"Zaaran is an Eternal—a God who lives beyond this world.\"","Yuan wasn’t worried that Patriarch Sun might die since he was a God Realm cultivator and had plenty of longevity to sacrifice. He also wanted to confirm if Patriarch Sun needed to sacrifice his longevity to learn this information as he did."]},{"number":2341,"title":"Chapter 2341: Meeting the Enlightened One(2)","paragraphs":["\"An Eternal...? A God who lives beyond our world?\" Patriarch Sun repeated Yuan’s words with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"That’s—\"","Just as Patriarch Sun opened his mouth to speak again, he abruptly froze, a look of excruciating pain twisting across his face.","\"Agh!\" Patriarch Sun collapsed to the ground, groaning as veins bulged across his face while he struggled to endure the pain.","Seeing this, Yuan reaffirmed that learning about the Eternals required sacrifice. However, this only made him more confused.","’Why didn’t Sun Rouxi and Ren Xia experience this?’ he wondered inwardly.","The pain disappeared a few moments later, and Patriarch Sun glared at Yuan with killing intent afterward.","\"What the hell was that?! What did you do to me?!\" he exclaimed as he jumped to his feet and grabbed Yuan by his collar.","\"That was the feeling of your longevity being forcefully sacrificed—the price for forbidden knowledge,\" Yuan calmly replied. \"Most people die just learning about their existence.\"","\"Are you insane?! Why would you reveal such information to me then?! What if I had died?!\" Patriarch Sun roared.","Yuan smiled and said, \"I told you because you asked. But don’t worry, there was pretty much zero chance that you’d die from it. After all, as a God Ascension cultivator, you have plenty of longevity.\"","\"God Ascension...? What is that?\" Patriarch Sun frowned.","\"Oh, right. You guys still call it the God Realm.\" Yuan muttered after realizing his mistake.","He proceeded to explain, \"You may know it as the God Realm, but you’re nowhere near becoming a real ’God’. There are nine levels you must ascend before you reach true godhood, hence why we call it God Ascension Realm instead of God Realm.\"","Patriarch Sun stared at Yuan with a look of disbelief.","\"Just...Just who the hell are you, and where did you acquire such profound knowledge?\" he asked in a trembling voice as his understanding of Tian Yang quickly shattered.","\"I’m from the future,\" Yuan casually joked.","\"What the hell are you—\"","Yuan suddenly interrupted, \"Let’s get moving. The Enlightened One is waiting for us, right? We shouldn’t make him wait too long.\"","Patriarch Sun could only silently nod his head and continued guiding Yuan to the Celestial Hall.","A few minutes later, they arrived at the massive manor known as the Celestial Hall.","’This place... It’s the Celestial Palace.’ Even though it was smaller and a little different, Yuan immediately recognized the place since he had gone on a slaughtering spree not too long ago in the very same place.","When they stepped inside, Yuan confirmed that the place was the Celestial Palace because it had the same design.","Soon, they arrived at the majestic double door at the end of the hall.","However, Patriarch Sun didn’t knock on the door and merely stood there in silence. This continued for a whole minute before Yuan asked out loud, \"Aren’t you going to tell him that we have arrived?\"","Patriarch Sun turned to look him in the eyes and responded with a serious face, \"We cannot disturb the Enlightened One, as he could be receiving a divination at any moment.\"","\"Are you telling me that we will have to wait here for him to come out at god-knows-when?\"","Patriarch Sun calmly nodded.","’This crazy bastard...’ Yuan sighed inwardly.","Suddenly, Patriarch Sun reached into his pocket and retrieved a communication jade slip.","After listening to the message that he’d just received, he said to Yuan, \"I have to leave for now. Do not, under any circumstances, disturb the Enlightened One while I am away.\"","\"Okay.\" Yuan obediently nodded.","After Patriarch Sun left, Yuan waited for another two whole minutes before he approached the door and, without hesitation, knocked on it.","After a few moments of stillness, the double doors abruptly opened just enough for a person to walk out, and a clear and displeased voice resounded.","\"Didn’t Patriarch Sun just tell you not to disturb me? What an impatient and rude bastard.\"","A moment later, a silhouette emerged from the divine radiance pouring through the open space, and Yuan’s eyes narrowed as he focused on its face that was completely blocked by a veil and hood.","\"I can have you executed for disturbing me, you know?\" said the Enlightened One.","Yuan shrugged and asked, \"How long did you intend on making me wait?\"","\"A few decades.\" The Enlightened One responded without hesitation.","Yuan chuckled, \"Then I made the right choice. Are you really going to execute me for it?\"","\"...\"","The Enlightened One remained silent for a moment before responding, \"No... at least not right now.\"","He turned around and disappeared inside the Celestial Chamber.","\"Follow me. We have a lot to talk about.\"","Yuan followed him into the room.","Upon entering the Celestial Chamber, Yuan found himself surrounded by flickering stars in a pitch-black background.","\"Do you know what kind of place this is?\" The Enlightened One suddenly questioned as he gazed at the void.","\"The starry sky, the world beyond our sky.\"","The Enlightened One turned to face Yuan and said, \"True, it’s a world beyond ours, but I call it the Celestial Domain, as it is owned and ruled by the Gods.\"","He continued, \"Not only does the Celestial Domain belong to them, so does this world that we live in. We are nothing more than insects in their eyes.\"","\"What are you trying to get at?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"That it’s only normal for us to obey and serve them. So, I have a proposal for you. Join me and serve my God—Bahrah!\"","Yuan sighed out loud, \"I was wondering what nonsense you were going to say, and it’s more pathetic than I anticipated.\"","\"Nonsense? Pathetic?\" The Enlightened One frowned.","\"Aren’t you serving a God as well? Otherwise, how else would you have defeated the Giant Emperor, who was supported by Zaaran?\" he asked.","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"While I have a connection with an Eternal, I wouldn’t say that I am serving him.\"","The Enlightened One fell silent at his words."]},{"number":2342,"title":"Chapter 2342: Speaking With Bahrah","paragraphs":["After a moment of silence, the Enlightened One spoke in a trembling voice, \"If you’re not serving the Eternal, then are you claiming to be on equal terms with them?\"","However, before Yuan could respond, the Enlightened One exploded with anger and roared loudly, \"Blasphemy! The Gods are above us! The only equals they have are each other!\"","Yuan shrugged.","\"I wouldn’t say we’re equals, but I am definitely not working for them, either.\"","He had an urge to say that Eternals were beneath him to see how the Enlightened One would react, but he decided not to stir up unnecessary trouble.","The Enlightened One glared at him for a good moment before speaking again, \"The God you’ve been in contact with... What is their name?\"","\"Sorry, but he told me not to reveal it to anyone, especially if they’re already working for another Eternal.\"","Of course, it was a lie, as Shura never said such a thing.","However, the Enlightened One didn’t question it and then said, \"Even if you’re in contact with another God, it doesn’t change my God’s orders to recruit you.\"","\"Oh?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this unexpected situation.","\"Your Eternal wants to recruit me? I’m listening.\"","He didn’t immediately refuse since this would help him learn more about the Eternal behind the Enlightened One.","The Enlightened One sucked his teeth after seeing Yuan’s unexpected enthusiasm.","\"I thought you didn’t want to serve the Gods?\"","\"Huh? When did I say that? I merely responded to your question—that I wasn’t serving one. I never said that I’d never serve one.\"","\"Hmph! I do not believe you.\"","\"So, when do I get to speak with your God?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Who the hell do you think you are? Do you think you can speak to my God whenever you want? Unfortunately for you, my God will speak with you when they’re ready, and you won’t be able to force your way as you did with me.\"","\"Relax. I am just asking a question. Are you always this aggressive? Or do you just dislike me for whatever reason?\" Yuan looked at him with a questioning gaze.","\"Your entire existence annoys me!\" The Enlightened One admitted. \"I don’t know why, but when I look at you, my entire being feels disgusted! Even now, I am resisting the urge to puke!\"","\"But this is our first time meeting. Or was my first impression really that bad?\" Yuan wondered out loud.","\"Anyway, if your God isn’t going to speak with me right now, I have no reason to linger, so I’ll be taking my leave.\"","\"Wait!\" The Enlightened One suddenly stopped him. \"Who said you could leave?\"","\"Do you want me to stay? I thought my existence disgusted you. If I were you, I’d want me to leave as soon as possible.\"","\"As much as I want you to get out of my sight, I still have some questions for you,\" he said.","\"I can’t say I’ll be able to answer all of your questions, but feel free to ask them.\"","\"What is your relationship with the Giant Emperor and the God behind him?\"","\"A tough question right from the get-go, huh?\" Yuan smiled.","\"He was a friend of mine. We’ve known each other long before he met the Eternal. As for the Eternal... I don’t have any relationship with him.\"","\"Then why did you kill the Giant Emperor?\"","\"Are you asking me why I saved the world from his invasion? Would you have done it if I didn’t intervene?\" Yuan asked.","The Enlightened One remained quiet for a moment before responding in a clear voice, \"Of course, I would’ve stopped him. In fact, if you had waited a day later, I would’ve already taken care of him.\"","\"And how would you have done that?\" Yuan pressed.","\"Does it even matter anymore?\" The Enlightened One shook his head, refusing to explain further.","Hearing his response, Yuan couldn’t help but laugh inwardly.","\"Anyway, how did you defeat the Giant Emperor?\" The Enlightened One continued to ask.","\"I chopped his head off.\"","\"That simple? I heard that even six God Realm cultivators working together weren’t able to penetrate his skin, much less injure him.\"","\"What can I say other than that I am simply stronger than them?\"","\"Then how—\"","The Enlightened One suddenly halted his sentence.","After a brief pause, he continued, \"My God has demanded your audience. I will now connect you to them. Don’t move.\"","The Enlightened One suddenly raised his arm and mumbled something before tapping Yuan on the forehead.","The next moment, Yuan found himself hovering before a massive entity staring down upon him from many light-years away.","\"So you’re the mortal who ruined Zaaran’s plans. You’re a lot weaker than I anticipated. Did you really defeat Zaaran’s puppet?\"","\"...\"","Yuan studied the Eternal before him with a calm gaze.","\"I see. So you’re the one supporting the Enlightened One, Bahrah.\"","\"?!?!\"","Bahrah’s eyes widened when Yuan called it by its name, even though this was their first meeting.","\"Why do you know my name? Did Zaaran tell you? Or was it the Eternal behind you?\" Bahrah asked.","Unbeknownst to Bahrah, Yuan knew its name because he’d fought it before, even putting it into a deep slumber.","Yuan ignored Bahrah’s question and continued asking, \"Where are the others?\"","\"The others? What nonsense are you spewing?\"","’I see... so he’s still working alone at this point.’","\"Never mind,\" he said out loud a moment later.","\"Answer my question, mortal. Who gave you my name? If you dare to ignore me again, I’ll erase you from existence.\"","\"It was Zaaran,\" Yuan lied with a calm face.","Bahrah narrowed his eyes at Yuan.","\"You have an odd atmosphere around you. You’re clearly mortal, yet I am getting a different feeling from you. Who is the Eternal that you serve?\"","\"I don’t serve any Eternal—at least not yet.\"","\"Then who is the Eternal supporting you?\"","\"Saaruk,\" Yuan said with a smile on his face.","\"What?! Saaruk?! I thought that bastard wasn’t interested in this place!\" Bahrah exclaimed in a surprised voice."]},{"number":2343,"title":"Chapter 2343: Bahrah’s Challenge","paragraphs":["\"That Saaruk! He’s much slyer than I expected! He makes himself look like an idiot, but he’s actually scheming behind our backs!\" Bahrah muttered.","He then focused on Yuan and spoke, \"Instead of working for Saaruk, why don’t you work for me instead? I don’t know what Saaruk promised you, but I can promise you this world and unlimited authority. I will make you its supreme ruler, second to none and above every living being to walk this earth.\"","\"That is a tempting offer, considering that Saaruk didn’t really promise me anything except some of his powers.\"","Bahrah laughed at such words and continued, \"In that case, you should definitely ditch that idiot and come work for me! In fact, it’s only a matter of time before we conquer this world—not with force like Zaaran but strategy and faith.\"","\"Is that why you’ve been forming an alliance with everyone?\"","Yuan already knew their plans but still asked anyway.","\"Indeed. This plan started long before Zaaran’s interference. Although it was a risky move, I made his puppet kill someone from the Three Pillars of Heaven, forcing Zaaran’s hands.\"","Yuan’s eyebrows twitched slightly after hearing this revelation.","’Is that why Kulas went on a rampage even though I was near him at that time? So it was this bastard’s doing...’","\"What would you have done if I never intervened?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"I have my own ways,\" said Bahrah with a mysterious smirk on its face.","\"What about the Enlightened One, then? If I am going to be second to none, that must include him, you know?\"","\"Hahaha! There’s no problem at all! He might be a little angry, but there’s nothing he can do about it!\"","\"So you’re just going to discard him like this?\" Yuan sneered. \"How am I supposed to work with someone who doesn’t hesitate to throw away their own pawn?\"","\"I am not going to discard him. He’s still useful, and there are other things he can do for me. If you’re worried that I might do the same to you, then you don’t have to worry, since you are countless times better than that kid. However, you still have to prove yourself.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before nodding, \"Alright, I’ll work with you for now. What do you want me to do?\"","\"I want you to surpass the Enlightened One’s authority within the Three Pillars of Heaven.\"","\"Surpass him? That is not going to be simple...\" Yuan muttered.","Bahrah laughed. \"I never said it would be easy. Did you really think I’d just hand everything to you? If you want his position, you’ll have to take it yourself.\"","He continued calmly, \"That said, without a handicap, it would be impossible for you. He’s amassed immense influence and faith over the years, while you’re nothing more than a stranger who appeared out of nowhere.\"","\"Ten thousand years. I will make it so that the Enlightened One cannot interfere with you for ten thousand years, so try your best to defeat him in that time.\"","\"So he’ll also be aware of our little competition?\" Yuan asked.","\"Of course.\"","\"Very well. I accept the challenge.\"","\"See you again in ten thousand years... if you’re still alive by then!\"","In the next moment, Yuan found himself back in the Celestial Chamber with the Enlightened One.","\"What did you speak to my God about?\" The Enlightened One immediately questioned.","\"You should ask him yourself.\"","\"What are you—\"","The Enlightened One suddenly halted his speech and stood there in silence, almost as if he was in a daze.","’So that’s how it looks when I am speaking with an Eternal...’ Yuan thought to himself, as this was his first time seeing someone in a conversation with one.","Moments later, the Enlightened One started to move again.","\"So you dare covet my position...\" he growled, his voice low and feral, like a threatened beast.","\"It wasn’t my idea, but your God’s, you know?\"","\"I don’t care! I will never hand my position over to someone like you!\" the Enlightened One roared as he suddenly lunged at Yuan.","Yuan stepped aside casually, causing the Enlightened One to stumble and crash to the ground.","\"...\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at him. During the fall, the Enlightened One’s veil and hood had slipped away, revealing his face.","’Celestial Emperor...’","Yuan instantly recognized his handsome face. The Enlightened One turned out to be the first Celestial Emperor.","However, Yuan wasn’t surprised in the slightest, as if he already suspected this when he couldn’t sense any cultivation from the Enlightened One.","\"I was wondering why I couldn’t sense your cultivation. To think you’re just a mere mortal...\" Yuan spoke with a cold smile.","The Enlightened One’s expression paled.","\"W-What nonsense are you spouting?! I’m merely concealing my cultivation!\" he shouted, panic seeping into his voice as he desperately tried to hide the truth.","Unfortunately for him, his lies held no weight with Yuan, who already knew the truth.","Yuan suddenly reached for his neck and dragged him off the ground and into the air.","\"I was given ten thousand years to replace you. At first, I thought it would be pretty difficult. But now... I don’t even need a day, as I can simply replace you by killing you,\" he spoke in a cold voice.","\"Y-You wouldn’t dare! If you kill me, the Three Pillars of Heaven and half of the world will turn into your enemy! At that point, you will no longer be able to rule the world!\"","Yuan fell silent for a moment before releasing him.","\"Don’t worry. It would be far too easy—and boring—to simply kill you,\" he said in a grim voice. \"I want you to watch as I slowly usurp your authority and replace you.\"","The Enlightened One glared at Yuan with teary eyes as he lay on the ground, yet there was nothing he could do, as Bahrah had forbidden him from interfering with Yuan for the next ten thousand years."]},{"number":2344,"title":"Chapter 2344: Becoming Heaven’s Envoy","paragraphs":["\"Y-You... I forbid it!\" The Enlightened One bit his lips to resist his fear and shouted at Yuan.","\"This position belongs to me! I worked nonstop for over 100,000 years to reach my current status! Who the hell are you to just appear and try take it away from me?! You don’t deserve it!\"","Yuan chuckled and replied, \"You think you deserve this position? If it weren’t for the Eternal, you wouldn’t even be alive right now, you idiot. And all you do is order people around and relay the Eternal’s message, pretending to be heaven’s envoy. If you think about it, you’ve really done nothing deserving of your position, hence why your Master wants me, someone more competent and useful, to replace you.\"","The Enlightened One’s face drained of color. Even though Yuan had yet to begin usurping his position, the mere weight of his presence was enough to make him feel threatened. Worse still, Yuan had Bahrah’s backing, while he himself was forbidden to act—forced to stand by and watch as Yuan slowly replaced him.","\"Be a good little boy and stay here. I have a lot to do.\" Yuan turned around and began making his way toward the exit.","Seeing this, the Enlightened One rushed to block the door with his own body, arms spread and everything.","\"How cute.\" Yuan chuckled before walking around him. \"There’s nothing you can do to stop me, so just sit back and enjoy whatever time you have left in that position.\"","The Enlightened One trembled.","\"No! I haven’t even achieved my dream of being the supreme ruler of this world yet! There’s no way I will let you take it from me!\"","The Enlightened One then spoke with a determined look on his face, \"I may not be able to directly interfere with you, but it’s not like there’s nothing I can do!\"","Meanwhile, Patriarch Sun returned to the Celestial Hall after dealing with his business.","\"What the...? He’s gone?\"","He was dumbfounded to find Yuan missing from the Celestial Hall.","\"Did he leave... or did he enter the Celestial Chamber to meet with the Enlightened One?\"","Patriarch Sun pondered for a moment before abandoning his latter thought, as there was no way the Enlightened One would invite someone to his chamber.","\"After all, even I have not been inside the Celestial Chamber...\" Patriarch Sun shook his head.","Just as he was about to turn around and leave in search of Yuan, the double doors swung open, and two figures emerged from the light.","Patriarch Sun’s eyes widened in disbelief as Yuan’s face came into clear view. Yet his shock did not end there. The Enlightened One stood right behind him, his veil and hood gone, his face fully exposed.","\"Your Majesty!\"","Despite his shock, Patriarch Sun subconsciously greeted the Enlightened One.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the way Patriarch Sun addressed the Enlightened One as if he were already the Celestial Emperor.","\"Your Majesty?\" Yuan looked at the Enlightened One and poked fun at him. \"Even though you have not unified the world yet?\"","\"S-Shut up!\"","Patriarch Sun lifted his head to stare at them with a bewildered expression.","\"T-Tian Yang... Y-You...\"","\"Hm?\" Yuan quickly realized why Patriarch Sun was staring at him in disbelief and smiled. \"Don’t worry, we’ve become best friends.\"","Yuan suddenly wrapped his arm around the Enlightened One’s shoulders as if they were best buddies.","\"Get your filthy hands off me, you crazy bastard!\" The Enlightened One swiftly pushed Yuan’s arm away.","\"Tian Yang! What have you done?!\" Patriarch Sun exclaimed in anger. \"Touching His Majesty is forbidden and punishable by death!\"","\"Oh? Are you going to execute me for touching you, ’Your Majesty’?\" Yuan asked the Enlightened One with a cold smile.","’Go ahead and execute me. I’ll kill you before that happens.’","Yuan suddenly spoke using voice transmission, causing the Enlightened One to tremble in fear.","\"Your Majesty!\" Patriarch Sun glared at him.","After a moment of silence, the Enlightened One spoke, \"It’s fine.\"","\"What?!\" Patriarch Sun almost couldn’t believe his ears.","\"What did I say? We’re best friends.\" Yuan chuckled. \"After all, I have also become Heaven’s Envoy after speaking with Heaven itself!\"","\"WHAT?!\" The Enlightened One and Patriarch Sun exclaimed.","’This sly bastard! I didn’t think he’d use me to turn himself into Heaven’s Envoy!’ The Enlightened One cried inwardly after realizing his mistake.","\"Why are you so surprised?\" Yuan asked the Enlightened One. \"We just finished speaking with ’Heaven’. Or are you saying that I am lying?\"","\"...\" The Enlightened One gritted his teeth.","If he were to invalidate Yuan’s claim, he’d be interfering with Yuan and denying Heaven’s Will. In other words, defying Bahrah’s orders.","\"I-It’s true...\" he spoke in a trembling voice. \"He has spoken with Heaven and received its approval...\"","\"T-This is...!\" Patriarch Sun was speechless.","Yuan couldn’t help but laugh inwardly.","’Oh, Celestial Emperor... you’re too young and naive right now, making it incredibly easy to manipulate you!’","Having spent most of his time in isolation within the Celestial Chamber and rarely interacting with others, the Enlightened One lacked real experience. Moreover, a lifetime of absolute authority had left him surrounded by a fragile wall of perceived safety. Yet that same fragility meant that once someone shattered that illusion and stepped into his personal domain as a threat, he had no idea how to respond and would panic easily.","Furthermore, Yuan had already instilled fear in the Enlightened One with a genuine threat of death, making it even harder for him to think clearly.","Yuan took advantage of this situation and spoke again, \"Not only have I received Heaven’s approval, but I have also received many divinations from Heaven that will allow me to unify the world within ten thousand years.\"","\"What?! That’s impossible!\" The Enlightened One exclaimed.","Yuan looked at him with a puzzled face and said, \"Didn’t Heaven tell you? I guess Heaven is really disappointed by your underwhelming performance, hence why it asked me to take charge.\"","\"Y-You...!\" The Enlightened One gritted his teeth and trembled in anger, but his mind was in too much of a mess to think of a proper response."]},{"number":2345,"title":"Chapter 2345: Becoming Heaven’s Envoy(2)","paragraphs":["Patriarch Sun watched Yuan and the Enlightened One with a gawking expressing, as he’d never seen anyone speaking and treating the Enlightened One like an equal.","In fact, Yuan even appeared superior in Patriarch Sun’s eyes. There was just something about him that made the Enlightened One’s presence feel weaker than usual.","\"Patriarch.\" Yuan suddenly called out to him.","\"Y-Yes?!\" Patriarch Sun hastily responded after snapping out of his daze.","\"Your Majesty...?\" he added after a brief pause.","\"Your Majesty?\" Yuan frowned. \"Do I look like an emperor to you? Just continue calling me like before.\"","\"As you wish, Senior Tian...\"","Even though Yuan had just announced his position as Heaven’s Envoy, his presence and confidence were so overwhelming that Patriarch Sun subconsciously treated him as if he were the Enlightened One.","\"Anyway, I want you to summon everyone in the family, so I can officially announce my presence to the entire family.\"","\"I will have everyone assemble at the Heavenly Assembly as soon as possible!\" Patriarch Sun acknowledged.","\"You may leave now,\" said Yuan.","\"Yes!\"","Patriarch Sun didn’t linger to ask any more questions and disappeared in the blink of an eye.","Once they were alone again, the Enlightened One cursed at Yuan, \"How dare you use me as a stepping stone, you damn bastard!\"","Yuan shrugged.","\"If you don’t want me to use you as a stepping stone, you’re free to surrender your position to me. I can even promise to let you live in peace for the rest of your life.\"","\"You expect me to surrender to a nobody like you? In your dreams!\" the Enlightened One roared, a ferocious flame burning in his eyes. \"Even if I cannot interfere with you directly, I can still continue to expand my influence! I will make sure you never defeat me, no matter how hard you try and prove my worth to God!\"","Yuan abruptly placed a hand on the Enlightened One’s head and proceeded to rub it fiercely, messing with his hair like an elder brother bullying a younger sibling.","\"Good luck with that,\" he laughed out loud as he left the Celestial Hall, leaving the Enlightened One trembling in anger.","’Seriously! Where in God’s name did such a bastard come from?!’ The Enlightened One clenched his fists and gritted his teeth at Yuan’s very existence, feeling emotions he never knew existed before—mostly anger.","After leaving, Patriarch Sun summoned every member of the three families to the Heavenly Assembly using the summoning bell—an instrument reserved only for emergencies.","The bell’s toll echoed across the Holy Continent, sending shock through everyone who heard it.","\"This sound... It’s Heaven’s Bell! Who the hell rang it?!\"","\"It wasn’t used even during our war with the Giant Race, yet it’s being used now?! What in heaven’s name happened?!\"","\"Everyone! Stop whatever you are doing and head to the Heavenly Assembly!\"","In just a few hours, tens of thousands of people from the Three Pillars of Heaven gathered at the Heavenly Assembly. Whether it was a mere servant or a high-ranking elder, everyone had to be there with no exception.","\"Patriarch Sun! Were you responsible for ringing the Heavenly Bell?!\"","A beautiful middle-aged woman questioned him.","\"Indeed, I rang the Heavenly Bell.\"","\"You’d better have a good explanation for this, Patriarch Sun!\" Another voice resounded.","\"Calm down, Patriarch Ji. Everything will be explained in a moment. However, I will not be the one speaking.\"","\"Wait a second...\" The middle-aged woman who questioned him earlier realized something and asked, \"Is this related to His Majesty, the Enlightened One?\"","The entire atmosphere changed upon hearing the Enlightened One’s name.","Patriarch Sun responded with only a silent nod.","Now that they knew the Enlightened One was involved, nobody there dared ask any more questions.","Some time later, a figure appeared on the platform beside Patriarch Sun.","\"Who the hell is that? And why is he standing there?\"","Among the thousands of people there, only a few recognized Yuan’s face, so the majority were puzzled by his random appearance.","\"Hello, everyone. My name is Tian Yang, and I was the one who called for you.\"","Yuan wasted no time and immediately introduced himself.","However, before he could say another word, someone shouted, \"Tian Yang?! Who the fuck is that?! Get out of there! His Majesty, the Enlightened One, will be here soon!\"","Many more voices followed right after, all of them cursing at Tian Yang.","Seeing this, Patriarch Sun, without a word, unleashed his cultivation base and attacked those who had just spoken, instantly killing them on the spot.","\"Patriarch Sun?!\" The Family Heads and Elders exclaimed in shock after witnessing his sudden and brutal response, especially since the first victim to speak was actually a high-ranking Elder.","\"What is the meaning of this?! Why did you kill Elder Wu?!\" Patriarch Ji demanded an answer, as Elder Wu was from his Ji Family.","\"Those who dare to interrupt and disrespect Heaven’s Envoy will be executed on the spot!\" Patriarch Sun declared.","\"WHAT!??!\"","Everyone there exclaimed in shock.","\"B-But the Enlightened One isn’t even present! And they were talking to—\"","They looked at Yuan, who stood calmly before them, faces puzzled.","\"Let me finish,\" Yuan said before continuing, \"I have spoken to Heaven and been accepted as its second Heaven’s Envoy.\"","Silence rippled throughout the crowd after his declaration as a second Heaven’s Envoy.","Someone suddenly raised his hand.","Yuan pointed at him and asked, \"What is it?\"","\"I am the patriarch of the Tian Family, Tian Liuming. I would like to ask you... How did this happen? And do you have evidence? Even if I want to believe you, it’s simply too sudden and hard to believe, especially since this is the first time many of us have even heard of you.\"","\"A good question. Allow me to explain everything from the beginning,\" said Yuan.","\"Initially, I came here to check up on Sun Rouxi, my partner. However, I was also curious about the Enlightened One, so I asked him to meet with me.\"","\"Sun Rouxi?! Your partner?!\"","The crowd was already in shock—and Yuan was only just beginning."]},{"number":2346,"title":"Chapter 2346: Convincing the Three Pillars of Heaven","paragraphs":["\"The Enlightened One, perhaps having sensed something familiar within me, agreed to meet me, even inviting me into his Celestial Chamber to chat.\" Yuan continued, sprinkling some nonsense into his truth, making it seem as if the Enlightened One already knew that he’d become Heaven’s second envoy.","\"The moment I entered the Celestial Chamber, I sensed a heavenly aura descend upon me, and that’s when I met and had a conversation with Heaven, who wanted me to be its second envoy because the Enlightened One was lacking something that I possessed.\"","\"The Enlightened One is lacking?! That’s blasphemy!\" Patriarch Ji exclaimed in disbelief. \"It’s because of His Majesty that we are able to live peacefully! His contributions to this world are endless, and he was also the first one to discover Celestial Qi!\"","Yuan calmly replied, \"I am not denying the Enlightened One’s achievements. Unfortunately, it wasn’t enough to satisfy Heaven, hence why I am here right now.\"","He narrowed his eyes slightly and continued, \"Or are you refuting Heaven’s Will?\"","\"T-That wasn’t my intention...\" Patriarch Ji swallowed nervously.","Matriarch Tian suddenly raised her hand and asked, \"Do you have any evidence to prove your claim of being Heaven’s second envoy?\"","Yuan turned to look at Patriarch Sun and said, \"Patriarch Sun is my evidence, as he was there as a witnessness.\"","Patriarch Sun nodded and revealed, \"When I was at the Celestial Hall, I watched him and the Enlightened One emerge from the Celestial Chamber together. Not only that, but the Enlightened One also treated him like an equal, even removing his hood and face veil. If you doubt my words, I am willing to swear an oath.\"","\"But that only proves he went inside the Celestial Chamber with the Enlightened One and became acquainted with each other... It, in no way, proves that he was chosen by Heaven to be its second envoy.\" Patriarch Tian said with a doubtful look on his face.","Yuan then asked, \"In that case, may I ask how the Enlightened One proved himself?\"","One of the Elders answered at once, \"His Majesty revealed countless cultivation techniques and pill recipes through Heaven’s Will—knowledge that had never existed before—propelling the cultivation world forward by leaps and bounds!\"","\"That’s it?\" Yuan asked, one eyebrow raised, clearly unimpressed.","\"H-He would also occasionally receive prophecies—visions of the future!\" the Elder hurriedly added. \"Our war with the Giant Race is one of many such examples!\"","Although Yuan could argue these claims, he decided not to expose himself as someone trying to challenge the Enlightened One for now.","And instead of refuting them, he said, \"If it’s just pill recipes and cultivation techniques, I have also received many of them from Heaven, and I am willing to share them to prove myself.\"","As someone who has lived multiple lifetimes and has hundreds of millions of years of experience, there was nobody in this world who possessed as much knowledge as him—not even close.","\"How do we know that these techniques and pill recipes are truly from Heaven? What if you created them yourself?\" Another Elder suddenly questioned. \"When the Enlightened One shared his techniques, he was not even a hundred years old, so it was impossible for him to have prepared them beforehand. You, on the other hand, had plenty of time.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan sighed and said, \"You know what? I have a better method to prove myself. Give me a moment. I will be right back.\"","Before anyone could say another word, Yuan disappeared from the platform like a ghost.","Minutes later, he returned, but he was not alone, and he’d returned with the Enlightened One by his side.","\"Y-Your Majesty!\"","Everyone there subconsciously lowered their heads the moment they realized it was him, so they were unable to see the anger on his face.","\"Enlightened One, my dear friend,\" Yuan said loudly. \"Why don’t you serve as my proof and tell everyone here that Heaven has chosen me as its second envoy?\"","’You know what will happen if you refuse, right?’ Yuan then said to him using voice transmission.","’I will cripple you in front of everyone before killing you like a pig.’","The Enlightened One began to tremble, the threat shattering his resolve as every thought of resisting Yuan vanished in an instant.","\"It... It’s true... Heaven has chosen him as its second envoy...\"","Even though he wasn’t forced to lie or anything, the Enlightened One still felt disgusted, as if he’d just stepped on shit. Yet, there was nothing he could do right now but endure it.","’Just you wait, you bastard! I will make sure to repay this humiliation a thousand-fold, no matter how long it takes!’ he cursed inwardly.","With the Enlightened One’s confirmation, any doubt about Yuan’s identity had been washed away, and he was quickly accepted as the second Heaven’s Envoy by the Three Pillars of Heaven.","Yuan dismissed everyone at the assembly but the Family Heads shortly after.","\"I know this may be too sudden for you, but it’s just as sudden for me, so I will need some time to organize myself. I’ll contact you again once I am ready,\" he said to them.","\"Take as much time as you need, Your Majesty.\"","\"You can just address me as Senior Tian. I don’t like too much formality.\"","\"I understand...\"","\"About your living quarters... we’ll prepare something more fitting for you as soon as possible,\" said Patriarch Sun.","\"There’s no need. I am satisfied with my current place.\"","\"As you wish...\"","Some time later, Yuan returned to his living quarters. When he arrived, he noticed two people standing at the doorstep.","One of them was Jing Ruye, and the other was Sun Rouxi, who had emerged from her seclusion shortly before Yuan entered the Celestial Chamber.","Yuan wasn’t surprised by her appearance since he already noticed her during the assembly.","\"It’s been a while, Rou—\"","\"I need to speak with you in private,\" Sun Rouxi suddenly interrupted, wearing a serious expression on her face.","\"Okay.\"","Without another word, they entered the building while Jing Ruye remained outside.","\"What’s wrong? Are you upset that I came here?\" Yuan asked.","However, Sun Rouxi didn’t respond. She merely stood there, silently inspecting him from head to toe.","\"Rouxi...?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows, looking confused by her actions.","After another moment of silence, Sun Rouxi spoke in a solemn voice, \"I will get straight to the point.\"","She took a deep breath before continuing, \"Who... the hell are you?\"","\"Eh?\" Yuan’s eyes widened with surprise at her unexpected question.","\"What do you mean? It’s me, Tian—\"","\"Stop right there,\" Sun Rouxi said flatly. \"You may look like Tian Yang and sound like him, and you may have convinced others, but you won’t fool me.\"","Yuan was truly bewildered by this situation.","After pondering for a bit, he spoke, \"If I am not Tian Yang, then how do I know about...\"","He proceeded to recall specific information about her and their time together—something that only the two of them would know.","Sun Rouxi gritted her teeth, glaring at him with blazing fury.","\"What the hell did you do to Tian Yang?!\" she roared. \"Did you steal his memories?!\"","Her cultivation erupted as she spoke, surging outward without restraint."]},{"number":2347,"title":"Chapter 2347: Imposter","paragraphs":["\"Calm down, Rouxi!\" Yuan shouted in a somewhat panicked voice as her overwhelming pressure descended on him like a mountain collapsing from above.","\"I never gave you permission to use my name, you damn imposter!\" Sun Rouxi snapped, her aura growing more violent and powerful.","’Seriously, what the hell is going on?!’ Yuan cried inwardly, completely bewildered and puzzled by the situation.","’Is this part of the trial?’ he couldn’t think of another reason why Sun Rouxi was acting like this.","\"I will give you one last chance! Identify yourself! And tell me what you did to Tian Yang!\" Sun Rouxi shouted as she retrieved her golden wheel, her entire being seeping with immense killing intent.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan replied, \"My name is Yuan. I may not be the Tian Yang you know, but I am definitely Tian Yang.\"","\"What bullshit is that?!\" she sneered, refusing to believe him.","This left him perplexed, as he couldn’t think of any other explanation that wouldn’t sound even more crazy.","Eventually, Yuan sighed and asked, \"How can you tell that I am not Tian Yang?\"","\"Your soul,\" she calmly replied.","\"I have never told anyone, but I had developed a technique that allows me to see another’s soul, and your soul is completely different from Tian Yang. No... It’s actually similar, but it’s too old to be Tian Yang.\"","\"My soul, huh?\" Yuan muttered.","\"Then can you tell how old my soul is?\" he then asked.","\"I cannot, but I tell that it’s old. In fact, it’s much older than anything I have seen before. Just how old are you?\"","\"If we’re only talking about the age of my soul, which has experienced several reincarnations and multiple different eras... at least a few hundred million, I guess.\"","\"Several hundred million years old?! There’s no way! I doubt this world is even that old!\" she exclaimed.","Yuan shrugged, \"I don’t know what else to tell you.\"","\"...\"","Sun Rouxi was speechless, but she eventually asked, \"What happened to Tian Yang? Is he still alive?\"","\"Well...\"","Yuan wasn’t sure how to explain further.","\"Actually—\"","Right as he opened his mouth, the entire building shook violently.","\"What the...? An earthquake?\" Sun Rouxi looked around. \"No, that shouldn’t be possible. The entire continent is protected by formations that prevent these sorts of disturbances!\"","Yuan spread his divine sense, but he couldn’t see anything out of the ordinary.","A few seconds later, the building... No, the entire world trembled again.","’Is this caused by an Eternal?’ Yuan wondered inwardly.","The shaking did not stop. In fact, it grew more frequent and violent.","Yuan turned to look at Sun Rouxi and said, \"Let’s postpone this conversation for later. Right now, we need to—\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Yuan’s vision blurred, and he found himself in a familiar place.","\"What the...?\"","He was suddenly back inside the Stairway to Heaven.","\"Tian’er, what is going on?\" he asked out loud.","In the next moment, Tian’er emerged from the void with a troubled face.","\"I apologize for interrupting your trial, Master, but we have a situation,\" she said.","\"Some troublemakers are attacking the Stairway to Heaven,\" she proceeded to explain.","\"What?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Under normal circumstances, this wouldn’t be a cause for concern,\" she said. \"But this situation is different. We’re being attacked by multiple individuals simultaneously, across several realms. Moreover, these people are wielding a power that is similar to Eternal Essence.\"","Although it was forbidden to attack the Stairway to Heaven, this wasn’t the first time someone had attempted to force their way inside. Of course, none had ever come close to succeeding.","\"At this rate, they might actually be able to force their way in,\" Tian’er said, worry etched across her face as she bit her nails.","\"Is there anything I can do?\" Yuan asked.","Tian’er shook her head and said, \"I’ll do something about it. Unfortunately, this means you’ll be unable to continue the trial, and you’ll have to return later.\"","\"That’s fine.\"","\"Then I’ll send you to ’that’ place right now.\"","\"Alright. Stay safe.\"","Tian’er snapped her fingers, creating a portal before Yuan.","Yuan had a lot of questions for Tian’er, but with how urgent she seemed, he decided to save them for next time.","\"Don’t forget about me!\" Kulas’ voice resounded as his soul appeared beside Yuan.","The next moment, Yuan stepped into the portal, disappearing from the Stairway to Heaven.","Once Kulas also entered the portal, Tian’er immediately activated the Stairway to Heaven’s defensive features, something that had never been utilized until this moment.","Meanwhile, outside the Stairway to Heaven, the troublemakers across different realms were taken by surprise when the Stairway to Heaven suddenly vanished into thin air.","\"What the? Where did it go?\"","\"Damn it! I was so close to cracking it open!\"","With the Stairway to Heaven gone, the troublemakers did not linger and quickly left the scene.","The Stairway to Heaven’s sudden disappearance was quickly noticed, and word spread like wildfire throughout the Nine Heavens, plunging all nine realms into chaos.","\"What?! The Stairway to Heaven vanished?! That’s impossible!\"","\"It’s true! I saw it with my own eyes—it was gone! And at the location where the Stairway once stood... There were corpses everywhere!\"","\"If the Stairway to Heaven is gone, how will people traverse between worlds now?\"","\"It’ll likely be impossible for the majority of people, and only those who can traverse the starry sky will be able to move between realms.\"","\"I heard from a friend that he witnessed from afar someone attacking the Stairway to Heaven right before it disappeared!\"","\"That must be why it disappeared! What kind of lunatic would attack the Stairway to Heaven—and for what reason?! It’s like burning the only bridge across a raging river!\"","\"My only concern right now is whether the Stairway to Heaven will return...\"","In just a few days, news of the Stairway to Heaven’s disappearance reached almost every single ear in the Nine Heavens.","Of course, this included the Celestial Emperor, who was just as baffled as everyone."]},{"number":2348,"title":"Chapter 2348: Stairway to Heaven’s Sudden Disappearance","paragraphs":["\"W-What did you just say? The Stairway to Heaven has vanished into thin air?\"","The Celestial Emperor glared at the messenger with a deep frown on his face.","\"When did this happen? And do we have any idea why it happened?\" he quickly asked.","\"It happened only four days ago,\" said the messenger. \"According to rumors, someone was attacking the Stairway to Heaven before its disappearance, and it wasn’t just a single individual. Apparently, there was a witness at every single realm from the First Heaven to the Ninth Heaven, implying it was a coordinated attack.\"","The messenger continued, \"There were also many casualties at the Stairway to Heaven’s location. We believe they were all killed by these individuals to keep their identity hidden. Unfortunately, we do not know of their motives at this moment.\"","The Celestial Emperor pondered for a moment before speaking out loud to himself, \"The Stairway to Heaven isn’t any ordinary treasure. It’s not the first time someone has attacked it, either. Yet, this is the first time it reacted in such a fashion, meaning that these individuals were not ordinary cultivators.\"","After a moment of silence, he gave a clear command.","\"Find out who these individuals are and their motives. With the Stairway to Heaven gone, transportation between the realms will essentially become impossible for most people, and we have no idea when the Stairway to Heaven will return—if it ever will. What a troublesome situation...\"","\"What should we do if the Stairway to Heaven never returns?\" The messenger swallowed nervously at this possibility before asking in a trembling voice.","\"We’ll have to replace it with something similar,\" he said.","\"The Stairway to Heaven was created many eras ago. Nowadays, there are master blacksmiths who are capable of creating something similar, so it’s not completely hopeless. I’ll give it a few years to return before we make a new one.\"","Some time later, the Celestial Emperor made a public announcement, reassuring the world that he would get to the bottom of the situation and replace the Stairway to Heaven if necessary.","Though the Celestial Emperor succeeded in calming the people, it did little to truly ease the situation or resolve the problem. The Stairway to Heaven was still missing, and replacing it could take decades—an unbearably long time for those living in the lower heavens.","Meanwhile, after leaving the Stairway to Heaven, Yuan found himself standing in a vast green plain. Two solitary buildings stood only several meters apart, the only structures in sight. Above him, the sky was a clear blue, and the spiritual energy in the area was unfathomably rich—so dense that it made even the Eighth Heaven’s spiritual energy seem pale by comparison.","\"This is... my personal world.\"","Yuan immediately recognized the location, as he’d spent tens of thousands of years in this place just recently.","\"This place looks exactly as I remember...\" Yuan muttered, somewhat surprised by how little had changed.","\"Anyway, let’s get to work.\"","He immediately retrieved the sword-shaped token given to him by Xiao Cangming, which was entrusted to him by the Immortal Monarch.","\"What’s that?\" Kulas asked out of curiosity.","\"The key to my storage in this place, which happens to contain countless treasures that I have gathered throughout many lifetimes. Hopefully, I already have enough materials to craft your new vessel.\"","\"Huh? Why do you need a key to a storage that’s within your personal world? It’s not like anyone can enter here.\"","\"I don’t know,\" Yuan replied with a nonchalant shrug. \"In fact, I don’t even remember where I hid the entrance to this place. Fortunately, I remember that I can access this place directly through the Stairway to Heaven.\"","\"How can you forget the entrance to your own world?\" Kulas would shake his head if he had one right now.","\"Then do you know where it’s located? You should know since your soul followed my precious incarnations around.\"","\"Nope. It’s not like I am constantly conscious during that time, as I would slumber from time to time, and you tossed me inside the Stairway to Heaven once it was completed.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Yuan entered one of the two buildings shortly after and went directly to the basement.","However, before he could even access the basement, he had to deal with the formations that protected it.","Fortunately, these formations recognized his soul and allowed him to bypass them without any issues.","\"You’ll have to wait here,\" Yuan stopped Kulas, who attempted to follow him.","\"Since these formations only recognize Ren Xia and me, your soul will be obliterated if you try to enter.\"","\"What the hell?! You should’ve told me that before you even approached this place! To think I almost died just now! Can you imagine how humiliating it would be to perish in such a fashion after surviving so many ordeals?!\" Kulas exclaimed, hastily backing away from the door to the basement.","\"Are there any more death traps in this place that I should be aware of?\" he then asked.","\"Not that I remember.\"","\"That’s not good enough! I’ll wait for you outside just in case.\" Kulas sighed as he left the house altogether.","\"What about me...?\" Yu Ning, who was residing within his Dantian, asked in a worried voice.","\"You’ll be fine.\"","Moments later, Yuan began descending the staircase to the basement. The path downward seemed endless, the steps stretching as far as the eye could see—reminiscent of the Stairway to Heaven itself.","Eventually, they reached a point where the walls vanished entirely, leaving behind nothing but a pitch-black expanse, as though they had stepped into the void. Yet despite the darkness, Yuan could still see where he was walking.","The steps suddenly began to split into multiple paths like branches on a tree, clearly trying to mislead him. However, with the sword-shaped token in his grasp, Yuan was able to discern the true path.","After what felt like an eternity, Yuan finally reached the end of the path, greeted by a lone golden door that exuded a profound radiance, illuminating the surrounding darkness."]},{"number":2349,"title":"Chapter 2349: Crafting Yu Ning’s Vessel","paragraphs":["Upon reaching the golden door, Yuan inserted the sword-shaped key into the lone keyhole. As expected, it fit perfectly.","The moment the door opened, a profound ripple swept through the darkness, transforming the void into a massive chamber filled with treasures.","The storage room was unimaginably massive, resembling a limitless space with no visible walls, filled with a sea of treasures that extended beyond sight.","\"This is... a lot more than I anticipated...\" Yuan’s eyes widened at the sight, his jaw slightly loose from shock.","\"Heavens... I’ve never seen so many treasures gathered in one place before!\" Yu Ning exclaimed, hardly daring to believe her eyes.","\"This is the first time the phrase ’sea of treasures’ truly feels appropriate.\"","There were so many treasures that they formed the very ground beneath Yuan’s feet.","\"Rather than worrying about not having enough materials, I’m now more concerned about finding them,\" Yuan sighed. \"Let’s hope it doesn’t take too long.\"","However, just as he was about to scour the storage with his divine sense, information about every single treasure abruptly flooded his mind—much like when he became the master of the Nameless Tomb and could view all of its contents through the system.","A smile immediately tugged at Yuan’s lips, and he said with enthusiasm, \"Not only will I be able to craft Kulas a new vessel, but I’ll also be able to craft yours, Yu Ning.\"","\"Eh?\"","Yu Ning’s mind blanked out for a brief moment after hearing Yuan’s words. She’s been so accustomed to and comfortable living inside his Dantian that she completely forgot about their promise.","\"Honestly, I wouldn’t mind living inside your Dantian as nothing but a soul forever,\" she chuckled.","\"That’s a little...\"","\"It’s just a joke.\"","Although he had a list of all of the treasures, Yuan still needed to choose which ones to use for their vessels, and that alone took several days.","Eventually, Yuan acquired all of the materials needed to craft not two but three vessels.","\"Can’t forget about Ji Ran,\" he mumbled as he tossed the materials into his spatial ring.","\"What are you going to do with the rest of these treasures?\" Yu Ning then asked.","\"It’s not like I can take them all with me. And even if I could, I doubt I’ll use most of them in my lifetime. If I ever need something, I can simply return here for them,\" he said.","\"That said, I’ll take a few treasures that might come in handy soon.\"","Of course, he didn’t forget about Xiao Hua and the others, selecting several treasures he believed would benefit them as well.","Once he was done, he left the storage room and retrieved the sword-shaped key.","\"Believe it or not, this is not the only stash I have,\" Yuan suddenly said. \"In fact, this is where most of the trash is kept.\"","\"Seriously?\" Yu Ning was speechless.","Some time later, Yuan returned to Kulas’ side.","\"I have the materials to craft your vessel, but I’ll need some time to master the technique I’ll be using to craft them and practice inside my head. Also, I’ll craft your vessel last since it’s going to be the most difficult out of the three.\"","\"You’re going to craft three vessels? What are you going to do with the other two?\" Kulas asked.","Yuan gave a brief explanation, telling him about Yu Ning and Ji Ran.","\"I see. Well, take your time.\"","Yuan nodded and immediately went to work.","First, he retrieved a particular technique he had acquired from the storage—a method for crafting vessels. Although he could imitate what Xiao Cangming had done when creating Xiao Hua’s vessel, that approach was outdated, and attempting to replicate such a technique carried far too much risk.","Now that he possessed a more advanced technique—one he could properly study and master—there was no reason to rely on Xiao Cangming’s method.","A few hours later—","<You have learned Karmic Vessel Creation Scripture>","<Karmic Vessel Creation Scripture>","<Rank: Supreme>","<Description: A unique technique created by the 7th Sect Leader of the Karmic Soul Sect, who was said to have crafted the perfect vessel using it.>","Although learning the technique took only a few hours, mastering it was a different story, and it took Yuan an entire week.","<Your comprehension of Karmic Vessel Creation Scripture has reached max level>","Once he had mastered the technique, Yuan began running simulations in his mind, crafting vessels within his thoughts just as he once forged treasures mentally as Tian Qiyuan, the Divine Blacksmith, before working on the real thing.","Naturally, this process took far longer than mastering the technique itself. Striving for perfection, Yuan lost track of time, and in the blink of an eye, half a year had passed.","\"Okay, I am ready.\" Yuan declared as he emerged from his training.","\"I’ll craft your vessel first, Yu Ning.\"","He immediately retrieved the necessary materials and began working with flawless precision, his movements so practiced that it was as though he had done it millions of times before.","Unlike Xiao Cangming’s method, Yuan didn’t require a cauldron. In addition to alchemical flames, he employed array symbols and intricate formations to further temper and refine the vessel.","Although the technique was far more advanced, it was also significantly more difficult to employ and demanded much more time. In the end, it took Yuan nearly two weeks to complete Yu Ning’s vessel, which took the form of a peerless marble.","\"Your new vessel is ready, Yu Ning. You’ll need to complete the rest yourself.\"","\"Okay.\"","Without hesitation, Yu Ning left his Dantian and entered her new vessel.","In the next instant, the marble trembled violently and began to expand, limbs rapidly forming as the vessel took shape.","Within moments, the fist-sized marble transformed into a peerless jadelike beauty with large breasts and round buttocks.","\"What do you think?\" Yuan asked. \"If you don’t like it, I can make you another one.\"","Yu Ning looked at him with her large emerald eyes. Then, without warning, she leaped forward with her arms wide open and wrapped him in a tight embrace.","\"I love it!\" she said, her voice brimming with joy."]},{"number":2350,"title":"Chapter 2350: Crafting Kulas a New Vessel","paragraphs":["After holding Yuan for a full minute—still completely naked—Yu Ning finally released him and said in amazement, \"I can’t believe how natural this feels. I don’t think even my original body was this comfortable.\"","\"That’s good to hear, but since it’s still new, it’ll take some time before you adjust to it and experience everything it has to offer. In the meantime, I’ll go get you some clothes...\"","Yuan quickly disappeared back inside his house and sifted through Ren Xia’s closet to acquire some clothes for Yu Ning.","When he returned outside with her clothes, Yuan noticed that Yu Ning’s cultivation had entered the God Ascension realm.","\"Look!\" she exclaimed with excitement. \"My cultivation, which had weakened to the Golden Immortal realm after spending too much time without a physical body, has returned to the God Ascension realm! And I haven’t even started cultivating yet! This vessel is truly amazing!\"","Yuan hastily handed the clothes to her and said, \"Looks like the vessel is working as intended. Anyway, put these on.\"","Yu Ning dressed herself unhurriedly, each motion subtly enhancing her beauty.","\"How do I look?\" she asked with a smile, turning in a graceful circle as her long brown hair danced in the wind.","\"So this is what it takes to receive the title Ethereal Immortal Fairy, huh?\" Yuan said with a smile.","\"I think I look even better than before,\" she chuckled.","\"Are you two done flirting? I am dying to move around with a body,\" Kulas sighed.","\"I still have one more vessel to complete before I work on yours,\" said Yuan.","Suddenly, Yu Ning lowered herself onto the ground and kneeled before Yuan.","\"What are you doing?\" he asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"I would like to pledge my loyalty to you once again,\" Yu Ning replied with her head lowered, her voice calm. Yet, if Yuan could see her face, he’d see a layer of tears in her eyes.","\"My name is Yu Ning, a Level Seven Array Master. Though my abilities may still be lacking, I ask that you allow me to serve you for the rest of my life. From this moment onward, my skills, my body, and my life all belong to you,\" Yu Ning swore with unwavering resolve.","Yuan then asked, \"Are you sure you want to follow me now? You’ve just regained your freedom after spending countless years in the Shadow Realm—without a physical body, no less. I wouldn’t mind if you took some time to enjoy your new life first. You can always find me in the future. It’s not like there is a time limit on these sorts of things, after all.\"","\"Even if you say that, I’m not sure what I want to do, and just wandering the world seems... pointless. Other than improving my skills as an Array Master, I don’t know what else to do.\"","\"Think about it for now. I’ll need at least another half a year to finish Kulas’ vessel, so you have plenty of time,\" said Yuan.","She nodded.","\"I understand.\"","Yuan immediately began working on Ji Ran’s vessel. Since he planned to make Ji Ran’s vessel similar to Yu Ning’s, he only spent a few days practicing in his mind before doing it for real.","Soon after, Ji Ran’s vessel was completed. However, since Ji Ran was not present, Yuan sealed the vessel inside a special container to preserve it. Vessels were similar to pills in nature, and if left exposed for too long, their efficacy would slowly deteriorate.","\"Finally, it’s my turn!\" Kulas laughed with excitement.","However, his excitement quickly died down after hearing Yuan’s following words.","\"Since you’re a body refiner, I’ll need to craft a vessel durable enough to withstand your cultivation technique. That won’t be easy—even for me—and the materials themselves will be difficult to work with.\"","\"So... how long do you think it’ll take?\" Kulas then asked.","\"Who knows? I’ll let you know once I practice a few times.\"","Without another word, Yuan sat down and began his mental simulations.","A few weeks later, Yuan opened his eyes and said, \"I’ll probably finish within five years.\"","\"Five years?!\" Kulas exclaimed.","Yuan frowned and said, \"I can rush the process and finish it within a year. However, are you sure you want me to half-ass your new vessel? If it breaks down unexpectedly, I won’t make another one for you.\"","\"I wasn’t trying to rush you... Take as much time as you need,\" he responded with a defeated sigh.","\"Good, then I’ll begin... with more practice.\"","Yuan closed his eyes again and returned to practicing inside his head.","Meanwhile, Yu Ning spent her time acclimating to her new vessel through exercises and ordinary martial arts. With each passing day, her amazement at the capabilities of her new body only grew.","\"Not only does this body absorb spiritual energy with incredible efficiency, but cultivation feels almost effortless,\" she muttered in amazement. \"It’s like waking up one day with brand-new talents!\"","Time slipped away unnoticed, and before Yuan realized it, three more months had passed since he started his mental practice.","\"I am going to start the real deal now,\" he suddenly announced as he stood up and retrieved the materials he needed for Kulas’ vessel.","\"About time!\"","After taking a deep breath, Yuan started working on the materials. However, preparing just one required immense focus and time, and there was a mountain of materials before him.","In the blink of an eye, two whole weeks passed, and Yuan just finished working on the first material.","Yet, he didn’t stop to take a break and immediately started on the next material.","One month... sixth months... a year...","For two whole years, Yuan moved without stopping, his speed and skills improving with every material.","In the end, it took nearly three years for Yuan to prepare all the materials. Now, he had to craft the vessel.","\"I am actually ahead of schedule,\" he said.","\"You should take a break,\" Kulas suggested.","Yuan shook his head and said, \"Unfortunately, the materials won’t wait for me, so I’ll have to continue.\""]},{"number":2351,"title":"Chapter 2351: Kulas’ Rebirth","paragraphs":["Before the prepared materials lost their effects, Yuan swiftly started the process of combining them together to craft Kulas’ vessel.","When Yuan combined the first materials, a profound ripple appeared, sweeping the entire world. As he continued combining them, the ripple grew stronger, and eventually the entire world began trembling from the immense aura emanating from the vessel.","If Kulas could swallow, he’d be swallowing nervously at this moment, his eyes glued to the process.","\"This phenomenon! It’s as if a treasure is being born!\" Yu Ning stopped her cultivation to watch, her pretty face full of awe.","One month... three months... six months...","Half a year passed in the blink of an eye. Yet, Yuan was still nowhere near finished with the vessel.","\"Hey, Kulas, I need you to enter the incomplete vessel.\"","Yuan suddenly said to him.","\"What? Now? Even though it’s still incomplete?\"","\"Hurry! I’ll explain later!\"","Hearing the urgency in Yuan’s voice, Kulas entered the incomplete vessel without hesitation, his trust in Yuan evident.","\"Wow! This feels amazing!\" Kulas’ surprised voice resounded a moment later. \"If it’s already this comfortable, I cannot imagine how much better the complete vessel will feel!\"","\"Since this vessel is incomparably more durable than the average body, I need you to start forming your shape before it’s completed, as it’d be impossible once the vessel finishes and hardens.\"","\"I understand. Then I’ll start forming my body now.\"","Soon, limbs began to sprout from the incomplete vessel, but at a far slower pace than when Yu Ning formed her body. In fact, the process was so gradual it resembled the growth of a plant, so slow that it appeared motionless even when watched for a long time.","Days passed. Then weeks. Then months.","After unceasing effort from both Yuan and Kulas, the vessel was finally finished.","\"HAHAHA! I AM FINALLY REBORN!\" Kulas bellowed, standing tall in a dominant pose as he stood completely naked, proudly displaying his perfectly refined body to the empty world.","Despite his ancient age, Kulas chose the appearance of a young man, with short golden hair, resembling how he looked when he first met Yuan. He was tall, with a lean yet slightly larger-than-average physique—a stark contrast to his days as the Giant Emperor, when his body had been as massive as a mountain and bulging with muscle.","\"Put this on,\" Yuan said as he tossed a pair of white robes at Kulas.","As Kulas adjusted his appearance, Yuan said, \"Because you remained in soul form for so long—and considering everything that happened—your entire cultivation base is gone. However, your new vessel is powerful enough to contend with Immortals on its own, so you won’t be completely helpless.\"","\"Is that so? I want to test the limits of my new body, so if you don’t mind, spar with me.\"","\"Why am I not surprised that’s the first thing you want to do after regaining a new body after countless years?\" Yuan remarked with a smile.","\"I’ve been without a body and unable to stretch for far too long, after all.\"","\"I can give you a few days to adjust to your body if you—\" Yuan had to stop his speech midway when Kulas abruptly lunged his fists at him.","Despite the sudden ambush, Yuan blocked Kulas effortlessly, even catching his fist mid-strike.","Without pause, Kulas hurled his other hand forward. Yuan caught it as well, but this blow was noticeably stronger than the first.","Kulas immediately launched himself off the ground and dropped-kicked into Yuan’s stomach.","Yuan absorbed the strike without flinching. He barely felt the impact, but the sheer force still forced him back a single step.","Kulas continued his relentless assault for several days, never once pausing to catch his breath. Yuan spent the first day on the defensive, letting Kulas grow accustomed to his new body. After that, he began to fight back.","Despite having no cultivation at all, Kulas’s strikes continued to intensify, each blow fiercer than the last, as though his power were being drawn from thin air.","\"Hahaha! This is it! I finally feel alive again!\" Kulas laughed with excitement.","A week later, Kulas finally stopped.","\"Although I am not satisfied with this little amount of warm-up, I’ll end it here,\" he said.","Yuan nodded and then asked, \"What about your cultivation technique?\"","Kulas fell silent to ponder for a moment before responding, \"I am considering training Great Mammoth Body Refinement again.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at his answer.","\"Even after everything you went through because of that technique?\"","\"It’s the strongest technique I know, and I have already mastered it. Moveover, I have no intention of giving up the path of a body refiner, either,\" he explained.","\"The Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique may be powerful, but it’s no longer the strongest technique out there. And since you already mastered it, you can simply learn and master another one.\"","Kulas pondered for another moment before nodding, \"You’re right. Since I already mastered it, there’s no reason not to try out other techniques, especially if they’re better. And if anything goes wrong, I can always just go back to my original technique.\"","Yuan then said, \"I don’t have any body refining techniques better than the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique at hand, but I’ll help you find one.\"","\"Thanks, brother.\"","Suddenly, an unfamiliar voice resounded.","\"I was wondering why this place smelled so bad despite my frequent cleaning,\" the voice said coldly. \"Turns out someone brought trash home.\"","\"Who?!\"","Both Yuan and Kulas were startled by the new voice, even shocked, as neither had been able to sense their presence until they spoke aloud. Hell, even now, they couldn’t sense them and had to follow the sound of their voice to locate them.","When they turned their heads and saw a slender figure slowly approaching them from afar, their eyes widened with disbelief.","\"Y-You! You’re still alive?!\" Kulas cried out, his voice trembling with shock.","Yuan also recognized their face instantly and swallowed nervously before muttering in a dazed voice, \"Ren Xia?\""]},{"number":2352,"title":"Chapter 2352: Indestructible Flesh Forging Scripture","paragraphs":["Yuan and Kulas watched with wide eyes as Ren Xia approached them with calm, graceful steps. She was tall and slender, her light pink hair reminiscent of cherry blossoms, her figure refined and well-proportioned, like an hourglass.","A faint frown creased Ren Xia’s beautiful face, one that rivaled even Yu Ning, renowned as one of the greatest beauties in the Nine Heavens, and she spoke, \"What’s with that reaction? You look like you’re staring at a ghost.\"","\"If you’re alive, why would it be strange for me to be alive as well?\"","Before they could respond, Ren Xia turned to look at Yuan and continued, \"For you to be surprised as well, I guess you haven’t fully recovered your memories yet, my dear.\"","\"Unfortunately, I only remember up to when I defeated Kulas during my life as Tian Yang,\" he replied with an apologetic smile.","\"Sorry.\"","Ren Xia silently stared at him for a good moment before releasing a deep sigh.","\"It’s not like this is the first time I’ve been through this,\" she then said.","\"Why don’t you just tell him?\" Kulas asked.","\"You’re just as clueless, huh?\" Ren Xia shook her head at Kulas.","She proceeded to explain, \"To keep it brief and simple, those who are powerful enough to control their own fate could alter others’ fate in unexpected ways. You know the saying, let fate take its course? I could alter that course for him if I interfere too much.\"","\"I still don’t get it.\" Kulas shook his head.","Ren Xia rubbed her eyes and sighed.","\"He will naturally recover his memories even if I don’t do anything because that’s his fate. However, if I intervene and help him remember much earlier than he was fated to, it would alter his fate.\"","Hearing this explanation, Kulas finally understood the situation. However, he still had questions.","\"I understand that it might alter his future, but is that really such a bad thing? Only the truly powerful take control of their own fate, and knowing my brother, he’s definitely strong enough to do that, so couldn’t he just fix his own fate if it goes awry?\"","\"Of course, he can. However, look at him right now. Only those who become a Cultivation God can possibly control their own fate, and he’s not even in the God Ascension Realm. Even if he has the potential to reach that level, it might already be too late by then.\"","\"For example, his fate is altered so much that he perishes before reaching Cultivation God, or something happens and prevents him from reaching that level. There are too many variables, so it’s best to avoid them altogether by being careful.\"","\"Anyway, I have said enough. If you still don’t understand it, you’re a lost cause.\"","Kulas shook his head, a bittersweet smile tugging at his lips.","\"You surviving so many eras is impressive,\" he remarked. \"But what really amazes me is how your nasty attitude managed to last just as long.\"","\"Oh? You think my attitude is nasty now? Let me show you just how nasty I can be!\"","Without warning, Ren Xia lunged at Kulas. Before he could even react, her hands had already clamped around his neck. Instinctively, he struck at her arm in an attempt to break free—but the moment his blow landed, it felt as though he had hit solid metal.","\"When did you become a body refiner?!\" he exclaimed in shock.","\"Do you have any idea how long I have been alive? With how much time I have, it’s only natural for me to try out different things!\" Ren Xia explained as she casually tossed Kulas into the air.","\"At my current level, I dare say that I have long surpassed your peak, Kulas!\"","Kulas tried to stabilize himself in the air, but he found it impossible, as Ren Xia had enveloped his body with her Celestial Qi.","\"Damn it! Why do you hate me so much?!\" Kulas cried out loud. \"I don’t remember offending you to such an extent!\"","\"Hate you? I don’t hate you,\" Ren Xia replied in a calm voice.","\"Bullshit! If you didn’t hate me, why are you always trying to argue with me?! Are you seriously that jealous of my brotherly bond with Tian Yang?! Or perhaps, you actually like me—\"","BOOM!","As if a mountain had been dropped onto him, Kulas suddenly fell from the sky and slammed into the ground without mercy.","\"I mess with you because my dear is too kind to lecture you. Despite all your foolishness in the past, he’d never once complained about your pain in the ass, and you’re taking his kindness for granted—at least that’s how it looks to me.\"","Kulas tried pushing himself off the ground, but Ren Xia’s pressure was too overbearing for someone without cultivation like him.","\"T-This pressure... You’re a Cultivation God!\" Kulas muttered with gritted teeth.","Despite his loud voice, he wasn’t actually surprised by this.","He continued, \"I know how much trouble I’ve caused you and my brother. That’s why I am going to spend the rest of this life that he granted me to repay you two... if you give me the chance!\"","Ren Xia suddenly released her pressure on him.","\"Your words mean nothing in your current state,\" she sneered. \"Forget repaying us. You can’t even protect yourself the way you are now.\"","\"T-That’s why I will train hard to—\"","Ren Xia suddenly flicked her sleeves, throwing a manual directly into Kulas’ face.","Kulas subconsciously caught the manual and read the title on the cover.","\"Indestructible Flesh Forging Scripture?\"","\"It’s one of the strongest body tempering techniques in the world right now. It was created by the Indestructible Titan, who is known as the most powerful body refiner to exist. Of course, not even the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique could compare to it.\"","Kulas stared at her, his eyes and mouth agape with shock and disbelief.","A moment of silence later, he asked, \"Did you acquire this technique specifically for—\"","\"Don’t get full of yourself.\"","Without hesitation, Ren Xia immediately denied it before he could even finish his sentence, leaving him speechless. Despite all that, Kulas was feeling nothing but delight at this moment.","\"Thank you...\" he said."]},{"number":2353,"title":"Chapter 2353: Leaving Kulas Behind","paragraphs":["\"Don’t thank me just yet,\" Ren Xia said to Kulas after hearing his appreciation.","\"What?\" Kulas raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","A sadistic grin tugged at Ren Xia’s face as she responded, \"It may be stronger than the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique, but it is also several times more difficult to cultivate. If you think you had it rough being tortured by the Immortal Clans, just wait until we start training.\"","A terrified look appeared on Kulas’ face after hearing her words, but it was not because he might have to endure unimagine pain. It was simply because he realized that he might be trained by Ren Xia.","\"Did I hear you correctly? That you’ll train with me? Hell no! I object!\" he openly opposed.","Ren Xia sneered and said, \"That wasn’t a question, so your objection is void.\"","\"Why?! It’s not like I am cultivating for the first time! Hell, I am technically older than you! I can train myself just fine!\" Kulas remained persistent.","\"You’re older than me? Don’t make me laugh,\" she sneered with disdain. \"You’ve been dead for most of your soul’s lifespan while I have lived all of mine.\"","\"And while you may be able to train yourself, you’ll progress much faster if I train you.\"","\"B-But! What about my journey with my brother?! If I train with you, does that mean I won’t be able to travel with him?! I have waited so long for this moment! You can’t take that away from me! You have no right!\" Kulas complained to their parent like a child after being told they couldn’t go out to play.","\"What?\" Ren Xia immediately frowned.","She glared at him and snapped, \"You want to travel with him at your current level? How dare you even think such a thing when you’ve just regained your body and have no cultivation at all! You’d only be a burden to him! Haven’t you already caused him enough trouble?\"","\"T-That’s...\" Kulas wanted to argue, but he found himself unable to retort, because everything Ren Xia said was true.","While he may have a powerful physique, Yuan was already fighting God Ascension-level cultivators. No matter how powerful his body is, he would never be able to clash with Celestial Qi as a mortal.","\"How long do you think it’ll take you before you reach a level where you won’t be a burden—training alone? Even with your experience, you’d need several thousand years. However, if you train with me, I can guarantee that you’ll be somewhat useful in just a few decades.\"","Hearing her words, Kulas turned to look at Yuan with a reluctant yet pondering face.","Seeing how Kulas was looking at him, Yuan realized what he wanted to say but couldn’t and sighed.","\"Kulas,\" Yuan suddenly called out to him.","\"Y-Yes?\" Kulas’ body subconsciously stiffened.","Yuan stared him in the eyes and spoke in a stern voice, \"I know what you want me to say. You want me to tell you that it’s okay to follow me—that I will be able to protect you. Unfortunately, it’s not the cultivators that I am worried about. The Eternals are aware of my return, and I have even attracted the attention of a few new ones.\"","\"No way...\" Kulas’ jaw dropped.","\"I cannot be certain that I will be able to protect myself, much less you. Therefore, you should stay here and train with Ren Xia for now,\" Yuan said.","\"Sorry, Kulas. I know you’re disappointed, but this is for the best for both of us.\"","A bitter smile tugged at Kulas’ lips, and he released a saddened sigh, \"No, I was being unreasonable to begin with, so there’s no need for you to apologize. In fact, I should be the one apologizing to you for trying to push my selfishness onto you even though I was aware that I’d only be a burden.\"","He clenched his fists and swore, \"However, I swear it will not be long! I will train my butt off and quickly follow you, my sworn brother and number one rival, Tian—Yuan!\"","\"Save that enthusiasm for later. You’ll need it,\" Ren Xia interrupted.","\"What about you? Aren’t you going to spend some time with your beloved?\" Kulas suddenly asked her. \"I bet it’s been a long time since you two met each other.\"","Ren Xia turned to look at Yuan and smiled, \"While it’s true that it’s been a while, I am satisfied with just seeing you alive and well now, dear. Let’s have a proper reunion later.\"","Yuan nodded, \"I’ll leave Kulas in your hands.\"","\"Don’t worry, I’ll discipline him properly,\" she chuckled with a beautiful smile on her face.","\"Oh, right.\"","Ren Xia suddenly turned to Yu Ning, who was minding her own business nearby.","\"What’s your name, again?\" she asked.","\"My name is Yu Ning, Senior Sword Goddess!\" Yu Ning respectfully bowed to her.","\"Oh? You know me?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"Is that so? Well, I heard what you said earlier, and I am willing to teach you, as well. If you want to serve my husband, you’ll need to pass my standards first. What do you say? Are you willing?\"","\"I-I am willing!\" Yu Ning responded after pondering for a brief second. \"However, I am an Array Master...\"","\"So am I,\" Ren Xia calmly remarked. \"In fact, I am a Level 9 Array Master.\"","\"What?! You’re a Level 9 Array Master, too?!\" Yu Ning exclaimed in shock.","Ren Xia nodded with a nonchalant face, acting like it was only normal for her.","\"In that case, I’ll be in your care, Senior Sword Goddess!\"","\"Just call me by my name.\"","\"Yes, Senior Ren!\"","Some time later, Yuan said, \"Since everything is dealt with here, I’ll be taking my leave now.\"","Ren Xia nodded, \"Take care, daring. I’ll come find you once I am done training them. We have much to talk about.\"","\"See ya later, brother!\"","\"Until next time, Young Master. Before you leave, I’d like to thank you again for saving me.\" Yu Ning said as she gave him a deep bow. \"If it weren’t for you, I’d still be rotting away in the Shadow Realm, after all.\"","Yuan nodded, and after saying his farewells, opened up a portal and disappeared into it."]},{"number":2354,"title":"Chapter 2354: Family Reunion(End of Giant Emperor Kulas Arc)","paragraphs":["After Yuan left, Ren Xia turned to face Yu Ning and said, \"Wait here for a bit. I have to take this idiot somewhere.\"","She gestured at Kulas, who stared at her with a frown.","\"You really need to fix how you address me. I was once an Emperor, you kn—\"","\"Shut up, you big idiot, and follow me.\"","Without giving him any explanation, Ren Xia turned around and began flying away.","Kulas wanted to rebel and stay behind, but something in his guts warned him that he’d regret it, so he begrudgingly followed her.","However, without any cultivation, he was unable to fly and had to travel on foot. Fortunately, his powerful physique allowed each step to propel him forward like a missile, enabling him to keep up with Ren Xia without too much difficulty.","Of course, Ren Xia could have easily carried him using her spiritual energy, but she decided to let him run instead.","Moreover, Ren Xia’s speed would occasionally speed up, forcing Kulas to put in more effort.","\"Hey! Where the hell are you taking me in this empty world?!\" Kulas asked her after running nonstop for a few hours.","\"Empty world? You speak as if you know this place at the back of your hands,\" Ren Xia sneered.","Kulas gritted his teeth and continued following her.","One hour... Six hours... Twelve hours...","In the blink of an eye, the two of them had been traveling for three days without rest. Even for someone like Kulas, he was starting to feel the fatigue.","\"You know I just regained my body after spending countless years as a soul, right? How can you make someone like me run like this? You’re much more sadistic than before!\" Kulas cried out loud.","\"Consider this part of your training. A warm-up before the real thing,\" she calmly replied before going silent again.","After another four days, an entire week since Kulas started running, he started slowing down, and eventually, came to a complete stop.","Seeing this, before Kulas could even complain, Ren Xia spoke, \"We can stop here, turn around, and return home to begin your training if that’s what you want, but you’ll regret not doing this.\"","\"...\"","Kulas silently glared at Ren Xia, who met his gaze with an uncharacteristically serious expression. He knew she loved to toy with him, but this didn’t feel like one of those times.","After a moment of silence, he took a deep breath and, without any words, started running after her again.","Ren Xia didn’t say anything either and continued to follow her route.","After nearly another week of traveling, Kulas finally noticed a change in the scenery—the faint outline of buildings rising along the horizon.","At first, he thought Ren Xia had made him run a full lap around the world and was on the verge of bursting in anger. But when he realized there were far more buildings than before, he restrained himself and even picked up his pace.","When he drew close enough to make out figures—silhouettes standing in neat rows, as if waiting for something—Kulas’s eyes widened.","’One... two... three...’","He began counting them subconsciously. And when their faces finally came into view, tears streamed down his cheeks.","\"Father!\" One of these figures cried out loud.","When that familiar voice echoed in Kulas’s mind, every trace of fatigue vanished like smoke. His speed exploded in an instant, and he shot forward like a flying sword, arriving before the group of women who were all staring at him with tearful eyes.","\"Y-You...\"","Kulas was at a loss for words. The women standing before him were none other than his own family—the ones who had chosen to leave the Giant Palace with Tian Yang before he lost control.","\"You’re all still alive...?\" he muttered in a daze, unable to believe his eyes. He had never dared to hope they had survived, and they looked exactly as he remembered, as though the passage of time did not affect them.","\"T-This is not an illusion, right? Ren Xia, I swear, if you—\"","Kulas was cut off when one of the women suddenly lunged at him, wrapping him in a tight embrace—one so firm and warm that it erased any lingering doubt that they were real.","\"Chao Shuying...\" Kulas mumbled the name of the woman hugging him, who was none other than one of his wives.","It wasn’t long before the others rushed in as well, surrounding him and pulling him into a trembling, tearful group embrace.","After enjoying their reunion, Kulas spoke, asking them in a worried voice, \"My rampage during the war didn’t affect any of you, right?\"","\"No, Zaaran’s influence couldn’t reach us in this place, so we were all unaffected,\" said Chao Shuying.","\"I see... thank the heavens...\" Kulas sighed.","He looked at them, tears streaming down his face, and spoke in a trembling voice. \"I’m sorry... I’m truly sorry for failing to protect you. I failed as a ruler, as a husband, and as a father.\"","\"Don’t shoulder all the blame alone,\" Chao Shuying said gently, cupping his tear-streaked face with her soft hand. \"Every single one of us here has failed in one way or another. What’s done is done. All we can do now is move forward—and make sure we don’t repeat our mistakes.\"","Kulas nodded, \"I swear that I will protect all of you properly this time.\"","Once they calmed down, Ren Xia descended before them and said, \"Aren’t you glad you followed me? Had you given up and returned, you would’ve left them waiting for you for even longer.\"","Kulas glared at her. \"Why didn’t you tell me we were going to meet my family? And what would’ve happened if I gave up?\"","Ren Xia shrugged as though it were none of her concern. \"Are you sure you would’ve preferred that? If I had told you earlier, you would’ve doubted me the entire way here. Besides, this wasn’t my idea—it was theirs.\"","\"And had you given up... you wouldn’t have the reunion until after you finished your training,\" she added with a cold smile."]},{"number":2355,"title":"Chapter 2355: Peak Celestial Qi Comprehension","paragraphs":["After letting Kulas spend several days with his family, Ren Xia appeared and said to him, \"Let’s go. It’s time to begin your training.\"","\"Already?! Can’t we start later? I’ve been separated from my family for so long! You cannot separate us again os quickly!\" he refuted.","Ren Xia sneered and said, \"What happened to your resolution to train as fast as possible from not long ago?\"","\"T-That’s different! I am still going to train hard! Just give me a little more—\"","\"Kulas, the longer you delay your training, the less effective your training will be,\" Ren Xia suddenly interrupted, dumbfounding him.","\"How does that work?\" he tilted his head, looking puzzled.","\"Since your vessel is still newly forged, the materials used to craft it remain active. If you train during this period, your growth will be explosive. However, once those materials begin to weaken, the effects will diminish,\" she explained.","\"What?!\"","\"Just go, my dear.\" Chao Shuying suddenly said. \"We all agreed not to interfere with your recovery, after all.\"","\"But...\" Kulas looked at her with reluctance.","\"It’s not like we’ll never see each other again. In fact, you can visit us whenever you have time.\"","Ren Xia then said, \"While it’ll be rare, there will definitely be some small breaks throughout your training.\"","After a moment of silence, Kulas sighed.","He then turned to face Ren Xia and nodded with a resolute face. \"Let’s begin my training.\"","\"Let’s get going.\"","Without another word, Ren Xia flew back in the direction of her living quarters, where Yu Ning was waiting for their return.","Since he still couldn’t fly, Kulas had to run after her again. However, he had much more enthusiasm this time. In fact, his body had already grown slightly stronger from their previous running session.","\"See you all later!\" Kulas gave his family a swift farewell before chasing after Ren Xia.","Meanwhile, after Yuan stepped through the portal and left his world behind, he found himself drifting within a tunnel of endless void for several days. Normally, teleportation was instantaneous—but for some reason, this passage was taking far longer than it should have.","As he drifted through the void, Yuan pondered his current situation.","\"It’s been a long while since I’ve traveled alone...\" he muttered.","Although Dragon Goddess Yeyou technically remained within one of his Soul Weapons, this was one of the rare times he was truly alone. Even in his previous lives, he was rarely alone.","\"Hope the others are doing fine...\"","When a few more days had passed, and he was still drifting in the tunnel, Yuan started feeling worried, and he couldn’t help but wonder if something was wrong with the teleport he took.","\"That world has several entrances and many more exits. Did I take the wrong one by accident? I should’ve asked Ren Xia before I entered it...\" he sighed out loud.","Although he could forcibly tear his way out of the tunnel using Void Manipulation, he was currently traveling through the void at light speed. If he did so, there was a high chance he would emerge somewhere in the boundless Starry Sky without any sense of direction—and becoming lost was the last thing he wanted.","With nothing else to occupy his time, Yuan decided to cultivate. Fortunately, the tunnel was overflowing with Celestial Qi.","He closed his eyes and took a deep breath before attempting to sense the Celestial Qi.","Due to regaining Tian Yang’s memories—even reliving his life—Yuan had gained the ability to sense Celestial Qi as natural as breathing.","<Your understanding of Celestial Qi has improved tremendously>","<Your understanding of Celestial Qi has improved tremendously>","<Your understanding of Celestial Qi has reached a new level>","<You have grasped the true essence of Celestial Qi and reached peak comprehension>","It took Yuan less than a day to reach the pinnacle comprehension of Celestial Qi, something that only a few since the beginning of time could achieve after countless years of cultivation.","Even though he could’ve started cultivating Celestial Qi much earlier, Yuan only started absorbing Celestial Qi once he reached peak mastery. After all, the quality and amount of Celestial Qi one could absorb greatly varied based on their understanding, so the higher one’s comprehension, the more effective their cultivation would be.","A vacuum suddenly formed around Yuan, violently drawing in the surrounding Celestial Qi like a whirlpool raging in the heart of a vast ocean.","Yet, when the Celestial Qi entered his body and then his Dantian, they did not push him closer to the God Ascension realm. Instead, it was all being consumed by the Spirit Tree dwelling within.","Realizing this, Yuan didn’t panic or mind, allowing the Spirit Tree to consume as much as it wanted.","As the Spirit Tree absorbed the Celestial Qi, its radiance grew increasingly pronounced. The entire tree began to glow in shades of blue and violet, an ethereal aurora forming and dancing around it.","Eventually, the Spirit Tree had its full with the Celestial Qi and stopped its feasting.","<The Spirit Tree trembled with excitement as a profound transformation began within it!>","<The Spirit Tree enters hibernation as it begins its evolution!>","[Progress: 1%]","Once the Spirit Tree stopped hogging all of the Celestial Qi, Yuan was finally able to cultivate properly, and very quickly, his Dantian and entire being were overflowing with refined Celestial Qi.","In just a few days, Yuan had accumulated enough Celestial Qi to breakthrough the Immortal Realm and enter the God Ascension Realm. However, there was still one issue—his physique.","\"Now... let’s see if my physique will allow me to enter the God Ascension Realm, or will it continue to restrict me in the Immortal Realm until I evolve it...\"","Yuan took a deep breath and prepared for his breakthrough.","One day... three days... five days later—","Suddenly, Yuan’s aura and pressure began to weaken, fading until they were nearly nonexistent. Then his physical body started to blur and grow transparent, as though his very existence were being erased from reality.","Yuan could feel his existence slowly fading, yet he persisted and continued his breakthrough."]},{"number":2356,"title":"Chapter 2356: Yuan’s Ascension","paragraphs":["As his existence continued to fade, Yuan felt the weight of his body completely vanish, as though he had been severed from it entirely.","Meanwhile, his consciousness—his very soul—felt as though it were drifting higher and higher, as if attempting to ascend toward the heavens themselves.","Although only seconds had passed since Yuan first felt his soul begin to ascend, to him, it felt as though tens of thousands of years had gone by, and he was still ascending.","Despite how long it felt, Yuan didn’t panic in the slightest, as he’d gone through this process more than once before.","In what felt like the blink of an eye, a million years passed, and throughout it all, Yuan felt his soul ascending without end. Then, suddenly, he sensed something in the distance—an invisible force. It was boundless, like a colossal wall stretching endlessly in every direction.","This was a phenomenon known as the Celestial Fate, something every Cultivator who has ascended to the God Ascension Realm has experienced.","’Here comes the first layer...’ Yuan thought to himself as his soul approached the invisible wall.","Before long, his soul collided with the invisible wall, pressing firmly against its boundless surface. This was the first barrier faced by all who sought ascension. Fail to cross it, and they would remain as a mere Immortal. The trial was simple in concept—yet countless cultivators had attempted it and fallen short.","As for Yuan... his soul easily slipped right through the wall without feeling any resistance at all. To him, it might as well not have existed.","After passing the first layer, Yuan’s soul continued to drift for another million years until he reached another wall.","Although passing the first layer would qualify one to enter the God Ascension Realm, that was far from the end of the journey. Beyond it lay additional layers, and with each one a cultivator bypassed, their power within the God Ascension Realm would grow increasingly stronger.","The results of this phenomenon varied greatly, shaping the very foundation of one’s celestial power. Unfortunately, it was not something that could be controlled. Most could only accept what they were granted—much like their innate talents.","However, those with exceptionally strong Soul Strength—like Yuan—possessed the ability to push themselves beyond their natural limits.","After passing the second layer with the same ease as before, Yuan continued to travel for another million years before reaching the third.","Of course, he also passed that one with ease.","Eventually, he reached the fourth... then the fifth... sixth... each layer requiring a million years to reach, or one minute in reality.","Though reality elapsed slowly, those undergoing the phenomenon experienced that million years in full, and such an immense stretch of time would inevitably erode their mental strength; hence, most stop after the second, third, or fourth layer.","Those who could reach the fifth or sixth layer were considered geniuses, and anyone who surpasses the seventh layer become powerhouses.","One minute... ten minutes... a hundred minutes passed in the real world. Yet Yuan remained within the phenomenon, his soul effortlessly bypassing one layer after another.","Thanks to his constantly active soul cultivation technique, his already formidable Soul Strength recovered faster than the phenomenon could exhaust it, so technically, he could last an eternity.","However, after the tenth layer, the time required to reach the next layer increased tenfold. Instead of one million years, it would now take ten million years to ascend further.","Therefore, Yuan had been drifting for 900 million years when he reached the 100th layer.","He had expected to pass it as effortlessly as the others. Yet the moment his soul pressed forward, it was pushed back slightly.","For the first time, there was resistance.","Yet, it wasn’t strong enough to stop him, and after some effort, Yuan pushed right through the 100th layer.","At this point, the time required to reach the next layer increased tenfold once again. To ascend to the 101st layer, Yuan would need to endure one hundred million years.","Yet despite experiencing a hundred million years within the phenomenon, only an hour would pass in reality.","One might assume that those undergoing ascension could empty their minds and enter a trance-like state to endure the passage of time. Unfortunately, they were required to remain fully conscious and focused throughout the entire ordeal.","A hundred million years... one billion years... ten billion years...","Thanks to the vast experience he had accumulated across multiple lifetimes, Yuan endured the unfathomable passage of time without losing his sanity. Even so, it was far from easy.","After nearly ninety billion years, he barely managed to pass the 999th layer.","Yet the ascent was not over. Without hesitation, Yuan set his sights on the 1,000th layer as time continued to flow.","However, even after a hundred million years had passed, Yuan had not reached the 1,000th layer.","Then a billion years passed.","Nothing.","Ten billion.","He was still drifting.","A hundred billion years later—","Yuan was beginning to think he’d reached the end.","Though that possibility was likely, he chose to continue until his mind could endure no more.","And so, time flowed on.","Two hundred billion years later, cracks began to form in his sanity.","After five hundred billion years of drifting through endless void without a single sensation to anchor him, he could feel his mind nearing its limit.","Yet somehow, he endured another five hundred billion years.","Finally, after a full trillion years had passed, Yuan—on the very brink of madness—sensed it.","The 1,000th layer.","Its presence washed over him like a bucket of cold water, instantly clearing the haze threatening to consume him.","The moment he reached the 1,000th layer, Yuan immediately attempted to push through it. However, no matter how much force he exerted, the barrier remained unmoved. He simply could not break through.","’I have no proof... but this is definitely the final layer. And I will break through it at all costs,’ Yuan declared inwardly.","With that resolve, he immediately began his second attempt."]},{"number":2357,"title":"Chapter 2357: Entering the God Ascension Realm","paragraphs":["After his first attempt failed, Yuan immediately launched a second assault on the 1,000th layer. Yet the outcome remained the same. If anything, the resistance felt even greater than before.","Realizing brute force would not suffice, Yuan chose a different approach. Stationed before the layer, he no longer needed to focus on advancing toward it, which allowed him to divert most of his attention elsewhere.","Thus, he began cultivating his soul on the spot.","Even so, he could not neglect the ascension entirely, and part of his consciousness still had to remain fixed on the 1,000th layer.","A year... a million years... a billion years...","After cultivating his soul for a billion years, Yuan launched his third attempt.","His soul drove forward with renewed strength, colliding with the 1,000th layer. For the first time, it yielded—warping under the pressure like fabric being forced outward by something beneath it.","However, after a few moments of struggle, Yuan’s soul bounced back once again, failing to breakthrough.","\"I will not leave this place until I break through—no matter how long it takes!\"","Fueled by nothing but sheer determination and stubborn resolve, Yuan resumed cultivating his soul.","Another billion years slipped by in what felt like a blink. Then ten billion. Then a hundred billion—time itself losing meaning as he persisted.","At last, after spending another trillion years cultivating his soul, Yuan made his fourth attempt.","Over that incomprehensible span of time, his Soul Strength had ascended to levels beyond measure—greater than the sum of all his past lives.","\"Breakthrough!\" Yuan roared as his soul smashed into the 1,000th layer.","The barrier, though thin, held firm for a heartbeat. Then, unable to withstand the pressure, it ruptured as Yuan’s soul shot through like a projectile tearing apart a fragile net.","\"I did it!\" Yuan shouted with excitement.","However, before he could even celebrate, Yuan sensed an indescribable presence descending upon him, forcing his full attention toward it.","What awaited beyond the 1,000th layer left Yuan utterly speechless.","In the boundless void stood a solitary silhouette. Its form was difficult to comprehend, resembling a human figure, yet distinctly not. Within its body flickered countless stars and swirling galaxies, as though the entire universe had been condensed into its frame.","This entity—this existence—exuded a presence that was both familiar and foreign. It carried the aura of an Eternal, yet there was something beyond that... something undeniably superior.","Seeing this existence, Yuan felt a subtle change within him, but he couldn’t discern what the change was.","\"Are you the Absolute—\"","The moment Yuan attempted to speak, an overwhelming force suddenly struck his soul.","His soul was violently repelled, hurled backward through the boundless void at a speed countless times faster than his ascent.","Though it had taken him more than a trillion years to reach that height, he returned to his body in the span of a heartbeat.","<You have transcended the limits of humanity and begun your ascent toward true divinity>","<You have entered the First Level of the God Ascension Realm>","The moment Yuan stepped into the God Ascension Realm, a profound ripple spread across the entire world—one that could only be perceived by those within the same realm.","Its arrival sent shockwaves through their hearts, but this was not the first time they had experienced such a ripple, as every single breakthrough into the God Ascension Realm triggered one.","But this... this ripple was on an entirely different level—unfathomably stronger than anything they had ever experienced before.","In fact, the only time they would sense something comparable was when someone reached the very peak of cultivation.","\"T-This feeling! The birth of a new Cultivation God?!\"","All around the world, experts misinterpreted Yuan’s breakthrough. The sheer magnitude of the phenomenon led them to believe that someone had just ascended to the rank of a Cultivation God.","Because of this misunderstanding, many powerful factions dispatched their forces to search for and identify the newly born Cultivation God, unaware that they were chasing nothing but a ghost.","However, unbeknownst to them, before the ripple that shook the Nine Heavens had spread, another ripple had already manifested. And it was unfathomably more powerful—so powerful that it swept across the entire universe.","Despite how powerful it was, nobody in the Nine Heavens sensed it—not even Cultivation Gods.","Yet that did not mean it went unnoticed. The Eternals who dwelled within the boundless void sensed it clearly, and it shook them more than the humans who sensed the second ripple.","When the ripple reached them, their bodies trembled uncontrollably. For many Eternals, it was the first time they had ever felt fear.","Those who had once tasted that emotion, however, needed no explanation. They instantly recognized its source.","Delight, awe, anticipation, fear, agitation, panic, dread, nervousness—an array of emotions surged through the Eternals. Yet among them all, fear and unease were the most dominant.","Of course, Yuan, the cause of all this, remained oblivious to the commotion he’d caused across the universe with his breakthrough into the God Ascension Realm.","\"How long have I been cultivating...?\" Yuan muttered to himself.","Though he had spent over two trillion years within the phenomenon, most of that experience faded upon returning to his body, as though it had all been a distant dream.","Yet one thing remained undeniable—his Soul Strength had grown tremendously, even if it was no longer as overwhelming as it had been during his ascension.","Before Yuan could gather his thoughts or examine his body, a brilliant light appeared at the end of the tunnel, its radiance cutting through and illuminating the void.","\"Ah... finally...\"","Yuan closed his eyes and embraced the light. Within moments, it enveloped his entire being.","As the gentle warmth dissolved, cool wind wrapped around him, caressing his skin like he was drifting—or perhaps falling—through the sky.","He snapped his eyes open, only to find himself plummeting from the sky toward a vast plain of crimson grass below.","A minute later, his descent ended gracefully. As soon as his feet touched the ground, he began examining his surroundings."]},{"number":2358,"title":"Chapter 2358: Deprived Crimson Valley","paragraphs":["As Yuan looked around, his gaze was met with a vast sea of crimson grass, its color disturbingly similar to dried blood. In the distance stood half-collapsed mountains, their jagged remains looming like silent witnesses to an ancient catastrophe.","The spiritual energy in the area was abundant and richer than anything he’d experienced in the Nine Heavens.","Yuan assumed he had arrived somewhere within the Nine Heavens, but his thoughts were suddenly interrupted by a sensation that made his brows knit tightly together.","It was an overwhelming foul smell—a stench so powerful that he was startled he hadn’t noticed it sooner.","\"Fuck!\" Yuan cursed aloud, instinctively pinching his nose.","The smell was so bad that Yuan felt like he had fallen into an ocean of decomposing bodies.","Although he was shaken for a moment, Yuan quickly composed himself, and that’s when he realized something.","\"This smell... It’s the same as that place... Did I—\"","Yuan’s thoughts were interrupted once again when several powerful presences suddenly emerged in the vicinity, surrounding him from every direction.","The presences were unmistakably those of God Ascension cultivators, but the killing intent radiating from them was wild and unrestrained—like rabid beasts that had not fed in ages.","\"Food! It’s food!\"","\"Hahaha! I can’t believe there’s food so deep in the Deprived Crimson Valley!\"","\"And it’s a lowly first-level False God!\"","Mere seconds after revealing their presence, three figures appeared before Yuan. Though they bore humanoid forms, they were anything but human—and Yuan recognized them instantly.","Crimson skin. Horns that protruded from their heads. And that unmistakable, foul stench they carried.","They were demons.","Not only were they demons, but they were all between the second and third level of God Ascension.","Despite facing three powerful demons, all with superior cultivation bases, Yuan remained calm, even speaking to them, \"Did you just say the Deprived Crimson Valley?\"","Instead of answering his question, they merely mocked him.","\"You don’t know where you are? Hahaha!\"","\"This idiot is so lost!\"","Suddenly, a terrifying aura exploded from Yuan, but it was neither spiritual energy nor Celestial Qi.","Instead, overwhelming Demon Sealing Aura surged outward, descending upon the three demons like a crushing tidal wave.","The demons’ movements froze in an instant, and a look of terror quickly washed over their faces.","\"T-This power!\"","\"This bastard is an Executioner!\"","\"So what?! Not only is his cultivation weaker than ours, but there’s only one of him against three of us!\"","After a brief moment of shock, the demons snapped out of their daze. Roaring in unison, they unleashed their own power and swiftly shattered the restraints binding them.","\"Oh?\" Yuan muttered with a somewhat surprised look.","Normally, Lower Demons like these crimson-skinned demons would not be able to resist his Demon Sealing Aura, regardless of their cultivation. Yet, they were able to do just that.","\"Kill him before he tries anything else!\"","The demons quickly pounced toward Yuan simultaneously.","Seeing this, Yuan merely shook his head and muttered, \"Demon Sealing Zone.\"","A small golden barrier suddenly materialized around Yuan, trapping the demons before they could even realize what had happened.","\"I can’t move my body!\"","\"What kind of technique is this?! I have never heard of anything like this before!\"","\"What’s happening to my body?! It feels like it’s stiffening!\"","\"Y-Your body! It’s turning into stone!\"","\"What?!\"","\"T-This can’t be! He’s not an Executioner, but a Sealer!\"","\"A Sealer?! That’s impossible! They should no longer exist!\"","\"How else is he turning our bodies into stone?! This phenomenon only happens when a demon is being sealed!\"","Yuan observed their noisy outburst with mild amusement. Despite being demons, they lacked the mindless madness of the Lower Demons he had faced in the past.","\"Hey!\" One of the demons suddenly called out to Yuan. \"Who the hell are you?! Are you really a Sealer?!\"","\"I will be the only one asking the questions here,\" Yuan calmly replied. \"Now, answer my question. Is this place the Deprived Crimson Valley? If the next words that come out of your mouths don’t answer my question, I’ll completely seal you.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, one of the demons responded, \"That’s right. This is the Deprived Crimson Valley—the Fourth Valley, to be exact.\"","Hearing this, Yuan rubbed his eyes and released a deep sigh.","Deprived Crimson Valley. Although he’d never visited this place, he had heard of its name before, so he knew where he’d been teleported.","However, there was one major problem.","The Deprived Crimson Valley did not exist within the Nine Heavens.","\"There’s no way...\"","The foul stench thick in the air, the crimson expanse of the Deprived Crimson Valley, and the unusual Lower Demons before him left little room for doubt.","\"Son of a bitch... How did I get teleported to the Demonic Realm?\" Yuan sighed out loud.","Even though he didn’t want to believe it, he couldn’t ignore all of the evidence before him.","He had somehow entered the Demonic Realm... a forbidden domain that the Divine Paragon had personally sealed long ago.","With the entrance to the Demonic Realm sealed, there should have been no way for anyone to enter.","And yet, he had somehow done so. Through his own world, no less.","Of course, there was a chance that the seal had been undone. However, if that were the case, he would’ve been able to sense it, as the seal was directly connected to his soul.","Though the mystery of his arrival weighed heavily on his mind, Yuan couldn’t afford to contemplate it, as he had more pressing issues at hand.","He turned to look at the demons and asked, \"You just said that Sealers no longer exist. Why did you say that?\"","\"Why? Isn’t it obvious? They were all annihilated!\"","\"Seriously. Where did an ignorant bumpkin like you come from—\"","The demon hadn’t even finished speaking when his body suddenly stiffened, then solidified into stone in an instant.","The other two demons stared at the sealed demon, their faces filled with horror."]},{"number":2359,"title":"Chapter 2359: The Demonic Realm","paragraphs":["After sealing away one of the demons, Yuan calmly asked the remaining two, \"Do you know of the name Divine Paragon?\"","\"Divine who?\"","The demons looked at him with raised eyebrows, appearing genuinely puzzled by the name.","\"...\"","’How long has passed since I came here as Tian Chenyu?’ Yuan wondered inwardly.","\"What about the Demon Sealing Clan?\" he continued to ask.","\"Those bastards? They were annihilated many billions of years ago!\"","Yuan’s eyes narrowed at this information.","\"Who is the current Supreme Ruler?\"","\"That... we cannot tell you since the Supreme Ruler has changed several times, even before we were tossed into the Deprived Crimson Valley,\" said the demon.","\"And we’ve been in here for at least a hundred million years.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment, trying to recall a certain name.","Then, he asked in a slow but clear voice, \"Do you know of a demon named Dena?\"","\"D-Dena?\"","The two demons’ expressions immediately twisted with surprise.","\"Supreme Ruler Dena! Now that’s a name I haven’t heard in forever!\" One of the demons laughed out loud.","\"You’re lucky that you uttered that name while inside the Deprived Crimson Valley, you Sealer. Had you uttered that forbidden name outside of this place, you would’ve been slaughtered on sight,\" remarked the other demon.","Their words caused Yuan’s eyebrows to raise with puzzlement.","Supreme Ruler Dena was one of the most powerful demons in the Demonic Realm, who ruled more than half of this realm when he visited as Tian Chenyu. How did such a powerful being become a forbidden subject, to the point where just uttering it would be a death sentence?","\"What happened to her?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Seriously, where did you come from to not know even common sen—\"","The demon who just spoke quickly covered his mouth after realizing his mistake.","\"W-Wait! That was by accident—\"","Without hesitation, Yuan sealed the demon.","Now, there was just one demon left.","Yuan turned to look at him, who swallowed nervously before responding, \"Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly went crazy one day and went on a rampage, burning many cities to the ground and killing countless innocent people. Because of her actions, she was branded as a ’Forsaken’ and exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley.\"","\"A Forsaken...\" Yuan muttered.","It was a term he knew all too well. Only demons who had lost their reason—those unable to control their hunger and bloodlust—were given such a title. The Deprived Crimson Valley was where these Forsaken and criminals were exiled, abandoned, and left to be forgotten.","\"So, Supreme Ruler Dena is currently in the Deprived Crimson Valley, huh?\" he mumbled out loud to himself.","The demon nodded, \"It’s been several billion years since she was exiled, but it’s not like anyone can execute that monster, so she should still be here. In the deepest part, the Final Valley, that is.\"","\"Is there anything else you want to know? If not, I’d like you to release me. I swear I won’t attack you again, and I am not a Forsaken, either.\"","Yuan glanced at him before asking, \"Why were you exiled to this place?\"","The demon suddenly fell silent as a heavy expression shaped his face. After a moment of silence, he spoke in a low voice, \"My family was starving because of my lack of capabilities, so I stole some food as a desperate measure. Turns out I stole from the wrong bastard, and he executed my entire family in front of me as punishment. I went into a frenzy after witnessing that and attacked that bastard, who turned out to be a noble.\"","\"...\"","Yuan listened in silence, his expression blank.","In the Demonic Realm, only demons existed. However, they were nothing like the bloodthirsty, cruel beings that once terrorized the Nine Heavens. The demons here were no different from ordinary humans—capable of reason, restraint, and emotion.","This was something the Divine Paragon, Tian Chenyu, had quickly realized when he first arrived in the Demonic Realm, and it had shaken him to his core.","Despite his deep-seated hatred for demons and his unwavering resolve to exterminate them all, he found himself in an unexpected dilemma after learning the truth about the demons of this realm.","\"What about those two?\" Yuan asked as his gaze darted between the two demons he’d sealed.","\"They... they’re also being punished for offending noble demons,\" he sighed.","\"Is that so?\"","Just as Yuan was about to make his move, several more powerful presences flared into existence, rapidly closing in on their location.","Sensing this, Yuan let out a quiet sigh.","\"I forgot... I need to completely mask my presence while I’m here...\"","In an instant, Yuan activated Shadow Veil, his aura vanishing as though he had never existed.","But it was too late. His position had already been locked onto, and the approaching presences continued to close in without hesitation.","Five demons appeared in just seconds, and they surrounded Yuan.","\"Food! How long has it been since I last tasted meat?!\"","Seeing this, the demon within Yuan’s Demon Sealing Aura hastily warned them, \"I wouldn’t offend him if I were you! He’s a Sealer!\"","\"Haha! Sealer?! What kind of nonsense is that? They’re long gone!\"","\"Are you fucking blind?! Look at the two stone statues beside me!\"","The demons froze when they finally noticed the sealed demons, which they initially thought were just strangely shaped rocks.","Yet, despite the evidence right before their eyes, they refused to believe it.","Even though they had no explanation for the situation before them, these new demons were starving and couldn’t care less. In the end, they all attacked Yuan.","Of course, Yuan, who was protected by the Demon Sealing Aura, instantly sealed the five of them.","After sealing the demons, Yuan calmly turned to look at the remaining demon and asked, \"Which way is it to the Final Valley?\"","The demon looked at him with a dumbfounded face.","\"The Final Valley?! Are you trying to meet Supreme Ruler Dena? That’s a death wish even for you!\" he exclaimed."]},{"number":2360,"title":"Chapter 2360: The Demonic Realm(2)","paragraphs":["\"I don’t know why you wish to meet Supreme Ruler Dena,\" the demon said, \"but I strongly advise you against it.\"","Hearing a demon caution him about danger left Yuan momentarily speechless. He was not accustomed to such conversations with their kind, even with the Divine Paragon’s memories.","\"I appreciate your concern, but I need to meet her,\" Yuan calmly said.","The demon sighed before responding, \"Alright, I’ll tell you. But can you remove my restrictions? I cannot answer you even if I want to in my current state.\"","Without a word, Yuan removed the restraints on him.","The demon did a quick arm stretch before pointing south.","\"If you travel in that direction, you will eventually arrive at the Final Valley.\"","\"How far is it from here?\" Yuan asked.","He knew the Deprived Crimson Valley was vast, but having never visited it—or paid much attention to it in his past life—he had no true understanding of just how immense it was.","\"Well, I have never gone further than the Fifth Valley, so I cannot really say. However, just going from the Fourth Valley to the Fifth Valley will take you at least several years.\"","\"Several years?!\" Yuan exclaimed in shock.","After the initial shock subsided, Yuan suddenly recalled a crucial detail about the Demonic Realm.","’Oh, right... Just like the Primal Expanse, the flow of time here differs from that of the Nine Heavens.’","In fact, time in the Demonic Realm moved far faster than in the Nine Heavens—and even the accelerated flow within the Primal Expanse paled in comparison.","’What was it again? A year in this world is only a day in the Nine Heavens?’ Yuan searched Tian Chenyu’s memories to find this information.","If the disparity in time was truly this great, Yuan no longer felt concerned about spending several years in this place.","\"How many valleys are there in the Deprived Crimson Valley?\" Yuan asked.","\"Ten in total,\" the demon replied. \"The first nine are known as the First Valley through the Ninth Valley. The Final Valley lies at the very heart of this land.\"","\"I see. Thank you for the information,\" Yuan said calmly as he began walking south.","\"W-Wait!\" the demon called out in a hesitant voice, pointing at the petrified figures. \"What about them? Are you really going to leave them like that forever? This is my first time witnessing it, but according to legend, once a demon is sealed, they remain conscious—trapped in that state for eternity.\"","\"That’s correct.\" Yuan said indifferently.\" They’re essentially buried alive for the remainder of their immortal lives. However, I didn’t permanently seal them, so they’ll return to normal after a few years.\"","\"Is that so... Thank you for sparing us...\"","\"...\"","Yuan stared at the demon for a moment before asking, \"Hey, want to come with me?\"","\"Excuse me?\" The demon’s eyes widened at Yuan’s abrupt question.","\"I still have a lot of questions about this place, and it’d be nice to have someone to talk to while I travel to the Final Valley.\"","\"Y-You might have a death wish, but I don’t want to die yet! I still need to avenge my family!\" The demon hastily refused, even though he might offend Yuan and risk being sealed.","\"I can promise you that nothing will happen to you,\" Yuan calmly said, trying to persuade him.","\"Also, how do you plan on taking revenge when you’re stuck in this place for the rest of your life?\"","\"T-That’s...\" The demon fell silent.","Once a demon is exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley, leaving is virtually impossible. Those cast here are condemned to remain for the rest of their lives. Yet with lifespans that border on eternity, their only true release is death.","In that sense, they were not so different from Yu Ning and Ji Ran, who were once trapped within the Shadow Realm, fated to wither away in isolation or consumed by other souls.","\"It’s not completely impossible to leave this place,\" the demon said, a flicker of hope in his eyes. \"I’ve heard that some exiles have managed to regain their freedom before.\"","Yuan chuckled softly. \"Perhaps a few fortunate ones were freed under special circumstances. But do you truly believe such luck will fall upon you?\"","\"...\"","The demon fell silent.","After a brief pause, Yuan added, \"Follow me. Keep me entertained, and I’ll help you leave this place.\"","The demon swallowed nervously at Yuan’s tempting offer.","\"How will you free me?\" he asked.","However, the demon’s jaw dropped when Yuan shrugged his shoulders and replied, \"I have no idea right now, but I’ll figure a way. I promise.\"","\"Seriously...?\" The demon sighed out loud.","Despite Yuan’s lousy response, the demon could not ignore the unwavering confidence in his voice. More than that, there was something about Yuan—an indescribable presence—that made him seem strangely trustworthy.","Without waiting for a reply, Yuan turned around and began walking away.","\"If you don’t wish to follow me, then don’t,\" he said over his shoulder. \"I won’t force you. You’re free to remain here for the rest of your life—clinging to a revenge that will never come.\"","When the demon heard such words, he felt something snap inside his head.","Then, without even realizing it, he started moving toward Yuan.","\"I... I will come with you!\" he declared.","\"What’s your name?\" Yuan then asked. \"I’m Yuan.\"","\"You can just call me Lev.\"","\"Let’s go, Lev. Try not to fall behind.\"","Yuan suddenly leaped into the sky. In the next instant, beautiful flames erupted around him, forming a pair of fiery wings on his back as he shot forward like a flaming meteor.","\"What the heck?!\" Lev exclaimed, stunned by Yuan’s movement technique.","But when he saw how quickly Yuan was vanishing into the horizon, he swallowed his shock and hurriedly gave chase.","Meanwhile, somewhere within the Ninth Heaven, those connected to Yuan—such as Feng Yuxiang and Xiao Hua—suddenly felt their bond with him severed.","\"This feeling... Young Master?!\"","\"Yuan?!\"","The moment their connection with Yuan was severed, Feng Yuxiang, Xiao Hua, and Lan Yingying immediately halted whatever they were doing."]},{"number":2361,"title":"Chapter 2361: Qian Chu’s Return","paragraphs":["Although they were startled when their connection with Yuan was suddenly severed, it wasn’t the first time they had experienced such a situation, so they did not immediately panic as they had before, choosing instead to calmly consider the possible reasons.","’The last time my connection with the Young Master severed like this, he was thrown into the Primal Expanse, but he should be doing the trial within the Stairway to Heaven... or did he finish?’ Feng Yuxiang pondered inwardly.","’The Stairway to Heaven disappeared not long ago and hasn’t returned since, so maybe it took the Young Master to some place that’s so far away that it severed our connection. Knowing the Young Master, he’ll most likely be fine...’","\"What’s the matter?\" Yingzi asked Feng Yuxiang after noticing that she’d abruptly stopped moving.","\"The Young Master’s trying to worry us like usual, but I won’t fall for it this time!\" Feng Yuxiang remarked with a resolute face.","\"Yuan? What happened to him?\" Yingzi asked with an intrigued face.","\"I don’t know, and there’s nothing we can really do about it now but trust in him. He definitely wouldn’t want us to worry, that I am sure.\"","\"Alright. Then let’s get back to training.\"","Meanwhile, Xiao Hua, Lingyue, and Lan Yingying had a similar conversation.","\"Knowing Yuan, he’s probably doing something crazy again,\" Xiao Hua sighed out loud.","\"Unless he’s fighting an Eternal, we don’t need to worry about him at all,\" Lan Yingying chuckled.","\"Brother Yuan will definitely be fine. Let’s focus on improving ourselves so that when he returns, we can surprise him,\" Lingyue said calmly as she flicked her arm, sending the blood coating her hands splattering onto the green grass below.","At her feet lay a massive magical beast, its enormous body motionless. Though it no longer breathed, the lingering aura of a True Immortal still clung to its corpse.","\"Un.\" Both Xiao Hua and Lan Yingying nodded.","Lan Yingying, who was in her beast form, opened her mouth and proceeded to consume the magical beast, causing her aura to soar.","At the same time, the rest of the Nine Heavens were in a wary state—particularly the Demon Sealing Clan and the Demon Sealing Grotto. In recent times, the activities of the Demon Worshippers and demons had increased at an alarming rate, swamping the Demon Sealers with work.","However, with demons having been absent for so many years, the Demon Sealers lacked real combat experience. It didn’t take long for them to realize how much they had declined—needing large groups just to handle a single Lower Demon.","Thankfully, the Demon Sealing Grotto wasn’t as helpless. Founded by a previous generation of formidable Demon Sealers with stricter requirements, it had a far stronger foundation. Moreover, under Yan Hara’s guidance, their strength had only continued to grow.","Somewhere in the Nine Heavens, a certain figure sat before an army of demons.","’It’s been over twenty years, but I haven’t heard a peep from that bastard since then... Did he forget about our deal... or is he up to something?’","Qian Chu wondered to himself as he gazed at the three Demon Sealing Treasures before him.","’Well, it doesn’t matter. The Demon Sealing Treasures are already in my possession, and it will only be a matter of time before I reopen the Demonic Realm!’","\"Master!\" A demon suddenly approached Qian Chu and bowed before him.","\"What is it?\"","\"Our plans to weaken the Demon Sealing Clan are not proceeding smoothly. Although most of their Demon Sealers are weak, they have a few exceptionally powerful ones, especially that woman named Yan Hara, who received the Divine Paragon’s legacy.\"","\"Yan Hara, huh?\" Qian Chu’s gaze narrowed at the Demon Sealing Flag, recalling the incident where it saved her on its own accord.","\"I don’t know how she acquired the Divine Paragon’s legacy, but she won’t be enough to stop us.\"","Qian Chu stood up and said, \"Anyways, it’s about time that I returned to the Demon Sealing Clan. As for Yan Hara... I’ll deal with her myself.\"","He turned to face the army of demons and said, \"Continue weakening the Demon Sealing Clan and the Demon Sealing Grotto as planned. We will open the Demonic Realm within the next ten years!\"","\"Yes, Master!\" The army of demons roared with excitement.","Meanwhile, within the Demon Sealing Clan, Yan Hara continued expanding her influence.","The surge in demonic activity provided her with ample opportunity to display her abilities. Time and again, she stepped forward to save the lives of fellow Demon Sealers, causing her reputation—and authority—to soar. Qian Chu’s prolonged absence only further advanced her ambitions.","Unfortunately for her, seizing his position was far from simple. Qian Chu had spent thousands of years consolidating his authority within the clan, and over that time, he had planted numerous loyalists and spies throughout its ranks.","\"Senior Yan! Did you hear? The Clan Leader, Qian Chu, has announced his return to the Demon Sealing Clan and will return by the end of the month!\"","Yan Hara nodded with a serious expression on her face. Although she was nervous about Qian Chu’s return, she expected it to happen eventually.","\"Is it finally time for us to clash?\" she muttered.","Despite her immense progress within the Demon Sealing Clan, she realized that unless she defeated Qian Chu, she would never claim his position as the Clan Leader.","After a moment of silence, Yan Hara faced the group of Demon Sealers before her and declared, \"The time to kick Qian Chu, the traitor, off his throne is near. Have all of our Elite Demon Sealers and above return to prepare for the battle.\"","\"Yes!\"","As the Demon Sealers left, leaving Yan Hara alone, she lifted her head and stared at the sky with a dazed face and mumbled, \"Where are you... Yuan?\"","Back at the Deprived Crimson Valley, Yuan and Lev had been traveling for nearly four years without rest.","\"I can see it! The Fifth Valley is just ahead!\" Lev exclaimed when he saw a certain mountain on the horizon."]},{"number":2362,"title":"Chapter 2362: Entering the Fifth Valley","paragraphs":["\"We’ll arrive at the Fifth Valley after we pass that mountain range,\" Lev commented shortly after seeing it.","\"To think it took four years just to reach the Fifth Valley. This place is a little too big,\" Yuan sighed out loud.","\"Considering how many have been exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley, it’s actually beneficial for those of us in here that this place is so vast. Otherwise, we’d be constantly fighting for territory,\" said Lev.","\"That being said, since we’re all Immortal, we won’t die of natural causes, so the population of exiles will continue to grow for an eternity. Sooner or later, we’ll have to fight, whether we want to or not. Food is already scarce as it is, after all.\"","\"...\"","Since demons were immortal by nature, and every being in the Demonic Realm was a demon, the only way to reduce their population was through killing one another.","And because of that very nature, they required an immense amount of energy to sustain themselves—whether by devouring magical beasts or... other demons.","While they won’t die if they don’t eat, it would mess with their mental stability or, in the worst case, cause them to lose control, thus turning them into a Forsaken.","\"Before we enter the Fifth Valley, I must warn you about something,\" Lev suddenly said as they closed in on the mountain range.","\"We haven’t been attacked so far because I am familiar with pretty much everyone in the Fourth Valley, and since your presence is nonexistent, they have no reason to approach us. However, things will be different in the Fifth Valley. Not only are the Exiles there more powerful than me, but there’s a high chance they’ll attack us.\"","\"And before you ask, no, I cannot conceal my presence as perfectly as you.\"","\"Don’t worry about it,\" Yuan calmly responded. \"If we are attacked, I will deal with it.\"","\"I don’t mean to be rude, but where is your confidence coming from? You’re just a first-level False God. The Exiles dwelling within the Fifth Valley are between the fourth and fifth levels. Are Sealers really that powerful—that you can ignore the differences in cultivation?\"","In the Demonic Realm, cultivators at the God Ascension level are called False Gods.","\"Well, what do you know about Sealers?\" Yuan questioned.","\"I know that they were a powerful force that existed for a short period when Supreme Ruler Dena was still in power, and that they have a special ability that allows them to seal others. Unfortunately, that’s all I know since information on them is restricted. In fact, it’s forbidden to talk about them outside of this place.\"","\"Again with that...\" Yuan shook his head, silently wondering who was trying so hard to control such information.","Yuan couldn’t help but recall his previous visit to the Demonic Realm, back when he was Tian Chengyu.","His first impression had been dreadful, largely due to the hatred he once harbored toward demons.","However, over time, the situation gradually improved, and he even befriended many demons. Among them was Supreme Ruler Dena, one of the three supreme rulers who governed the entire Demonic Realm.","\"If you don’t mind me asking, what do you intend to do after meeting Supreme Ruler Dena? Since she’s now a Forsaken, I doubt you’ll even be able to have a proper conversation.\"","Yuan casually shrugged.","\"I’ll figure it out once I meet her.\"","Lev was left speechless. He couldn’t believe how careless Yuan was being about meeting one of the most dangerous entities in their world.","A few days later, they crossed the mountain range and officially entered the Fifth Valley.","And not even an hour into the Fifth Valley, Yuan and Lev were attacked by a fourth-level False God Lower Demon.","\"A first-level and second-level False God dares to enter the Fifth Valley?! You’re only begging me to eat you!\"","\"A Forsaken!\" Lev exclaimed.","\"Is that so?\"","Hearing this, Yuan retrieved the Demon Devouring Sword from his spatial ring and, without hesitation, swung it at the incoming demon.","When the Demon Devouring Sword appeared, both Lev and the Forsaken demon suddenly felt their strength vanish into thin air.","\"What is going on?!\" The Forsaken exclaimed in shock.","\"You’re dead, that’s what.\"","In the next moment, Yuan swung his sword. Infused with Demon Sealing Aura and amplified by Supreme Sword Aura, the blade cleaved through the demon instantly, splitting it cleanly in half before sealing it.","However, the demon was not dead yet.","\"Devour,\" Yuan muttered before the demon could recover.","Suddenly, a massive hole appeared in the demon’s bisected body, as if something had taken an enormous bite out of it. Before the demon could even comprehend what was happening, the rest of its body was completely devoured.","Despite witnessing everything from beginning to end, Lev failed to comprehend what had just happened. He could only stare at Yuan with a bewildered expression.","Though he had no idea what Yuan had done to the Forsaken demon, Lev silently swore to himself that he would never offend Yuan—no matter the cost.","\"Let’s continue,\" Yuan said calmly, sheathing his sword before flying onward as though nothing had happened.","Lev swallowed nervously and followed behind. Though he wanted to ask what had just occurred, fear kept his mouth shut.","’He killed a fourth-level Forsaken just like that?! If he wanted to, he could’ve easily killed all of us back then, and we wouldn’t even know it happened!’ he cried inwardly.","A few hours later, another demon attacked them.","\"Stay away or you’ll regret it!\" Lev warned the approaching demon.","\"Hahah! Who the hell do you think you’re trying to scare with that cultivation?! You’ll be my first meal in a million years!\"","\"Is this idiot a Forsaken?\" Yuan asked.","Lev shook his head, \"No...\"","\"In that case...\"","[Swords of Eternal Torment!]","Several golden swords of light materialized in the sky above the demon before plunging downward, impaling it and pinning its body to the ground.","\"AHHH! IT HURTS! IT HURTTTSSS!\" The demon immediately cried out in agony, its scream so loud that it shook the air around them."]},{"number":2363,"title":"Chapter 2363: Scarecrow","paragraphs":["Lev stared at the demon pinned to the ground by Yuan’s Swords of Eternal Torment, a dazed expression plastered on his face.","\"Wait... pain? It’s painful?\" he suddenly muttered, realizing the strange remark.","’He’s actually feeling pain?!’ Lev cried inwardly. ’But our pain tolerance is so high that even being thrown into a shredder wouldn’t make us feel anything!’","After allowing the demon to endure a few moments of agony, Yuan deactivated the swords’ ability and casually made a gesture with his hand.","In the next instant, the demon was lifted off the ground and dragged into the air—still impaled by the swords embedded in his body.","\"W-What do you plan on doing with him?\" Lev asked in a fearful voice.","\"I’m going to use him to make our journey more smooth,\" Yuan calmly replied, refusing to elaborate.","\"What have you done to me?! Let me go!\"","Meanwhile, the demon struggled desperately to free himself from the swords. However, no matter how much he twisted or pulled, they refused to budge, as if they had fused with his body.","Seeing this, Yuan activated the swords’ ability once more.","\"AHHHH!\"","Agony surged through the demon’s body again, forcing another ear-piercing scream from his throat.","\"The less you talk, the less painful it will be,\" Yuan said in a cold voice.","The demon wanted to cry but had no tears, and he reluctantly nodded in silence.","\"Let’s continue forward,\" Yuan said to Lev, who was still trying to figure out what Yuan was planning.","A few hours later, Lev sensed another presence approaching them.","However, before he could even warn Yuan, a loud scream suddenly tore through the air, startling him.","He quickly turned toward the source of the scream, and sure enough, it came from the demon Yuan had captured and forced to follow them.","’Don’t tell me he’s—!’","A chilling realization crept into Lev’s bones the moment he understood why Yuan had dragged the demon along with them.","’He’s using him like a scarecrow... to drive others away!’ Lev cried inwardly.","Even though the demon attacked them first, Lev couldn’t help but pity him.","Sure enough, when the approaching presence heard the demon’s agonized screams and saw the dreadful sight of an impaled demon being dragged through the air, they immediately turned around and fled at twice their original speed.","However, they didn’t leave completely. Instead, they lingered at a safe distance, observing the situation with clear curiosity.","Using this method, Yuan and Lev were able to travel in peace for several months. Unfortunately, their strange spectacle had also drawn a growing audience of demons quietly following behind them.","\"Who the fuck is that crazy bastard? He’s dragging Dune around while torturing him!\"","\"Do you think Dune is genuinely feeling pain, or is he merely acting for some reason?\"","\"I don’t know, but his screams are real enough to send shivers down my spine, no matter how many times I’ve heard them.\"","\"Poor guy. I wonder what he did to offend that madman.\"","\"I have never witnessed such savagery in all my life...\"","\"Look at his perfect appearance. He’s definitely a noble.\"","\"But what would a noble be doing so deep inside the Deprived Crimson Valley?\"","After using the demon as a scarecrow for an entire year, Yuan also started feeling bad about it, so he decided to release the demon.","\"Thanks for your assistance for the past year,\" Yuan said as he completely deactivated Swords of Eternal Torment.","The demon coughed up a mouthful of blood when Yuan made it sound like he volunteered to help them. However, he didn’t dare to correct Yuan and simply said, \"It was a pleasure...\"","The moment he was freed, the demon spun around and fled at full speed, running as though death itself were chasing him, completely ignoring the group of demons signaling to him from afar.","Seeing that the demon had no intention of stopping for them, several of the demons broke away from the group and chased after him.","\"Hey! Dune! What the hell was that about?!\"","\"Did you really feel pain? Or were you only pretending?!\"","\"What did it feel like?!\"","Since demons were incapable of feeling pain, the concept itself naturally stirred their curiosity.","\"Fuck! Get away from me! I don’t want to talk about it!\" The demon named Dune shouted at them.","\"If you’re so curious, go attack that fucking crazy bastard yourselves! I bet he’s already looking for my replacement!\"","Hearing this, several demons actually paused to consider the idea. Since they had never experienced pain before, the thought of feeling it for the first time strangely intrigued them.","Eventually, a few of them turned around and flew at Yuan while exuding killing intent.","\"I don’t believe that you can actually inflict pain on us!\"","\"If you can really hurt us, I’d really like to experience it myself!\"","\"You want to experience pain?\" Yuan’s expression remained nonchalant as he watched three demons soaring toward him.","\"Then I’ll let you experience so much of it that you’ll never want to experience it ever again!\"","[Swords of Eternal Torment!]","A dozen swords glowing with golden brilliance materialized around the demons, surrounding them from all sides.","Although the demons could have easily avoided the attack, they chose not to, allowing the swords to impale their bodies.","The instant the swords drove through their bodies, a foreign sensation erupted within them, overwhelming their senses and plunging them into unimaginable pain.","\"AAAGH!\"","\"WHAT IS THIS FEELING?!\"","\"IS THIS PAIN?! IT HURTS LIKE HELL!\"","Even as the unbearable pain overwhelmed them, not a single demon asked Yuan to stop.","Lev swallowed nervously as he watched the demons willingly subject themselves to such agony. Yet at the same time, he found himself growing intrigued. The concept of pain was so foreign to demons that it held a strange allure.","Yuan was no stranger to their masochistic behavior. In the past, many demons would deliberately provoke him, hoping to experience pain for the first time."]},{"number":2364,"title":"Chapter 2364: The Sixth Valley","paragraphs":["With three willing scarecrows now in tow, Yuan resumed his journey toward the Sixth Valley. Whenever a demon approached with hostile intent, he would activate the swords, and the scarecrows’ agonized screams would echo like a warning siren.","However, while most demons either fled or joined the growing crowd spectating Yuan, some ignored the warnings entirely and attacked anyway. Without exception, they were all Forsaken—demons who feared nothing.","Seeing this, Yuan did not hesitate to strike them down with the Demon Devouring Sword.","Just as he had done with the first one, he cleaved the demon in half before allowing the sword to consume its body.","Upon witnessing Yuan slaughter the Forsaken, the demons trailing him trembled subconsciously, their eyes flickering with growing fear. However, it wasn’t Yuan that made them fearful.","\"What kind of weapon is that? My senses are screaming at me to run away from it!\"","The demons couldn’t comprehend why the sword in Yuan’s hand filled them with such unease. What they didn’t know was that the Demon Devouring Sword had devoured countless demons over the ages. By absorbing their power, the blade had developed an oppressive aura that caused other demons to instinctively feel inferior before it.","\"So he can kill a Forsaken with such ease...\"","The demons swallowed nervously, their curiosity for Yuan’s identity growing stronger than ever. Yet, none of them dared to approach him.","Time passed swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, several more years had passed.","\"We’re approaching the Sixth Valley,\" said Lev when he noticed the change in the atmosphere.","There were no mountain ranges separating the Fifth Valley from the Sixth Valley, but there was a drastic change in atmosphere, and when the demons following Yuan sensed it, they began slowing down until they came to a complete stop.","\"What’s wrong with them?\" Yuan asked Lev, who also appeared to be struggling against something.","\"Y-You can’t sense it?\" Lev looked at him with a bewildered face.","Yuan raised an eyebrow and focused on his surroundings. Yet, he was unable to sense anything out of the ordinary.","’Perhaps it’s something that can only be sensed by demons...’ he thought to himself.","\"You might not know this, but inside the Deprived Crimson Valley, most of the Forsakens dwell within the Sixth Valley and beyond, and only the weakest ones wander to the other valleys.\"","\"Is there a reason they gather at the Sixth Valley?\" Yuan asked, finding the phenomenon somewhat intriguing.","Lev shook his head. \"Honestly, we don’t know. Forsaken think and act differently from the rest of us, but for so many of them to gather in one place, there has to be a reason.\"","He then shrugged. \"Unfortunately, no one’s brave enough to find out. Getting close to them is far too dangerous. On top of that, many fear their condition might be contagious, so most demons keep their distance.\"","\"Contagious?\" Yuan wore a puzzled expression. \"When did that become a concern?\"","When he had visited the Demonic Realm as Tian Chenyu, it was widely believed that the Forsaken had become what they were because they had been abandoned by their God—hence their name. Since it wasn’t considered an illness, very few demons had ever feared it might be contagious.","\"Well... more and more people are turning into a Forsaken these days, so...\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"Although I cannot guarantee you that you will never become a Forsaken, I can guarantee you that it’s not contagious.\"","\"Anyway, let’s enter the Sixth Valley. Even if Forsakens attack us, I’ll make sure to protect you.\"","\"Alright...\"","After witnessing Yuan effortlessly execute multiple Forsaken, Lev no longer doubted his abilities. That said, he was still nervous about entering the Sixth Valley, something he had never done before.","After taking a moment to resolve himself, Lev followed Yuan into the Sixth Valley while trying his best to ignore the oppressive and dreadful pressure emitting from the place.","\"Hey... if I ever turn into a Forsaken, can you kill me?\" Lev suddenly asked.","\"Sure,\" Yuan replied without hesitation.","His immediate answer both surprised and relieved Lev.","\"Thank you. I’d rather die than spend an eternity living like a beast.\"","Suddenly, the presence of two sixth-level False Gods appeared in the distance.","\"They’re here! Forsakens!\" Lev warned.","Yuan, who noticed their presence before Lev, was already prepared to confront them.","However, when the demons arrived, they did not attack immediately. Instead, they stopped at a distance and silently observed them—or more precisely, the Demon Devouring Sword in Yuan’s grasp.","’Oh? Are they wary of the Demon Devouring Sword? Is it instinct, or is it something else?’ Yuan wondered.","After lingering for a few moments, the two demons suddenly turned around and left without a word, leaving Yuan and Lev puzzled.","\"What was that about?\" Lev wondered out loud.","Yuan didn’t say anything.","Then, after a moment of silence, he said, \"You should hide for a bit.\"","\"Huh?\"","Before Lev could even process Yuan’s words, multiple powerful presences appeared out of thin air.","\"W-What a strong presence!\" Lev felt as if his entire body was being crushed by a mountain.","\"Leave before it’s too late,\" Yuan warned him again.","Without hesitation, Lev descended to the ground before going into hiding.","A moment after Lev left, a group of demons appeared on the horizon, steadily approaching Yuan. There were around a dozen of them, with a single demon leading from the front.","Unlike the others—who were clearly Lower Demons—the one leading them had a black crystal embedded in the center of his chest, marking him as an Elite Demon.","Intrigued by their purpose, Yuan didn’t immediately start slaughtering them and waited for them to act first.","However, instead of doing anything, they merely stared at the Demon Devouring Sword.","\"Interested?\" Yuan suddenly lifted his sword in their direction and asked, starting the conversation.","\"Where did you acquire that sword?\" The Elite Demon questioned with a wary look on his face, as if he knew about the Demon Devouring Sword."]},{"number":2365,"title":"Chapter 2365: The Seventh Valley","paragraphs":["\"Why do you care where I acquired it?\" Yuan responded to the Elite Demon inquiring about the Demon Devouring Sword.","The Elite Demon narrowed his eyes and spoke in a cold voice, \"That thing should not exist in this world. If you hand it over willingly, I’ll spare your life.\"","Yuan couldn’t help but let out a cold chuckle.","\"Do you even know what this sword is?\" he questioned.","\"That’s the Demon Devouring Sword... isn’t it?\" the Elite Demon said calmly.","\"Although there’s almost no chance that it’s the real one, I won’t take that risk. That thing is a threat to our entire race.\"","\"Whether it’s real or fake... you’ll find out very soon.\"","The moment Yuan showed even the slightest sign of resistance, the demons behind the Elite Demon sprang into action, swiftly surrounding him from every direction.","\"Kill him and bring that sword to me,\" the Elite Demon commanded.","In the next instant, fifteen Lower Demons attacked Yuan simultaneously.","Yuan merely shook his head as he activated the Demon Sealing Zone, instantly entrapping the demons in its domain.","Before the demons could even get close, their bodies were frozen stiff without being sealed.","\"What did he do?! I cannot move my body!\"","The demons tried to fight against the invisible force, but even with their superior cultivation, they could only make their fingers twitch slightly.","\"This power! Demon Sealing Aura! So you were a Sealer!\" The Elite Demon exclaimed in shock after realizing their situation.","\"Oh? You seem to know a lot more than the others.\" Yuan calmly approached the Elite Demon and asked, \"Then do you know the name Tian Chenyu? Or Divine Paragon?\"","\"T-Tian Chenyu...?\"","The Elite Demon wore a puzzled look on his face before it suddenly turned blank, as if he’d gone into a daze. Then, without warning, he started screaming.","\"AHHH!\"","Sensing something was wrong, Yuan immediately backed away from the Elite Demon.","The following moment, the Elite Demon’s body started to bloat rapidly, swelling as if something inside him were forcing it outward.","In mere moments, he had ballooned to a grotesque size, resembling that of a hot balloon.","Then, with a violent pop, his body burst apart.","\"?!?!\"","Not just Yuan, but even Lev and the other demons were shocked by the Elite Demon’s random death, something they’d never seen before.","’What the hell? He died after hearing my name?’ Yuan tried to process what had happened.","Then, he turned to look at the Lower Demons and asked, \"Do you know Tian Chenyu or the Divine Paragon?\"","He weakened their restrictions so they could move.","Immediately, they all shook their heads.","\"Then what do you know about this sword? And what was your purpose just now?\"","\"W-We were only following his orders! We know nothing about the sword!\" They exclaimed.","Yuan focused his gaze on the two demons from the beginning and said, \"You know nothing about the sword, yet you were able to recognize it?\"","\"That’s because our boss would talk about it all the time! He said that he’d witnessed its prowess when he was outside the Deprived Crimson Valley and that if he had it, he’d be able to conquer this world!\"","Yuan sighed.","\"What a stupid reason.\" Yuan shook his head.","\"Anyways, let’s get this over with.\"","Without another word, he slaughtered all of the demons before feeding them to the Demon Devouring Sword.","\"You can stop hiding now,\" Yuan said to Lev afterward.","A few moments later, Lev emerged from his hiding spot and asked, \"What was that about?\"","Yuan shrugged.","There was definitely something happening within the Demonic Realm, but he had no clue what.","’Hopefully, Supreme Ruler Dena will have some answers for me,’ he sighed inwardly.","They continued their journey, and over the next several years, they would encounter hundreds of Forsakens. However, none of them would recognize the Demon Devouring Sword or the name Tian Chenyu and simply attacked on sight.","Eventually, they arrived at the Seventh Valley.","\"So this is what the Seventh Valley looks like...\" Lev muttered to himself as he surveyed the surroundings in awe.","The endless plains of crimson grass had disappeared, replaced by patches of black and purple flowers scattered across the land.","The atmosphere itself was overwhelming. A crushing pressure weighed down on Lev’s body, making it difficult for him to even move.","\"At this rate, I won’t be able to go any further than the Seventh Valley even if I wanted to,\" he said to Yuan, who appeared to be completely nonchalant, almost as if the pressure was nonexistent to him.","\"Let me try something,\" said Yuan.","He suddenly activated Demon Sealing Zone, forming a domain around Lev like a barrier. However, instead of restricting him, it protected him from the oppressive presence.","\"Wow! I don’t feel the pressure anymore!\" Lev exclaimed with excitement. \"Is there anything you can’t do?!\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"If you feel fine, let’s get going.\"","Soon, they encountered their first Forsaken in the Seventh Valley, and it was another Lower Demon. However, it had the cultivation of an eighth-level False God.","If they were still in the Nine Heavens, this Forsaken would’ve been a catastrophe.","’The demons these days are much stronger than before.’ Yuan thought to himself after realizing this. However, if he considered how much time had passed since his last visit, this was only natural.","Fortunately for him, a demon’s cultivation meant little in the face of Demon Sealing Aura.","It might require a little more effort and time, but in the end, even an eight-level False God, which is equivalent to the eighth-level God Ascension, ended up being devoured by the Demon Devouring Sword.","\"If all of the demons in the Seventh Valley are already between the seventh and ninth level of False God, are we going to encounter True Gods in the Eighth Valley? What about the Ninth Valley?\" Yuan asked Lev.","A True God in the Demonic Realm was essentially a Cultivation God in the Nine Heavens. It was an existence that even Yuan was wary of."]},{"number":2366,"title":"Chapter 2366: True Chaotic Qi","paragraphs":["Hearing Yuan’s question, Lev pondered for a moment before responding, \"From what I’ve heard, all of the True Gods dwell within the Ninth Valley and the Final Valley. Unfortunately, I don’t know anything about the Eighth Valley.\"","He silently stared at Yuan for a moment before continuing, \"You know... it’s not too late to turn around and go back...\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"If we do encounter a True God, I will have to get a little serious, but we will be fine.\"","Lev’s jaw dropped as he asked, \"Have you even fought seriously once since we started our journey?\"","\"What do you think?\"","\"Uh... no?\"","Yuan silently smiled.","As they drew closer to the Eighth Valley, the Forsaken they encountered grew increasingly powerful. Eventually, the Lower Demons disappeared altogether, and only Elite Demons and Superior Demons would appear.","\"I have never seen so many Black Cores in my life!\" Lev swallowed nervously as Superior Demons showed up one after another.","In the Demonic Realm, the ranking system used to categorize demon ranks did not exist. Instead, demons were identified by their crystals. Superior Demons, who possessed black crystals, were known as Black Cores, while Lower Demons were referred to as Crimson Cores.","Of course, there was still a social hierarchy. Demons with red crystals were regarded as ordinary commoners, while those with black crystals were considered elites.","Demons whose appearance closely resembled that of ordinary humans were usually considered nobles, as many believed these forms reflected the original appearance of their ancestors. For this reason, some demons naturally assumed Yuan belonged to that class.","Eventually, they arrived at the borders of the Eighth Valley. Although it had taken them nearly thirty years to reach this point, only a month had passed in the Nine Heavens.","Yuan and Lev halted at the edge of the Eighth Valley.","It appeared to be raining, but the rain was far from normal. Dark droplets of black liquid fell from the sky, each one carrying a familiar and unsettling aura.","’This is... Chaotic Essence!’","Yuan suddenly extended his arm toward the rain, but when Lev saw this, he hastily pulled Yuan back and shouted, \"Are you crazy?! Do you not know what that is?!\"","\"It’s just rain, though?\"","\"Of course not! This is not ordinary rain! It’s a Corruption Shower! And those who are contaminated by the liquid are more likely to turn into a Forsaken!\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this and said, \"Isn’t this just another rumor? Like Forsaken being contagious.\"","\"No, it’s not just a rumor,\" said Lev.","\"In a certain experiment, they had a group of one thousand people drenched in a Corruption Shower, and not even a year later, more than half of them turned into Forsaken!\"","\"Is that so? In any case, I’ll be fine.\" Yuan said as he reached his arm into the rain, soaking it with the black liquid.","Lev watched with a nervous face, but Yuan remained as nonchalant as ever. If anything, he was quite excited inwardly. After all, he was able to absorb the Chaotic Essence from the Corruption Shower, and his second cultivation, which had stopped at the Chaotic Immortal Realm, was starting to show progress again.","\"Does this rain go on forever?\" Yuan turned to ask Lev, who quickly shook his head.","\"No, they usually stop after a few years.\"","\"Then I cannot waste this opportunity.\"","Without another word, Yuan entered the Corruption Shower, completely drenching himself in it.","\"My lord!\" Lev cried out loud.","\"Wait for me. I’m going to cultivate for a bit,\" said Yuan.","\"Cultivate?! In the Corruption Shower?! That’s reckless!\"","Lev tried to convince Yuan to come back out, but Yuan completely ignored him and spent the next seven years cultivating in the Corruption Shower.","Upon reaching the God Ascension Realm, Yuan gained the ability to perceive Celestial Qi with ease. And for the first time, he also sensed a familiar power within the Chaotic Essence.","While it wasn’t the same as Celestial Qi, the power it contained felt remarkably similar.","’What is this? I never sensed anything like this, even when I was Tian Yi, the Immortal Monarch.’ Yuan thought to himself.","Even though he’d created multiple Chaotic Hearts as the Immortal Monarch, he’d never sensed this sort of energy in Chaotic Essence.","’Now that I think about it, I think the Primal Monarch had mentioned something like this in the past...’","Yuan thought long and hard about what the Primal Monarch told him, but he was unable to recall such a memory for some reason.","In the end, he stopped thinking and focused on studying this new energy.","After spending five whole years studying the new energy, Yuan received a notification.","<You have discovered the existence of True Chaotic Qi>","<Your comprehension of True Chaotic Qi has improved significantly>","At the end of his seven-year cultivation, Yuan not only deepened his understanding of True Chaotic Qi, but his second cultivation also broke through Chaotic Immortal and entered Early Chaotic Supreme.","Despite that, he was unable to actually utilize True Chaotic Qi.","If he had more time, it might’ve been possible, but alas, the Corruption Shower ended.","\"Hey... are you... okay?\" Lev cautiously approached Yuan, fearing that he might have turned into a Forsaken.","Yuan looked at him and said, \"I am fine.\"","\"Seriously? You don’t feel off? Even slightly?\"","Yuan nodded.","Some time later, Lev followed Yuan into the Eighth Valley, and they immediately continued moving toward the Ninth Valley.","Even though Yuan assured him that everything was fine, Lev remained on edge. If someone as powerful as Yuan were to become a Forsaken, it wouldn’t just spell disaster for Lev—it would threaten every demon in existence.","\"It’s been a while since we encountered a Forsaken,\" Yuan remarked a few weeks into the Eighth Valley without any encounters.","\"Why does it sound like you want to encounter them?\" Lev shook his head and sighed. \"There’s a good chance we might run into a True God, you know.\"","Just as the words left his mouth, a crushing pressure suddenly descended upon them, suffocating the air around them."]},{"number":2367,"title":"Chapter 2367: Killing a True God","paragraphs":["\"T-This presence! It’s a True God!\" The moment Lev sensed this oppressive aura, he immediately descended from the sky and went into hiding without even needing Yuan to tell him.","Not even a full second after Lev left, a silhouette slowly approached Yuan from a distance, its figure exuding an unfathomable aura that twisted and wrapped the space around them.","\"In my fifty billion years of experience in this place, this is the first time I’ve seen a first-level False God who is bold enough to trespass into this domain meant for real Gods,\" remarked the demon, who had a unique appearance that looked half human and half demon.","Yuan calmly replied, \"To call it trespassing, you’d have to own this place.\"","\"Oh? And you even dare to talk back?\"","In the next instant, Yuan sensed a powerful wave of Celestial Qi rushing toward him. However, it was clear that the attack wasn’t meant to kill him—it was simply meant to intimidate.","In response, Yuan also released some of his Celestial Qi for the first time, and despite only being at the first level of God Ascension, his Celestial Qi was strong enough to rival that of the True God.","Seeing its Celestial Qi being destroyed by Yuan, the True God expressed surprise on their face.","\"I see why you dare to come here. Unfortunately for you, that wasn’t even half of my true power.\"","As they spoke, an even more powerful pressure suddenly descended, bearing down on Yuan like a colossal mountain.","Without a word, Yuan mixed his Chaotic Essence with his Celestial Qi, causing it to explode tremendously, even overwhelming the True God for a good moment.","\"What is that power?\" The True God narrowed their gaze at Yuan, looking befuddled.","\"Are you just going to stand there, or are you actually going to fight me?\" Yuan asked, beckoning the True God.","\"Interesting. Let’s see what you have up your sleeves. I am also interested in that power.\"","The next moment, the True God vanished from his position like a ghost before appearing right in front of Yuan.","\"Blood Arts, Hell’s Scythe!\"","The True God condensed his own blood into a massive scythe before swinging it toward Yuan.","Instead of dodging, Yuan raised the Demon Devouring Sword and met the attack head-on.","The True God raised an eyebrow when he noticed the Demon Devouring Sword.","\"What a nasty weapon you have there,\" he remarked.","\"Thanks,\" Yuan responded.","In the next instant, he vanished with a movement technique and reappeared behind the True God, striking without hesitation.","Without even turning around, the True God created a turtle-like shell on his back, blocking the strike. Yet, the impact from Yuan’s strike was much stronger than he anticipated, and it launched him several meters away.","\"You’re not a Forsaken, are you?\" Yuan asked the demon afterward.","Instead of answering, the True God narrowed his eyes and asked, \"What are you? You may be hiding your presence, but I can tell that you’re fundamentally different.\"","\"I’ll tell you if you can beat me.\"","\"...\"","The True God fell silent for a moment before suddenly releasing a tyrannical amount of aura.","\"Try not to die,\" he said after releasing his full cultivation.","An excited smile appeared on Yuan’s face as he activated True Dragon Awakening without hesitation.","\"What kind of appearance is that?\"","Not just the True God, but even Lev were taken aback by Yuan’s sudden transformation.","\"Enough questions. I’ll answer all of your questions if you can beat me,\" said Yuan as he launched an attack first.","It’d been a long time since he was able to fight at full strength, and this was a good opportunity for him to see his current limits.","Despite Yuan only being at the First Level of the God Ascension Realm, the True God—whose strength rivaled that of a Cultivation God—did not dare underestimate him and responded with his full power.","A powerful ripple swept across the Eighth Valley, their clash so violent that the very space around them began to crack.","For the first several hours, the two of them used only basic techniques and raw strength to fight, but eventually, they started using actual martial techniques.","[Heaven Splitting Sword Strike!]","Without needing to gather his energy like previously, Yuan could effortlessly launch Heaven Splitting Sword Strikes one after another, each powerful enough to completely erase mountains and change landscapes.","\"What overwhelming and devastating prowess!\" The True God could feel his back soaked in cold sweat after seeing how effortlessly and frequently Yuan was unleashing these landscape-altering attacks one after another.","\"Blood Arts, Crimson Downpour!\"","Moments later, it burst like a bubble, releasing countless needle-like projectiles that rained down upon Yuan.","[Void Manipulation!]","Yuan’s figure vanished into thin air and entered the void, completely avoiding the attack.","\"You’re not the only one who can use Void Manipulation!\" The True God declared before also entering the void.","\"What the hell is going on?! These two are monsters!\" Lev cried out loud as he continued to distance himself from the battlefield.","Even though their next several exchanges occurred within the void, Lev could sense the ripple caused by their clashes, sending chills down his entire being.","He’d witnessed many fights in his lifetime, but this was the first time it made him feel so small and terrified.","Then, he realized that Yuan had been fighting without his usual Demon Sealing Techniques and relied on his own prowess for some reason.","One day... three days... five days...","Yuan and the True God clashed relentlessly for an entire month. Yet even after all that time, neither side had gained a decisive advantage. Although Yuan appeared to hold the upper hand, it still wasn’t enough to secure victory.","\"You’re not bad. I haven’t had this much fun in a long time!\" The True God remarked as he distanced himself from Yuan. \"However, I can tell that you’re still holding back.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"I wouldn’t be able to enjoy it if I were to fight you with all of my power.\"","The True God opened his mouth, but before he could speak, another presence suddenly appeared.","\"HEYYY! LET ME IN ON THE FUN!\" A loud and obnoxious voice suddenly echoed.","A moment later, another demon appeared. Purple skin, crimson eyes, and four black horns marked its appearance.","It too possessed the aura of a True God, but its presence was clearly stronger than the one Yuan had been fighting for the past month.","A look of disgust appeared on Yuan’s face when he saw the newcomer, his brows furrowing deeply as he stared at it.","The rotting stench emanating from the demon was overwhelming. It was unmistakably a Forsaken.","\"Mind your own business, Mov,\" the True God snickered, sounding just as displeased as Yuan by the interruption.","However, the Forsaken completely ignored the True God and focused solely on Yuan.","\"A False God fighting on equal terms with a True God? I wonder how you’ll taste!\"","Without warning, the Forsaken named Mov lunged at Yuan with its mouth wide open, as if it wanted to take a bite out of his flesh.","Yuan sneered in disgust before activating the Demon Sealing Zone.","However, the Demon Sealing Zone was only strong enough to slow the Mov’s movements by about twenty-five percent.","[Swords of Eternal Torment!]","Then, a hundred golden swords materialized in the sky and quickly surrounded Mov.","\"What’s this power?\"","The True God swallowed nervously when he sensed the overwhelming amount of Demon Sealing Aura gushing from Yuan’s body at this moment.","\"Fuck! What the hell is this?! It hurts!\" Mov screamed out loud when the swords impaled its body.","Before Mov could even process what was happening to him, Yuan launched his next attack.","His Demon Sealing Aura erupted to unprecedented levels, its overwhelming presence reaching demons as far as the Seventh—and even the Sixth Valley.","Mov ignored the pain in his body and focused his gaze on Yuan, who was now emitting a different aura.","When Mov sensed the aura, a look of awe and reverence appeared on his face—though he was completely unaware of it himself.","\"Our... God?\" Mov muttered under his breath.","Yuan suddenly swung the Demon Devouring Sword in his grasp.","In the next moment, Mov felt a gentle breeze brush across his face.","Then, he ceased to exist.","The True God’s eyes widened in stunned shock. But when he confirmed that Mov had actually been killed, the shock in his eyes turned into pure terror and disbelief.","’Impossible! He actually killed Mov?! And that easily?!’ he cried inwardly.","Mov was a True God just like him—no, he was even stronger. Yet Yuan had killed him in the blink of an eye, making it look utterly effortless.","Not to mention the unfamiliar power Yuan had displayed. The Demon Sealing Aura alone was already shocking enough, but the second power he used—something even the True God couldn’t comprehend—left him completely speechless.","\"You... Who the hell are you? And what was that power you used to kill Mov?\" The True God asked with clenched fists."]},{"number":2368,"title":"Chapter 2368: The Realm of Absolute God","paragraphs":["\"Who am I...?\" Yuan turned to look at the True God after killing Mov. \"I’m Yuan. As for the power I used, it was Demon Sealing Aura.\"","\"Demon Sealing Aura? You were a Sealer this entire time?\" The True God frowned when he realized that Yuan had been going easy on him this entire time.","Had Yuan used Demon Sealing Aura from the start to suppress him, he wouldn’t have been able to fight with his full capability. However, there was another reason he felt upset.","\"I don’t mean your Demon Sealing Aura,\" he said. \"That power you displayed to kill Mov... that was something entirely different!\"","Yuan shrugged, pretending he had no idea what the True God was talking about.","In truth, he had briefly unleashed his Eternal Essence, overwhelming Mov instantly and killing him before he could even comprehend what had happened.","This was also Yuan’s first time fusing his Eternal Essence with his Demon Sealing Aura, and unsurprisingly, the results were astonishing.","\"Want to continue?\" Yuan asked the True God a moment later.","\"...\"","The True God took a deep breath before shaking his head.","\"I’m no longer in the mood, especially after realizing you’ve been going easy on me. I still can’t believe a first-level False God was holding back against me.\"","\"Why did you attack me in the first place?\" Yuan asked suddenly. \"Were you really that bothered by my presence?\"","The True God shook his head. \"No. At first, I believed you had wandered here by mistake, so I wanted to drive you away. This place is too dangerous for a False God, after all.\"","He continued, \"But after fighting you, I realized I had underestimated you. Now that I know you can even kill True Gods, there’s no reason for me to chase you away anymore.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the explanation. According to him, the True God had actually been trying to help, which was truly unexpected.","\"Why were you exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley?\" Yuan asked, seemingly interested in the True God’s background.","\"My reason for being exiled...?\" The True God fell silent for a moment before responding, \"To be frank, I have long forgotten the reason. I wasn’t even a False God when I was exiled over fifty billion years ago.\"","\"Have you ever thought about leaving?\" Yuan asked.","\"Many times,\" the True God answered. \"But escaping this place with my own strength is impossible—even for a True God.\"","He continued in a low voice, \"And even if I did manage to escape, it wouldn’t matter. We exiles carry a brand etched into our souls. No matter where we go or what disguise we wear, we will always be recognized and hunted.\"","The exiles of the Deprived Crimson Valley were much like the exiles of the Primordial Realm. Even if they somehow managed to escape, their branding ensured they could never truly run from their fate.","\"Enough questions about me. What are you doing in the Eighth Valley? Are you just looking to fight True Gods?\"","\"My destination isn’t the Eighth Valley, but the Final Valley,\" Yuan calmly replied.","\"The Final Valley?! Are you out of your mind?!\" The True God exclaimed in shock after hearing this.","\"Forget about the Final Valley, even the Ninth Valley is too dangerous these days! Why the hell would you want to go there?\"","\"I have some business with Supreme Ruler Dena, that’s all.\"","\"Supreme Ruler Dena?!\" The True God nearly turned and ran away the moment he heard her name.","\"What’s going on with the Ninth Valley?\" Yuan ignored his shock and asked.","\"I don’t know how to explain it. It’s better if you witnessed it yourself. Because of what’s happening in the Ninth Valley, all of the True Gods and Absolute Gods dwelling there have moved to the Eighth Valley.\"","\"Wait... Absolute Gods?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this new terminology. \"What are those?\"","The True God looked at Yuan with a puzzled face.","\"You... don’t know about Absolute Gods?\" he had to confirm what he heard.","Yuan calmly nodded before giving a random excuse, \"I was in seclusion for a long time.\"","\"How long were you in seclusion for? The realm of Absolute God was discovered over ten billion years ago! It’s basically what’s above the True God Realm, and only about twenty individuals have managed to reach that level even after its discovery ten billion years ago.\"","’A realm above Cultivation God, huh?’ Yuan thought to himself.","While the Cultivation God was considered the peak of cultivation in the Nine Heavens, the path of cultivation itself was infinite. There was no true peak—only new realms waiting to be discovered with time.","With how much time passed in the Demonic Realm compared to the Nine Heavens, it was no surprise that they had managed to discover what’s above Cultivation God.","The Demonic Realm being ahead of the Nine Heavens wasn’t anything new to Yuan, as there were already hundreds of Cultivation Gods when he visited as Tian Chenyu, while the Nine Heavens had only discovered its existence.","\"An Absolute God... I’d like to meet and fight one,\" Yuan remarked with a smile on his face.","\"If you have a death wish, go ahead and fight one. They’ll kill you before you can even register what happened,\" said the True God.","\"Are there any in the Deprived Crimson Valley?\" Yuan asked.","\"There are... two of them.\"","\"If they’re really that powerful, why are they afraid of the Ninth Valley?\"","\"It’s not that they’re scared. They just don’t want to deal with it since it’s a hassle.\"","\"Now I really want to see what’s at the Ninth Valley. Thanks for the information. I’ll be taking my leave now.\"","Yuan then called out, \"Come out, Lev! We’re moving again!\"","A few moments later, Lev emerged from a hole he’d dug in the ground and slowly approached them with his head lowered, as if he were too afraid to even look at the True God."]},{"number":2369,"title":"Chapter 2369: Demon God","paragraphs":["\"Are you really determined to go to the Ninth Valley?\" The True God suddenly spoke when Yuan and Lev prepared to depart.","\"That’s right. Why? You wanna come with us?\" Yuan asked.","The True God fell silent for a moment before nodding, \"I still have questions that need to be answered, so I’ll follow you for a bit. I also want to see if the situation in the Ninth Valley has gotten any better or worse.\"","\"If you want to follow us, go ahead,\" said Yuan.","\"By the way, do you have a name?\"","\"You can call me Duk.\"","\"Duck, huh,\" Yuan repeated, unaware that he’d misheard the name. Yet, he wasn’t corrected.","They started making their way towards the Ninth Valley together shortly after.","Over the next several days, they sensed the presence of multiple True Gods. However, most of them didn’t even bother approaching, and those who did suddenly turned back halfway for some reason.","\"Thanks for sending them away, Senior.\" Lev suddenly said to Duk.","\"What?\" However, Duk wore a puzzled look on his face before calmly responding, \"I didn’t do anything.\"","\"Then why did those True Gods turn around midway?\"","Duk turned to look at Yuan and replied, \"Probably because of the unfathomable aura he exudes when they get too close.\"","\"What?\" Lev shifted his gaze to Yuan. \"I haven’t sensed anything unusual from him, though.\"","\"So you cannot sense that crazy aura, huh?\" Duk muttered, sounding like he had just acquired new information.","This was the main reason he had decided to follow Yuan. He wanted to learn more about Eternal Essence. Yet even with his vast experience, he found himself unable to comprehend it, almost as if it were something he was never meant to understand.","As for the other True Gods, although they couldn’t understand what they sensed from Yuan, their instincts screamed at them to retreat, and so they did.","About a month later, a True God who didn’t fear Yuan’s Eternal Essence went to block his path.","\"It’s a Forsaken,\" Duk warned Yuan. \"I doubt you’ll need any help, but if you do...\"","\"Thanks for the offer, but I’ll be fine.\"","Yuan approached the Forsaken with a calm expression.","However, instead of attacking, the Forsaken questioned with a frown on his face, \"A mere first-level False God? How did you acquire that power?\"","\"What power are you referring to?\" Yuan asked, pretending not to know what the Forsaken was talking about.","\"Don’t act dumb! That aura surrounding you... That’s the Demon God’s powers!\" The Forsaken roared.","\"What?\"","Not just Duk, but even Yuan was surprised by the Forsaken’s claims.","\"The Demon God? What the hell are you talking about?\"","Rather than Yuan, it was Duk who stepped forward and questioned.","\"I will not ask you again! How and where did you acquire that power!\" The Forsaken completely ignored Duk and glared at Yuan with an unwavering gaze. \"If you won’t tell me, I’ll kill you and obtain it for myself!\"","A provocative smile tugged at Yuan’s lips as he beckoned, \"If you think you have what it takes, come get it.\"","Despite Yuan’s blatant provocation, the Forsaken hesitated, as if weighing its decision. However, in the end, it chose to attack.","Seeing this, Yuan didn’t hesitate to use Eternal Essence to fight back.","While this Forsaken was weaker than Mov, he was clearly cautious of Yuan’s Eternal Essence and fought carefully instead of attacking recklessly.","It was a sight Yuan would rarely see, as most Forsaken he had faced would attack without hesitation, confident in their overwhelming regeneration and immorality.","However, in the Demonic Realm, demons were not as invincible and could be killed by other demons, hence why they were not as reckless.","\"How are you going to kill me when you’re too afraid to even come near me?!\" Yuan mocked the Forsaken, even laughing at it.","But the Forsaken remained cautious.","\"You want this power, don’t you? Well, come get it!\" Yuan provoked it by unleashing even more Eternal Essence.","When the Forsaken sensed the overwhelming amount of Eternal Essence radiating from Yuan, its expression suddenly went blank.","In the next instant, it charged at Yuan like a wild beast, as if it had lost all reasoning.","\"Whoa!\" Yuan hadn’t expected his plan to be so effective, especially since he was only trying it out.","\"Give it to me! The Demon God’s power!\" The Forsaken shouted as it charged at Yuan.","[Demon Sealing Zone!]","[Swords of Eternal Torment!]","Yuan activated his Demon Sealing Techniques, restricting the Forsaken’s movements before striking with the Demon Devouring Sword.","The Forsaken, who had seemingly lost all reason, was killed in the very next moment.","\"You...\"","Both Duk and Lev stared at Yuan with bewildered expressions, but it wasn’t because of his overwhelming prowess. Rather, it was because of his Eternal Essence, which had been associated with the Demon God by the Forsaken.","In the Demonic Realm, it was commonly believed that all demons were born from the Demon God, an omnipotent existence.","To demons, the Demon God was much like the Heavens to humans in the Nine Heavens—an entity that stood above everything.","Moreover, it was widely believed that the Forsaken were demons who had been cast aside by the Demon God for going against its will—stripped of their reason and reduced to little more than wild beasts.","\"That power you’ve been using... was the power of the Demon God?! Who the hell are you, Yuan?! I thought only the Supreme Rulers are capable of wielding such power!\" Duk exclaimed.","Yuan sighed and said, \"It’s a misunderstanding. How could I possibly wield the Demon God’s power?\"","\"If it’s not that, then what kind of power is it?\" Duk pressed, his curiosity about Eternal Essence growing stronger by the moment.","Yuan looked at him in the eyes and said, \"I know you want to learn how to use this power, but unfortunately, it’s not something you can learn to wield.\"","\"How can you be so sure when I haven’t even tried?!\" Duk exclaimed, refusing to believe that it was something he couldn’t wield."]},{"number":2370,"title":"Chapter 2370: Supreme Ruler Dena","paragraphs":["\"I just know,\" Yuan calmly shrugged.","\"Fine, keep it to yourself,\" Duk said with a snort. \"But I’ll definitely learn it one day! Just you wait!\"","He assumed Yuan was simply keeping the power to himself, which was hardly unusual. After all, only fools would share their powers so easily.","Unbeknownst to Duk, however, it was a power that only Eternals could wield. Even if he spent his entire life chasing after it, he would never be able to learn it.","Shortly after defeating the Forsaken, Yuan resumed his journey toward the Ninth Valley.","The closer they drew to the Ninth Valley, the more Forsaken appeared to confront them.","Now that Yuan knew his Eternal Essence was attracting them, he refrained from revealing it unless he intended to kill his opponent.","Over the next three years, Yuan slew more than a dozen Forsaken, each one at the True God realm. This meant he had effectively killed over a dozen beings equivalent to Cultivation Gods.","Even with his Demon Sealing Aura giving him an advantage against demons, such an achievement was nothing short of astonishing. If news of this spread throughout the Nine Heavens, it would shock the entire world—especially since Yuan had only just stepped into the God Ascension Realm.","’If he’s already this powerful as a False God, I cannot imagine how terrifying he’d be once he steps into the True God Realm...’ Lev swallowed nervously as he watched Yuan kill True Gods after True Gods.","Meanwhile, Duk devoted all of his attention to Yuan’s Eternal Essence, carefully observing it whenever Yuan used it. However, the moment the Eternal Essence faded, the memory of it would also slip from his mind, as though he was fundamentally incapable of grasping it.","’If only I could grasp that power!’ Duk gritted his teeth.","Suddenly, Yuan began to slow down when something on the distant horizon caught his attention.","At first glance, it looked as though the crimson grass of the Fourth Valley had returned. However, upon closer inspection, it turned out to be something else entirely.","\"What is that...? A crimson sea?\" Lev asked aloud as he stared into the distance. \"No... it looks like... hair?\"","Upon closer inspection, the crimson \"grass\" turned out to be a vast sea of countless crimson threads that resembled strands of hair.","\"Goodness... We should still be in the Eighth Valley,\" Duk muttered, his body trembling as he stared at the crimson hair with clear unease. \"To think it has spread this far already...\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the crimson sea and asked, \"What exactly are we looking at?\"","\"Supreme Ruler Dena,\" Duk responded.","\"Excuse me?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow, convinced he had misheard.","\"You heard me right,\" Duk said grimly. \"That... is Supreme Ruler Dena. Not long after she arrived in the Final Valley, she began devouring everything within it and anything that entered her territory. Countless demons have already been consumed by her.\"","\"Wait here for a moment,\" Duk said before suddenly flying off somewhere.","Several minutes later, Duk returned with a magical beast in his grasp.","\"Watch this.\"","Duk threw the magical beast high into the air above the crimson sea.","As if they possessed a will of their own, the crimson hair shot upward, snatching the beast from the sky like a toad’s tongue striking a fly, piercing the prey the instant it was captured.","Once the prey was caught, the crimson hair pulled the magical beast inward, embracing it like the sea swallowing a ship, until it disappeared entirely.","After witnessing such a horrifying scene, Lev felt every hair on his body stand on end, his body trembling uncontrollably with fear.","\"As you can see, anything that tries to get close will be devoured,\" Duk sighed. \"Forget about meeting Supreme Ruler Dena. You’ll be consumed by her long before you even reach her in the Final Valley. Hell, even Absolute Gods would rather move to the Eighth Valley than deal with Supreme Ruler Dena.\"","Lev then said, \"He’s right, Yuan. This is beyond fighting True Gods. Let’s just turn around and give up on meeting Supreme Ruler Dena.\"","Yuan turned to face them and said with a calm smile, \"Sorry, but that is not an option for me.\"","\"Why are you so intent on meeting her, anyway? Now that she’s turned Forsaken, I doubt you’ll even be able to have a proper conversation.\"","\"I have my reasons.\"","Yuan looked at Lev and continued, \"Thanks for accompanying me all this way. It’ll be too dangerous for you to continue following me, so just wait here for my return.\"","\"Wait for your return...?\" Lev repeated in a daze.","In his heart, he was convinced that Yuan would never return if he entered Supreme Ruler Dena’s territory. Still, he couldn’t bring himself to say it out loud.","\"Trust me. I’ll come back.\"","Yuan said it as if he had read Lev’s thoughts.","Without waiting for their response, Yuan immediately flew into Supreme Ruler Dena’s territory.","\"My god! He’s actually doing it!\" Lev exclaimed in shock as he watched Yuan soar into the crimson sea.","The crimson hair attacked Yuan the moment he stepped into its territory, even though he was still hiding his presence with Shadow Veil.","\"So hiding my presence doesn’t matter...\" Yuan muttered.","Abandoning the attempt to conceal himself, he focused entirely on evasion as the crimson strands lunged at him without pause. When a single strike failed, the crimson hair adapted, attacking from every direction as its strands lashed toward him like countless grasping hands.","Before long, the attacks became too numerous for Yuan to dodge alone, forcing him to fight back.","Wielding the Demon Devouring Sword, he cut down every strand that approached him. But even with his Supreme Sword Aura, he found it surprisingly difficult to slice through the crimson hair, almost as if every strand of hair was a Celestial-grade treasure.","Meanwhile, Duk and Lev continued to watch from afar.","\"That lunatic is... smiling?\" Duk muttered in disbelief when he saw a smile forming on Yuan’s face amidst the relentless attacks."]},{"number":2371,"title":"Chapter 2371: Supreme Ruler Dena(2)","paragraphs":["\"He’s actually doing it! He’s crossing the crimson sea and advancing toward the Ninth Valley!\" Lev exclaimed, shock and awe written all over his face.","However, Duk shook his head. \"Most True Gods can do the same. The real problem is how long he can endure without making a single mistake. One slip is all it takes to cost him his life. And the closer he gets to Supreme Ruler Dena, the more aggressive the attacks become.\"","Days passed in the blink of an eye, and Yuan continued to advance toward the Ninth Valley without slowing down.","Eventually, he made it so far that Lev could no longer see him, even with divine sense.","\"I can’t see him anymore,\" Lev sighed.","\"I can still see him, and he’s the same as ever, wielding that weird and sharp energy.\"","Although the demons’ cultivation was far more advanced than that of the Nine Heavens, it didn’t mean they surpassed them in every aspect. One area they lacked was weapon auras. Demons rarely used conventional weapons, relying primarily on their own bodies, and any weapons they wielded were usually formed from their own blood.","As a result, while demons were aware of the existence of weapon auras, none of them had attempted to master them. To them, it was pointless, especially since ordinary weapons and their auras were incapable of killing them.","Days turned into weeks, and Supreme Ruler Dena’s attacks only grew more intense and powerful.","As for Yuan, he gradually increased his own power, almost as if he were deliberately matching the strength of her attacks.","Weeks turned into months, and unbeknownst to Yuan, he’d already entered the Ninth Valley and had begun approaching the Final Valley.","He’d also traveled so far that even Duk could no longer see him with divine sense.","\"Hey, Dena, can you hear me?!\" Yuan suddenly spoke out loud.","\"This reminds me of our first encounter!\"","\"When I first came to the Demonic Realm and didn’t understand the full situation, I went on an indiscriminate killing spree, slaughtering every demon I encountered. If it weren’t for you, I would have killed many more,\" Yuan said as he recalled his memories as Tian Chenyu.","When Tian Chenyu first entered the Demonic Realm and found himself surrounded by demons, he didn’t hesitate in the slightest. Without questioning anything, he began sealing and slaughtering every demon he saw, unaware that there was a distinction between ordinary demons and the Forsaken. To him, all demons were the same—and all of them had to be eliminated.","Tian Chenyu rampaged through the Demonic Realm like an unstoppable natural disaster. Only when Supreme Ruler Dena appeared to confront him did his indiscriminate slaughter finally cease.","That was also when Tian Chenyu learned the truth about the Forsaken—the demons who had invaded and terrorized his world—and the ordinary demons, who were no different from the people of the Divine Heaven.","[True Dragon Awakening!]","After spending a year inside the Ninth Valley, Supreme Ruler Dena’s attacks had grown so powerful that Yuan could no longer cut them down with Supreme Sword Aura alone, forcing him to activate True Dragon Awakening and use Chaotic Essence.","[Absolute Dragon Awakening!]","After another year, Yuan had to use Absolute Dragon Awakening just to defend against Supreme Ruler Dena’s attacks.","\"Damn it... just how much stronger have you become, Dena?!\" Yuan shouted as he began using Eternal Essence.","Despite being capable of killing True Gods with ease, he was barely able to keep up with Supreme Ruler Dena’s attacks—and he wasn’t even facing her true body, only a mere part of it: her hair.","However, Yuan wasn’t particularly surprised by this. After all, in the past, Supreme Ruler Dena was the only demon Tian Chenyu couldn’t defeat, even with all of his powers.","After traversing the Ninth Valley nonstop for three years and seeing nothing but Supreme Ruler Dena’s crimson hair, Yuan suddenly noticed something different on the distant horizon—a massive crimson sphere floating in the sky.","However, upon closer inspection, he realized that it wasn’t a sphere at all, but a gigantic cocoon-like structure woven from the same crimson hair.","As Yuan drew closer, the relentless attacks from the crimson hair suddenly ceased.","Then, before his eyes, the crimson strands twisted and intertwined, slowly shaping themselves into the figure of a woman.","Seeing this figure, Yuan tried speaking to it.","\"Hey, Dena. Do you recognize me?\"","\"...\"","\"Can you hear me?\"","\"...\"","\"It’s me, Tian Chenyu.\"","No matter how much Yuan tried to communicate with it, the figure remained silent.","\"Looks like I’ll have to wake you up by force, huh?\" Yuan sighed out loud.","Although it was faint—almost nonexistent—Yuan could sense a presence within the cocoon.","The next moment, he moved toward it, only to be immediately blocked by Supreme Ruler Dena’s clone.","\"Scram!\"","Yuan swung the Demon Devouring Sword, unleashing a burst of Eternal Essence.","In response, the clone swung its arm to meet the attack, exuding a similar aura.","Their energies collided, and to Yuan’s surprise, they perfectly canceled each other out.","’What was that?’ Yuan wondered, a slight frown appearing on his face.","The aura felt similar to Eternal Essence, but he could tell it wasn’t the same.","The next moment, Yuan attacked again without hesitation, unleashing Eternal Essence once more. As expected, the clone countered with that same strange energy.","This time, however, Yuan paid close attention and carefully analyzed it.","’Although it’s not real Eternal Essence, it’s a carefully recreated imitation of it,’ Yuan concluded after carefully analyzing the power, feeling astonished that Supreme Ruler Dena had managed to recreate Eternal Essence.","In order to imitate something, one had to understand it first. For Supreme Ruler Dena to imitate Eternal Essence meant that she had managed to grasp it to a certain degree—an astonishing feat, considering that only Eternals were capable of truly understanding and wielding it.","Even though her fake Eternal Essence wasn’t as powerful as the real thing, Supreme Ruler Dena had mastered it to such a degree that it could rival Yuan’s true Eternal Essence."]},{"number":2372,"title":"Chapter 2372: Supreme Ruler Dena’s World","paragraphs":["\"Good heavens, Dena... To recreate Eternal Essence like this...\" Yuan sighed in disbelief. \"I’m speechless.\"","He couldn’t help but wonder what had pushed her to recreate Eternal Essence, and how she had managed to understand it deeply enough to replicate it.","’Did she fight with an Eternal and somehow studied Eternal Essence that way? Or is she in contact with an Eternal?’ Yuan had many questions, but unless he dealt with the clone before him, he had no way of asking Supreme Ruler Dena these questions.","Unfortunately, Supreme Ruler Dena’s clone seemed to have no plan to let Yuan disturb the real her.","\"Looks like I’ll have to take this seriously...\" Yuan said as he took a deep breath and unleashed even more Eternal Essence.","Up until now, he had only been using about half of his strength. Now, he was raising it to nearly eighty percent.","The Eternal Essence radiating from Yuan became so intense that an invisible barrier formed around him, automatically repelling everything in its vicinity, including Supreme Ruler Dena’s crimson hair.","\"Let’s see if your fake Eternal Essence can withstand this!\" Yuan roared as he swung the Demon Devouring Sword toward the clone.","The clone’s aura skyrocketed in response, desperately trying to match Yuan’s power. Yet even as it pushed itself further, it still fell short of Yuan’s genuine Eternal Essence.","In the following second, Yuan’s sword tore through the clone’s arm like a knife through fragile threads, continuing through its body and splitting it in half.","But the Eternal Essence didn’t stop there. The overwhelming power instantly evaporated the clone, leaving nothing behind.","However, the instant the clone was destroyed, another one formed from the endless sea of crimson hair.","But it didn’t stop there. This time, two clones appeared, standing side by side as they blocked Yuan’s path to the cocoon.","Seeing this, Yuan pressed forward, cutting down every clone that stood in his way—both the two before him and any others that appeared to replace them.","Before long, he arrived in front of the cocoon.","When Yuan got close enough to the cocoon, the clones continued to spawn, but they no longer attacked him. Instead, they simply stood there and surrounded the cocoon in silence, quietly glaring at him with blank expressions.","Seeing that they weren’t attacking him, Yuan stopped paying attention to the clones and focused on the cocoon instead.","At first glance, the cocoon appeared to be made from the same hair-like material as the clones. However, upon closer inspection, it was several times more durable and was even reinforced by fake Eternal Essence.","After a moment of silence, Yuan raised the Demon Devouring Sword and swung it at the cocoon, unleashing eighty percent of his Eternal Essence.","A powerful ripple swept across the area when his sword collided with the cocoon. Yet even with such overwhelming power, Yuan was shocked to see that it remained completely unharmed, with not even a scratch appearing on its surface.","Yuan struck again, this time using ninety percent of his full strength.","A far more violent ripple erupted from the impact, shaking the entire cocoon. Even so, it remained unscathed.","Seeing this, Yuan paused for a moment, gathering as much Eternal Essence as he could before striking the cocoon for a third time.","The impact was so powerful that it blasted away the clones surrounding him.","When Yuan looked at the spot he had struck a moment later, he felt a brief sense of relief after noticing a small cut on the cocoon. However, that relief quickly vanished, as the damage repaired itself in less than a second, leaving the cocoon looking completely untouched once again.","Yuan closed his eyes and took a deep breath before unleashing a rapid series of strikes against the cocoon. However, no matter how quickly he attacked, the cocoon seemed to heal itself faster than he could damage it.","Moreover, it was far thicker than Yuan had anticipated, and despite his relentless assault, he had only managed to carve about thirty inches into it before it restored itself.","\"If this is how you want to play...\"","Yuan inhaled deeply before activating God of War’s Astral Arts, followed by Limitless Sword Domain.","Moments later, thousands of swords appeared in the sky. Infused with Eternal Essence and Supreme Sword Aura, they shot toward the cocoon with perfect precision, relentlessly striking the same point.","Meanwhile, Yuan advanced with his own blade, unleashing the Nine Supreme Swords, each strike more powerful than the previous one.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The entire Deprived Crimson Valley trembled as Yuan’s full prowess clashed against the crimson cocoon, shocking every exile within the valley.","Eventually, Yuan broke through the cocoon, leaving behind a small opening barely wide enough for him to pass through.","Without a moment of hesitation, he dashed forward and slipped inside just as the cocoon sealed itself once more.","When Yuan entered the cocoon, he was surprised to find an enormous space within.","From the outside, the cocoon was only four to five times larger than his own body, yet the interior stretched endlessly, as though he had stepped into another world.","\"This place must be Dena’s personal world...\" Yuan muttered as he immediately understood where he was.","The world looked quite similar to the Fourth Valley of the Deprived Crimson Valley—a vast, empty plain covered in crimson flowers and the same crimson hair that attacked him, though they didn’t react to his presence.","The sky above was dyed crimson as well, almost as if a god had been slain and its blood had spilled across the entire world.","Yuan didn’t wander and stayed still as he used his divine sense to look for Supreme Ruler Dena.","Several minutes later, Yuan started walking in a certain direction.","After walking for a short while, Yuan spotted a small pale figure in the distance.","The figure sat quietly on the ground, hugging her legs with slender arms while her face remained buried in her knees. Behind her stretched endless crimson hair, cascading like a boundless cape.","\"Dena...\"","Yuan muttered in a low voice before approaching her in slow, calm steps."]},{"number":2373,"title":"Chapter 2373: An Unfathomable Curse","paragraphs":["Even as Yuan slowly approached her, Supreme Ruler Dena remained completely motionless, as though she hadn’t noticed him at all.","Yuan, however, didn’t let his guard down. Despite her stillness, he approached cautiously. Even in silence, her body radiated an invisible but overwhelming aura of tyranny, not to mention the immense amount of natural killing intent that oozed from her very existence, likely a result of her killing and devouring countless demons since she was exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley.","Yuan stopped a few meters in front of Supreme Ruler Dena and called out in a soft, gentle voice, as if he was beckoning a child, \"Dena, can you hear me?\"","\"...\"","Silence.","He waited for a few more moments before taking another step.","\"Dena.\"","Once again, he was met with silence.","Yuan continued approaching her one step at a time until he stood right in front of her, remaining cautious the entire time and ready to attack or defend at a moment’s notice.","However, when he was standing only inches away from her, Supreme Ruler Dena remained motionless, her head buried in her knees.","After a moment of silence, Yuan suddenly sat down directly in front of her.","\"Dena,\" he called out to her again in a gentle voice. \"It’s me, Tian Chenyu.\"","\"...\"","Although Supreme Ruler Dena remained silent, Yuan sensed a subtle change within her aura—a faint fluctuation, almost as if she reacted to his name.","\"I don’t know why you’re doing all of this, but it’s time to wake up,\" Yuan continued speaking to her.","\"Remember our promise? Although I’m a bit late, I have returned to fulfill it.\"","The fluctuation became even stronger, but for some reason, Supreme Ruler Dena remained motionless.","Yuan suddenly narrowed his eyes, staring at her—or more specifically, into her.","He then reached out and gently touched her soft hand with a finger.","However, the very next moment, Yuan quickly pulled his hand back, which was now throbbing with pain.","He stared at his hand with raised eyebrows.","\"This is... a curse?\" he muttered.","Yuan could instinctively tell that a powerful curse was binding Supreme Ruler Dena, likely the reason she remained unresponsive. However, it was clearly no ordinary curse.","Strangely, despite not understanding it, the aura of the curse felt oddly familiar to him.","Yuan took out the Sacred Chalice of Purification and tried to remove the curse with it. However, getting her blood proved far more difficult than he expected.","Even though she remained completely still, Yuan had to exert all his strength just to make a small cut on her hand.","\"Her blood is... black...\" Yuan swallowed nervously when he saw it, the color completely different from what he remembered.","However, an even greater shock came when Supreme Ruler Dena’s blood was absorbed by the Sacred Chalice of Purification.","The treasure suddenly trembled violently, and cracks began to appear across its surface.","<Sacred Chalice of Purification has been damaged!>","\"Ah?!\"","Yuan cried out in disbelief. He never expected the curse binding Supreme Ruler Dena to be so powerful that it would damage the Sacred Chalice of Purification.","Although the outcome was disastrous and unexpected, it wasn’t entirely futile since he could feel that the curse binding her had weakened significantly afterward.","\"Looks like I won’t be able to use this thing until I get it fixed...\" Yuan sighed.","After putting away the damaged Sacred Chalice of Purification, Yuan returned his focus to Supreme Ruler Dena.","A moment later, Yuan reached out and touched her hand again. The pain immediately surged back, and he could feel the curse devouring his longevity as if trying to replenish the power it had lost.","Seeing this, Yuan quickly realized that the curse was a living one—requiring energy to sustain itself, as well as growing stronger over time.","\"Is the calamity outside caused by this damn curse trying to grow itself?\" Yuan muttered after realizing this possibility.","\"This curse might not even be a curse at all... but an organism—a parasite!\"","Realizing this, Yuan immediately infused his spiritual energy into Supreme Ruler Dena’s body and began examining every inch of it.","Despite her petite appearance, the inside of her body was incredibly vast, much like the space within the cocoon, almost as if it were its own world.","Yuan spent days searching through her body before finally discovering the source of the problem.","Hidden deep within her dantian, he found a grotesque mass of flesh tethered to her core, constantly siphoning Supreme Ruler Dena’s energy and converting it into its own strength.","It was unlike anything Yuan had ever seen. However, he remembered hearing a theory in the past that powerful curses could eventually evolve into living entities—much like how Soul Weapons could awaken their own consciousness and give birth to a spirit.","\"So it’s actually possible for a curse to evolve... What an unsettling existence...\" Yuan narrowed his eyes at the parasite-like curse, which looked like a caterpillar sealed inside a cocoon, waiting for the day it would transform and emerge.","Just as Yuan prepared to attack the curse before it could fully evolve, the curse sensed him, and a massive eye suddenly opened up on the lump of flesh.","Moments later, numerous smaller eyes opened across the fleshy mass. At the same time, a large mouth split open beneath them, drooling with dark, viscous blood.","\"Who... are... you?\"","The curse spoke in a chilling voice with an eerie tone.","\"My identity doesn’t matter,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"But I can tell you why I’m here.\"","\"Oh...?\"","\"I’m here to get rid of you, you disgusting parasite.\"","\"Get rid... of me...? Why...?\"","\"Not only do you not belong here, but you’re feeding off my friend while wreaking havoc outside. Just how many beings have you devoured to strengthen yourself?\"","\"Do you mean... the host...? This was... something... she... brought upon... herself...\"","\"What the hell are you talking about?\" Yuan asked with a frown.","\"If she hadn’t... devoured me... If she had just allowed me... to be born properly...!\" the curse snarled with hatred in its voice, leaving Yuan stunned into silence."]},{"number":2374,"title":"Chapter 2374: Consuming the Curse","paragraphs":["\"Wait... Wait a second...\" Yuan had to do a double-take after hearing the curse’s unexpected declaration, which confused the hell out of him, as the curse made it sound like it was a baby that was consumed before it could be born.","\"She devoured you? Before you were born? Are you not a curse? If no, what in Heaven’s name are you?\" Yuan asked.","\"I am... a curse now... as I cursed her... right before my death,\" said the curse.","\"But before I became one... and before she... consumed me... I was ... in the process of being born...\"","\"Had I been... born... I would have... become... an... Eternal!\"","\"?!?!\"","Yuan’s eyes widened with shock and disbelief after learning the curse’s true identity—that Supreme Ruler Dena had actually consumed an Eternal before it could be born!","This explained why Supreme Ruler Dena was able to recreate Eternal Essence without being an Eternal herself, and why Yuan felt familiar with the curse’s aura.","\"However... I will not... allow myself... to die... so easily...!\" The curse continued.","\"I will... consume every... living being... in this world... and be reborn...!\"","The curse stared at Yuan and said, \"I can sense... Eternal Essence... emitting from you...\"","\"Help me... and I will... grant you any... wish...!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the curse.","’Does it think I am an Eternal because I can use Eternal Essence?’","Suddenly, an idea came to Yuan.","Rather than attempting to destroy the curse while it was still inside Supreme Ruler Dena—risking her life in the process—Yuan realized there was another option.","It was a method that would guarantee her safety... but it would be incredibly reckless for him.","\"Sure, I’ll help you, but I don’t need anything from you. After all, we’re both Eternals. It’s only right to help out a fellow comrade,\" Yuan spoke with a smile on his face.","The eyes on the mass of lump grinned into a crescent, clearly very happy to hear that Yuan was willing to help it.","\"However, I will need you to do something first in order for me to help you.\"","\"What is... it...?\"","Yuan extended his arm toward it and said, \"Leave your current host and use me as a vessel instead!\"","\"What...?\"","The curse looked at him with wide eyes, unable to comprehend why Yuan would make such a suggestion.","\"Listen carefully. How close are you to completing your rebirth right now?\" Yuan asked.","The curse fell silent for a moment before replying, \"I am about... thirty percent... done.\"","Yuan shook his head and released a pitiful sigh.","\"And how long have you been doing this? Tens of billions of years? At this rate, not only will it take you forever to finish, but I doubt you’ll even succeed in being reborn.\"","\"What...!?\"","\"Why are you surprised?\" Yuan chuckled. \"What do you think is the most important for Eternals?\"","\"Eternal Essence!\" Yuan answered before the curse could respond.","\"Even if you consumed every living being on this world, you would lack the necessary Eternal Essence to be reborn. However, if you enter my body and use me as a host, I will be able to gather and feed you Eternal Essence.\"","\"Oh... oh... OH...!\" The curse exclaimed with excitement after hearing Yuan’s logical explanation.","\"You are... amazing...!\"","\"Very well... I shall... enter your body... now...\"","The next moment, Yuan felt the curse begin transferring from Supreme Ruler Dena’s body into his own.","The process only took a few minutes, but to Yuan, it felt as though days had passed. Throughout the entire ordeal, he had to endure immense, searing pain that felt like someone was injecting lava into his veins.","<??? has invaded your body>","<??? has taken root within your Dantian>","\"Your body is... a little smaller... but... it’s much more... comfortable...!\" The curse remarked shortly after entering his Dantian.","\"Oh...? What is... this...?\"","It was also intrigued by the nearby Spirit Tree.","The very next moment—","<Spirit Tree has sensed ???>","<Spirit Tree temporarily emerges from hibernation>","<Spirit Tree has begun to absorb ???>","\"W-WHAT IS... HAPPENING...?!\"","The curse cried out loud when the Spirit Tree’s roots suddenly attacked it and began draining it of its energy.","’Oh?’","Yuan was pleasantly surprised to see the Spirit Tree waking up to absorb the curse even without needing him to do anything. He’d initially planned on absorbing the curse himself, but if the Spirit Tree was going to do all of the work, he was fine with that, as well.","’You...! You... lied... to me...!\"","The curse immediately started fighting back, slowly overpowering the Spirit Tree.","Seeing this, Yuan decided to step in and started attacking the curse with Eternal Essence.","\"Why...?! Why are you... attacking me...?!\"","\"I thought... we were... comrades...?!\"","The curse shouted.","\"Comrades?\" Yuan sneered. \"Although you and I have no enmity for you, I am not an Eternal.\"","\"What...?! Then how... can you... use... Eternal Essence...?!\"","\"You have no need for that knowledge since you’ll also turn into my Eternal Essence soon.\"","\"No...! I... curse you...!\"","\"Good luck with that!\" Yuan laughed out loud as he continued weakening the curse and refining it into his own Eternal Essence at the same time.","However, the process took much longer than Yuan had anticipated.","The curse, although weak and only thirty percent completed, was still tens of billions of years old with immense energy from consuming countless demons.","One year... five years... twenty years...","It’d taken Yuan nearly thirty years to finish refining the curse.","\"I will... return... one day...\"","The curse muttered its last words before it was completely absorbed by Yuan.","<Spirit Tree has returned to hibernation>","<Spirit Tree has entered deep hibernation>","<You have refined an incompleted Eternal>","<Your Eternal Essence has improved significantly!>","<You have learned the Skill ’Curse Creation’>","After examining his condition, Yuan discovered that his Eternal Essence had strengthened by at least triple after consuming the curse. It was an immense gain considering how little effort it took him.","\"So this is what it feels like to consume an Eternal, huh? To think I’d grow this much from an Eternal that wasn’t even fully born.\" Yuan started wondering how much stronger he’d get if he were to refine a completed Eternal.","After finishing, Yuan slowly opened his eyes.","Immediately, he was met with a pair of beautiful crimson eyes, gleaming like two ruby jewels just inches from his face.","\"Hey, Dena. How are you feeling?\" Yuan asked her with a calm smile on his face.","\"...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena had awakened, and she was crouched directly in front of him, her crimson eyes fixed on Yuan as if she were examining him.","\"Tian... Chenyu?\" she muttered in a low voice, sounding as if she was doubting her own eyes.","\"I was Tian Chenyu, but that was long ago. Now, I am simply Yuan.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena nodded and then said, \"Were you the one who woke me up from that everlasting nightmare?\"","\"What do you think? Who else besides me is here?\"","A warm smile tugged at Supreme Ruler Dena’s lips, causing her already ethereal beauty to shine even more radiantly.","\"I have a lot of questions for you,\" Yuan said.","\"As do I,\" said Dena. \"But you may ask your questions first.\"","Yuan nodded and proceeded to ask about the Eternal.","\"You... consumed an Eternal before it was born? How does that work? And why did you do it?\"","Supreme Ruler Dena pondered her answer for a moment before speaking, \"That’s right. I sensed a familiar energy appearing somewhere in the void, so I went to investigate it, thinking it was you.\"","\"But when I arrived, it turned out to be something else entirely. It was some kind of crystal, and it emitted an energy that I could not comprehend, so I ate it.\"","\"You ate it just like that? Have you ever considered the consequences?\" Yuan asked, even though he had no right to lecture someone else about their eating habits.","She calmly shrugged before continuing, \"I thought I would be able to acquire that power after consuming it, but alas, even though I was able to comprehend it to a certain extent, I was unable to wield it.\"","\"But you were able to replicate it. How did you do that?\"","Supreme Ruler Dena raised an eyebrow and asked, \"What are you talking about?\"","\"You... don’t remember? I fought with your clones not long ago, and they were able to wield an energy similar to Eternal Essence.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena then said, \"My memories are still a bit blurry since I’ve only just woken up.\"","\"Well, what do you remember?\"","\"That I consumed the crystal and returned home. But anything after that is a haze.\"","\"Is that so...\" Yuan muttered.","\"It’s my turn to ask some questions,\" Supreme Ruler Dena then said.","\"Where are we?\" she then asked.","\"Huh? When did you wake up?\" Yuan asked.","\"Shortly after you removed that thing inside me.\"","\"And you haven’t bothered to go outside even once?\"","\"No. I didn’t want to leave your side,\" she calmly replied, leaving him speechless."]},{"number":2375,"title":"Chapter 2375: Supreme Ruler Dena’s Awakening","paragraphs":["\"You didn’t want to leave me alone? What am I, a child who cannot be left alone?\" Yuan shook his head at her reasoning, but a smile tugged at his face.","\"By the way, we’re inside the Deprived Crimson Valley. The Final Valley, at that.\"","\"...Is that so?\" said Supreme Ruler Dena, seemingly not surprised by their location.","\"You’re not surprised? Do you remember being exiled?\" Yuan inquired with a raised eyebrow.","She shook her head.","\"I think I vaguely remember something like that. Not that it matters. I can leave this place whenever I want, anyway.\"","\"Because you were given the title of Supreme Ruler, right? Now that I think about it, you might be the first Supreme Ruler to be exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley,\" Yuan remarked.","\"Probably,\" she calmly replied with a nonchalant look on her face, almost as if she couldn’t care less about such an achievement.","\"Now, back to my questions.\"","\"You... Why have you returned to this world?\" Supreme Ruler Dena’s expression suddenly turned serious as her crimson eyes stared directly into his.","Yuan sighed before replying, \"To be honest, it wasn’t my intention. I ended up here by accident.\"","\"So you don’t have any business with our world... or our people?\" she continued to ask, clearly seeking reassurance.","\"Don’t worry, I have already promised not to interfere with the people of this world as long as you don’t invade my world again.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena nodded and said, \"As long as I am here, such a thing will never occur again.\"","\"You mean as long as you are the Supreme Ruler. Unfortunately, since you have been exiled for some reason, we have a new Supreme Ruler,\" Yuan sighed.","\"So what if I had been exiled and replaced? I can simply reclaim my position by getting rid of the current Supreme Ruler.\"","\"...\"","’Despite her calm voice and cute face, she’s saying some awfully terrible thing,’ Yuan sighed inwardly. However, he was already used to her character, so it wasn’t too surprising.","\"If you do that, you’ll become a tyrannical ruler. Do you remember what happened to the last one who tried to rule with absolute authority?\" Yuan said a moment later.","\"Then what should I do?\" she asked him.","\"Before we even consider anything, we need to figure out the reason behind your exile. I thought it was because you had turned into Forsaken at first because of what I was told, but that’s clearly not the case.\"","\"Me? A Forsaken? Ridiculous,\" she quietly sneered in disdain at whoever made up such a bold lie.","\"Honestly, I wouldn’t blame them if they thought you had turned Forsaken. After all, you were being controlled by that curse.\"","\"...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena fell silent, as she had no excuses for that.","\"Anyway, are you ready to leave this place?\" Yuan then asked.","Supreme Ruler Dena stood up and replied, \"Yes.\"","Yuan also got off the ground and did a quick stretch. The next moment, Supreme Ruler Dena withdrew her personal domain, sending them back to the world outside.","When they returned to the Final Valley, Yuan was stunned by the barren landscape that stretched before him.","The crimson sea was gone, but it had already consumed all life that once existed there.","\"...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena stared silently at the barren land for a moment before asking quietly, \"Am I responsible for this?\"","Yuan didn’t try to sugarcoat his answer. \"Even if it wasn’t by your own will, you are technically responsible.\"","After another moment of silence, Supreme Ruler Dena lifted her palm above the lifeless land and let a single drop of her now-crimson blood fall to the ground.","In the next instant, a powerful ripple spread outward, restoring the land’s lost life force and breathing new vitality into it.","The land, which had remained dead for billions of years, suddenly came back to life as crimson grass and weirdly shaped trees began to grow rapidly.","\"Where do you want to go?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked after taking a moment to admire her own work.","\"The Eighth Valley. I have some people waiting for me there.\"","Without another word, Supreme Ruler Dena grabbed Yuan’s hand and took a step forward.","In the next instant, Yuan was pulled into a different dimension.","’Void Manipulation!’","He immediately recognized the power she had used, and it was several levels more advanced than his own.","In mere moments, they arrived at the border between the Eighth and Ninth Valleys—something that had taken Yuan several years to traverse before.","Seeing how convenient Void Manipulation was, Yuan decided to master it as soon as possible.","Meanwhile, Lev, who had been hiding not far away, suddenly sensed Yuan’s presence return.","\"This presence... he’s back!?\"","Realizing whose presence it belonged to, Lev hurried out of his hiding place, unable to hide his excitement.","However, his excitement quickly turned into shock and terror when he noticed the beautiful young woman standing beside Yuan.","She possessed a slender and modest figure, her head almost reaching Yuan’s chest, and she looked as though she had only recently reached adulthood. Her pale skin, long crimson hair, and sharp crimson eyes made her appearance both striking and unsettling.","Yet the most frightening thing about her was the terrifying aura she emitted, one that could not be hidden—not that she was trying to hide it in the first place.","\"S-S-Supreme Ruler Dena?!?!\" Lev cried out loud, not daring to believe his eyes.","When he saw her, he subconsciously turned around and started running away, even though Yuan was also with her.","\"Where do you think you’re going?\"","Yuan immediately activated Demon Sealing Zone to prevent Lev from running away without hurting him.","\"Please spare my life!\" Lev cried as tears literally flowed from his eyes.","\"Calm down. Nobody is trying to take your pitiful life.\" Yuan sighed out loud, but Lev continued pleading for his life, as if he couldn’t hear Yuan.","\"Who is this weirdo?\" Supreme Ruler Dena questioned Yuan about his relationship with this odd individual.","\"A friend I made along the way to meet you,\" he replied with a weak smile."]},{"number":2376,"title":"Chapter 2376: Leaving Deprived Crimson Valley","paragraphs":["When Lev refused to calm down even after his movements were restricted by the Demon Sealing Zone, Yuan realized he had no choice but to take more drastic measures.","Without hesitation, he summoned the Swords of Eternal Torment and impaled Lev with a single blade, unleashing intense agony upon him like brutal shock therapy.","\"Ah! I’m dying!\" Lev screamed after experiencing physical pain for the first time.","However, as the agony persisted and he realized that he wasn’t actually dying, he slowly turned toward Yuan and begged, \"P-Please...\"","Yuan deactivated the techniques and asked, \"Have you finally calmed down a little?\"","Lev nodded, but when his gaze noticed Supreme Ruler Dena again, his body started to tremble uncontrollably.","\"I-I’m sorry... I don’t know what’s happening to my body... It’s not listening to me...\" Lev said as he struggled to stop himself from running away again.","Yuan glanced at Supreme Ruler Dena and sighed. \"I completely forgot that your presence can terrorize others. Can you do something about it like before?\"","\"What a pain in the ass,\" she muttered before suppressing her presence.","However, even after Supreme Ruler Dena suppressed all of her presence, the aura naturally emitted by her soul could not be completely concealed, not to mention her naturally cold gaze.","Although he no longer felt the overwhelming urge to flee, Lev’s body continued to tremble slightly.","\"You’ll get used to it,\" Yuan said to him.","Lev nodded and quickly bowed to Supreme Ruler Dena. \"I-I apologize for my earlier reaction. It was disrespectful of me. This lowly subject greets the Supreme Ruler.\"","\"...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena remained silent, not even bothering to acknowledge his greeting.","Lev didn’t mind in the slightest.","Genuinely.","In the Demonic Realm, the Supreme Rulers stood above all, and they rarely spared even a glance at those beneath them. For her to simply look in his direction without turning away was already an immense honor.","Of course, Yuan also knew of this, so he didn’t mention it.","\"Lev, where’s Duck?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","\"Oh... he left shortly after he could no longer see you, saying that it would only be a waste of time to wait for your return,\" Lev sighed.","\"Well, I can’t blame him for that,\" Yuan said with a slight chuckle. \"Then why did you stay?\"","Lev scratched the back of his head awkwardly. \"To be frank with you, I would’ve left if I could. But with my cultivation, there’s no way I’d make it back alone. So my only options were to wait for your return... or wait for death to come for me here.\"","\"Sorry...\" Yuan couldn’t help but pity Lev.","\"You have no reason to apologize. I was the one who decided to follow you here while knowing full well that I would probably never return alive.\"","Yuan then said to Supreme Ruler Dena, \"He’s going to leave the Deprived Crimson Valley with us.\"","In response, she gave a simple head nod.","The next moment, without warning, Supreme Ruler Dena casually tore open the space before her with a single motion of her arm and stepped forward, pulling Yuan with her.","Lev was dragged along as well, though far less elegantly, carried by her spiritual energy like a piece of luggage.","Several moments later, they emerged from the void.","While Supreme Ruler Dena and Yuan landed gracefully, Lev fell face-first onto the ground.","As he scrambled back to his feet and surveyed his surroundings, his eyes widened in shock when he realized they were already at the First Valley.","\"This is... the First Valley?!\"","The only reason he realized this so quickly was because of the sight before him.","A massive semi-transparent barrier that stretched across the horizon, surrounding the entire Deprived Crimson Valley and keeping the exiles imprisoned within.","The barrier had existed for longer than anyone could remember. Some even believed it had been formed by nature itself when the world was first created.","Every demon ever exiled to the Deprived Crimson Valley had attempted to break through it at least once, but no matter how much time passed, the barrier remained untouched and unscarred.","Because of this, it came to be known as \"The Invincible Wall.\"","Seeing the barrier, Lev couldn’t help but recall the numerous times he had tried—and failed—to break through it.","The Invincible Wall wasn’t just indestructible. It even prevented those capable of using Void Manipulation from passing through.","It was, without question, the perfect barrier.","\"So, how are you going to get us out of here?\" Yuan asked as he stared at the barrier. \"I doubt I will be able to crack it even with my full strength.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena calmly replied, \"Only those who have been given the title of Supreme Ruler are allowed to control the barrier.\"","\"Will it work even if you are no longer the Supreme Ruler?\"","\"It’s not just a title, you know,\" she said. \"Although anyone can claim to be one, only those who have undergone the ritual and experienced the process are considered a true Supreme Ruler.\"","\"During that ritual, we are granted the authority to govern this world through our souls. One such authority is control over the Invincible Wall. The only way for that power to be removed is through the same ritual... or true death.\"","\"And since I can still sense that authority within me, there should be no problem.\"","\"Is that so? In that case, I’ll leave it to you.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena nodded before shifting her gaze to the Invincible Wall.","Suddenly, the word ’Authority’ manifested on her forehead, emitting a soft but profound crimson glow.","She then gently tapped the surface of the Invincible Wall.","In the next instant, as if obeying her command, the barrier parted, creating an opening just large enough for three people to walk through.","Without saying a word, Supreme Ruler Dena calmly stepped through the barrier and then turned to look back at them.","Yuan followed her without hesitation.","Lev, however, remained frozen for a brief moment, as if needing to confirm he wasn’t dreaming before finally stepping forward."]},{"number":2377,"title":"Chapter 2377: Demon God’s Wrath","paragraphs":["After leaving the Deprived Crimson Valley, Supreme Ruler Dena looked at Yuan and asked, \"What now?\"","\"Before we decide what we want to do, I need to know what you plan on doing now, Lev.\" Yuan turned to face Lev, who stood still with a dumbfounded look on his face, almost as if he was still having trouble believing that he was outside of the Deprived Crimson Valley.","However, he quickly snapped out of it and said, \"Although I am grateful to you for helping me leave the Deprived Crimson Valley, it won’t change the fact that I am still an exile, and that my soul is still branded as one. But that won’t stop me from avenging my family!\"","Yuan then asked Supreme Ruler Dena, \"Can you do something about the branding with your Authority?\"","She calmly nodded and pointed a finger at Lev.","\"...\"","Lev swallowed nervously, wondering what she was going to do to him.","The ’Authority’ symbol appeared on Supreme Ruler Dena’s forehead again, and the next second, a single strand of her crimson hair suddenly shot toward Lev’s forehead, penetrating his skin like it was wet paper and striking his soul.","\"It’s done,\" she calmly said as she retrieved her hair.","\"What...?\"","Lev wore a blank look on his face, as if he didn’t even realize what she’d done to him. In fact, it happened so fast that he wasn’t even able to react!","\"Congratulations, Lev. You’re no longer an exile,\" Yuan said with a faint smile.","Before Lev could respond, Yuan continued, \"I won’t tell you how to live your life, but I wouldn’t recommend dedicating it entirely to revenge. I’ve lived that way before, and it leads nowhere good.\"","Lev lowered his head to stare at the ground for a moment before responding in a low voice, \"Then what else am I supposed to do?\"","\"I survived the Deprived Crimson Valley for so long because of my desire to avenge my family. However, now that I think about it, with how much time has passed, I doubt I will even be able to find the person who killed them—if they’re even still alive.\"","Yuan then spoke, \"If you don’t know what you want to do, why don’t you continue following us for now and think it over? Perhaps you might find a new purpose in life. That said, I cannot guarantee your safety.\"","Lev didn’t need to spend much time pondering about Yuan’s offer and quickly nodded, \"If you don’t mind having me, it’d be an honor to continue being by your side.\"","\"Now then...\" Yuan looked at Supreme Ruler Dena and said, \"Let’s figure out why you were exiled first before we decide on anything.\"","\"How are we going to do that?\"","\"We can ask around—\"","\"Please don’t do that.\" Lev suddenly interrupted.","\"Have you forgotten? We are prohibited from mentioning her name outside the Deprived Crimson Valley,\" he reminded Yuan.","\"So what? It’s not like such rules have never been broken before.\"","However, instead of Lev, Supreme Ruler Dena spoke, \"No, he’s right. If the current Supreme Ruler prohibited my name from being mentioned, anyone who utters it—even if nobody is listening—will be struck by the Demon God’s Wrath.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this information, wondering if this Demon God’s Wrath was akin to Heavenly Tribulation in his world, where those who defy the Heavenly Laws will be punished.","\"This is my first time hearing about such a thing,\" he remarked.","\"What? How is that even possible?\" Lev stared at Yuan in disbelief. \"The Demon God’s Wrath is basic common sense. Even a newborn knows about it.\"","\"Oh, right.\" Yuan glanced at him and smiled. \"Since you’ll continue traveling with us from now on, I should probably catch you up on a few things.\"","\"First of all, I am not from this world.\"","\"Huh?\" Lev’s eyes widened as he tried to comprehend Yuan’s words.","However, Yuan wasn’t done, and he continued to bombard Lev with more shocking revelations.","\"Not only do I not belong to this world, but I’m also not a demon. I’m actually a human. That’s why there are many things about this world that I don’t know,\" Yuan revealed.","\"Although I visited this place before, it’s been so long that most of my knowledge is probably no longer reliable.\"","\"...\"","After several moments of silence, Lev finally spoke in a nervous tone, \"I knew you were strange, but to think you’re actually from the world of countless legends... the Divine Heaven!\"","He continued, \"I read in some ancient history books that the Forsaken used to be sent there to save resources and space, but for some reason, that practice stopped.\"","\"Ahem.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly cleared her throat loudly before speaking. \"That’s not correct. We didn’t send the Forsaken to the Divine Heaven. At the time, we weren’t even aware of its existence. We only believed we were sending the Forsaken somewhere into the boundless void.\"","\"It wasn’t until a certain individual appeared in our world and began wreaking havoc that we realized the truth—and the consequences of our careless actions,\" she continued with a soft sigh, her crimson eyes staring directly at Yuan with a somewhat apologetic gaze.","\"Is that so...? I was born after that period, so I had no idea.\"","\"Hm? If you’re not from our world, then what were you doing inside the Deprived Crimson Valley? In fact, how the hell did you even get inside?\" Lev turned to look at Yuan and asked.","Yuan shrugged and said, \"I came here by accident.\"","\"Seriously...? Then you’re incredibly lucky that Supreme Ruler—\"","Lev abruptly sealed his mouth with his hands when he realized that he had nearly committed a serious offense and invoked Demon God’s Wrath.","\"That was close. I almost uttered something I shouldn’t have.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at his reaction. Then, after a moment of silence, he said, \"Lev, move away from me. You too, Dena.\"","\"What are you trying to do?\" Lev asked with a puzzled face.","He smiled and calmly replied, \"I want to see for myself the prowess of the Demon God’s Wrath and whether it’s truly threatening or not.\"","\"You want to purposefully invoke Demon God’s Wrath?! Are you insane?!\" Lev cried out loud.","Then, without hesitation, he distanced himself from Yuan, moving so far away that he turned into a tiny black dot in the distance.","\"Are you really going to do it?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked.","Although her words sounded concerned, her face remained completely calm.","\"The Demon God’s Wrath is unfathomably powerful, and depending on the severity of your crime, it could even exterminate a True God,\" she explained.","Yuan nodded, \"I will be fine.\"","Without another word, Supreme Ruler Dena distanced herself from Yuan. However, unlike Lev, she moved only several meters back and remained very much in view.","Yuan took a deep breath before mumbling in a low voice, \"Supreme Ruler Dena.\"","He immediately prepared to confront the Demon God’s Wrath after uttering her name.","\"...\"","However, nothing happened even a few seconds later, prompting Yuan to try again, this time louder.","\"Supreme Ruler Dena,\" he spoke in a normal tone.","When nothing happened again, he shouted loudly, \"SUPREME RULER DENA!\"","Yet, even after waiting for many moments, the Demon God’s Wrath never occurred.","\"What the hell?\" Yuan cursed out loud before turning to look at Lev. \"Are you sure it’s forbidden to say her name?\"","Lev’s head popped out from behind a tree as he replied, \"Of course! I remember very clearly when the Supreme Ruler publicly announced it, as well as the hundreds of Demon God’s Wrath that followed!\"","\"Then why isn’t it coming after me? Is it because I don’t belong to this world, so its rules don’t apply to me?\" he wondered out loud.","\"Seriously...?\" Lev mumbled in a dumbfounded voice, suddenly feeling an urge to test it out himself.","However, before he could do so, Supreme Ruler Dena beat him to the punch, speaking in a calm voice, \"Supreme Ruler Dena.\"","The very next moment, Yuan sensed a sudden change in the surrounding atmosphere, sending a faint shiver down his body.","\"This feeling...\"","He subconsciously lifted his head to look at the sky, and sure enough, there was a reaction above. The clouds had darkened and twisted into a swirling vortex that resembled the eye of a hurricane.","Then, from the very center of that eye, a massive crimson beam suddenly descended.","Unsurprisingly, its target was Supreme Ruler Dena.","The beam was so massive that Yuan had to retreat to avoid being caught in it.","And the moment he exited its range, the beam struck Supreme Ruler Dena without mercy, completely engulfing her figure in its massive crimson light.","The Demon God’s Wrath lasted only a little over a second, yet in that brief moment, it carved a massive crater into the ground—so deep that its depths were swallowed in pitch-black darkness.","Meanwhile, Supreme Ruler Dena was nowhere to be seen, as if she had been completely vaporized by the attack."]},{"number":2378,"title":"Chapter 2378: Demise Ravine","paragraphs":["\"M-My god! Don’t tell me she’s dead?!\" Lev approached the hole after witnessing the Demon God’s Wrath strike Supreme Ruler Dena with enough prowess to completely obliterate a True God with ease.","However, Yuan remained calm as he looked down the pitch-black hole and asked, \"Hey, are you hurt?\"","A few moments later, Yuan and Lev watched as a crimson sphere slowly rose from the crater.","It was Supreme Ruler Dena, her entire figure concealed beneath her crimson hair, which wrapped tightly around her body like a protective barrier.","Once she landed, the hair slowly retracted, revealing that she was completely unharmed.","\"What do you think?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked Yuan, acting like nothing out of the ordinary had just occurred.","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"It’s a little more powerful than I expected. Not only that, but I could sense a hint of Eternal Essence within that attack just now.\"","\"Eternal Essence...\" Supreme Ruler Dena raised an eyebrow.","\"What is Eternal Essence? I feel like I have heard it before,\" she suddenly asked.","\"What?\" Yuan stared at her with wide eyes. \"You don’t know?\"","He figured that with her prowess and experience, she would’ve already been aware of Eternals and their power.","\"That power you sensed from the crystal you consumed. That’s Eternal Essence,\" he gave a brief explanation.","He then emitted a little Eternal Essence just to let her see it again.","\"This is Eternal Essence.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena gazed at the unique aura emanating from him, her crimson eyes flickering with intrigue and excitement, seemingly mesmerized.","\"How did you acquire that power?\" she quickly asked.","She consumed the crystal without knowing its identity because she wanted to acquire its power, but it backfired on her.","\"How...? It’s a long story, so let’s save it for later.\"","\"Why? We have time,\" she said.","\"Um...\" Lev suddenly interrupted. \"We should probably get out of here as soon as possible. Not only did we escape from the Deprived Crimson Valley, but we even invoked Demon God’s Wrath.\"","\"Lev’s right. Let’s leave before we give ourselves into unnecessary trouble.\"","Without another word, Yuan picked a random direction and started flying away.","Lev immediately followed, with Supreme Ruler Dena being the last to leave.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the Demonic Realm, a messenger approached a fully cloaked figure and said, \"Supreme Ruler, we have a situation.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"We have just received reports that the one who dwelled within the Final Valley of the Deprived Crimson Valley has vanished. Someone also invoked Demon God’s Wrath right outside the Invincible Wall.\"","The Supreme Ruler turned to face the messenger and asked, \"Are you telling me the ’9th’ had left the Deprived Crimson Valley and invoked Demon God’s Wrath so soon afterward?\"","\"We’re not certain if she had really left the Deprived Crimson Valley, but we can never be too careful. It’s that monster we’re talking about, after all.\"","\"The ’9th’ has spent tens of billions of years inside the Final Valley without leaving that area. Why would she suddenly leave the Deprived Crimson Valley now? Investigate it immediately,\" commanded the Supreme Ruler.","\"I have already sent some people to investigate the Demon God’s Wrath. As for the situation inside the Deprived Crimson Valley, that will take a little longer...\"","\"What should we do if it turns out that she’d really left the Deprived Crimson Valley?\"","\"...\"","The Supreme Ruler remained silent for an entire minute before responding, \"If we allow a monster like her to roam our world, who knows how much longer it’ll last.\"","\"Don’t worry, if it really comes down to it, I’ll deal with her myself.\"","\"Yes, Supreme Ruler.\"","Shortly after Yuan and his group left, several True Gods arrived at their location to investigate the cause of the Demon God’s Wrath.","\"I can’t believe they sent five whole True Gods to investigate a mere Demon God’s Wrath,\" one of them remarked as they arrived.","\"What a waste of time. Whoever invoked it is definitely already dead,\" said another.","\"I have never seen a Demon God’s Wrath cause such destruction before. Whoever invoked it must have been either really powerful or did something unfathomably evil.\"","\"Likely the latter. Only an Absolute God would be powerful enough to invoke such a strong reaction, but none of them would be foolish enough to offend the Demon God.\"","The True Gods barely investigated the scene before leaving to report that nothing was out of the ordinary.","At the same time, Yuan and his group arrived at a new location.","\"Where are we?\" Yuan asked, his gaze fixed on the eerie landscape before him.","Lev answered in a subdued voice, \"The Deprived Crimson Valley is bordered by four dangerous regions—the Death Desert in the south, the Forest of Entrapment in the north, the Sea of Death in the west, and the Demise Ravine... which is where we are now.\"","\"The Demise Ravine, huh? I’ve heard of it,\" Yuan remarked as Tian Chenyu’s memories resurfaced in his mind.","Although he had never personally visited the Demise Ravine before, he was familiar with its infamous reputation—a perilous land where powerful spiritual beings, similar to ghosts, roamed freely.","These ghost-like entities were known as Nether Wraiths. Not only did they possess spectral appearances, but they were also immune to physical attacks, making them troublesome opponents for demons, who mostly relied on their own blood as weapons.","It didn’t help that spiritual techniques were extremely rare in the Demonic Realm. Although demons could still use their Soul Strength to attack, they could only release it outward in a crude manner, like expending spiritual energy without any technique behind it. It was both incredibly inefficient and lacking in power.","\"Um... do you think it’s possible to just use Void Manipulation and skip this entire place? This place is arguably even more dangerous than the Deprived Crimson Valley itself...\" Lev suggested out loud as he looked at Yuan, while his eyes would glance at Supreme Ruler Dena, not daring to actually ask her.","Supreme Ruler Dena then said, \"Using Void Manipulation is too tiring.\"","Although she didn’t outright reject the idea, it was basically the same thing.","\"Even though you used it inside the Deprived Crimson Valley...?\" Lev mumbled in a dumbfounded voice.","Yuan smiled and said, \"She doesn’t want to admit it, but she’s a little tired from blocking the Demon God’s Wrath.\"","\"Really? Even though she looks perfectly fine?\"","\"That’s precisely why she’s exhausted. That Demon God’s Wrath was powerful enough to obliterate a dozen True Gods with ease. Moreover, she’s not currently at her full strength.\"","\"What?\" Lev raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","However, Yuan refused to elaborate further and said, \"What are you so worried about? It’s just some spirit. I’ll handle them with ease.\"","\"If you say so...\" Lev decided not to question further and accepted his fate.","\"Let’s go then. Stay close to me.\"","Yuan entered the Demise Ravine shortly after, where only a single wide path cut through the land, trapped between two enormous mountain ranges whose towering peaks seemed to pierce the heavens.","An eerie silence filled the Demise Ravine, broken only by the occasional sound of rocks tumbling down the mountains and splashing into the river beneath.","A thin layer of fog lingered throughout the ravine, veiling anything beyond several miles from view. Though that might sound far, such a distance could be closed in an instant.","As they traveled, Yuan spoke to Supreme Ruler Dena using voice transmission.","\"How are you feeling?\"","\"Fine.\"","\"We both know that’s not true.\"","\"...\"","Although Supreme Ruler Dena appeared perfectly fine on the outside, she was actually greatly weakened after having her life force and energy drained by the curse for tens of billions of years.","To make matters worse, she had just invoked the Demon God’s Wrath, which forced her to expend the little energy she had recovered since awakening.","In her current state, Supreme Ruler Dena didn’t even possess ten percent of her former strength.","\"I am fine,\" Supreme Ruler Dena repeated after a moment of silence.","Seeing how stubborn she was being, Yuan said, \"Is that so? If you’re fine, then I guess I won’t need to feed you.\"","\"Huh?\" Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly turned to look at him with wide eyes. \"What did you just say?\"","Yuan smiled and replied, \"I was going to feed you some of my blood to help you recover. However, since you’re fine, you won’t need it.\"","\"T-That’s...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly recalled the taste of Yuan’s blood. Even though tens of billions of years had passed since she last tasted it, the memory remained as vivid as if it were only yesterday.","At the thought of that heavenly taste, Supreme Ruler Dena subconsciously began to drool.","When Lev saw this, he initially thought he was seeing things. However, after turning away and looking back a few seconds later, only to find the drool still there—even increasing in quantity—he became utterly bewildered.","\"Blood... I want it!\" Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly declared out loud."]},{"number":2379,"title":"Chapter 2379: Nether Wraiths","paragraphs":["\"Blood? Are you hungry?\" Lev misunderstood Supreme Ruler Dena’s random demand and asked.","Unlike humans, who could completely replace food and water with spiritual energy, demons lacked such an ability due to their heavy reliance on blood-based techniques. To strengthen or replenish their blood, they needed to consume meat or drink blood.","Fortunately, if they did not use any blood techniques or seek to strengthen their blood, demons could survive for far longer without food. However, doing so would essentially cripple them, as they would be unable to grow stronger or even fight properly.","Because of this weakness, the food resources of the Demonic Realm had grown incredibly scarce after billions of years of overhunting, leading to a widespread shortage.","Nowadays, only nobles and powerful demons were able to enjoy meat and fresh blood. Ordinary demons like Lev and everyone else had no choice but to resort to cannibalizing one another.","The Demonic Realm had tried to curb the problem by suppressing birth rates, but the demons’ immoral nature made such a solution short-lived. Eventually, they turned to harsher rules and ruthless enforcement to reduce their population.","However, one day, they discovered that they could send their people—or more specifically, the Forsaken who had been abandoned by the Demon God—into the boundless void. As a result, living conditions in the Demonic Realm improved significantly. Of course, this gave rise to another problem, but it was not something they became aware of until a certain someone appeared in their world and caused havoc.","\"I doubt we’ll be able to find any within the Demise Ravine, since there are only spiritual beings here,\" Lev continued.","Hearing his words, Supreme Ruler Dena turned to look at him.","\"D-Don’t tell me...\" Lev swallowed nervously, suddenly wondering if she intended to consume him instead.","Although demons possessed endless regeneration and could theoretically sustain themselves by consuming their own flesh or that of others, such a thing was not actually possible—as though the universe had anticipated this loophole and corrected it in advance. Because of this, the only way for a demon to strengthen itself or satisfy its hunger through another demon was to consume that demon’s core, an act that would inevitably result in the other demon’s death.","\"I haven’t consumed another demon for billions of years now. Why would I want to consume you?\" Supreme Ruler Dena remarked.","\"...\"","Lev opened his mouth but quickly closed it without uttering a word. He wanted to say that she’d consumed countless demons within the Deprived Crimson Valley over the course of billions of years, but he decided not to question it.","Of course, Lev was unaware of Supreme Ruler Dena’s situation with the curse. He wanted to ask Yuan about what happened between them and why the crimson sea suddenly vanished with Supreme Ruler Dena acting like she wasn’t even responsible for it, but decided not to question it.","Yuan then spoke, \"I’ll let you consume my blood later, once we find a safe place to sit down.\"","Without a word, Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly unleashed some of her aura and proceeded to punch the mountain beside them, creating a massive hole in it.","\"We can do it here,\" she calmly said afterward.","\"...\"","Yuan and Lev stared at her with dumbfounded expressions.","\"You...! Why did you do that?! That definitely alerted the Nether Wraiths!\" Lev cried out loud. \"We need to leave immediately before we’re swarmed by them!\"","Yuan rubbed his eyes and let out a sigh. \"Dena, you really need to stop acting before you think...\"","The next moment, ghostly wails reverberated throughout the ravine, sending chills down Lev’s spine.","\"T-They’re coming!\" he cried out loud.","\"Let’s go.\"","Without hesitation, Yuan surged forward. Lev hurried after him, with Supreme Ruler Dena following close behind, a slight pout still on her face.","However, they weren’t able to get far before a dozen Nether Wraiths surrounded them.","These Nether Wraiths possessed a spectral appearance, their semi-transparent bodies drifting through the air like human figures shrouded in crimson veils.","Although these beings possessed no discernible presence, a subtle aura still lingered around them, revealing their cultivation at the peak of the False God realm.","\"Oh my god! There are so many of them!\" Lev exclaimed in a terrified voice.","Yuan retrieved the Demon Devouring Sword and wanted to try devouring them. However, in the end, the Demon Devouring Sword could only devour demons.","\"What are you doing?! Nether Wraiths are immune to physical attacks!\" Lev, who thought Yuan wanted to fight using his sword, loudly explained.","\"I know. I just wanted to try something.\" Yuan calmly replied.","’If they’re anything like the corrupted souls in the Shadow Realm...’","With that thought in mind, Yuan suddenly unleashed a tremendous amount of Soul Strength, causing a profound pressure to blanket the entire area. It startled not only the Nether Wraiths but even Lev.","But he didn’t stop there and continued to increase the output. Soon, the Nether Wraiths quickly began screaming in agony, their shrill wails echoing throughout the ravine. A few seconds later, their figures began to fade, as if they were being erased from existence itself.","Yuan’s Soul Strength had reached an unfathomable level after cultivating for trillions of years during the phenomenon. Of course, he had not received its full benefits, but even so, it had improved so drastically that it had surpassed what even Cultivation Gods could achieve.","\"Hm? That was it? They’re a lot weaker than I anticipated,\" Yuan remarked after killing all Nether Wraiths without even lifting a finger.","Lev could only stare at him in awe.","\"Just what the hell are you? That amount of Soul Power... I have never felt anything that powerful!\" he commented.","In the Demonic Realm, Soul Strength was called Soul Power.","Even Supreme Ruler Dena was looking at him with her eyebrows slightly raised, seemingly surprised.","\"That power is not something a first-level False God should possess,\" she spoke a moment later, before asking, \"How did you train your Soul Power?\"","\"How? I cultivated it normally,\" he calmly replied."]},{"number":2380,"title":"Chapter 2380: Path of Enlightenment","paragraphs":["\"Cultivate normally...?\" Lev’s face twitched at Yuan’s ridiculous answer.","There was simply no way that was true, but Lev had no evidence to prove it.","Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly asked, \"When you entered False God, how long did you spend inside the Path of Enlightenment? How far did you go?\"","The phenomenon one experiences when attempting to enter God Ascension or False God is called the Path of Enlightenment in the Demonic Realm.","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"It happened only recently, but for some reason, I cannot recall exactly how far I was able to traverse, but I definitely remember passing 600 layers.\"","\"Six hundred layers?!\"","Not just Lev, but even Supreme Ruler Dena exclaimed in disbelief, their faces full of shock.","\"I don’t mean to be rude, but there’s absolutely no way you have broken through 600 layers! You must have recalled wrong!\" Lev said, refusing to believe Yuan’s claim of 600 layers, unaware that Yuan had actually passed the 1,000th layer.","\"I don’t know if it still holds true now, but I was once considered to have gone the furthest at the Path of Enlightenment,\" said Supreme Ruler Dena. \"And I was only able to reach the 300th layer. Yet, you somehow managed to double that?\"","\"You don’t believe me?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows. \"I’m not lying, though.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena shook her head and said, \"I believe you, since that’s the only logical reasoning to your absurd level of Soul Power. I can only imagine how much stronger it’ll get once your level advances and you reach True God, as your Soul Power will continuously grow with every level, depending on how far you have traversed in the Path of Enlightenment.\"","\"And once you become a True God...you will regain all of the Soul Power you’ve lost.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this information.","\"I will regain all of the Soul Power I cultivated during the Path of Enlightenment when I reach True God?\"","He had reached Cultivation God before, but he never regained all of his Soul Strength, so this was news to him.","Supreme Ruler Dena fell silent for a moment before replying, \"Or maybe it was the realm of Absolute God. I forgot.\"","\"It’s likely Absolute God, but the furthest I’ve ever gotten was True God. I wasn’t even aware of the existence of the Absolute God until I returned here,\" Yuan said.","\"Wait a second,\" Lev suddenly cut in. \"What do you mean the furthest you’ve gotten was True God when you’re clearly only at the first level False God? Did your cultivation regress?\"","\"No, I died and reincarnated.\" Yuan calmly explained his bizarre existence as if it were something ordinary.","\"R-Reincarnated...?\" Lev’s jaw dropped.","The concept of reincarnation also existed within the Demonic Realm, but nobody had ever been able to prove that it was real.","\"You... died?\" Even Supreme Ruler Dena was looking at him with a dumbfounded expression, as Yuan had never explained in detail why he was now called Yuan instead of Tian Chenyu.","She simply assumed that he’d decided to change his name for some reason.","However, what truly surprised her wasn’t the fact that he’d been reincarnated but that he’d died.","\"How did you die?\" Supreme Ruler Dena inquired, her crimson eyes narrowing slightly as a dangerous glint flickered within them.","Having fought Tian Chenyu herself, she was very well aware of his prowess. In fact, Tian Chenyu was the only individual whom she couldn’t kill, even with all of her might.","\"You don’t want to know,\" Yuan said with a calm smile.","\"I do,\" she insisted.","\"I’ll tell you when the time comes.\"","\"...\"","\"Then give me your blood,\" she then said. \"We’ve gotten rid of the Nether Wraiths, after all.\"","However, Yuan started stretching and responded in a tired voice, \"I would love to, but after using so much power to get rid of them, I am now exhausted. I’ll give you my blood once I recover a little.\"","Anyone, including Lev, could tell that Yuan was making things up, as he’d barely exerted any effort to deal with the Nether Wraiths. Yet, Supreme Ruler Dena could only accept it while silently gritting her teeth.","’Was the Supreme Ruler always this... docile?’ Lev wondered inwardly as he glanced at Supreme Ruler Dena.","According to rumors, Supreme Ruler Dena was one of the most stubborn and troublesome Supreme Rulers to ever rule the Demonic Realm. Not only was she lazy and quick to push all of her responsibilities onto her subordinates, but she was also notoriously overbearing whenever things did not go her way.","Yet the Supreme Ruler Dena was the complete opposite right now, as she seemed to listen to Yuan without questioning his demands or forcing herself on him.","They resumed their journey shortly afterward.","Unsurprisingly, more Nether Wraiths appeared to attack them along the way. However, Yuan easily erased them from existence with his Soul Strength.","’This journey is far more relaxing than I anticipated...’ Lev thought to himself, having already prepared for the worst.","He turned to look at Yuan, who was doing all of the work, and asked, \"If you don’t mind me asking, what’s your world, the Divine Heaven, like?\"","\"It’s pretty much the same as this world, but nowhere near as grim.\"","\"Huh? What do you mean by grim?\" Lev asked with a genuinely puzzled look on his face.","\"Deprived Crimson Valley, Sea of Death, Valley of Blood, Corpse Mountain... most of the places in this world bear such grim names. Even the world itself is dyed in crimson, as if the entire realm has been soaked in blood.\"","\"Is that so? They sound pretty ordinary to me,\" Lev said.","\"Oh, my world is no longer called the Divine Heaven. After it was split into nine separate realms, it came to be known as the Nine Heavens.\"","\"What?! Is that even possible? How could something like that even happen?\" Lev asked, his gaze brimming with intrigue.","\"Long story short, a huge fight broke out, and as a result, it split the world.\""]},{"number":2381,"title":"Chapter 2381: Forsaken","paragraphs":["\"A fight intense enough to split an entire world? I can’t even begin to imagine what kind of beings would be involved,\" Lev said, shaking his head. \"More importantly, how could a world remain intact after being split apart? If you smash a toy into several pieces, it becomes useless.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at Lev’s comment, as the thought had never really occurred to him before.","’Now that I think about it, the Divine Heavens didn’t collapse after being split apart. Normally, when a star is shattered, it explodes. Could the Absolute Power have had something to do with it?’ he wondered inwardly.","\"What about the people living in your world? Are they all as strong as you... Or near your level?\" Lev continued to ask.","\"There are many people with a higher cultivation base than I out there. However, if we’re talking about pure combat prowess... I wouldn’t lose to Cultivation Gods... probably. They’re basically equivalent to True Gods in this world.\"","\"Huh?\" Lev looked at him with a puzzled expression. \"What do you mean by ’probably’? If Cultivation Gods are equivalent to True Gods, you’ll definitely defeat them, as you have already killed several of them here—with relative ease, at that.\"","Yuan shook his head and explained, \"While that may be true, I possess an overwhelming advantage against the people of this world because of my Demon Sealing Aura, a power created specifically to counter your kind. If I were fighting a fellow human cultivator, I wouldn’t have such an advantage. Even so, I am fairly confident that I would still be able to defeat them.\"","\"Demon Sealing Aura... I’ve heard many stories about it, but its origins still remain a mystery to me. Why would someone create such a power? Were they trying to exterminate our race or something?\" Lev asked.","A stiff smile appeared on Yuan’s face as he replied, \"Indeed, that’s exactly why that individual created such a power. He wanted to completely annihilate demons—the same demons who killed his lover and terrorized his entire world for hundreds of years. However, he later learned that the demons who terrorized his world were different from the ones that lived in this world.\"","\"The Forsaken, huh?\" Lev immediately understood what Yuan meant and let out a sigh.","\"They were once ordinary people. But after being ’abandoned’ by the Demon God, they turn into bloodthirsty monsters. Every day, every living being in this world lives with the constant fear of becoming a Forsaken, which is especially cruel for us, who are immortal. If I could meet the Demon God, I would want to ask him why he made us this way.\"","Moreover, according to some of the most ancient records available, the inhabitants of the Demonic Realm had not always been demons. Some accounts even claimed that they had once all resembled humans, just like Supreme Ruler Dena and those regarded as having ’noble’ bloodlines.","\"The Demon God, huh?\" Yuan mumbled before asking aloud, \"Has anyone actually seen the Demon God before? Or any evidence that he truly exists and isn’t just some imaginary being?\"","Lev shook his head and replied, \"While I have never seen the Demon God before, he definitely exists.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena then said, \"The Demon God is real.\"","Hearing the confidence in her voice, Yuan had to ask, \"You... have you seen the Demon God before? I find it hard to believe that a Supreme Ruler would never have any contact with him.\"","\"I have never personally met the Demon God before, but I have definitely spoken to him. It happened during the ritual where I obtained my title. It was also the Demon God who granted me this power.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena said while pointing to her forehead, or more specifically, the ’Authority’ branded into her soul.","\"What did you talk about?\" Yuan asked, his interest piqued.","Supreme Ruler Dena pondered for a moment before replying, \"It happened so long ago that I can no longer remember much of it, but most of what he said concerned my responsibilities as a Supreme Ruler and the things I was forbidden from doing.\"","\"Such as?\"","\"Such as...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena paused for a bit before shrugging, \"I don’t remember.\"","\"What? How can you forget about something so important?\" Yuan exclaimed in disbelief. \"What if you accidentally do said forbidden thing?\"","\"I was able to remember it perfectly when I was still the Supreme Ruler. However, after being replaced, I can feel my memories of the Demon God slowly vanishing. It’ll only be a matter of time before I completely forget about our conversation.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"But the Demon God is definitely real. I can guarantee you that,\" she insisted, thinking Yuan didn’t believe her.","However, to her surprise, Yuan spoke with a calm smile, \"You do not have to convince me. I never doubted the Demon God’s existence. In fact, I have personally met the Demon God before.\"","\"What?! Is that true?!\"","Both Lev and Supreme Ruler Dena halted their movements and shouted at him simultaneously.","He nodded and elaborated, \"It happened shortly after I left the Demonic Realm in the past, and he was the one who approached me.\"","\"What... What did the Demon God look like?\" Lev asked.","\"What did you talk about?\" Supreme Ruler Dena questioned.","The two of them stared at Yuan with gazes so intense it felt as though they could burn a hole through his body.","Yuan opened his mouth but delayed his words for a good moment.","Then, he said, \"I... forgot.\"","\"What?! How can you forget about something so important?!\" Lev exclaimed.","Yuan shrugged. \"Since I died several times before my current incarnation, I’m still in the process of recovering all of my memories, so I don’t remember everything.\"","\"No way!\"","Just as they were about to voice their complaints, an overwhelming pressure suddenly descended, swallowing what felt like the entire ravine.","The instant Yuan and his group sensed it, their bodies froze stiff.","\"T-This presence! It could only be that thing!\" Lev exclaimed in a low voice, his body shivering in fear.","\"What thing?\" Yuan asked with a slight frown.","\"The undisputed ruler of the Demise Ravine—the Wraith Queen of Demise!\""]},{"number":2382,"title":"Chapter 2382: Queen Wraith of Demise","paragraphs":["\"Queen Wraith of Demise? What’s so special about it? Isn’t it just a slightly stronger Nether Wraith?\" Yuan asked.","\"Of course not! The Queen Wraith of Demise is immortal! Like, true immortality! Unlike ordinary Nether Wraiths, it will keep returning no matter how many times you kill it!\" Lev explained.","\"True immortality, huh? We’ll see about that...\" Yuan mumbled, doubting it truly couldn’t be killed.","A few moments later, the Queen Wraith of Demise emerged from the right side of the mountain, its enormous figure slowly coming into view as it loomed over them like a giant.","\"Holy shit...\" Lev muttered with a dumbfounded look, clearly not expecting the Queen Wraith of Demise to be so massive.","Even Yuan was a bit surprised by its sheer size. As for its appearance, it resembled the Nether Wraiths, but rather than crimson, it was a deep violet.","\"True God, huh.\" Supreme Ruler Dena calmly gazed at the massive wraith.","The Queen Wraith of Demise did not attack immediately after appearing. Instead, it merely watched them from above, like a god staring down at insignificant mortals.","Soon, even more wraiths appeared, and within moments, thousands of Nether Wraiths surrounded the Queen Wraith of Demise like an army of soldiers protecting their queen.","\"Yuan... do you think you can handle this...?\" Lev asked him in a trembling voice.","\"...\"","Yuan remained silent, which only further worried him.","\"The Nether Wraiths seem to be communicating with the queen,\" Yuan suddenly remarked.","Although they had no mouths and could only produce ghostly noises, he could tell they were conveying something to the Queen Wraith of Demise.","\"They’re probably seeking the queen’s help because you killed so many of them,\" Supreme Ruler Dena said.","\"Well, what else was I supposed to do when they attacked us first?\" Yuan shook his head.","\"Thirty-five...\"","A voice suddenly spoke to Yuan, but it was transmitted directly into his mind through voice transmission.","Yuan immediately realized who this unfamiliar voice belonged to and turned to stare at the Queen Wraith of Demise.","\"That is the number of my children that you have killed,\" the Queen Wraith of Demise continued in a grim voice.","\"Do you deny your crimes?\"","Yuan calmly responded to it, \"I won’t deny it since it’s true. However, they attacked us first.\"","\"Nay!\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise loudly declared. \"According to the witnesses, you were the ones who attacked first! You even declared war by damaging our territory!\"","\"...\"","Yuan was rendered speechless by this new revelation and turned to look at Supreme Ruler Dena, who was casually hovering behind him with a nonchalant expression, utterly oblivious to the trouble she had caused them.","\"What is it?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked after noticing his gaze.","\"This is all your fault,\" Yuan said with a sigh.","\"Then do you want me to handle it?\" She took Yuan’s words at face value and made no attempt to refute them.","\"Do you really think you can handle that in your current state?\" Yuan asked while pointing at the Queen Wraith of Demise.","Supreme Ruler Dena shifted her gaze to it and fell silent for a moment before shaking her head, \"Probably not.\"","\"Then let me handle it.\"","Yuan turned back to the Queen Wraith of Demise and spoke, \"I admit that we were at fault for damaging your territory, but nothing good will come from dwelling on what has already happened. Let us set aside our grievances and avoid escalating this any further.\"","\"You dare to tell me to forget about my children’s death?!\" The Queen Wraith of Demise shouted as her aura surged, seemingly prepared to attack.","\"Either that or you’ll have to experience even more losses.\" Yuan suddenly unleashed some of his Soul Strength to show the Queen Wraith of Demise that he had the capability to kill many of them with ease.","\"Of course, I am also willing to compensate for your losses.\"","\"...\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise fell silent after sensing Yuan’s overwhelming Soul Strength.","She could tell just from his Soul Strength that he wasn’t going all out and that even if the army of thousands of Nether Wraiths around her were to attack him simultaneously, he would likely be able to kill them all just by scattering his Soul Strength.","The Queen Wraith of Demise was enraged by the deaths of her children and was, by nature, a vengeful being. However, she was neither foolish nor reckless, and she realized that attacking the man before her could cost her countless more of her children.","After several minutes of silence, the Queen Wraith of Demise spoke again, \"I am willing to forgive you for killing my children if you do something for me.\"","\"I am listening.\"","\"I will tell you more about it later. Wait here for my return.\"","Without any explanation, the Queen Wraith of Demise turned around and disappeared. However, her army of Nether Wraiths remained to keep watch, ensuring they wouldn’t run away.","\"What’s happening?\" Lev asked, as he wasn’t able to listen to their conversation. \"Why did the Queen Wraith of Demise suddenly leave without doing anything?\"","He had even prepared himself for a massive fight when the Queen Wraith of Demise released her aura.","Yuan proceeded to explain the whole situation to them.","\"What?! They attacked us because we—she destroyed their territory?!\" Lev exclaimed after learning of this.","\"Can we even believe her words? What if she’s just making shit up?\" he then asked.","Yuan shrugged, \"That could be the case, but it doesn’t change the fact that I killed her children. If we can avoid an all-out war with these beings, I don’t mind helping them out... as long as it’s not something unreasonable.\"","\"What kind of help?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked.","\"I don’t know yet, but we should find out soon enough.\"","However, even after waiting around for several days, the Queen Wraith of Demise did not return.","\"Hey, what happened to your queen?\" Yuan tried to communicate with the Nether Wraiths, but it was a pointless effort, as none of them were able to speak like their queen."]},{"number":2383,"title":"Chapter 2383: Feeding Supreme Ruler Dena","paragraphs":["Yuan had no choice but to continue waiting when his communication with the Nether Wraiths failed.","Several more days passed by without any information.","\"Are you sure we’re not being scammed?\" Lev remarked with a bored look on his face.","\"Have some patience,\" Yuan said as he cultivated his Soul Strength.","\"Hey.\"","Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly approached him and called out.","\"What is it?\" Yuan asked, his eyes still closed.","\"I think this is a good time to feed me your blood,\" she calmly said.","\"...\"","Yuan was speechless.","\"It will also help me recover some of my strength,\" she continued, trying to convince him.","Yuan opened one of his eyes to look at her face and said in a sighing voice, \"You still dare to ask for blood after causing all of this trouble? Even if I give you my blood now, you’ll only recover a little of your strength—not nearly enough to help our current situation.\"","\"I might recover enough to use Void Manipulation to take us out of here,\" she said without an ounce of shame on her face.","Yuan pondered for a moment, but before he could give her an answer, he suddenly stopped his cultivation and opened both eyes.","\"She’s back,\" he said.","The next moment, a familiar presence appeared. However, something about it felt different, even though it clearly belonged to the Queen Wraith of Demise.","Soon, Yuan realized why it felt so different. Her appearance had changed. Instead of her ghostly, spectral form, she now stood before them in a human vessel—a beautiful woman with an alluring figure, black hair, pale skin, and violet eyes.","\"Are you... the Queen Wraith of Demise...?\" Lev almost couldn’t believe his eyes asked.","\"Indeed, I am,\" she calmly replied.","\"Where did you get that vessel? And did you really just leave to change your form?\" Yuan then asked.","\"This vessel belonged to someone who perished in this place a few billion years ago. I decided to use it since it no longer has an owner,\" she answered.","\"Did you kill her?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Does it matter?\" The Queen Wraith of Demise shrugged off his question before continuing, \"As for why I have decided to take this form, it’s simply because the place I will be taking you requires it. Without this vessel, I am unable to get close to it.\"","\"Is the place that dangerous? What do you even need my help with?\"","\"You will know once we get there. Now, enough chattering and follow me.\"","Without giving them an opportunity to respond, the Queen Wraith of Demise turned around and began flying away.","Half of the Nether Wraiths followed her while the other half remained to watch over Yuan and his group to ensure they wouldn’t run away.","\"Let’s go,\" Yuan said as he followed the wraiths with a calm demeanor.","Meanwhile, Lev was shaking in his boots—not because of the situation, but because of the subtle aura Supreme Ruler Dena was emitting.","\"There’s no need to pout,\" Yuan suddenly spoke without looking back. \"I’ll let you suck my blood as we travel since it’ll probably take some time.\"","Hearing his words, the displeasure on her face vanished in an instant, replaced by a delighted expression.","The next instant, Supreme Ruler Dena flew right behind Yuan before wrapping her legs around his waist, clinging to his back like a kuala hugging a tree.","\"What the...?\" Lev’s eyes nearly popped out of their sockets after seeing Supreme Ruler Dena’s shocking actions that were definitely not befitting of someone with her status.","Then, with a single smooth motion, as if she’d done this a million times before, she loosened the robe around Yuan’s neck. Without hesitation, she sank her canine teeth—sharper and longer than a human’s—into his neck, drawing blood.","Despite Yuan’s powerful physique that could repel even top-quality treasures, Supreme Ruler Dena’s teeth very easily penetrated his skin and flesh.","When Supreme Ruler Dena’s teeth entered his neck, Yuan could instantly feel his blood being consumed at a rapid rate, faster than even a severed arm would expel.","\"Slow down, or you’ll kill me,\" he hastily said, even though his regeneration was keeping up with his blood loss.","Queen Wraith of Demise glanced back when she noticed their actions, but after looking for a brief moment, she lost interest and no longer cared, as it was ordinary for demons to drink blood and eat flesh.","After she began her feasting, Supreme Ruler Dena did not stop sucking for an hour straight.","Seeing this, Lev couldn’t help but drool, the scent of Yuan’s blood wafting into his nose.","’Fuck! Why does his blood smell so damn good?! I have never smelled anything this delicious before!’ he cried inwardly.","However, as much as he wanted to also take a bite at Yuan’s neck, he knew that if he couldn’t control his urges, he’d likely end up being killed by Supreme Ruler Dena.","An hour later, Supreme Ruler Dena finally removed her mouth from Yuan’s neck and took a deep breath.","\"Hey, your blood tastes different from before,\" she remarked afterward.","\"How so?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s much more delicious!\" she replied before reaching for his neck and licking the leftover blood.","\"Can I drink more?\" she asked, then added a second later, \"I’ll let you drink my blood later in return.\"","\"?!?!?\"","It wasn’t Yuan who was shocked by Supreme Ruler Dena’s seemingly casual remark, but Lev, who looked even more stunned than when she had clung to Yuan earlier.","A Supreme Ruler’s blood was unimaginably sought after for its ability to strengthen other demons. However, throughout history, the number of times a Supreme Ruler had shared their blood could be counted on one’s fingers, despite the many who had held that position.","\"Your blood, huh?\" Even though he was human, Yuan didn’t immediately dismiss such an offer, as he had never tasted the blood of a Supreme Ruler before, even as Tian Chenyu. In fact, he was actually very intrigued by its taste and whether it would benefit him."]},{"number":2384,"title":"Chapter 2384: A Black Mountain","paragraphs":["\"I’ll let you drink as much as you want, too,\" Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly improved her offer when Yuan took a moment to ponder, worried that he might refuse.","’Unlimited blood?!’ Lev nearly fell from the sky in shock after hearing her once-in-a-lifetime offer. Countless beings in the Demonic Realm would be willing to do anything for such an opportunity, yet Supreme Ruler Dena offered it so casually in exchange for Yuan’s blood. This only deepened Lev’s curiosity about its taste.","\"Alright, I’ll accept your offer, but I doubt I will need too much of it—\"","Before Yuan could even finish his sentence, Supreme Ruler Dena dug her teeth into his neck and began sucking again.","Fearing that he might fail to control his urges, Lev sealed his sense of smell and stopped looking at Supreme Ruler Dena feed on Yuan, pretending they no longer existed.","This went on for several weeks until the Queen Wraith of Demise slowed down.","Of course, Supreme Ruler Dena fed on Yuan’s blood until she was completely full, which took a little over two weeks.","\"We’ll arrive at our destination soon,\" said Queen Wraith of Demise.","Suddenly, the atmosphere changed, and the air became noticeably heavier.","Lev and Supreme Ruler Dena frowned when they sensed this aura, and they came to a complete halt.","\"This feeling...\" Lev trembled.","\"Chaotic Essence, huh?\" Yuan mumbled after sensing what was clearly Chaotic Essence in the air. Not only that, but it was an immense amount.","\"Sorry, but this is as far as I’ll go,\" Lev said. \"This is the same energy from the Corruption Shower. If I get too close, I’m afraid I might turn into a Forsaken.\"","Yuan nodded, not blaming him in the slightest. \"I understand. You can stay here and wait for our return.\"","He turned to look at Supreme Ruler Dena and asked her, \"What are you going to do? Want to stay here, too?\"","However, she shook her head and said, \"As a Supreme Ruler, my resistance to this sort of energy is much higher.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this revelation.","\"Is that how it works? Does that mean Supreme Rulers cannot turn into Forsaken?\"","\"Not necessary. It just means we’re less likely to do so. However, we’ve never had a Supreme Ruler turn Forsaken, as we’re essentially the Demon God’s envoy.\"","\"Makes sense,\" Yuan nodded.","\"But I am not sure that I want to risk it. If you turned into a Forsaken... even I won’t be able to stop you.\"","\"If I stay here, that means you’ll be with the Queen Wraith of Demise by yourself...\" Supreme Ruler Dena said with a slight frown on her face.","\"I’ll be fine,\" Yuan said with a confident smile.","\"If you say so.\"","Yuan continued following the Queen Wraith of Demise, while the others stayed outside the Chaotic Essence. However, it wasn’t just Lev and Supreme Ruler Dena who were forced to stop—even the ordinary Nether Wraiths halted their advance, clearly against their will, as they released wails unlike anything heard before, as if declaring their concern for their queen.","Seeing this, Yuan finally understood why the Queen Wraith of Demise had to enter a vessel.","’So these beings are weak against Chaotic Essence too, huh?’ Yuan noted to himself.","As if she could read his thoughts, the Queen Wraith of Demise suddenly spoke out loud, \"Not only are we weak against this sort of energy, but if we get too close, it will absorb us.\"","\"Absorb you...?\" Yuan muttered with a puzzled face.","He had no idea that Chaotic Essence was capable of such a thing. However, this wasn’t necessarily a bad thing. In fact, it was quite advantageous for Yuan, who could wield its power.","Of course, the Queen Wraith of Demise wasn’t aware of this and unknowingly revealed their weakness to the worst individual possible.","After traveling for several more days, Yuan suddenly spotted a black dot on the horizon. As they approached, it gradually came into view, revealing itself to be a massive black mountain. However, once they got close enough to see it in detail, it became apparent that the mountain was not made of stone but of an unknown material resembling obsidian.","Moreover, it was clearly the source of the Chaotic Essence, and the amount it emitted was unlike anything Yuan had ever experienced before—even during his time as Tian Yi, the Immortal Monarch, who was most familiar with Chaotic Essence.","In fact, even if he combined all of the Chaotic Essence that he absorbed from the Chaos Coins he’d amassed inside the Primordial Realm, it still wouldn’t come close to the amount contained within the mountain.","Just how much stronger would his Chaotic Essence become if he were to absorb all of it? Yuan almost started drooling at that mere thought.","\"Isn’t it about time you tell me what you need my help with? I can assume it has something to do with that mountain, right?\" Yuan said as they got closer.","The Queen Wraith of Demise nodded and said, \"This object appeared out of thin air—or more specifically, fell from the sky—several billion years ago. When it first appeared, it was barely larger than a boulder. The energy it emitted wasn’t particularly remarkable at the time, but it grew stronger and larger after absorbing some of my children who got too close out of curiosity.\"","\"Once we realized it could absorb us and turn us into its own power, I forbade my children from approaching it. However, it continued to grow stronger and larger during a certain phenomenon.\"","\"Let me guess... the Corruption Shower,\" Yuan said.","\"Correct.\" The Queen Wraith of Demise turned to look at Yuan and spoke with a serious expression. \"If this continues, this object will eventually take over our territory and threaten our existence, not to mention those living outside.\"","Yuan fell silent for a moment before speaking, \"You clearly know that demons like the two following me are afraid of this energy, so why did you ask me to help you? Weren’t you concerned that I might also be too afraid to get close and refuse to help?\""]},{"number":2385,"title":"Chapter 2385: True Dragon Chaotic Core","paragraphs":["Hearing Yuan’s question, the Queen Wraith of Demise spoke as it calmly glared at him, \"I don’t know what you are, but you’re clearly different from those two from the color of your soul, so I took a gamble. If you ran away and refused to help, I would’ve simply killed you.\"","\"Do you really think you can kill me?\" Yuan asked with a slight smile on his face.","\"...\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise remained silent, but her gaze lacked confidence.","\"So, how do you want me to help you?\" Yuan then asked.","\"I don’t care how, but I want you to get rid of this energy,\" she quickly answered.","\"Get rid of that...?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows as he looked at the black mountain that was oozing with Chaotic Essence.","He started calculating how long it would take him to absorb all the Chaotic Essence emanating from the black mountain and quickly reached a conclusion.","A thousand years. That’s how long he estimated it would take.","\"Alright, I’ll do my best,\" Yuan said as he started approaching the black mountain.","Of course, he had no intention of spending the next thousand years absorbing the Chaotic Essence. Instead, he decided to spend a few years absorbing just enough to improve his cultivation and hopefully learn more about True Chaotic Qi.","’My second cultivation is now on par with my main cultivation base, so it would be best to keep them balanced. Instead of increasing my cultivation further, I can use this opportunity to create as many Chaotic Hearts as possible, which will also enhance my overall strength,’ Yuan thought to himself as he reached the black mountain.","\"What are you going to do?\" The Queen Wraith of Demise suddenly asked him from afar, not daring to get too close, even with her vessel.","\"You’ll see soon,\" Yuan replied as he flew straight to the very peak of the mountain and sat down.","The Queen Wraith of Demise raised an eyebrow at his puzzling actions, wondering how he intended to deal with the energy this way.","In the very next moment, her eyes widened in shock and disbelief as Yuan began absorbing the energy, just as it had absorbed her children.","’He’s absorbing that energy?!’ she cried inwardly.","<You have absorbed Chaotic Essence>","<You have begun forming your third Chaotic Heart!>","With how much Chaotic Essence he was absorbing, Yuan started forming his third Chaotic Heart within days of his cultivation, completing it just a week later.","<You have successfully formed your third Chaotic Heart!>","<Your third Chaotic Heart has merged with your Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","After his Chaotic Dragon Core was strengthened, so did Yuan’s speed when absorbing the Chaotic Essence.","Then, two weeks later, he started forming his fourth Chaotic Heart.","<You have begun forming your fourth Chaotic Heart!>","<You have successfully formed your fourth Chaotic Heart!>","<Your fourth Chaotic Heart has merged with your Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","<Your Chaotic Dragon Core has activated!>","<Your Chaotic Dragon Core has begun evolving!>","Yuan was pleasantly surprised to discover that his Chaotic Dragon Core was capable of evolving, and his anticipation skyrocketed as he wondered how much stronger it would make him.","Three months later—","<Progress: 100%>","<Your Chaotic Dragon Core has evolved into a True Chaotic Dragon Core!>","<Due to your True Chaotic Dragon Core, your cultivation speed when absorbing Chaotic Essence has increased by 300,000%!>","<Due to your True Chaotic Dragon Core, your efficiency when using Chaotic Essence has improved by 50,000%, allowing you to unleash more strength while using less Chaotic Essence!>","However, even with his increased cultivation speed, the amount of Chaotic Essence required for each new Chaotic Heart continued to grow, and it still took Yuan half a year to begin forming his fifth Chaotic Heart.","Then, after another year—","<You have successfully formed your fifth Chaotic Heart!>","<Your fifth Chaotic Heart has merged with your True Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","’A thousand years? At this rate, I will only need a hundred years to absorb all of the Chaotic Essence!’ Yuan laughed inwardly at his rapid progress.","Meanwhile, the Queen Wraith of Demise was utterly stunned by how quickly Yuan was eliminating the energy.","’I don’t know how he’s doing it, but at this rate, he might really get rid of it!’","She was in total disbelief.","’I was even prepared to dispose of him!’","The Queen Wraith of Demise had never truly expected Yuan to help solve their problem. Yet, against all expectations, he was doing exactly that.","Since the Chaotic Essence got weaker, Supreme Ruler Dena and Lev, who were waiting outside its influence, began moving closer and closer to the black mountain.","\"This reminds me of when he purposefully entered the Corruption Shower,\" Lev suddenly remarked. \"This energy turns us into Forsaken, but he seems unaffected by it. I wonder if it has something to do with being a human.\"","He turned to look at Supreme Ruler Dena and asked, \"Just who is that man?\"","\"A troublemaker,\" she calmly replied and refused to further elaborate, puzzling Lev even more.","In the blink of an eye, another five years passed, and Yuan just finished his sixth Chaotic Heart.","<You have successfully formed your sixth Chaotic Heart!>","<Your sixth Chaotic Heart has merged with your True Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","<Your True Chaotic Dragon Core has begun evolving!>","’Hm? It’s evolving again?’ Yuan thought to himself.","One year... ten years... twenty years later—","<Progress: 100%>","<Your True Chaotic Dragon Core has evolved into a Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core!>","<Due to your Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core, your cultivation speed when absorbing Chaotic Essence has increased by 1,000,000%!>","<Due to your Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core, your efficiency when using Chaotic Essence has improved by 200,000%>","<Due to your Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core, your ability to sense True Chaotic Qi has drastically improved!>","\"I can sense True Chaotic Qi more clearly now!\" Yuan exclaimed with a look of surprise on his face."]},{"number":2386,"title":"Chapter 2386: The Essence of True Chaotic Qi","paragraphs":["Now that he could sense True Chaotic Qi clearly, Yuan temporarily stopped absorbing the Chaotic Essence to focus on studying it.","His sudden pause caused the Queen Wraith of Demise to raise her eyebrows.","\"Are you... done?\" She questioned him shortly after.","\"No, I am just taking a break,\" he calmly replied before falling into complete silence again.","Very quickly, Yuan realized that the Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core not only helped him sense True Chaotic Qi better, but it even helped with his comprehension, allowing him to study it with more ease.","<Your understanding of True Chaotic Qi has improved significantly>","It didn’t take long before Yuan started to grasp the essence of the energy. Perhaps it was because of his Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core, or that he’d already mastered Celestial Qi, but he was progressing much faster than usual.","Several weeks into his training, Yuan suddenly fell into a trance-like state.","He had entered the state of Enlightenment.","’What is he doing?’","The Queen Wraith of Demise could sense the atmosphere around Yuan shifting, along with his aura. However, she had never seen someone enter a state of Enlightenment before, leaving her both intrigued and puzzled.","Supreme Ruler Dena, who was watching from afar with her divine sense, also noticed this change and became somewhat worried.","Although demons could also experience Enlightenment, it was far more uncommon. Moreover, they would emit a different aura, so Supreme Ruler Dena had no idea what was happening to Yuan at this moment.","\"If Celestial Qi embodies the essence of life... then the true essence of True Chaotic Qi is to consume it!\"","A year into his Enlightenment, Yuan’s eyes snapped open, gleaming with a profound light. The aura around him changed drastically, as though something unseen was bowing before him.","<You have fully comprehended the essence of True Chaotic Qi!>","<You can now wield True Chaotic Qi!>","Unlike Celestial Qi, which was its own separate energy from ordinary Qi and Immortal Qi, True Chaotic Qi already existed within Chaotic Essence. However, only those who comprehend True Chaotic Qi are capable of sensing it and wield it.","After comprehending True Chaotic Qi, Yuan finally understood why ordinary cultivators couldn’t use their spiritual energy normally when surrounded by Chaotic Essence. It was because the True Chaotic Qi within it was extremely sensitive to spiritual energy and would actively absorb it.","True Chaotic Qi didn’t merely respond to spiritual energy; it was attracted to anything spiritual in nature. As such, entities like Nether Wraiths, which were completely spectral, became its prime targets.","Moreover, not only could it absorb energy, but it can use that energy to strengthen itself. In a way, it was similar to Yuan’s physique, which can absorb all sorts of energy and turn it into his own power.","Yuan had a strong desire to test out his newfound strength, but with the Queen Wraith of Demise nearby, Yuan didn’t want to make her feel threatened.","Thus, he started to absorb the rest of the Chaotic Essence from the black mountain.","Even though he’d already formed five additional Chaotic Hearts, he had only absorbed about a third of the available Chaotic Essence, so he could easily create a few more.","When Yuan resumed his cultivation, he shifted his focus from the Chaotic Essence to the True Chaotic Qi within it, allowing him to absorb it at a far greater speed.","A small black vortex suddenly formed around him as he devoured the Chaotic Essence. It steadily grew larger until Yuan resembled a black hole.","Five years later—","<You have successfully formed your seventh Chaotic Heart!>","<Your seventh Chaotic Heart has merged with your Supreme Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","Although it had taken him over twenty years to absorb 30 percent of the Chaotic Essence within the black mountain, it now took him only five years to absorb another 20 percent.","Suddenly, Yuan halted his cultivation and lowered his gaze, a slight frown appearing on his face as he stared at the mountain beneath him.","Perhaps the overwhelming Chaotic Essence had concealed it, but only after absorbing half of it did he finally sense a hidden presence within the black mountain.","Something had been lurking inside it all along.","The moment Yuan sensed the presence, it reacted. As if awakened, the black mountain suddenly began to tremble.","Yuan immediately got up and distanced himself from the black mountain.","\"What’s happening?!\" Queen Wraith of Demise exclaimed with a puzzled look on her face.","\"There’s something hidden within that!\" Yuan shouted back as he pointed at the black mountain.","\"What?!\"","The pitch-black mountain suddenly began to fade in color, gradually turning semi-transparent and revealing a massive silhouette within it.","The silhouette had a long, snake-like body with ten lizard-like limbs—five on each side. Most striking was its head—or rather, its heads, as there were two.","Moments later, the trembling stopped briefly before returning even stronger than before. Cracks began to spread across the mountain, making it clear that the entity within was trying to emerge.","It wasn’t long before the mountain exploded and collapsed, completely revealing the entity hidden within.","The entity was a massive black lizard with a long, snake-like body and two menacing heads, each bearing a deadly gaze.","It radiated an overwhelming amount of Chaotic Essence, far surpassing what the black mountain had contained, as though the mountain had only housed a portion of its true strength.","As for its cultivation, it was clearly above the True God realm but not quite at the level of an Absolute God. However, since its cultivation was based on Chaotic Essence rather than Celestial Qi, it was far more powerful.","\"What the hell is that?!\" Lev cried out loud when he saw the lizard-like being.","Supreme Ruler Dena did not say a word. Instead, she flew to Yuan, despite the Chaotic Essence in that area growing stronger than before.","\"Wait a—!\" Lev wanted to follow, but he lacked the confidence and could only watch as she disappeared into the horizon."]},{"number":2387,"title":"Chapter 2387: Ancient Chaos","paragraphs":["\"What a disgusting thing!\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise’s expression twisted in disgust at the sight of the beast, yet it was not its grotesque form that repulsed her, but the sheer density of Chaotic Essence it exuded.","Unlike the black mountain, which leaked its Chaotic Essence in all directions, this creature possessed absolute control over its aura, compressing it into something far more concentrated—and infinitely more terrifying.","\"What kind of beast is that?\" Yuan asked, as he had never seen or heard of such a being before.","\"I don’t know,\" said the Queen Wratih of Demise. \"But you’ll get rid of it, right?\"","\"I might have no other choice...\" Yuan sighed with a bitter smile.","Meanwhile, the unknown beast remained eerily still, its gaze fixed solely on Yuan after its emergence—completely disregarding the Queen Wraith of Demise despite her close proximity. In fact, it did not spare her even a single glance.","Suddenly, it parted its massive jaws, revealing its sharp teeth, and a hoarse, eerie voice resounded from within, \"How dare a mere human covet my power...\"","Yuan raised a brow at the beast’s words, a flicker of surprise crossing his face. Yet it wasn’t its ability to speak that caught him off guard, but it was the fact that it had seen through him and recognized him as human.","\"What are you?\" Yuan asked.","\"I am Ancient Chaos, one of the most primordial beings in this universe!\" The beast declared.","\"Ancient Chaos? Never heard of you.\"","\"Ignorant human... I have existed long before your kind ever came into existence...\"","\"Then enlighten me. Why were you hiding inside that mountain?\"","The Ancient Chaos narrowed its eyes and fell silent for a moment before speaking, \"What you just witnessed was not my emergence... but my birth.\"","\"Your birth? So you’re nothing more than a newborn?\" Yuan said, his disbelief evident. It was hard to fathom how a being born mere moments ago could speak so clearly, let alone possess such overwhelming power.","Suddenly, a chilling sensation crawled up Yuan’s spine as the Ancient Chaos began to exude overwhelming killing intent.","\"Had you not stolen my power and interrupted my birth, I would have been born whole! For your crime, I shall devour your existence!\"","The Ancient Chaos shot toward Yuan in a blur, its immense body tearing through the air as both heads lunged forward, jaws stretched wide to devour him whole.","However, before it could reach Yuan, the Ancient Chaos snapped its jaws shut—biting into nothing but empty air.","’This is—!’","Sensing something amiss, Yuan reacted instantly and left his position.","The very moment he moved, a black hole manifested where he had stood. It vanished less than a heartbeat later, leaving behind a gaping void in space itself, as though everything within it had been completely erased from existence.","’What the hell?!’ Yuan cried inwardly.","The attack resembled his Demon Devouring Sword’s ability but appeared far more versatile and powerful.","\"Oh? You actually managed to dodge that?\" The Ancient Chaos commented in a somewhat impressed tone.","\"So you can also use Void Manipulation, huh? Even though you were just born...\" Yuan remarked with a cold smile.","Realizing this would be no easy battle, Yuan immediately activated Absolute Dragon Awakening and retrieved Number One Under Heaven. And seeing that the creature bore some resemblance to a dragon, he also summoned the Dragon God’s Vengeance without hesitation.","\"Toys like that won’t be able to harm me!\" The Ancient Chaos laughed menacingly as it lunged forward again.","Yuan swung his sword, unleashing a torrent of Supreme Sword Aura infused with Chaotic Essence.","Yet the Ancient Chaos did not so much as flinch, charging straight into the attack without hesitation. To Yuan’s astonishment, the strike passed cleanly through its body, as though it were nothing more than an illusion.","\"Use Void Manipulation to attack it!\" A familiar voice suddenly resounded from afar.","It was Supreme Ruler Dena.","Hearing this, Yuan immediately attacked again, this time using Void Manipulation.","\"Your Void Manipulation is far too weak!\" the Ancient Chaos mocked as it devoured Yuan’s second attack without effort.","\"Then how about mine?!\" Supreme Ruler Dena roared, unleashing her power as she struck with Void Manipulation.","This time, the Ancient Chaos did not charge in so recklessly, and its figure vanished into the void as it chose to evade her attack instead.","\"He’s behind you!\" Supreme Ruler Dena shouted, but the Ancient Chaos had already slipped behind Yuan like a phantom.","Just as its jaws began to part, a surge of Eternal Essence erupted from Yuan’s body, forcing the Ancient Chaos to recoil in startled surprise.","Then, it hastily retreated to a safe distance.","\"That power...!\"","The Ancient Chaos fixed Yuan with its pitch-black gaze, a storm of fear and hatred churning within its eyes, its expression twisted as though recalling a distant, long-buried memory.","\"You recognize this power as well?\" Yuan asked, his intrigue deepening at the creature’s increasingly enigmatic existence.","\"What is your name?\" The Ancient Chaos suddenly asked.","\"Yuan.\"","\"Yuan...?\"","The Ancient Chaos fell silent for a moment, its presence turning eerily still before it spoke once more, its voice cold and resolute.","\"Consider yourself fortunate today, Yuan. Newly born and incomplete, I lack the power to contend with both of you at once. But mark my words—I will return, and when I do, I will kill... devour you.\"","\"You’re going to run away? Do you think I’ll let you do that?\" Yuan said.","\"Try to stop me if you can...\"","As it finished those words, the Ancient Chaos slipped into the void again.","Yuan tried to stop its retreat, but alas, his Void Manipulation was too weak to do anything. As for Supreme Ruler Dena, she was also in no condition to chase after it.","\"Seriously, what the hell was that thing?\" Yuan muttered out loud as he helplessly watched the Ancient Chaos disappear toward the Starry Sky.","Suddenly, a voice resounded inside Yuan’s head.","\"Ancient Chaos... It’s been a while since I heard that name...\"","Hearing this voice, Yuan turned to look at the Dragon God’s Vengeance.","\"Yeyou? You recognize it?\" he immediately asked."]},{"number":2388,"title":"Chapter 2388: Ancient Chaos(2)","paragraphs":["Dragon Goddess Yeyou responded to Yuan’s inquiry, her tone wary, \"The Ancient Chaos is a singular existence of unfathomable power—one that came into being long before even I did. From the moment of its birth, it wields Void Manipulation with flawless mastery, and its cultivation already stands at the level of a Cultivation God.\"","\"Though never confirmed, there are rumors that even if it is slain, it will one day reincarnate, retaining all of its past memories. To be frank, its existence is somewhat like yours. Completely abnormal.\"","\"What is its purpose?\" Yuan asked.","\"The Ancient Chaos’ purpose?\" Dragon Goddess Yeyou murmured. \"It lies within its very name—Chaos. It devours all things to strengthen itself. In that sense, it is similar to the Eater of Stars... yet it does not feast out of hunger. It devours simply because that is its nature.\"","\"Since it was just reborn, it must have been killed before. I wonder who killed a monster like that,\" Yuan wondered out loud.","\"...\"","Dragon Goddess Yeyou returned to being quiet.","Not wanting to bother her any longer, Yuan stowed away his weapons and deactivated his Absolute Dragon Awakening.","\"Although that thing is gone...\"","Yuan’s gaze shifted to the shattered remains of the black mountain—the Ancient Chaos’ discarded shell—its fragments strewn across the land, still faintly leaking traces of Chaotic Essence.","He proceeded to absorb every last trace of Chaotic Essence until nothing remained. However, upon closer inspection of the shattered shell, he realized it possessed the potential to become an invaluable material.","So, he gathered all of the shells and tossed them into his spatial ring.","<You have obtained Ancient Chaos’ Shell>","Afterward, he returned to the Queen Wraith of Demise and said, \"I’ve cleared out that energy as promised. You should honor your end of the bargain and let bygones be bygones.\"","\"...\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise remained silent.","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and spoke again, this time in a colder voice, \"Don’t tell me you still want to fight?\"","The Queen Wraith of Demise closed her eyes and drew a slow, steady breath before replying in a resigned voice, \"No... I will abide by my word and forgive you for slaughtering my children.\"","Though she did not voice it, after witnessing Yuan’s overwhelming prowess and his command over Chaotic Essence, the very power her kind feared, she realized he could easily defeat them.","If she were to escalate things between them, it would only result in the extinction of her race.","Yuan nodded and said, \"I will also promise not to attack any more Nether Wraiths for as long as I am within the Demise Ravine. Of course, that is if they don’t attack us first.\"","\"You need not worry about that, as I will guarantee that not a single one of my children will attack you from this point forth,\" said the Queen Wraith of Demise.","\"I’m glad we managed to settle this without bloodshed. Then, I’ll be taking my leave now.\"","Yuan turned around and flew away with Supreme Ruler Dena closely following behind.","The Queen Wraith of Demise did not follow and stayed behind.","\"You’re back!\" Lev almost started crying when he saw Yuan and Supreme Ruler Dena, as he’d been alone with thousands of Nether Wraiths this entire time.","\"We’ve settled things with the Queen Wraith of Demise, so we’re leaving now,\" Yuan said to him.","Lev nodded and followed them.","Meanwhile, the Nether Wraiths completely ignored them and returned to their queen’s side.","\"They won’t attack us again, right?\" Lev asked as he watched them leave.","\"Unless they want to die.\"","\"Then the rest of our journey through this Demise Ravine should be smooth sailing.\"","Sure enough, for the next several months, they were not bothered by any more Nether Wraiths. While they would occasionally spot some, the Nether Wraiths would only watch them from afar and never approach.","\"I’m hungry.\" Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly said.","\"I fed you not long ago,\" Yuan said.","\"I used too much energy saving you.\"","\"You only unleashed a single attack with Void Manipulation...\"","\"You wouldn’t understand how much power I used because your level of Void Manipulation is lacking,\" she countered.","\"...\"","Yuan was left speechless, unable to refute her reasoning.","’I really need to improve my Void Manipulation soon...’ he sighed inwardly.","\"Go ahead.\"","Yuan pulled down the clothes around his neck.","Without hesitation, Supreme Ruler Dena jumped on his back and started feasting on his blood.","Yuan noticed Lev staring at them with an envious gaze and said to him a moment later, \"I would let you taste my blood, but you’ll likely regret it.\"","\"Huh? What makes you say that?\" Lev asked, looking confused.","\"Because my blood contains Demon Sealing Aura. If you drink it, you’ll likely be sealed.\"","\"Then how come she’s fine?\" Lev pointed at Supreme Ruler Dena, who was sucking away without a care in the world.","\"She’s strong enough to ignore it.\"","\"That’s it?\"","\"That’s all.\"","Of course, Yuan could unseal him if Lev got sealed, but since it would be a hassle, he decided not to say anything.","Luckily, Lev no longer dared to drink his blood.","Eventually, they reached the end of the Demise Ravine. But since they started traveling from the end, they were technically exiting from the entrance.","\"I’m so glad we’re finally out of that place...\" Lev released a deep sigh after they escaped the place.","\"Now where to?\" Yuan asked Supreme Ruler Dena.","Supreme Ruler Dena pondered for a moment before pointing in a certain direction.","\"The closest city should be in that direction.\"","They followed the direction she pointed at shortly later.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the Starry Sky...","\"That was a little dangerous...\" The Ancient Chaos sighed aloud once it confirmed it was safe.","\"That bastard called Yuan... just what the hell is he? How can a mere human use Eternal Essence? And that familiar scent on him... Is he related to that monster?\"","The Ancient Chaos trembled just at the thought of that ’monster’.","\"No matter! Once I regain my strength and mature into my true form, I will surely devour him!\" he swore loudly as he continued drifting deeper into the Starry Sky."]},{"number":2389,"title":"Chapter 2389: Bloody Expanse","paragraphs":["Somewhere in the Demonic Realm, the current Supreme Leader sat before several high-ranking demons as they relayed their news to him.","\"I have just received confirmation that ’woman’ has disappeared from the Deprived Crimson Valley’s Final Valley. However, we have yet to confirm whether she simply left the Final Valley and moved to a new location or the Deprived Crimson Valley altogether.\"","\"Does she even have the capability to leave the Deprived Crimson Valley?\" someone suddenly asked.","The Supreme Ruler responded, \"Since we have never replaced a Supreme Ruler without the former one dying or being properly removed, there is no telling how much of the Demon God’s Authority she still retains—if she can access it at all.\"","\"However, we will proceed under the assumption that she still retains her powers and may have already escaped the Deprived Crimson Valley. Dispatch both the Elite Execution Squad and the Special Execution Squad, but do not engage. Observe her movements and report back to me immediately.\"","\"As you command, Supreme Ruler!\"","\"Is there anything else I should be aware of?\" the Supreme Ruler asked.","After a brief silence, one of the individuals raised his hand and spoke hesitantly, \"I’m not certain how credible it is—or even if it’s real—but there’s been a rumor circulating within the Deprived Crimson Valley... of someone wielding Demon Sealing Aura.\"","\"What?! Demon Sealing Aura?!\"","The room erupted into chaos. \"But all of the Sealers are dead—at least, they should be!\"","\"Perhaps one of them managed to escape? If they’re already within the Deprived Crimson Valley, then there’s no need to panic,\" another suggested.","\"Right? It’s not like they can leave the Deprived Crimson Valley alone.\"","However, the Supreme Ruler spoke once more, his voice turning cold and resolute.","\"No. We will treat this matter with the same urgency as Dena. The Demon Sealing Aura, with its accursed power against our kind, is a blatant affront to the Demon God. I will not permit anyone to wield such power... even within the confines of the Deprived Crimson Valley.\"","\"Trace the source of this rumor and verify its truth. If a Demon Sealer is indeed alive... execute them without hesitation.\"","\"As you command, Supreme Ruler!\"","The meeting ended shortly after, and everyone but the Supreme Ruler left.","\"The reemergence of a Demon Sealer... and Dena’s disappearance...\" The Supreme Ruler muttered, his expression turning grave. \"Is this mere coincidence... or something far more deliberate?\"","Meanwhile, Yuan and his group arrived at a new location—a boundless sea of deep crimson liquid, as though it were an endless ocean of blood.","\"This must be the Bloody Expanse,\" Yuan remarked as he took in the scene.","\"It looks even redder than I remember,\" he added, recalling the moment Tian Chenyu had first laid eyes upon it.","True to its name, the Bloody Expanse was a vast sea stained crimson with blood, spilled by the countless sea creatures that endlessly slaughtered and devoured one another, as well as demons fighting over it. After all, the Bloody Expanse encompassed more than half of the entire Demonic Realm.","Unlike the beings of the Nine Heavens, those within the Demonic Realm possessed unnaturally thick blood that did not easily disperse in water. After trillions of years of ceaseless slaughter and corruption, that very blood accumulated, giving rise to the Bloody Expanse.","Moreover, despite being an ocean of blood, it was unfit for consumption—even by demons—its essence so deeply corrupted that not even their kind could safely devour it without getting sick.","Of course, for a demon to fall ill meant that something was wrong with its blood, and for their kind, that was no different from becoming crippled, akin to a cultivator whose spiritual energy had been corrupted.","\"Whenever you’re ready,\" Supreme Ruler Dena said as she hovered above the blood-red sea.","Yuan followed without hesitation. Lev, however, trailed behind with visible reluctance. Even as a First Level False God, the Bloody Expanse remained an exceedingly perilous domain, where a single lapse in awareness could result in being dragged beneath the surface and devoured by the lurking sea creatures below.","Though one might assume they could simply ascend into the sky and distance themselves from the sea, such thoughts were futile, as many of the creatures below were capable of leaping beyond the clouds themselves.","Yet, even after traveling for three consecutive days, not a single sea creature made an attempt to attack them.","This left Lev puzzled.","\"Is there something wrong with the Bloody Expanse? The Sea Devils aren’t attacking at all,\" he wondered out loud.","In the Demonic Realm, the sea creatures were called Sea Devils.","\"They’re likely wary of Dena’s presence,\" Yuan remarked calmly.","However, Supreme Ruler Dena shook her head. \"No... that can’t be. They’ve attacked me before.\"","\"Seriously?\" Even Yuan couldn’t hide his surprise now, his curiosity piqued as his earlier assumption began to falter.","He proceeded to expand his divine sense even deeper into the sea.","\"It’s empty,\" he said a moment later. \"I cannot sense a single creature in the water within a ten-thousand-mile radius.\"","\"What? How is that possible? The Bloody Expanse is usually teeming with Sea Devils,\" Lev said, bewildered. \"It’s common knowledge that they reproduce far faster than they can kill one another.\"","Suddenly, Lev came to an abrupt halt, his face draining of color as an expression of absolute terror took hold.","\"What’s wrong?\" Yuan asked, his brows furrowing slightly.","\"Actually... I think I might know what happened here...\" Lev replied, swallowing hard as unease crept into his voice.","\"There is a legend of a powerful Sea Devil that dwells within the Bloody Expanse—the Bloody Devil Emperor. It is a mysterious entity said to appear only once every hundred billion years. And whenever it does, the Bloody Expanse deepens in crimson, while all other Sea Devils retreat into hiding until it vanishes again.\"","\"Bloody Devil Emperor? Do you know anything about this entity?\" Yuan asked, turning to Supreme Ruler Dena.","\"It’s nothing more than folklore,\" she replied calmly. \"No one has ever actually laid eyes on this so-called Bloody Devil Emperor.\""]},{"number":2390,"title":"Chapter 2390: Bloody Devil Emperor","paragraphs":["\"Folktale or not, it doesn’t change the fact that something weird is happening within the Bloody Expanse,\" Yuan said. \"Let’s keep moving. If we encounter the source, we’ll deal with it then.\"","\"Deal with it...?\" Lev’s jaw dropped. \"If the Bloody Devil Emperor is real, I’d rather we just run from it.\"","\"What are you so afraid of? You’re traveling with the strongest Supreme Ruler and Demon Sealer in the world. If I were you, I’d even dare provoke the Demon God,\" Yuan laughed.","Lev glanced at Supreme Ruler Dena with a wry smile. Though she was undoubtedly the strongest among the Supreme Rulers, she had yet to recover her full strength. As for Yuan—despite his overwhelming prowess—he was still only at the First Level False God.","They continued their journey shortly after.","However, even after traveling for another week, they have yet to encounter a single Sea Devil, almost as if their existence had been completely wiped from this world.","It wasn’t just Lev who found the situation unsettling. Even Supreme Ruler Dena felt a faint sense of unease at the unusual stillness.","Suddenly, Supreme Ruler Dena stopped moving and shouted, \"Something is coming!\"","Supreme Ruler Dena was the first to spot this presence due to her superior cultivation, but Yuan wasn’t too far behind and also sensed it a few moments later. As for Lev, he remained oblivious.","\"What a terrifying presence...\" Yuan swallowed, a rare hint of unease surfacing in his voice.","Whatever was emitting this aura surpassed even the Ancient Chaos. In fact, he had only encountered something remotely similar a handful of times. If he had to draw a comparison, the closest would be Long Wu Qing, the eldest daughter of the Dragon God.","\"W-What is it?! What’s coming?!\" Lev cried out, panic rising as he caught sight of their tense expressions.","Several agonizing minutes passed in silence. Just as Lev was about to speak again, the surface of the crimson sea began to swell—bulging outward as though a colossal air bubble were forming beneath it.","First, a massive crimson horn broke through the surface, followed by the rest of its form—a bloated, balloon-like figure rising from the blood sea.","When Yuan saw the creature, his brows lifted, disbelief flickering across his face.","\"This is... a goldfish?!\" Yuan exclaimed, startled by how the creature’s plump, rounded form resembled that of a goldfish—albeit an absurdly massive one.","Sure enough, the Sea Devil bore a striking resemblance to a goldfish, its body cloaked in crimson and silver scales. Six majestic fins fanned out from its sides, while a regal dorsal fin rose from its back, shaped like a crown.","The crimson goldfish rose fully from the Bloody Expanse, ascending into the sky until it hovered above Yuan’s group like a blazing sun.","Then, its round, golden eyes settled upon them—or more precisely... upon Yuan.","Suddenly, a voice resounded, its origin impossible to discern, echoing from all directions at once.","\"I came here because I sensed a familiar presence, but you are not who I first believed you to be. More surprising still... you are merely a human,\" the goldfish spoke, its voice still echoing from all directions at once.","\"Are you the Bloody Devil Emperor?\" Yuan asked.","\"Bloody Devil Emperor? What a dreadful name,\" the goldfish replied, its voice laced with disdain. \"Do I truly resemble a being that would bear something so distasteful?\"","It continued, \"I am the splendid, dignified, majestic, Primal Sovereign of the Seas!\"","The goldfish introduced itself as the Primal Sovereign of the Seas.","\"Primal?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this familiar word.","\"Are you a being from the Primal Expanse? If so, how did you come to be here?\" Yuan asked.","\"Oh? So you have set foot in the Primal Expanse as well,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied, a hint of intrigue in its voice. \"I am the Sovereign of the Seas—there is no body of water in this universe beyond my reach. Wherever water exists, I may travel as I please.\"","Yuan glanced at the Bloody Expanse before continuing, \"Are you responsible for the absence of Sea Devils?\"","\"Indeed,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied without hesitation.","\"These waters had grown far too crowded, so I purged half of their population. And this is hardly the first time I’ve done so,\" it added, its tone laced with pride.","\"Why would you do something like that?\" Yuan asked, his brows knitting in confusion.","\"It is my hobby—duty as the Sovereign of the Seas to maintain balance and prevent these waters from descending into unchecked chaos, no matter the world they belong to,\" it replied calmly.","Then, with a hint of satisfaction in its tone, it added, \"Besides... the creatures here are far more succulent—fresh and full of vitality, unlike the tasteless refuse of the Primal Expanse.\"","\"Now, it is my turn to ask you some questions.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas narrowed its eyes at Yuan and asked in a serious voice, \"You... why do you smell like the Primal Monarch? Because of your scent, I came here. However, now that I think about it, there’s no reason that old man would be here.\"","\"The Primal Monarch, huh? I had a feeling you knew him.\" Yuan said with a smile. \"He’s my father.\"","\"WHAT!\"","The Primal Sovereign exclaimed in disbelief, its eyes widening until they bulged like overinflated orbs on the verge of bursting.","Then, its massive body plunged back into the crimson sea, sending a towering tidal wave surging outward.","\"What the hell?!\" Lev shouted in alarm.","With a casual flick of her sleeve, Supreme Ruler Dena split the oncoming wave in two, parting it cleanly so it flowed past them without harm.","\"...\"","After a few minutes of silence, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas emerged from the Bloody Expanse once again and asked in an awkward voice, \"The Primal Monarch... giving birth to a human? Is that even possible?\"","\"Oh, I should clarify,\" Yuan said suddenly. \"He’s not my real father—more of an adoptive one.\"","\"You should have stated that earlier! Nearly gave me a heart attack!\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas roared."]},{"number":2391,"title":"Chapter 2391: Primal Sovereign of the Seas","paragraphs":["Yuan watched the Primal Sovereign of the Seas with amusement before asking, his curiosity piqued, \"What is your relationship with the Primal Monarch?\"","\"...\"","After a brief pause, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied, \"We are... something akin to acquaintances.\"","\"Something akin?\" Yuan echoed, raising a brow at the peculiar choice of words.","\"If you’re concerned that we might be enemies, you may set your mind at ease. Anyone who understands what the Primal Monarch is capable of would never be foolish enough to stand against him.\"","\"Well, he is the most powerful being in the Primal Expanse,\" Yuan remarked.","However, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas let out a low chuckle, as though it found Yuan’s statement rather amusing for some reason.","\"What is it?\" Yuan inquired with a puzzled face.","\"You really know nothing about the Primal Monarch despite being his adopted son, huh? Just how much do you know about the Primal Monarch?\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas asked.","Yuan sifted through his memories, trying to recall everything he knew about the Primal Monarch. Yet after some time, he came to a realization—that beyond the fact that the Primal Monarch stood at the very apex of the Primal Expanse, he knew almost nothing about him.","\"Now that you mention it... I don’t really know much about him. I trained under him for a time, yet he never spoke of himself or revealed his true capabilities,\" Yuan said aloud.","\"I see. So the Primal Monarch told you nothing,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied. \"I suppose he has his reasons.\"","\"How about you share some insight about him?\" Yuan said with a faint smile.","\"And potentially offend the Primal Monarch? You might as well starve me to death.\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas viciously shook his head, causing his round body to shake like firm jello.","\"If you want to know more about him, you can simply ask him yourself.\"","\"I will do just that... whenever I see him again.\"","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"What is it? I noticed that you have been glaring at me for some time now. If you have any questions, go ahead and ask.\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas said after a moment of silence.","Yuan hesitated for a second before asking, \"Do you have any connections to the True Emperor of the Seas? I noticed that both of you have a similar name.\"","\"True Emperor of the Seas?\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas repeated, its voice dripping with immense disdain, as though it were spitting out something foul.","\"There is absolutely no connection between this majestic one and that disgusting impostor. In fact, I would kill it if I could.\"","Yuan was genuinely taken aback by the sheer intensity of its response—and the deep-seated repulsion it harbored toward the so-called True Emperor of the Seas.","\"You mean even you are not strong enough to kill it?\" Yuan asked, genuine surprise coloring his voice.","Even he lacked the confidence to defeat the Primal Sovereign of the Seas at full strength—yet such a being spoke as though it could not deal with the True Emperor of the Seas. If that were the case... just how powerful was that creature?","\"Let me correct you first. It’s not that I am unable to kill it. I simply do not wish to entangle myself in unnecessary trouble by killing it. If I wished to kill that imposter, I could easily do so with a single flap.\"","However, such a response only gave Yuan more questions than answers.","\"Do you mind telling me what kind of consequences killing it would bring? To be frank... it’s on my kill list,\" he said.","\"What?\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ round eyes widened with delight.","\"You... want to kill it? I’d like to ask why.\"","\"It’s a long story, but I have some unsettled grudges with it.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas suddenly fell silent.","Then, it spoke with a profound grin on its face, \"Since you are the Primal Monarch’s son, I suppose it will be fine even if you kill it.\"","\"Huh? What’s that supposed to mean?\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas chuckled, \"Don’t mind the minor details. Instead, I have a proposition for you.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ suspicious behavior.","\"I’m listening.\"","\"If you succeed in killing that impostor known as the True Emperor of the Seas, I shall reward you with a single drop of this majestic being’s Blood Essence!\"","\"What?!\" Yuan exclaimed, his shock palpable.","\"You heard correctly,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas continued, leaving no room for doubt. \"Slay the True Emperor of the Seas, and I will grant you my Blood Essence. You need the Blood Essence of Supreme Bloodlines to complete your bloodline, right?\"","\"How do you know about that?\" Yuan muttered in a daze.","To know about his bloodline so well, there was no way the Primal Sovereign of the Seas was a mere ’acquaintance’ to the Primal Monarch.","\"There are very few things this majestic one does not know, especially when it pertains to the Primal Monarch.\"","\"I’ll do it! I’ll kill the True Emperor of the Seas!\" Yuan declared without a hint of hesitation, his voice firm and resolute.","It was something he had intended to do one day, regardless of the consequences, so he might as well reap some amazing rewards that came with it.","\"That’s what I like to hear, Primal Monarch’s son! Now, prepare yourself!\"","\"Wait, what?\" Yuan tilted his head with a puzzled expression after hearing the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ last few words.","\"What is there to be confused about? I am going to drag the True Emperor of the Seas here so you can kill it,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas explained, leaving Yuan momentarily speechless.","\"You mean you’re going to summon it? Here? Right now?\" Yuan asked, struggling to process how abruptly the situation had escalated.","\"That’s right,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied calmly, as though summoning such a being were no more extraordinary than stirring the tides."]},{"number":2392,"title":"Chapter 2392: Primal Sovereign of the Seas(2)","paragraphs":["\"You can’t be serious...\" Yuan refused to believe that the Primal Sovereign of the Seas would drag the True Emperor of the Seas to the Demonic Realm just so he could kill it.","\"Don’t worry, it won’t take long to drag that imposter here,\" said the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, thinking that Yuan was worried it might take too long to bring the True Emperors of the Seas to him.","\"...\"","Yuan fell silent, deep in thought, questioning whether he truly possessed the strength to face the True Emperor of the Seas—a being said to be beyond even the reach of Cultivation Gods—at his current level.","\"It’s now or never,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas suddenly said, snapping Yuan out of his thoughts. \"Once I depart, I will enter hibernation, and I will not emerge again for millions of years.\"","Yuan rubbed his eyes and let out a long sigh before nodding, a trace of resignation in his expression.","\"Alright... I’ll fight it now. But whether I can kill it is another matter, so don’t be disappointed if I fail.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas let out a low chuckle before replying, \"In my eyes, you possess what it takes to slay that impostor, but it will be a difficult fight. However, if you would rather have more time to prepare, I can afford to wait a while longer. I am still in the midst of my purge and will remain awake for a few hundred more years.\"","\"...\"","Yuan stared into the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ eyes for a moment before asking, \"Are you really not going to tell me the consequences of killing it—why you are hesitant to kill it?\"","A grin appeared on the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ face as it responded, \"If you are worried that it might be a trap, you are free to refuse. But there’s a reason I am offering you my Blood Essence as a reward, something I have never even considered doing until today.\"","Yuan closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he opened his eyes, they were brimming with resolve and confidence.","\"Very well. I accept your challenge. There’s no need to wait, either. We’ll do it now,\" Yuan declared.","\"WELL SAID!\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas roared, its massive form surging skyward as it shot toward the heavens.","Then, it performed a majestic backflip in the sky before plunging back down toward the crimson sea.","Yuan and the others braced themselves for a towering tidal wave, yet to their astonishment, when the Primal Sovereign of the Seas struck the surface, not a single drop of water stirred, and its immense form vanished instantly into the crimson depths.","\"I will return within a few days. You may use this time to prepare yourself.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ voice resounded shortly after.","Instead of immediately beginning his preparations, Yuan took a moment to explain the situation to Supreme Ruler Dena and Lev, who had been observing from the sidelines, utterly bewildered by everything that had transpired.","\"So, to sum it up,\" Lev began, trying to piece everything together, \"the Bloody Devil Emperor is actually called the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, a being from an entirely different world—a third world—and it’s going to drag another creature here for you to kill?\"","\"That sounds about right.\" Yuan calmly nodded.","Supreme Ruler Dena then asked, \"Can we assist you?\"","She had little interest in the situation itself, and her only concern was whether she could be of help to him.","Yuan smiled faintly and shook his head. \"I appreciate the offer, but I’ll handle this on my own. I’m not doing this solely because of the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, either. I have my own reasons for wanting it dead.\"","His gaze darkened slightly. \"This is... a grudge carried over from a distant past.\"","\"Then we’ll wait for you to take care of it.\" Supreme Ruler Dena didn’t say anything else and flew away, giving Yuan some space.","\"Good luck, I guess.\" Lev didn’t know what else to say and followed Supreme Ruler Dena shortly after.","Now that he was somewhat alone, Yuan sat in the lotus position in midair and closed his eyes to cultivate, preparing for the upcoming battle.","Meanwhile, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas had already departed the Demonic Realm, gliding through a spatial tunnel accessible only through its unique authority, its presence weaving effortlessly between worlds as it set out in search of the True Emperor of the Seas.","When the Primal Sovereign of the Seas emerged from the spatial tunnel, it found itself within a vast, boundless sea in the Nine Heavens.","It then began its search for the True Emperor of the Seas, and within mere moments, it found it.","To the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, locating any living creature within the waters of the three worlds was as effortless as a human observing the lines upon their own palm.","\"Found you, you little imposter!\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas slipped back into its spatial tunnel, traveling for only a few fleeting seconds before arriving at its destination.","When it emerged once more, it had arrived in the Ninth Heaven, within the Sea of Infinite Descent, one of the Four Gateways to Hell.","Meanwhile, not far from the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, the True Emperor of the Seas—who had slumbered for thousands of years—suddenly jolted awake, stirred by a menacing and all-too-familiar presence.","The moment it recognized the owner of that presence, the True Emperor of the Seas reacted without hesitation, immediately attempting to flee through its own spatial tunnel—one that connected every sea within the Nine Heavens.","\"To think you would try to flee from me within water... how laughable!\"","Behind it, the True Emperor of the Seas could hear the Primal Sovereign’s mocking laughter, sounding like a chilling tide closing in.","\"Damn it! What the hell do you want from me, you fat fuck?!\" the True Emperor of the Seas cried out, not even daring to glance back."]},{"number":2393,"title":"Chapter 2393: I Just Want to Talk","paragraphs":["\"How dare you address this majestic one with such foul language!\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas exclaimed with disbelief after hearing the True Emperor of the Seas’ curse at it.","\"I have a name, you know? I am the Primal Sovereign of the Seas—the true Ruler of the Seas, you imposter!\"","\"I know who the hell you are! Every sea creature in this world is aware of you! What I don’t know is why the hell you’re chasing after me!\" The True Emperor of the Seas shouted, panic in its voice.","\"Why are you running? I just want to talk,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas said in a calm voice, trying to convince it to stop.","\"Do you think I am stupid or something?! There’s no way in hell you’re only here to talk when you’re chasing after me so vigorously! If you really want to talk, we can talk like this!\"","Unsurprisingly, the True Emperor of the Seas did not fall for such an obvious trick.","\"You’re only making this more difficult for yourself later with all this running around.\"","\"What are you talking about?!\"","\"Stop for a moment, and I’ll tell you everything.\"","\"Seriously, you can stop that nonsense! I am not going to stop running until you leave!\"","\"I guess we’ll have to do this the hard way...\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas sighed out loud as it casually chased after the True Emperor of the Seas.","Of course, if it truly wanted to catch up, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas could easily do so. However, it wanted to toy with the True Emperor of the Seas for some time before doing so. This also allowed Yuan some more time to prepare for the battle.","The True Emperor of the Seas quickly realized that it was being toyed with and shouted in desperation, \"Don’t you know who’s behind me?! If you kill me, you’ll definitely be killed, too!\"","\"Of course, I am aware of your master. That’s why I haven’t touched you for so long despite my desire to.\"","\"Then why the hell are you trying to kill me now?!\"","\"Who said I am trying to kill you? I just want to talk.\"","\"We’re talking right now!\"","\"No, this is something that we can only discuss while motionless.\"","\"That’s utter bullshit!\"","\"Truly, I just want to talk.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas remained insistent that it merely wanted to talk, but the True Emperor of the Seas was having none of it and continued fleeing as if its life depended on it.","Over the course of the next week, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas relentlessly pursued the True Emperor of the Seas, chasing it across hundreds of seas and oceans throughout every realm within the Nine Heavens.","\"Oh, right. A day in this world is a year in that world...\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas suddenly recalled this important detail after a week of chasing.","\"I am a bit reluctant to end something this entertaining, but alas... consider yourself lucky that I hadn’t thought of doing this earlier, as I could easily do this for thousands of years without getting bored.\"","\"What are you going to do to me?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas cried out in terror when it noticed its pursuer increasing in speed and gradually catching up to it.","\"I just want to talk.\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas kept to his original joke.","Eventually, the True Emperor of the Seas reached its limit.","It came to an abrupt halt and turned to face its pursuer after having already realized it could not outrun the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, leaving it no choice but to fight.","\"Eat this, you fat fuck!\"","The True Emperor of the Seas lashed out in desperation, unleashing a devastating attack that consumed half of its energy in the blink of an eye.","Yet the Primal Sovereign of the Seas did not so much as flinch. Instead, it merely laughed, its mocking voice echoing through the depths, \"What a waste of energy! You’ll regret exhausting yourself soon!\"","Then it confronted the attack, opening its mouth to devour it.","\"What?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas exclaimed in shock, its eyes widening as its attack was so effortlessly deflected.","It had always known the Primal Sovereign of the Seas was overwhelmingly powerful, but it had never imagined the gap between them would be this vast, almost like comparing a small lake to the boundless ocean.","After swallowing the attack, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ round figure vanished for a split second before reappearing directly before the True Emperor of the Seas.","Then, without hesitation, it opened its massive jaws and bit down. Yet it neither devoured nor harmed it. Instead, it simply held the True Emperor of the Seas in its mouth, as though a cat had caught its prey and was toying with it.","The next moment, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas activated its ability and disappeared from the Nine Heavens.","Meanwhile, Yuan had been waiting for the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ return for seven years straight, and he was beginning to wonder if something had gone wrong or if it had simply forgotten.","Just as Yuan lowered his gaze to the crimson sea and let out a deep sigh, he noticed the surface begin to bulge once more, but this time, it swelled far larger than before.","A second later, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas emerged from the crimson sea with a familiar-looking being in its mouth.","’No way! He actually dragged it here!’ Yuan cried inwardly after seeing the True Emperor of the Seas.","\"He’s all yours!\" The Sovereign of the Seas said to Yuan before spitting the True Emperor of the Seas out.","Without hesitation, Yuan activated Absolute Dragon Awakening and summoned Number One Under Heaven, even using Chaotic Essence and Eternal Essence before striking at the True Emperor of the Seas as it fell from the sky—its mind still in utter disbelief and confusion.","\"WHAT THE FUCK IS GOING ON?!\" It cried out loud as Yuan cut through its tentacles like tofu."]},{"number":2394,"title":"Chapter 2394: Fighting the True Emperor of the Seas","paragraphs":["The True Emperor of the Seas fell from the sky after the Primal Sovereign of the Seas spat it out, but before the True Emperor of the Seas could even touch the surface of the crimson sea, Yuan had severed all of its massive tentacles.","Splash!","The True Emperor of the Seas fell into the water, causing a massive tidal wave to surge in all directions.","Yet, despite having all of its tentacles severed, the True Emperor of the Seas regenerated them almost instantly, its recovery ability surpassing even that of high-ranking demons.","Then, it rose from the crimson sea, an overwhelming aura erupting from its body—dense with bloodlust and seething fury.","\"I don’t care anymore! I am going to kill all of you, even if it’s the last thing I do!\" The True Emperor of the Seas declared as it set its eyes on Yuan, who was clearly the easiest target there.","\"Oh? It can actually speak?\" Yuan mumbled after confirming the True Emperor of the Seas could speak, as he doubted his ears earlier when it cursed out loud.","The True Emperor of the Seas wasted no time. Having marked Yuan, it raised its massive tentacles—each capable of flattening an entire mountain—before bringing them crashing down toward him.","\"The same trick as last time, huh?\" Yuan muttered, recalling how it had used the very same attack against Tian Yang before.","However, this time, he wasn’t as weak as Tian Yang, and he actually had the prowess to fight back.","He gathered his Supreme Sword Aura and Eternal Essence before swinging his sword at the incoming tentacles, slicing them as easily as a hot blade going through a thin stick of butter.","\"What?! That power is—!\" The True Emperor of the Seas couldn’t believe its eyes after seeing Yuan use Eternal Essence.","Although Yuan had also used Eternal Essence during his earlier attack, the True Emperor of the Seas was too distracted to notice. This time, however, he sensed it clearly.","\"Why the hell do you have that power as a human?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas questioned Yuan. No, it demanded an answer.","\"Who the hell are you?! And why are you colluding with the Primal Sovereign of the Seas against me?!\" It continued to bombard Yuan with questions.","\"You don’t remember me?\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Well... I suppose that’s only natural, given how much time has passed,\" he added.","\"My name is Yu—Tian Yang, and I am here to collect a debt you owe... one long overdue,\" he declared.","\"A debt?! When the hell did that happen?!\"","\"Some time during the Primordial Era.\"","\"Primordial Era?! You’ve got to be kidding me! That was countless years ago!\"","Yuan let out a cold sneer, his gaze turning frigid. \"I don’t care how much time has passed—or whether you remember. Today... I will be the one to hunt you!\"","After his declaration, Yuan started attacking the True Emperor of the Seas again.","\"Fuck!\"","The True Emperor of the Seas was quickly overwhelmed by Yuan’s immense prowess. Not only had it spent an entire week being relentlessly pursued by the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, but it had also exhausted half of its energy just moments before encountering Yuan, leaving it in the most weakened state it had ever experienced.","\"It’s useless! Even with that power, you cannot kill me!\" the True Emperor of the Seas declared, its mocking laughter echoing across the sea as Yuan severed thousands of its tentacles only for it to recover fully in the blink of an eye.","Even though Yuan had fought and defeated it before during the Supreme Sword Emperor Qualifications, the True Emperor of the Seas at that time was merely a fake clone, and all of its weak points were fabricated for the trial, so Yuan couldn’t use the same method for the real thing.","Yet, he didn’t seem worried in the slightest and continued to swing his sword at the giant squid.","\"Hahaha! Are you dumb or something?! No matter how many times you sever my arms, they will endlessly regenerate!\" The True Emperor of the Seas laughed out loud.","However, Yuan completely ignored it and continued attacking for the next several days, until the entire sea was littered with the True Emperor of the Seas’ severed tentacles.","\"Useless! Useless! Useless! Hahaha—?!\"","The True Emperor of the Seas’ laughter abruptly ceased as it sensed something amiss within its body after days of relentless regeneration. Its recovery—once near-instant—had begun to noticeably slow.","\"What?! My regeneration! What the hell did you do to my body?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas cried out in a terrified voice.","\"...\"","Yuan paid it no mind and continued his assault, unleashing a relentless barrage of attacks with shifting energies. At times, he struck with Supreme Sword Aura; at others, with Chaotic Essence—and sometimes, he wielded both in tandem, layering their might into a single, devastating strike.","The True Emperor of the Seas recognized four of the five energies Yuan wielded—his Supreme Sword Aura, Chaotic Essence, Celestial Qi, and Eternal Essence. However, the fifth was completely unfamiliar to it, and it immediately assumed that unknown power to be the source of the anomaly.","While the True Emperor of the Seas remained unaware, Lev and Supreme Ruler Dena—watching from afar—recognized that energy all too well. They had seen Yuan wield it before, and there was no mistaking it.","It was none other than Demon Sealing Aura.","Although Demon Sealing Aura was most effective against demons, it could also affect other beings if wielded with sufficient strength. It had been created specifically to counter demons and their regenerative abilities. In other words, it could suppress and weaken one’s capacity to regenerate.","Despite Yuan’s overwhelmingly powerful Demon Sealing Aura, the True Emperor of the Seas possessed the cultivation of a Cultivation God and an enormous physique, meaning it required a tremendous amount of that aura before its effects began to show.","When the True Emperor of the Seas realized that Yuan was somehow suppressing its regenerative ability and that it currently lacked the strength to fight back, it immediately began contemplating escape. However, with the Primal Sovereign of the Seas lurking nearby, such a plan was far easier imagined than executed."]},{"number":2395,"title":"Chapter 2395: The True Emperor of the Seas’ Master","paragraphs":["\"Wait! Let’s talk about this!\" The True Emperor of the Seas suddenly shouted aloud, hoping to cease Yuan’s relentless attack for a moment.","However, Yuan immediately rejected, \"There’s nothing to talk about!\"","And he continued attacking.","Seeing that Yuan had no intention of listening, the True Emperor of the Seas had no choice but to dive toward the depths of the crimson sea to evade his attacks.","However, in the very next instant, it was struck with shock when it could not descend. It was as though an invisible barrier had formed beneath it, preventing it from entering the deeper waters entirely.","\"YOU FAT FUCK!\" The True Emperor of the Seas instantly realized the reason behind this phenomenon and turned to curse at the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, who was watching from afar with a wide grin on its face.","\"LET ME GO RIGHT THIS INSTANT!\" It roared with desperation.","\"I have no idea what you’re referring to,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas replied, its tone as nonchalant as ever.","The True Emperor of the Seas quickly returned its attention to Yuan and hastily said, \"I don’t know what he promised you, but he’s definitely tricking you into killing me since he’s afraid of doing it himself!\"","\"I am well aware of the risks,\" Yuan calmly remarked.","\"You do not!\" The True Emperor of the Seas insisted. \"Do you know who my master is?! If you kill me, my master will definitely kill you!\"","\"Your master?\" Yuan halted his attacks for the first time and inquired with a raised eyebrow. \"Who is that?\"","A hopeful grin appeared on the True Emperor of the Seas after it realized that Yuan wasn’t aware of its master. This meant that there was a chance he would stop attacking if he knew.","\"Listen well because I will only say this once!\" The True Emperor of the Seas proceeded to announce in a bold and prideful voice, \"My master is none other than Morveth!\"","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"...Who?\" Yuan asked without batting an eye at this unfamiliar name.","\"Y-You don’t know Master Morveth?! Even though you can wield Eternal Essence?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas couldn’t believe what was happening.","\"So what if I can use Eternal Essence? Should I automatically know every single Eternal in existence because of that?\" Yuan remarked with a sneer.","\"But Master Morveth is a Prime Eternal! Even if you don’t know all of the Eternals, there’s no way you wouldn’t know about the top ten!\"","\"Prime Eternal?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this unfamiliar term.","\"This is my first time hearing such a title,\" he said a moment later. \"So the top ten strongest Eternals are called Prime Eternals, huh?\"","\"You really aren’t aware of this...?\" The True Emperor of the Seas was in disbelief.","He’d never seen anyone so oblivious before.","After a moment of silence, it continued, \"Now that you know the identity of my master, do you still dare to attack me?!\"","\"...\"","Yuan silently looked at the True Emperor of the Seas before turning to look at the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, who was clearly aware of this and purposefully kept it a secret from him for some reason.","Yet, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas remained silent as it calmly met Yuan’s gaze, almost as if it couldn’t care less whether he knew about Morveth or not.","The True Emperor of the Seas smiled after seeing their weird interaction and asked, \"Did that fat fuck not tell you about my master? I told you that he was tricking you! Why don’t you help me kill him instead? I’ll be sure to let my master know of your good deeds.\"","Hearing such words, Yuan returned his attention to the True Emperor of the Seas and smiled.","\"Morveth?\" he muttered.","\"I don’t care if they’re top ten or the strongest Eternal in the universe! Nothing will stop me from killing you!\"","Yuan laughed as he continued his relentless assault on the bewildered True Emperor of the Seas.","\"Y-You’re only saying that because you don’t know how powerful my master is!\"","\"Like I said... I don’t care!\"","The True Emperor of the Seas’ attempts at negotiation failed, and with no means of escape, it was reduced to nothing more than prey on the brink of slaughter.","For the first time—despite its immortality and unparalleled regenerative abilities—it felt utterly helpless.","\"Fuck! I am not going to sit here and let you humiliate me like this any longer!\"","The True Emperor of the Seas roared in defiance, lashing out in retaliation, yet its efforts were desperate, almost pitiful in their futility.","Several weeks of relentless battle passed before Yuan finally muttered under his breath, \"It should be weak enough now...\"","The True Emperor of the Seas’ regenerative ability had deteriorated to the point where it now required an entire minute to restore even a single tentacle.","\"I haven’t used this ability since the incident with Bai Xutao, and since I am not in the Nine Heavens, there should be no issue using it now.\"","Yuan raised his hand and pointed toward the True Emperor of the Seas, drawing in a deep breath as a strange, unfamiliar energy began to surge from within his aura.","The moment the Primal Sovereign of the Seas sensed that aura, its eyes widened in shock.","\"That power! Don’t tell me he’s going to...!\" It immediately understood what Yuan was about to do, and its massive form trembled with excitement.","\"W-What are you trying to do?!\" the True Emperor of the Seas cried out, an ominous dread rising deep within its core.","\"I heard that you’re immortal and cannot be killed, right?\" Yuan suddenly remarked. \"Well, let’s see how you’ll deal with this!\"","<Forbidden Blood Extraction!>","Yuan activated Forbidden Blood Extraction and started forcibly drawing out the True Emperor of the Seas’ Blood Essence.","\"T-This is—!? It can’t be! You’re extracting my Blood Essence?!\" the True Emperor of the Seas cried out in panic as it realized what Yuan was doing."]},{"number":2396,"title":"Chapter 2396: Defeating the True Emperor of the Seas","paragraphs":["\"Hahaha! That kid is actually doing it! He’s actually forcefully extracting that imposter’s Blood Essence!\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas couldn’t contain its amusement and burst out laughing.","\"That Primal Monarch! He actually gave so much power to a mere human! Just what in heaven’s name is he thinking?!\"","Before Yuan revealed such a power, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas had not fully believed his claim of being the Primal Monarch’s adopted son. Now, after witnessing Yuan wield the power, all doubt vanished like smoke.","In fact, the Primal Sovereign of the Seas was even shocked that the Primal Monarch would grant a mere human such a terrifying power.","\"S-STOP! STOP IT RIGHT THIS INSTANT!\" The True Emperor of the Seas exclaimed in terror as it sensed its Blood Essence being formed and forcefully being extracted.","Of course, Yuan completely ignored its plea and continued to extract its Blood Essence.","With no other choice, the True Emperor of the Seas turned and fled in sheer panic. Though it could not escape into the water, it could still try to put distance between itself and Yuan.","It hoisted its massive, severed tentacles into the air and slammed them down like makeshift legs, scrambling away in a sight so desperate and absurd that it would have been laughable were it not so pitiful.","\"Hahaha!\" The Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ laughter grew louder and louder as it watched the True Emperor of the Seas’ desperate attempt.","As for Yuan, he didn’t even bother giving chase and merely muttered a single command.","\"Halt.\"","In an instant, the True Emperor of the Seas obeyed Yuan’s command and halted its movements.","\"T-This power! Primal Monarch?! What is your relationship with the Primal Monarch?!\" The True Emperor of the Seas finally recognized Yuan’s frightening power.","\"Did the Primal Monarch tell you to do this?! Why?! WHYYY?!\"","\"The Primal Monarch has nothing to do with this,\" Yuan calmly replied. \"As I said from the very beginning, I am here to settle a personal grudge.\"","\"BUT I DON’T EVEN REMEMBER DOING ANYTHING TO YOU!\" The True Emperor of the Seas roared in anger.","Yuan suddenly tapped his forehead with a finger, drawing out a dim, glowing orb from within. With a flick of his arm, he sent the orb streaking across the sky before it plunged into the True Emperor of the Seas.","What he had just bestowed upon it was a fragment of his memories—the moment of its own crimes.","After receiving the memory, the True Emperor of the Seas became as stiff as a rock. It was so shocked by the memory’s contents that it became a statue.","It could hardly believe that a single act—toying with a small group of people out of sheer boredom hundreds of millions of years ago—had led to this very moment... to its current humiliation and impending downfall.","\"You’re killing me over something like that?! I didn’t even kill you!\" the True Emperor of the Seas roared, snapping out of its daze.","\"No,\" Yuan replied coldly, \"but you killed my partner’s family... and I would even say it indirectly led to her death later.\"","He paused briefly before continuing, his voice lowering. \"That said... If I’m being honest, this is nothing more than a petty act of revenge. I was too weak—too pathetic—to do anything back then. So now... I’m making up for that weakness.\"","\"That’s utterly ridiculous! Are you really going to invoke the wrath of a Prime Eternal over something like that?!\"","\"This is not my first time offending an Eternal, and I doubt it will be the last,\" Yuan admitted.","\"SCREW YOOOOUUUU!!!\" The True Emperor of the Seas released its loudest roar yet.","The next moment, Yuan finished forming the True Emperor of the Seas’ Blood Essence and extracted it.","But instead of consuming it instantly, Yuan stored it inside a glass vial.","\"Seeing that you’re still alive...\" Yuan remarked, his gaze cold as he observed the True Emperor of the Seas’ sluggish movements, \"I wonder if I can extract more than just a single drop of Blood Essence from you?\"","\"YOU DARE?!\"","\"Why wouldn’t I dare?!\"","Yuan immediately attempted to extract another drop of Blood Essence from the True Emperor of the Seas. However, it felt as though he were trying to squeeze juice from an already dried fruit.","\"Most beings can only produce a single drop of Blood Essence in their lifetime,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas suddenly remarked. \"If you forcefully try, it’ll only devour their longevity.\"","\"Is that so? In that case...\"","A cold smile suddenly tugged at Yuan’s lips, sending chills down the True Emperor of the Seas’ boneless being.","\"Let’s keep at it until you’re dead!\" Yuan continued using Forbidden Blood Extraction on the True Emperor of the Seas in an attempt to kill it using this method.","With its Blood Essence forcibly extracted, the True Emperor of the Seas had been weakened to such an extent that it could barely move, let alone resist.","Yet Yuan showed no mercy and continued.","Eventually, with its lifeforce completely drained, the True Emperor of the Seas collapsed onto the surface of the sea, its immense body finally falling still.","However, even after its death, Yuan was not finished with it.","The next moment, Yuan activated another technique.","<Absolute Core Creation!>","Using his second forbidden technique, Yuan turned the True Emperor of the Seas’ corpse into a monster core!","Meanwhile, somewhere within the boundless Starry Sky, a certain entity sensed the exact moment the True Emperor of the Seas perished and released a cry filled with piercing anguish.","\"Who?! Who dared to kill my cute little pet?!\"","This entity immediately set its sights on the direction of the Demonic Realm.","Then, it raised a finger and pointed it toward the world.","\"I shall expunge you from this universe! Spear of Extinction!\"","A radiant glow gathered at its fingertip, swiftly condensing into a spear-like construct before it shot forward.","The attack tore through space itself, piercing the fabric of reality as it traversed the void—hurtling toward Yuan’s location at an unimaginable speed."]},{"number":2397,"title":"Chapter 2397: Prime Eternal Morveth","paragraphs":["As the Spear of Extinction streaked through the Starry Sky at speeds beyond light itself, anything that came into its path, or even drifted too close, was reduced to nothingness, dispersing like smoke.","In mere moments, hundreds of stars were erased from existence, their light extinguished as though they had never been.","The amount of Eternal Essence that surrounded this attack was immense and several times more powerful than Saaruk’s final attack on Yuan.","Because Yuan was currently within the Demonic Realm and not the Nine Heavens, there was no Absolute Power to shield him.","Of course, Yuan remained completely unaware that he had been targeted... or that the attack would reach him within mere minutes.","However, just as the Spear of Extinction was mere moments from reaching the Demonic Realm, a profound and unfathomable energy suddenly enveloped it—halting its advance mid-flight before obliterating it entirely.","Sensing that her attack had been destroyed, Prime Eternal Morveth turned her attention to the individual who had intervened and spoke to them.","\"What is the meaning of this, Deemo?\" she questioned, addressing this individual as Deemo.","\"I should be asking you that, Morveth,\" Deemo replied, his voice dripping with agitation. \"What reason do you have for attempting to destroy my world without provocation?\"","\"I wasn’t trying to destroy your world,\" she replied calmly. \"I was merely punishing the bastard who killed my beloved pet.\"","\"What kind of nonsense is that?\" Deemo shot back, his voice rising with anger. \"That attack of yours would have torn a hole straight through my entire world!\"","\"I may have used a bit more power than intended, given my... frustration,\" she replied, offering a rather half-hearted excuse.","Then, she continued, \"Anyway, hand over the bastard who killed my pet, and I’ll leave your world alone.\"","\"Hahaha!\" Deemo burst into laughter. \"Who do you think you are, making demands of me? Don’t mistake me for one of those ordinary Eternals you can order around. Have you forgotten? I stand as a Prime Eternal, just like you.\"","He continued, his voice laced with scorn, \"Your pet was killed because it was weak. And yet you seek vengeance for it. Have you no shame, given your status and power?\"","Morveth sneered with clear disdain. \"Had it been slain by some ordinary being from your world, I wouldn’t have cared. But it was killed by someone wielding Eternal Essence, which is no different from a direct challenge to me!\"","\"Oh? Someone who wields Eternal Essence is in my world?\" Deemo remarked with intrigue.","Then, he fell silent, presumably to look into his world.","A few moments later, he noticed three distinct and unique individuals in the same location somewhere at the Bloody Expanse.","’That’s the Primal Sovereign of the Seas, as well as the old Supreme Ruler Dena... Hmm? A human? In my world? He also looks familiar...’","It took a moment, but Deemo recognized Yuan’s face, and his soul, and his expression subtly stiffened.","’T-That human... Tian Chenyu?! When and how did he return to the Demonic Realm?! The gateway between our worlds is still clearly sealed!’ he cried inwardly.","He wasn’t sure how Yuan appeared in his world, but it was definitely a surprise he wasn’t expecting.","’And to think the first thing he does after returning is stir up trouble that nearly destroyed my world...’ Deemo sighed.","\"I have located and identified the individual who killed your pet,\" Deemo revealed to Morveth shortly later.","\"Then what are you waiting for? Hurry up and hand him over to me, and I will get out of your hair.\"","\"Do you truly expect me to help you for nothing?\" Deemo sneered.","\"You... What is it that you desire that you cannot already obtain yourself?\" Morveth asked, genuine intrigue flickering in her voice.","\"It’s not about what I want,\" he replied, a faint smirk tugging at his lips. \"It’s about what you’re willing to offer for my trouble. You see... that individual is quite the nuisance to deal with, so I’ll require proper compensation.\"","\"A nuisance? For a Prime Eternal like you? And within your own domain, no less?\" she replied, her voice thick with skepticism. \"I don’t believe that for a second.\"","\"You don’t have to believe me, but without proper compensation, I will not do anything for you,\" Deemo said in a stubborn tone.","\"...\"","After a long minute of silence, Morveth asked, \"Just out of curiosity, what kind of compensation would you consider proper?\"","\"Let’s see...\" Deemo pondered for a moment before responding, \"Thirty percent of your territory, as well as ten trillion years’ worth of Eternal Essence.\"","Morveth’s entire body stiffened, her composure cracking as disbelief surged through her upon hearing Deemo’s demand.","\"Are you out of your damn mind?! What kind of unreasonable compensation is that?! It’s not like I am asking you to kill another Prime Eternal for me!\" she exclaimed in bewilderment.","\"The cost of your earlier transgression will be included in the compensation as well,\" he added nonchalantly. \"In return, I will overlook your attack on my world.\"","\"Deemo, how dare you mock me with such nonsense?! Are you trying to start a war with me?!\" Morveth shouted in anger.","\"No, I am being super serious with you right now,\" Deemo replied with a clear voice. \"I believe that compensation is needed for me to get involved with that individual.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Morveth spoke, her tone sharp with suspicion. \"Just who is that bastard, for you to act so hesitant—so cowardly?\"","\"Don’t bother trying to provoke me with such petty tactics, Morveth,\" Deemo replied coolly. \"I am not afraid of him. He is simply... too troublesome to deal with, especially when there is nothing to be gained from it.\"","\"But you’re asking for far too much!\" she snapped. \"Thirty percent of my territory? Ten trillion years’ worth of Eternal Essence? Even a dozen Eternals wouldn’t be worth that, let alone a single individual! At that point, you might as well demand I become your servant!\"","\"So, you’re refusing my offer?\" Deemo asked.","\"Of course I am!\" she shot back without hesitation. \"That’s nothing short of robbery! Nobody would be foolish enough to accept it!\""]},{"number":2398,"title":"Chapter 2398: Acquiring Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ Blood Essence","paragraphs":["\"I see... so you refuse,\" Deemo said after Morveth rejected his terms. \"In that case, best of luck with your endeavors.\"","He paused briefly before adding, his tone turning colder, \"And I still expect compensation for your aggression toward my world.\"","\"Oh? And what will you do if I refuse?\" Morveth asked, her tone laced with provocation.","\"I won’t allow anyone to attack my territory and walk away unscathed,\" Deemo replied coldly.","\"Even if that individual is a Prime Eternal,\" he added.","\"Do you truly intend to fight me over something so trivial? It’s not as though I actually harmed your world,\" Morveth said.","Though her words suggested a desire to avoid conflict, it was not out of fear. As a Prime Eternal, her strength stood on equal footing with Deemo’s, making the outcome of such a clash uncertain. Still, it would be a troublesome ordeal, especially over such insignificant matters.","\"It’s not about the outcome—it’s about the principle,\" Deemo replied. \"If I entered your territory, defiled it, and you were left to clean up after me, would you simply let it go because no lasting damage was done?\"","Mervoth rubbed her eyes in a somewhat annoyed manner before speaking again, \"Fine, I will compensate you for attacking your world later. As for that person you’re protecting for some reason... I’ll deal with him later as well, as I am no longer in the mood after dealing with your nonsense.\"","Deemo let out a cold chuckle before responding, \"I am protecting him? That’s quite the misunderstanding you have there.\"","\"I don’t care what you say. I cannot see it any other way.\"","Deemo suddenly released a deep sigh and spoke with an odd flicker in his eyes, \"That man doesn’t need any protection.\"","After a brief pause, he continued, \"Morveth, speaking as someone who has experience with that man before, he’s not someone you want to meddle with.\"","\"That’s exactly what someone who’s afraid would say! That bastard killed my pet! I will kill him, no matter the cost!\"","Deemo simply shrugged in silence, having already anticipated her refusal to listen.","\"I couldn’t care less what you do, but do not involve me in your mess, and don’t enter or mess with my territory again.\"","After issuing one final warning, Deemo’s presence vanished completely, as though he had never been there at all.","Morveth departed as well, making preparations both to compensate Deemo for her attack on the Demonic Realm... and to deal with Yuan.","Meanwhile, in the Demonic Realm, after Yuan defeated the True Emperor of the Seas and turned it into a monster core, he stored it and its Blood Essence inside his spatial ring.","\"I must say, you have far exceeded all of my expectations, son of the Primal Monarch,\" the Primal Sovereign of the Seas said, approaching Yuan with a satisfied grin on its round face.","\"Though that impostor was weakened during my pursuit, I have little doubt you would have defeated him with relative ease even at full strength,\" it added.","Yuan turned to face the Primal Sovereign of the Seas and let out a quiet sigh.","\"So you were wary of the Prime Eternal backing that squid, huh? I should’ve known... No, perhaps I did know and simply chose to accept it.\"","\"Can you blame me? I cannot even handle an ordinary Eternal, let alone a Prime Eternal. Anyway, as promised, I shall bestow you my Blood Essence for getting rid of that nuisance.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas immediately extracted its own Blood Essence and offered it to Yuan.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at how quickly the Primal Sovereign of the Seas produced its Blood Essence since it was something that usually required a tremendous amount of time and energy to create, almost as if it had prepared it in advance.","Regardless, he didn’t question it and accepted the Blood Essence with a smile on his face.","<Acquired Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ Blood Essence!>","’Acquiring two Blood Essence at once... what a great harvest.’","Although he wasn’t sure whether the True Emperor of the Seas’ Blood Essence would qualify as a Supreme-grade Bloodline, he would find out soon enough.","\"What are you going to do now? Return to your feast?\" Yuan asked the Primal Sovereign of the Seas after putting away its Blood Essence.","\"That’s right. These waters won’t purge themselves, after all.\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas suddenly started submerging its body into the crimson sea.","\"It was a pleasure meeting you, son of the Primal Monarch.\"","It disappeared under the sea... only to return a few seconds later, as if it had forgotten something.","\"Oh, one more thing before I leave. Can you do me a solid and let the Primal Monarch know that I’d given you my Blood Essence when you see him?\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the goldfish and asked, \"The Blood Essence wasn’t actually a reward, was it? I bet you would’ve given it to me without needing me to do anything if I never mentioned the True Emperor of the Seas.\"","\"Hahaha! I have no idea what you’re talking about! Until next time, young man!\"","The Primal Sovereign of the Seas let out a nervous laugh as it hastily disappeared into the crimson water once again.","\"...\"","\"Is it finally over?\" Supreme Ruler Dena asked him shortly later.","\"I think so.\" Yuan nodded.","\"No, it’s not.\"","An unfamiliar voice suddenly resounded.","However, before Supreme Ruler Dena or Yuan could even react, an unfathomable energy enveloped the area, and in the next instant, a crimson barrier materialized around Yuan, trapping him within.","\"Yuan?!\"","Startled by the sudden turn of events, Supreme Ruler Dena reacted instantly, unleashing her strongest attack in an attempt to free Yuan. Yet, even with all of her power clashing against it, the crimson barrier remained utterly unscathed.","Meanwhile, within the barrier, Yuan found himself in a boundless expanse resembling the starry sky, but instead of darkness, it was drenched entirely in crimson.","And hovering not far away from him was a single silhouette, silently staring at him."]},{"number":2399,"title":"Chapter 2399: A Brief Conversation With the Demon God","paragraphs":["The first thing that came to Yuan’s mind when seeing this silhouette was Prime Eternal Morveth, as he’d just killed her pet, the True Emperor of the Seas.","\"Are you Morveth?\" he asked out loud.","\"What?\" The silhouette immediately frowned at Yuan’s question and said, \"I know it’s been a while since our last encounter, but to think you’d forgotten about me already.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this familiar voice and quickly corrected himself, \"You are... the Demon God?\"","\"I wasn’t expecting you to approach me first, much less this soon,\" he added.","The Demon God slowly raised an arm and rubbed his eyes before speaking, \"Do you have any idea what sort of trouble you’ve just caused for me?\"","\"Trouble...?\" Yuan tilted his head with a puzzled look on his face, as he was unaware of Prime Eternal Morveth’s earlier attack.","\"Because you killed Morveth’s little pet within my territory, she launched an attack on this world,\" the Demon God revealed, his tone calm yet heavy. \"Had I not intervened... this entire realm would have been erased just now.\"","\"Seriously...?\" Yuan muttered, momentarily dazed. He had never expected Prime Eternal Morveth to retaliate so swiftly, nor had he realized how close he had come to death just moments ago.","\"So you protected me? Thanks.\"","\"What? Don’t get it twisted,\" the Demon God sneered, his tone sharp with displeasure. \"I didn’t do it for you. I simply protected my world.\"","\"Either way, I’m still alive because of your actions,\" he chuckled lightly. \"So, in a sense... You did protect me.\"","\"And to think we once fought each other with our lives on the line,\" Yuan suddenly remarked.","\"Hahaha!\" The Demon God burst into laughter. \"You really do enjoy rewriting history, don’t you? My life was never at risk back then, and it was yours that hung by a thread.\"","\"Enough reminiscing,\" the Demon God suddenly said, his tone turning cold. \"I didn’t come here for that. I’m here to remind you that you owe me—for the trouble you’ve caused just now, and for entering my domain without permission, which is a direct violation of our agreement.\"","\"How did you even enter my world? The gateway is still sealed,\" he then asked.","Yuan shrugged, \"Honestly, I don’t know. I was in my personal world before coming here, and it was never my intention to come here, so it was an accident.\"","\"Bastard... you created a pathway from your personal world to my world? Just what are you planning?\" The Demon God narrowed his eyes at Yuan.","Yuan merely shook his head and explained, \"I don’t remember. As you can probably tell, I am not the same Tian Chenyu who fought you in the past. I am his reincarnation.\"","\"That explains why your soul is so much stronger than before,\" the Demon God sucked his teeth in annoyance.","\"Anyway, it’s true that I owe you for saving me, but what do you want from me?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Frankly, there’s nothing you can give me that I don’t already have or can’t acquire myself, nor is there anything you can do for me right now, so I will collect this debt later.\"","\"That’s fine too, I guess.\"","Yuan then asked, \"By the way, what happened to Prime Eternal Morveth?\"","\"I chased her away for now, but she will definitely get her revenge one way or another. That said, as long as you’re within the Demonic Realm, I doubt she will try to attack again.\"","\"In that case, I’ll stay here for a little longer,\" Yuan said in a joking voice.","\"...\"","The Demon God fell silent.","\"What? Are you going to kick me out of the Demonic Realm because I came back here without your permission?\"","\"I had considered removing you,\" the Demon God said, his voice calm yet deliberate, \"but there is something about you that intrigues me. So, I will allow you to remain here a while longer.\"","Yuan raised a brow but said nothing. Though the Demon God could have easily asked whatever piqued his curiosity, Yuan chose to remain silent. After all, this gave him the chance to stay in the Demonic Realm a little longer.","\"I will be keeping a close eye on you... Tian Chenyu.\"","After saying that, the crimson world immediately collapsed, and the Demon God vanished into thin air.","\"Yuan! Are you okay? What happened just now?\"","The moment Yuan was released from the crimson sphere, Supreme Ruler Dena rushed to his side, a rare look of concern evident on her face.","\"As you can see, I am perfectly fine,\" he responded with a calm smile on his face.","\"I just had a small conversation with the Demon God, that’s all,\" he added.","\"What did you just say?!\" Supreme Ruler Dena and Lev exclaimed in unison.","\"How can you say something that shocking so casually, as if it were nothing?!\" Lev added, his voice filled with disbelief.","\"You just spoke with the Demon God? Really?\" Even Supreme Ruler Dena found it difficult to believe.","However, when she recalled how her full-power attack had failed to leave even a scratch on that barrier, the possibility no longer seemed so far-fetched.","\"Yes,\" Yuan confirmed with a slight nod.","\"...\"","The two of them could only stare at Yuan in stunned silence, their mouths slightly agape. Though countless questions burned at the tip of their tongues, they dared not ask. After all, it would be like a mere servant inquiring what a general had discussed with the emperor.","\"So... what now?\" Lev asked after a long moment of silence.","\"We resume whatever we were doing before meeting the Primal Sovereign of the Seas,\" Yuan said.","They nodded before continuing their journey across the Bloody Expanse.","Several months later, they had ventured far enough that the Sea Devils were no longer in hiding and began launching attacks on them.","Seeing this, Yuan thought of something and retrieved the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ Blood Essence.","The moment the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ aura appeared, the Sea Devils immediately stopped attacking and went into hiding, allowing them to travel in peace again."]},{"number":2400,"title":"Chapter 2400: Leaving the Bloody Expanse","paragraphs":["With the Primal Sovereign of the Seas’ Blood Essence keeping the Sea Devils away, Yuan and his group were able to traverse the rest of the Bloody Expanse in peace.","After several more years of travel, they finally reached land.","However, before actually entering the land, Yuan asked out loud, \"Hey, Dena, will it be fine for you to walk around without any disguise? You’re supposed to be inside the Deprived Crimson Valley, after all.\"","\"There’s no point in disguising myself. They’ll discover that I’ve left sooner or later. In fact, I wouldn’t be surprised if they already know,\" she replied calmly. \"Besides... It’s a hassle.\"","\"Even so, it’ll help us avoid detection for the time being,\" Yuan insisted. \"You’re still recovering, so it’s better if you conceal yourself for now.\"","Had Supreme Ruler Dena been at full strength, such precautions would have been unnecessary. But in her current state, Yuan had no desire to deal with the current Supreme Ruler. More importantly, he wanted to avoid unnecessary trouble before fully understanding the circumstances behind her exile and the current state of the world.","\"Fine...\"","Supreme Ruler Dena let out a soft sigh before shifting her appearance, her hair turning pitch black as her figure grew several inches taller, and her presence transformed into something barely noticeable.","\"What about me?\" Lev suddenly asked aloud.","Yuan turned to look at him with raised eyebrows.","\"Sorry, that was a dumb question...\" An awkward smile tugged at Lev’s lips when he realized that he was essentially a nobody.","\"What about you?\" Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly said to Yuan. \"You will cause misunderstandings if you walk around like tha.\"","Yuan looked down at his own body and replied, \"Is it because I look like a noble?\"","She quietly nodded.","\"In that case...\"","Unlike Supreme Ruler Dena, Yuan had to swallow an appearance-altering pill to change his appearance.","Moments later, Yuan transformed into a red-skinned Lower Demon.","Shortly after, they departed the crimson sea and entered a harbor at its very edge, one that belonged to a medium-sized city known as the City of Devils.","Upon arrival, Yuan extended his divine sense, sweeping it across the entire city in an instant.","There were just over ten million inhabitants, the majority of them Lower Demons. While the sheer population was already surprising for a city of this size, what truly caught Yuan off guard was that more than half of them had already reached the God Ascension realm.","’The number of God Ascension demons in this medium-sized city alone likely surpasses the entire population of God Ascension cultivators within the Nine Heavens! And this is just one city!’","Thanks to their immortality, demons were free from one of humanity’s greatest limitations—their finite lifespan. With eternity at their disposal, they never had to fear running out of time before reaching the next realm.","Moreover, demons were inherently superior to humans in terms of physique and bloodline, granting them a natural advantage in cultivation.","Where humans required extraordinary talent to ascend to higher realms like the God Ascension Realm, demons could do so with far greater ease.","Seeing such an overwhelming number of demons at this level, Yuan could easily imagine them sweeping across the Nine Heavens should they ever choose to invade.","Fortunately, these demons were not Forsaken and had no reason nor desire to invade another world.","Once they were inside the city, Yuan looked at the two and asked, \"Now, where should we begin? How does one acquire information in this world?\"","\"Well, it depends on what sort of information you’re after. For general questions, just about anyone can help. But for lucrative intel like what you seek, you’ll need the Crimson Brokers.\"","\"Where can we find them?\" Yuan asked.","\"There’s at least one stationed in almost every city. In a medium-sized city like this, they’re almost certainly here. They usually wear a black robe with a crimson symbol on their chest.\"","Yuan used his divine sense to scan the entire city again.","\"I found him. Let’s go.\"","Some time later, Yuan and his companions approached a black‐robed figure loitering in a shadowy alley, looking extremely suspicious.","\"Hey, are you a Crimson Broker?\" Yuan asked as he calmly approached the individual.","\"Why are you asking?\" The Crimson Broker asked.","\"I’m looking for information on a certain individual.\"","\"What’s their reputation like?\"","\"One of the most famous—or infamous individuals in this world.\"","\"In that case, there’s likely no need for an investigation. Who is this person? And what sort of information are you looking for?\"","\"She’s Supreme Ruler—\" Yuan abruptly halted his speech when he remembered that Supreme Ruler Dena’s name was forbidden.","\"Ahem,\" he cleared his throat before restarting, \"She used to be a Supreme Ruler, and her name is one that cannot be uttered. I want to know what she did that caused her to be—\"","\"W-Wait!\" the Crimson Broker suddenly interrupted him. \"If you’re talking about ’that’ Supreme Ruler, then you can forget it because I cannot help you!\"","Without elaborating, the Crimson Broker hastily left the scene the next second.","\"...\"","\"Looks like this will be more difficult than I initially anticipated...\" Yuan sighed out loud after a moment of silence.","He turned to look at Lev and asked, \"What now? Is there anyone else who can provide us with the information we seek?\"","\"Well...\" Lev started, his gaze shifting to Supreme Ruler Dena. \"Considering how that Crimson Broker reacted just now, I doubt we’ll be able to gather information on ’her’ through normal means.\"","\"Although Crimson Brokers aren’t official informants, they just skirt the edges of shady. As for those in the shadows who are willing to do anything for money... I only know of the Abyssal Council.\"","\"Great. Where can we find them?\" Yuan asked without hesitation and a single ounce of fear in his voice.","\"Um... sorry, but I have no clue. I am only aware of their existence,\" Lev said while shaking his head.","However, before Yuan could respond, Supreme Ruler Dena suddenly spoke, \"I know where we can find the Abyssal Council.\""]}]);
